ur Temple (Candi Borobudur) the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. You will tour around the temple, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was built during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano has been producing during its history. When you finish our visit to Borobudur, you will head northeast towards Candi Prambanan, the Hindu temple and classified as a World Heritage Site by Unesco since 1991. This temple was finished building around the year 856 to commemorate the victory of the descendant Sanjaya de Siva, Rikai Pikatan on the last sovereign Sailendra of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to the Trimurti, the expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the Destroyer. After this day you will never forget and take to your hotel.',NULL,'Please be ready at hotel\'s lobby at : 08.00am for pick up Pick up point : Meliá Purosani Yogyakarta Jl. Mayor Suryotomo No.31, Ngupasan, Kec. Gondomanan, Kota Yogyakarta, Daerah Istimewa Yogyakarta 55122 Telepon: (0274) 589521','{\"date\": \"2024-01-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-01-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(4931633,'93','Fiona MacKillop',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-01-09','2024-01-10','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Single',728000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot