orong with all the comforts you would expect from an international chain of four-star hotels in Sorong. Enjoy 37-inch LED TVs, cable channels, high-speed internet access and a full range of other amenities that will make your stay here the most comfortable one possible.',NULL,'Check-in time 14.00 Check-out time 12.00 Early check-in is subject to availability upon arrival.','{\"date\": \"2024-05-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5043393,'264','Beate Jungwirth',30719,214472,'Transport Fee (from Hotel to Airport)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-05-05','2024-05-05','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Per Car',280000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-05-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5043475,'265','Elizabeth Jane Carter',31083,203779,'9D8N Flores - Riung - Warebo (2D1N LOB Rinca - Komodo Tour)','Confirmed',NULL,9,'2024-08-08','2024-08-16','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Persons (2-3 / Single)',46668000.00,'TOUR ITINERARY DAY 1 : ARRIVAL IN MAUMERE - MONI Arrival in Maumere, the cultural capital of the Isla de Flores, in this part of the trip, we will cross the island of Flores, from east to west, along the famous and only road that crosses the island, known among locals as La Transflores. At the Frans Seda airport, our native Flores guide will be waiting for you, along with him and a driver, we drive to Moni by private car. It will take about four hours, but we will be able to make some stops in the towns of Ledadero, Sikka and other places on the way to Moni. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Kelimutu Ecolodge or Kelimutu Paradiso Resort DAY 2 : MONI - KELIMUTU - RIUNG It’s worth to experience the sun rise at Kelimutu three colored crater lakes you will begin your day early in the morning (start about 04.00 o’clock). Last update: 15 Jul 2013, Typical eruption style: Explosive, Kelimutu volcano eruptions: 1968, 1938, 1865. Kelimutu (Keli Mutu) volcano in central Flores, Indonesia, is famous for its 3 colorful acid crater lakes, where different salts and oxides in suspension or solution give the lakes varying colors ranging from blue and dark green to intense red. In historic times, few small phreatic explosions have been the only activity at the volcano. The scenic craters with their lakes are popular tourist destinations. Background: The western lake, Tiwu Ata Mbupu (Lake of Old People) is commonly blue. Tiwu Nua Muri Kooh Tai (Lake of Young Men and Maidens) and Tiwu Ata Polo (Bewitched, or Enchanted Lake), which share a common crater wall, are commonly green- and red-coloured, respectively, although lake colours vary periodically. During the dry season reduction processes let Ba, Cu, and As minerals precipitate, in the wet season, the oxidation and precipitation of iron minerals (ferric oxide: Fe2O3) produces intense red colors. Active upwelling occurs at the two eastern lakes and is probably fed by subaqueous fumaroles. Kelimutu volcano is flanked by the older cones of Kelido and Kelibara 3 km to the north and 2 km to the south, respectively (Source: GVP) On the way you will experience the dramatic change in both nature pattern and ethnicity. You could be found yourself in the Lio ethnic’s environment – pay at call to their villages SAGA village or Wologai and try to comprehend the local’s daily life or just having closer look into their work of architectures. Lunch will be served at a local restaurant in Ende. Continue drive to Riung with Stop at Penggajawa BLUE stone beach, here you could see local woman collect the stones to sell and building the house of garden. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Pondok SVD or Nirvana Lodge or Similar DAY 3 : RIUNG - BAJAWA After breakfast take a boat trip to explore the spectacular sea garden of seventeen islands. The reef of “Seventeen Islands” is very spectacular – with a variety of hard and soft corals and lots of colorful fish. There are 17 islands in total, with plenty of idyllic white sand beaches for swimming and a multitude of coral species and sea creatures to discover. Lunch & BBQ will be provided at the island, sail back to Riung then driving up to Bajawa. With stop at Soa -a natural hot spring water for taking bathing-. Bajawa is a cool and small town as a capital city of Ngada Regency (home of Ngada, Riung and Nagekeo tribes). Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : New Virgo Hotel DAY 4 : BAJAWA - BENA - GURU SINA - AIMERE - RUTENG Today in the morning we will be able to pay a visit to the Wawo Muda volcano, a one hour walk, in a quite gentle voluntary trekking, where we will see a great volcano, with lakes, that when they have water, they form colors, similar to those of their older brother Kelimutu. We will also enjoy views of impressive volcanoes such as the Inerie and Ebulobo. After seeing the sunrise, we return to the hotel, to have our well-deserved breakfast. And then, we go to Bena, one of the traditional towns, better known in Flores, they belong to the Ngada tribes. Tribes that despite being Christianized, still maintain their animistic beliefs. We will take the opportunity to go further on foot, and reach other villages Ngada as located behind a jungle of bamboo. After having lunch in Bajawa, our new and long drive begins, around another 4-5 hours until we reach Ruteng. But we will stop in a traditional town, called Aimere, where we will see and (those who want to try) how the Palm liquor is distilled, called \"Arak.\" Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Spring Hill or Sinda or Revaya Hotel DAY 5 : RUTENG - DENGE - TREK WAEREBO Today begins your journey to Waerebo, to the tribes of the high Manggarai Mountains, but before you start, you will pass by a place, where you will be able to see the only spider web rice fields in the world. Then 5 - 6 hours by car, bordering the south coast of flowers, overlooking the Sea of Savu, to arrive at the time to go inland, to reach a town called Dintor, here you can having lunch at local restaurant. Moving forward to get wae lomba the starting point of trekking to Waerebo for -+ 2.30 hours, Waerebo is the oldest traditional village of Manggarainesse. The rain forest along the trek to Waerebo is one of the Wealthiest areas in Indonesia in biological terms. The forest is simply like a huge Garden of Eden. Then walk through the forest with deferent vegetation is of great interest, from the families of orchids, palms, ferns, etc. Natural voice of various type singing birds will entertain you along the trip. The clear and fresh water river on the way up to the village is a good point to take rest. In the village of Waerebo, visitor can see conical houses, which one of it is a ‘drum house’ with very unique architectures, place for holding meetings, rituals and Sunday morning prayers. The drum house is a communal building for a clan or clan branch, symbolizing the ideal unity of patrilineal descent. The place has been developed as tourism site, sleeping on the traditional house and having local cuisine together with local community is very wonderful and unforgettable moment for the visitor. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Waerebo Guest House (with mattresses on the floor.) DAY 6 : WAEREBO - DENGE - DINTOR - LABUAN BAJO After breakfast trekking down to Waelomba then continue Labuan Bajo -the Western tip of Flores Island-. On the way stops will be made at REPI Beach for quick swimming, relaxing or beach walking, lunch boxes are provided. Driving along the south coast is very fantastic with breathtaking panoramic of sea and hill view. Stop at Lembor area for afternoon coffee break and to have closer look of huge area Rice field in Flores Island. Then direct driving to Labuan Bajo, On arrival direct check into your hotel. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Puri Sari or La Cecile or Seasta or Golo Hilltop DAY 7 : LABUAN BAJO - MENJARITE - RINCA - KALONG ISLAND - PADAR Arrival at Komodo Airport in Labuan Bajo west Flores, meeting service with our guide and transfer to the pier of Labuan Bajo for Kalong island. Stop at Menjalite and Kelor islands for snorkeling, relaxing and trekking, then continue to Kalong island, Here you can see the amazing thousands fling foxes set out from mangrove tree at 06 – 07 pm, the lovely sunset really enjoyable could be seen from your boat trip in this place. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : CABIN AC BOAT DAY 8 : PADAR - KOMODO - PINK BEACH - MANTA POINT - TAKA MAKASSAR - LABUAN BAJO After having breakfast in your boat, heading to Padar Island, taking trek to Padar Island until having the top view point to get breathtaking scenery of three bays around, Padar Island hike in Komodo has some of the most amazing views in Indonesia, trek to downhill and back to the Boat for sailing directly to Loh Liang –the Ranger station in Komodo Island-. By passing through many small islands, After registering start to take basic trekking to see the Giant Rizard / Komodo Dragon and other wild animals as: Timor deer, wild pig, wild chicken and many variously of tropical bird. Please keep your look at any directions as sometimes you will also find young Komodo dragon hanging over the trees. A local ranger will be led you during the trek. Return to the boat on to Pink beach for snorkeling, swimming and relaxing. It is really spectacular and unspoiled coral reef and many color fish. This is one of best side for snorkeling diving. Sail toward Manta Point to exploring Huge Mantas by snorkeling even watching from your boat trip (can’t be guaranteed if weather is not good, like wave and current are strongly) visit also the taka Makaasar its really tiny island with white sand beach really enjoyable to relaxing or beach walking then heading to Labuan Bajo for overnight and dinner. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Puri Sari or La Cecile or Golo Hilltop DAY 9 : LABUAN BAJO - DENPASAR After breakfast, taking short city sightseeing with visiting the Batu Cermin (Mirror Stone) Cave. The grotto is 75 by 75 meters large, and contains stalactites and stalagmites. Some tunnels are narrow and dark but in others sunlight falls. Then local market before taking you to the airport for flight to Denpasar. Meals : Breakfast',NULL,'Guide contact: Mr Konstant +62812-3875-7858','{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": \"Nairoa Waipare Street, Alok, Sikka, Watumilok, Flores, Kabupaten Sikka\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"Capa Resort Maumere\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": \"Jalan Golo No.Silatey, Labuan Bajo, Kec. Komodo, Kabupaten Manggarai Barat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"La Cecile Komodo Hotel and Cafe\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5044702,'90','Alice Camilla Louise Edinger',30508,207250,'Airport to Kuta','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-24','2024-04-24','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Persons (1-3)',300000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-24\", \"text\": \"ETA: 15.05 by Cathay Pacific CX785 to Hong Kong on 24 Apr\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Denpasar Airport\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"The Anvaya Beach Resort Bali\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5044703,'90','Alice Camilla Louise Edinger',30508,207266,'Kuta to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-25','2024-04-25','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Persons (1-3)',300000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-25\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in hotel lobby\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": \"The Anvaya Beach Resort Bali\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-25\", \"text\": \"ETD: 11.05 by Lion Air JT924 to Kupang on 25 Apr\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Denpasar Airport\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5044806,'266','RONAN ERTUS',30508,215968,'1D Bali Tour (Custom Itinerary)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-10','2024-04-10','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Person (1)',0.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-10\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in hotel lobby\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": \"Lotus Bungalow Candidasa\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Wapa Di Ume Ubud\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5044807,'266','RONAN ERTUS',30508,215968,'1D Bali Tour (Custom Itinerary)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-11','2024-04-11','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Person (1)',0.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-11\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in hotel lobby\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": \"Wapa Di Ume Ubud\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Wapa Di Ume Ubud\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5044808,'266','RONAN ERTUS',30508,215968,'1D Bali Tour (Custom Itinerary)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-13','2024-04-13','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Person (1)',0.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-13\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in hotel lobby\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": \"Wapa Di Ume Ubud\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Wapa Di Ume Ubud\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5044809,'266','RONAN ERTUS',30508,207262,'Ubud to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-14','2024-04-14','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Persons (1-3)',392000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-14\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in hotel lobby\", \"time\": \"20:00\", \"locality\": \"Wapa Di Ume Ubud\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-14\", \"text\": \"ETD: 01.05 by Qatar Airways QR961 to Doha on 15 Apr\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Denpasar Airport\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5047090,'267','Patricia Lopez del Pozo',30783,215156,'Java Bali Overload Tour : Yogyakarta City, Mount Bromo & Ijen Crater 5D4N / A. The Phoenix Hotel - J','Confirmed','JS-JAVA05',5,'2024-04-30','2024-05-04','Jacob','Tami',2,'Persons (2 / Double)',24120000.00,'Travel overland from Java all the way to Bali! This tour takes you to an amazing road trip you will never forget. From discovering the ancient wonders Borobudur and Prambanan in Yogyakarta, a city rich of authentic Javanese culture, to climbing the majestic volcanoes of Bromo and Ijen to witness the spectacular sunrises and unique blue fire, and finish on the island of the gods, Bali. You have the option of going by train from Yogyakarta until Surabaya before you reach Bromo, less tiring, more convenient but it comes at different price. On the other hand, with car you can make some stops along the way so you have a chance to see something new. It is up to you! Day 1 : Welcome to Yogyakarta Welcome to the cradle of Indonesian culture, Yogyakarta. A tourist destination for its ancient palaces, temples, batik workshops, gamelan music orchestras, court dances and wayang puppet shows. Upon your arrival in Yogyakarta a representative of come2indonesia will be waiting for you with a sign indicating your name to take you to your hotel and the rest of the day is for you. The journey from the airport should be around 2-2,5 hours. Meals : - Accommodation : A. The Phoenix Hotel - Deluxe Legacy Room Day 2 : Yogyakarta City Tour - Borobodur Temple - Prambanan Temple After breakfast, your guide will pick you up with your hotel to start exploring the city. This excursion will make you lose yourselves in the authentic magic of Yogyakarta. One of the most beautiful and complete routes of the cultural capital of Indonesia. At the scheduled time, your guide will pick you up to begin the tour of Borobudur, the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. Depending on where you stay in the city, the drive can be 1-1,5 hours to the temple. Arrival at the temple, you will walk around the garden area, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano has been producing during its history. After visiting one of the most important Buddhist temples in Southeast Asia, you will continue the journey to the heart of the city. You will visit the Keraton, or also known as the Sultan’s Palace. The palace is a complex building two centuries old. Next, you will hear the song of the “freedom” of the birds in the bird market, you will visit the “Water Castle” that occupies the highest part at the northern end of the vast complex of Taman Sari. Then, stroll around Malioboro Street, one of the main streets of Yogyakarta, with its merchants, horse carriages, taxi-bikes and markets. An incredible experience that will make the hours fly by. Finishing the tour in the centre of the city of Yogyakarta, you will head northeast towards Prambanan, the temple of Hinduists and classified as a World Heritage Site by UNESCO since 1991. This temple was completed in 856 AD to commemorate the victory of the descendant of Sanjaya dynasty, Rikai Pikatan, against the last Shailendra sovereign of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to Shiva, one of the Trimurti which is an expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the Destroyer. After this unforgettable day, you will take you to your hotel. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : A. The Phoenix Hotel - Deluxe Legacy Room Day 3 : Yogyakarta - Bromo (By Train) Ready with your suitcases, the time has come to say a farewell to this dream city. You will enjoy your breakfast at the hotel, and at the indicated time, with your guide, you will travel to Jombang / Mojokerta by train. Then by private car you will go to your hotel located on the slopes of the Bromo volcano. In total it will be about 8 hours of travel. check-in at the hotel and deserved rest. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : A. Jiwa Jawa Bromo - Deluxe Room Day 4 : Bromo - Ijen Very early, your guide and a jeep driver will be waiting for you at the hotel to attend one of the most spectacular sunrises in Indonesia. Even though you have to get up early, it will be worth it. You will climb to a high point first in full darkness and, little by little the first rays of sun are giving way to a huge and indescribable caldera that makes up the entire view of the Bromo and Semeru Natural Park. With Bromo, a volcano of great fumaroles and behind it, the Semeru Volcano with explosions every 20 minutes exactly, will make you have one of the most rewarding experiences ever. After enjoying the sunset, by jeep, we will go to the slopes of the volcano where you can go to the Bromo volcano and after climbing some stairs you can reach the very edge of its crater and see the impressive activity it has. We return to the hotel to cool off and enjoy your breakfast. At the agreed time, we will leave for our next destination, the Ijen volcano. This section lasts about 7-8 hours by car where we will make a stop to eat. Take this trip to rest. Arriving in Ijen, we will leave you at your hotel, check in and enjoy your deserved rest. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : A. Ijen Resort - Villa\'s Deluxe Day 5 : Ijen Tour - Ketapang - Bali The day has finally come to visit one of the most attractive volcanoes in Indonesia! One of the last open pit sulfur mines that survive on the planet. For this climb you can choose between two schedules; leave very early at 1 AM to see the blue fire (please not that it is not always visible, for example during rainy days) or leave more quietly at 4 AM only for the sunrise. You can decide later when you meet the guide. Once we pick you up at your hotel, you will head towards the village of Licin to reach the slope of the volcano to begin the steep climb to the crater of the volcano. During this trek, your guide will give you double filter masks to protect you from the natural chemicals of sulfur. At an altitude of 2883 meters and when dawn begins, an incredible contrast of colors will open before your eyes. A yellow earth scene and a large turquoise blue lake inside the crater that contrast with a suspended white cloud that is continuously expelling the volcano. In turn, among so much beauty you will see the local miners do what is said to be one of the toughest jobs in the world. These miners go down to the crater of the volcano to load 80 to 100 kilos of sulfur on their shoulders and then sell it. After this amazing experience on the edge of Ijen volcano crater, we begin the descent with an incredible panoramic view of the mountains that make up the national park. We will take you to your hotel to cool off and have breakfast and we start the journey to Bali for about 5 hours at least, depending on where you stay in Bali. To do this, we will go first to the port of Banyuwangi where we will take the ferry to cross to Bali. It is a journey of only 30 minutes, but remember to adjust your watch by an hour due to the time zone change. Welcome to the island of the Gods. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Flight details ETA : 14.35 by Batik Air ID6360 from Jakarta on 30 April 2024 Drop off Point Goya Boutique Resort Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : (0361) 9083368','{\"date\": \"2024-04-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5047192,'267','Patricia Lopez del Pozo',31083,212374,'3D2N LOB Rinca - Padar - Komodo Island Tour (Medium Standard Boat)','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-05-11','2024-05-13','Jacob','Tami',2,'Persons (2-3)',29196000.00,'TOUR ITINERARY Highlights: Menjarite, Kelor, Strawberry Rock, Kalong, Rinca, Padar, Komodo Island, Pink Beach, Taka Makassar, Manta Point, Kanawa, B.Cermin Mirror Cave DAY 1 : DENPASAR - LABUAN BAJO - MENJARITE - KELOR - KALONG ISLAND Arrival at Komodo Airport in Labuan Bajo west Flores, meeting service with our tour guide and transfer to the pier of Labuan Bajo for Rinca Island. It’s about 2 hours sail to the island of Komodo Dragon, stop at Menjarite island for snorkeling then continue to Rinca island-the Island of Komodo dragon, you will find not just e Dragons but also many wild animals like, deer, wild buffalo, long-tailed macaque and wild pig also numerous of birds. Keep your eyes look up as sometime you will find the young Komodo dragons on the trees. A local ranger will lead you through this natural preservation. Late afternoon sailing directly to Kalong Rinca Island to see the hundreds of fling foxes set out from the mangrove tree at 06-07pm, the lovely sunset from the boat trip really enjoyable. Lunch and dinner on boat. Meals : Lunch - Dinner DAY 2 : KALONG - PADAR - KOMODO - PINK BEACH - MANTA POINT - TAKA MAKASSAR - SEBAYUR After having breakfast in your boat, heading to Padar Island, taking trek to Padar Island until having the top view point to get breathtaking scenery of three bays around, Padar Island hike in Komodo has some of the most amazing views in Indonesia, trek to downhill and back to the Boat for sailing directly to Loh Liang – the Ranger station in Komodo Island. By passing through many small islands, After registering start to take basic trekking to see the GIANT RIZARD / KOMODO DRAGON and other wild animals as: Timor deer, wild pig, wild chicken and many variously of tropical bird. Please keep your look at any directions as sometimes you will also find young Komodo dragon hanging over the trees. A local ranger will be led you during the trek. Return to the boat on to Pink beach for snorkeling, swimming and relaxing. It is really spectacular and unspoiled coral reef and many color fish. This is one of best side for snorkeling diving. Sail toward MANTA POINT to exploring Huge Mantas by snorkeling even watching from your boat trip (can’t be guaranteed if weather is not good, like wave and current are strongly) visit also the taka Makassar its really tiny island with white sand beach really enjoyable to relaxing or beach walking then heading to Sebayur island, overnight dinner on boat. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner DAY 3 : SEBAYUR - KANAWA ISLANDS - LABUAN BAJO - DENPASAR After breakfast on the boat, taking swimming, snorkeling and relaxing as well at seraya and Kanawa. Then back to Labuan Bajo to continue your next excursion with visiting the Batu Cermin (Mirror Stone) Cave. The grotto is 75 by 75 meters large, and contains stalactites and stalagmites. Some tunnels are narrow and dark but in others sunlight falls. Then local market before taking you to the airport for flight to Denpasar. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Attention: The itinerary is subject to change due to the weather, tide level and operating conditions without prior notice.',NULL,'Pick up time : 07.00AM (Please be ready at hotel\'s lobby) Pick up point: Hotel Sudamala Resort Jl. Pantai Pede No.Km. 3, Labuan Bajo, Kabupaten Manggarai Barat, Nusa Tenggara Tim. 86554 Phone : (0385) 2385555 Drop off point Labuan Bajo Airport ETD : 17.20 by Air Asia QZ647 to Denpasar on 13 May 2024','{\"date\": \"2024-05-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5047303,'268','Iera Gonzalez',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-22','2024-04-22','Guio','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',392000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-22\", \"text\": \"ETA 16.55 BY Qatar Airways QR962 from Doha on 22 April 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-22\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Komaneka at Bisma\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5049436,'173','Harald Lang',30805,202689,'CGK-PKN','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-03-11','2024-03-11','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Person',3424000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-03-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-03-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5049437,'173','Harald Lang',30805,212272,'PKN-SUB','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-03-14','2024-03-14','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Person',3740000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-03-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-03-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5049761,'181','Scuba Travel Group - Misool March 2024',30680,200914,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-03-28','2024-03-29','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Single',840000.00,'Enjoy our spacious elegant deluxe room with 40 m2 of room size. Enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, hot and cold shower, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel.','{\"date\": \"2024-03-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-03-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5049762,'181','Scuba Travel Group - Misool March 2024',30680,200914,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-03-28','2024-03-29','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Twin',1680000.00,'Enjoy our spacious elegant deluxe room with 40 m2 of room size. Enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, hot and cold shower, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel.','{\"date\": \"2024-03-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-03-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5050488,'268','Iera Gonzalez',30711,200833,'One Bedroom Pool Villa','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-04-22','2024-04-24','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',13518400.00,'A secluded one-bedroom pool villa of 210 sqm with 30 sqm private swimming pool overlooking the valley. The villa room is luxuriously spacious with elegant interiors. Ideal for honeymooners.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5050491,'266','RONAN ERTUS',30508,207257,'Airport to Candidasa','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-02','2024-04-02','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Persons (1-3)',616000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-02\", \"text\": \"ETA: 22.40 by Qatar Airways QR960 from Doha on 02 Apr\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Denpasar Airport\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Lotus Bungalow Candidasa\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5050512,'268','Iera Gonzalez',30508,202896,'Cascada Leke Leke - Templo Ulun Danu','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-23','2024-04-23','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',2352000.00,'At 08.00 am, we pick you up from your hotel and start our journey to Tunjuk Village in Tabanan district. Upon arrival, you will be greeted with open arms and with the warm smiles of the locals you meet along the way. You\'ll meet in the outer courtyard of the village temple and meet your local guides. Throughout the hike you will meet people from the village involved in the tasks that keep their lives busy day in and day out. You can choose to observe or participate in them to gain a better understanding of village life. The mighty water buffalo is still used to drag the plough through the muddy rice paddies and prepare the land for planting. Or maybe you want to help with planting or harvesting, depending on the time of year. When you complete the tour in the rice paddies, you\'ll follow your guide on a path through lush gardens where villagers go about their daily chores. There are women who beat the rice with heavy mallets to remove the hooves. After lunch we leave Tunjuk Village and continue our journey to visit THE TANAH LOT. We\'ll close the visit by watching the sunset at the most famous and photographed temple in Bali. Torn from the earth on a stone pedestal sculpted by the incoming tides, the solitary black towers of Tanah Lot and the plumes of foliage spilling over the precipices, recall the delicacy of Chinese painting. The Pura Tanah Lot or the Earth Temple in the middle of the sea was built in the 16th century. At the end of the day, you\'ll be transferred to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Komaneka at Bisma\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5050566,'268','Iera Gonzalez',30508,202892,'Tegalalang - Cafe Luwak - Kintamani - Besakih - Tirta Gangga','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-24','2024-04-24','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',2352000.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Komaneka at Bisma\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Camaya Bali\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5050658,'268','Iera Gonzalez',32650,216128,'Butterfly Bamboo House','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-04-24','2024-04-26','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',22960000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5050682,'268','Iera Gonzalez',30508,213310,'Karangasem to Uluwatu','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-26','2024-04-26','Guio','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',616000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"12:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Camaya Bali\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Bvlgari Resort Bali\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5050769,'269','PUI WA VICKY CHEUNG',30671,200626,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-03-28','2024-03-29','Rendy','Rendy',11,'Twin',11704000.00,'Deluxe Room with a room area of 28 square meters each, there are 2 types of bed, king and twin bed with a size of 28 square meters each.',NULL,'Check-in time 14.00 Check-out time 12.00 Early check-in is subject to availability upon arrival. Flights information ETA: 13.20 by Cathay Pacific CX 777 from Hong Kong on 28 Mar ETD: 00.10 by Garuda Indonesia GA 682 to Sorong on 29 Mar','{\"date\": \"2024-03-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-03-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5050792,'268','Iera Gonzalez',32651,216129,'One Bedroom Ocean View Villa','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-04-26','2024-04-28','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',48787200.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5050847,'268','Iera Gonzalez',30508,212544,'Uluwatu to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-28','2024-04-28','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (1-3)',560000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"10:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Bvlgari Resort Bali\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-28\", \"text\": \"ETD 15.10 by Garuda Indonesia GA842 to Singapore on 28 April 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5052591,'270','Juan Pablo Gonzalez',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-12','2024-04-12','Guio','Eddy',1,'Persons (1-3)',420000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.','ETA : 12APR 24 JQ 90 Denpasar (Bali) 22:25 Drop off : Komaneka at Tanggayuda Alamat: Br. Tanggayuda, Kedewatan, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 978123','ETA : 12APR 24 JQ 90 Denpasar (Bali) 22:25 Drop off : Komaneka at Tanggayuda Alamat: Br. Tanggayuda, Kedewatan, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 978123','{\"date\": \"2024-04-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5052594,'270','Juan Pablo Gonzalez',30710,200847,'Valley Pool Villa','Confirmed',NULL,5,'2024-04-12','2024-04-17','Guio','Eddy',1,'Double',23715000.00,'This beautifully appointed 179 sqm pavilion has a 12 sqm private swimming pool has a wooden sunning deck and traditional Balinese gazebo. The luxurious bathroom has a large bathtub of polished volcanic stone and separate shower. With spectacular views of the valley, this one-bedroom villa is ideal for unwinding after a long day.','These rates are applicable for the capacity specified, non-commissionable and inclusive of breakfast, 10% service charge and 11% government tax.','Note : Honey Moon Guest','{\"date\": \"2024-04-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5052640,'270','Juan Pablo Gonzalez',30508,202882,'Tegalalang – Tirta Empul – Kintamani – Besakih – Tukad Cepung','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-13','2024-04-13','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (2)',2040000.00,'The first destination is Kusamba Beach, it is one of the favorite places of interest in Bali which is famous with the beautiful beach, we can also meet a fish market in this place which is usually held between 10 am until 4 pm. Then we go to Goa Lawah, this is one of the favourite place to be visited, because here is a nature cave dwelt by thousands of tail bat located at north side from Jeroan/center of Goa Lawah Temple. Next we go to Bukit Jambul, it is strategically located beside of the main road from Denpasar to Besakih Temple and it is one of the tourist destinations that visited on Besakih Tour. It is situated in the plateau area which is blessed with the beautiful panorama of rice terrace and green coconuts three unfolding to the sea. After visit Bukit Jambul, we’ll continue to Besakih Temple is the biggest Hindu temple in Bali which the local people call Pura Besakih. It owns beautiful view from the top of temple area where we can see the wide nature panorama until to the ocean so that’s why this temple is many visited by tourists from all over the world. Then go to Kertagosa, This place also owns Taman Gili, a building floating or sees like floating because it is intentionally founded in the middle of a fish pond.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-13\", \"text\": \"Please Ready at Lobby\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5052646,'270','Juan Pablo Gonzalez',30508,202882,'Ubud – Ulun Danu Beratan – Cascada Leke–Leke – Tanah Lot','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-14','2024-04-14','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (2)',2040000.00,'The first destination is Kusamba Beach, it is one of the favorite places of interest in Bali which is famous with the beautiful beach, we can also meet a fish market in this place which is usually held between 10 am until 4 pm. Then we go to Goa Lawah, this is one of the favourite place to be visited, because here is a nature cave dwelt by thousands of tail bat located at north side from Jeroan/center of Goa Lawah Temple. Next we go to Bukit Jambul, it is strategically located beside of the main road from Denpasar to Besakih Temple and it is one of the tourist destinations that visited on Besakih Tour. It is situated in the plateau area which is blessed with the beautiful panorama of rice terrace and green coconuts three unfolding to the sea. After visit Bukit Jambul, we’ll continue to Besakih Temple is the biggest Hindu temple in Bali which the local people call Pura Besakih. It owns beautiful view from the top of temple area where we can see the wide nature panorama until to the ocean so that’s why this temple is many visited by tourists from all over the world. Then go to Kertagosa, This place also owns Taman Gili, a building floating or sees like floating because it is intentionally founded in the middle of a fish pond.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5052656,'270','Juan Pablo Gonzalez',30508,202882,'Tenganan – Playa Virgin – Templo Lempuyang – Tirta Gangga','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-15','2024-04-15','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (2)',2040000.00,'The first destination is Kusamba Beach, it is one of the favorite places of interest in Bali which is famous with the beautiful beach, we can also meet a fish market in this place which is usually held between 10 am until 4 pm. Then we go to Goa Lawah, this is one of the favourite place to be visited, because here is a nature cave dwelt by thousands of tail bat located at north side from Jeroan/center of Goa Lawah Temple. Next we go to Bukit Jambul, it is strategically located beside of the main road from Denpasar to Besakih Temple and it is one of the tourist destinations that visited on Besakih Tour. It is situated in the plateau area which is blessed with the beautiful panorama of rice terrace and green coconuts three unfolding to the sea. After visit Bukit Jambul, we’ll continue to Besakih Temple is the biggest Hindu temple in Bali which the local people call Pura Besakih. It owns beautiful view from the top of temple area where we can see the wide nature panorama until to the ocean so that’s why this temple is many visited by tourists from all over the world. Then go to Kertagosa, This place also owns Taman Gili, a building floating or sees like floating because it is intentionally founded in the middle of a fish pond.',NULL,'Pick Up & Droop off : Komaneka at Tanggayuda Alamat: Br. Tanggayuda, Kedewatan, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 978123','{\"date\": \"2024-04-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5052663,'270','Juan Pablo Gonzalez',30508,212411,'Ubud to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-17','2024-04-17','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (1-3)',840000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,'Pick Up: Please be Ready at the Lobby At 06:00 AM Komaneka at Tanggayuda Alamat: Br. Tanggayuda, Kedewatan, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Drop Off : Kusamba - The Angkal Fast Boat. Boat trip : Kusamba - Nusa Penida (ETD 08.00AM)','{\"date\": \"2024-04-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5052688,'270','Juan Pablo Gonzalez',30508,207112,'Trip To Nusa Penida from Bali','Confirmed','C2I-BALI19',1,'2024-04-17','2024-04-17','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (2)',1020000.00,'Today, embark on a unique adventure as you explore the enchanting Nusa Penida, a neighboring island of Bali. Your day begins with a convenient hotel pick-up, followed by a journey to the Sanur port where a fast boat awaits to transport you to Nusa Penida in just 30 minutes. Nusa Penida, located in the southeast of Bali, is a true paradise waiting to be discovered. Upon your arrival, a friendly driver will be ready to guide you through the day\'s captivating itinerary. Your first destination is the mesmerizing Angel\'s Billabong, a natural wonder resembling a pristine pool nestled in the heart of nature. Take a refreshing swim, but exercise caution on the steps and heed your driver\'s recommendations. Next, we head to Broken Beach, a charming bay that was once a cave, now open to the sky, offering a unique and captivating scenery. Although inaccessible by land, the view from above is nothing short of breathtaking. Keep an eye out for the possibility of spotting giant manta rays gracefully gliding on the water\'s surface. Our journey continues to the renowned Kelingking Beach, famous for its stunning cliffs and the iconic hand-shaped mountain. This beach is not only one of the island\'s most famous attractions but also a favorite subject for photographers. We conclude the day at the pristine Crystal Beach, where white sands meet turquoise waters in perfect harmony. As the sun sets, you\'ll have the opportunity to relax and savor the beauty that surrounds you. This unforgettable experience concludes with a return boat trip to Bali from the Toya Pakeh port at 16:30, followed by a comfortable transfer to your hotel.',NULL,'ETA : 08.20 WITA At Nusa Penida Harbour Drop off : MĀUA Nusa Penida Jalan Gamat Bay, Nusa Penida Island, Klungkung,Bali - Indonesia Phone : +62361 6208999','{\"date\": \"2024-04-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5052699,'270','Juan Pablo Gonzalez',30582,203387,'One Bedroom Luxury Villas','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-04-17','2024-04-19','Guio','Eddy',1,'Double',7488000.00,'Each One Bedroom Luxury Villa is designed with a private infinity pool, scenic view across the Gamat Bay or garden view, and some have a small private garden. Every villas features the following: An integrated universal power outlet, Room safe (suitable for storing laptops), Cable TV with international news and movie channels, Eco-friendly bathroom amenities, Coffee and tea-making facilities.',NULL,'Note : Honey Moon Guest','{\"date\": \"2024-04-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5052771,'270','Juan Pablo Gonzalez',30852,202033,'Villa Surya - One Bedroom Private Pool and Tropical Garden','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-04-19','2024-04-21','Guio','Eddy',1,'Double',5760000.00,'Our cozy one bed Villa Surya is perfect for a solo traveler or a romantic getaway at 150 sqm private property. The spacious bedroom features a king-size bed with an extra thick mattress with 100% cotton linen, ensuring a blissful sleep. With high-ceilings, large windows, and a pivoting door onto your patio, the space is able to breathe whilst being basked in a beautiful, natural light. The ensuite bathroom, equipped with a bespoke basin area, rainfall shower, quality toiletries and 100% cotton towels leads out to the real star of this villa, the indulgent open-air bathtub. Large enough for two, with views of your private pool and tropical garden, while away hours in pure relaxation.',NULL,'Note : Honey Moom Guest (Include Breafkast)','{\"date\": \"2024-04-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5052783,'270','Juan Pablo Gonzalez',30508,212301,'Padang Bai to Uluwatu','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-21','2024-04-21','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (1-3)',1200000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,'ETA : Arrival / Padang Bai (Central Bali) / 13:55 PM ByBlue Water Drop Off : Green Escape Alamat: Jl. Bangbang Metuug, Pecatu, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Telepon: 0811-3997-903','{\"date\": \"2024-04-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5052786,'270','Juan Pablo Gonzalez',30930,202592,'One Bedroom Bungalow','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-04-21','2024-04-25','Guio','Eddy',1,'Double',10560000.00,'Room size : 37 sqm. Our One-Bedroom Bungalow is a unique Romantic Eco-Boho Bungalow nestles in Green Escape Resort. You will stay in a sumptuous air-conditioned bungalow that has been handcrafted using recycled wood and tastefully decorated to offer you an authentic Balinese getaway. It\'s the very epitome of a tranquil escape. This Bungalow offers a deluxe king-size bed and a daybed to relax. It offers a comfy mattress, as we know the benefits of a good night’s sleep. The semi-outdoor bathroom with a rain shower will help you revive yourself. Enjoy the comfy sofa on your private terrace which opens onto the exotic garden & pool. The daybed can be used to extend the sleeping capacity of your private bungalow.',NULL,'Note: Honey Moon Guest','{\"date\": \"2024-04-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5052793,'263','Danny Van Belle 20235019',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-12-01','2024-12-02','Rendy','Rendy',6,'Double + Twin',4704000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Early check-in on 01 Dec at 08.00 Late check-out on 02 Dec at 18.00 Flights information ETA: 06.55 by Garuda Indonesia GA89 from Amsterdam on 01 Dec ETD: 00.10 by Garuda Indonesia GA682 to Sorong on 03 Dec','{\"date\": \"2024-12-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-12-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5052870,'270','Juan Pablo Gonzalez',30508,216161,'Uluwatu to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-25','2024-04-25','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (1-3)',840000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,'Pick Up : Ready at Lobby at 15:00 PM Green Escape Alamat: Jl. Bangbang Metuug, Pecatu, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Telepon: 0811-3997-903 Drop Off : Aiport ETD : 25 April TK67 Denpasar-Bali 920 PM Turkish Airlines','{\"date\": \"2024-04-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5052910,'271','WILLY VANHEULENBERGHE',30671,200626,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-01','2024-11-02','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Double',1120000.00,'Deluxe Room with a room area of 28 square meters each, there are 2 types of bed, king and twin bed with a size of 28 square meters each.',NULL,'Check-in time 14.00 Check-out time 12.00 Flights information ETA: 14.55 by Qatar Airways QR956 from Doha on 01 Nov ETD: 09.50 by Batik Air ID6526 to Labuan Bajo on 02 Nov','{\"date\": \"2024-11-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5052960,'270','Juan Pablo Gonzalez',30508,207337,'Snorkeling to Nusa Penida (from Nusa Penida) (Sharing Trip)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-18','2024-04-18','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (2)',1320000.00,NULL,NULL,'Pick Up: Please be Ready at the Lobby At 08:00 AM Pick up and Drop off : MĀUA Nusa Penida Jalan Gamat Bay, Nusa Penida Island, Klungkung,Bali - Indonesia Phone : +62361 6208999','{\"date\": \"2024-04-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5053313,'272','Annatasha Bartel',30662,213270,'5D4N Orang Utan + Batak Country Tour','Confirmed','RVL-05D OUBC',5,'2024-03-29','2024-04-02','Nicholas','Tami',1,'Person (1)',13680000.00,'DAY 01 : AIRPORT / MEDAN - BUKIT LAWANG Arrival at Kuala Namu International airport pick up by our tour guide and then transfer to the center of Medan city and then drive to Bukit Lawang via Binjai and Kuala pass several plantations of rubber and oilpalm. Upon arrival in Bukit Lawang check-in hotel. Meals : - Accommodation : Bukit Lawang Cottages or Rindu Alam Hotel DAY 02 : BUKIT LAWANG - JUNGLE TRACKING - BRASTAGI After breakfast and then climbing up to the jungle to see Orangutan, walking deeper inside the jungle where the possibility to see several kinds of flora and fauna at tropical rain forest, the trekking will take about 3 hours. After the trekking, return to Hotel. Afterwards drive to Brastagi, via new route and passing several village such as Namu Ukur, Rumah Galuh and Simpang Kuta Buluh, on the way you can enjoying the panorama of Sinabung Volcano. Afternoon arrival in Brastagi visiting Lhumbini Park (its duplicate of Shwedagon pagoda), fruit market, and Gundaling hill. And afternoon check in to hotel. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Mikie Holiday Resort or Sinabung Hotel DAY 03 : BRASTAGI - SAMOSIR / LAKE TOBA After breakfast drive head for Samosir Island in Lake Toba via TELE. En-route stop at : - Dokan (to see the traditional village of the Batak Karo tribe). - Sipisopiso Waterfall (from here you can admire the scenic view of the Lake Toba from its northern tip combined with the slender 90 meters high waterfall). - Tele (a nice place for over-viewing the lake from its western part). - Efrata (another beautiful waterfall found on the way to Samosir Island). - Lumban Suhi-suhi (to see the Tobanase traditional houses where we could observe also the women doing the weaving). In mid afternoon arriving at Tuktuk area on Samosir and check-in to hotel. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Tabo Cottages or Samosir Villa or Toledo Inn DAY 04 : SAMOSIR EXCURSION BY CAR After breakfast we start for our fullday excursion by car in the interior of Samosir island and en-route visiting : - Ambarita (to see the stone chairs and tables where once used as the execution site by the ancient tribal chieftains). - Aek Natonang (here we can see the small lake found of the top of Samosir Island and its panorama view). - Tomok (to see the old sarcophages belonged to former Sidabutar Kings and his descendants). In afternoon return back to hotel and free at leisure. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Tabo Cottages or Samosir Villa or Toledo Inn DAY 05 : SAMOSIR - MEDAN / AIRPORT After breakfast transfer from Lake Toba to Medan via Pematang Siantar with view of rubber, oilpalm and cacao plantations. Arriving in Medan proceed to airport for flight to the next destination. Tour ends. Meals : Breakfast',NULL,'Flight details ETA 07.55 by Singapore Airlines SQ990 from Singapore on 29 Mar ETD 20.05 by Singapore Airlines SQ995 to Singapore on 02 Apr','{\"date\": \"2024-03-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5053434,'273','Itzell Escorcia Garcia',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-01','2024-04-02','Guio','Tami',2,'Double',1680000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Flight details ETA: 23.45 by All Nippon Airways NH835 from Tokyo on 01 Apr ETD: 06.00 by Batik Air ID6202 to Pangkalan Bun on 02 Apr Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel.','{\"date\": \"2024-04-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5053445,'273','Itzell Escorcia Garcia',30806,202005,'3D2N Orangutan Tour - With Trekking and Canoe in Tanjung Harapan','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-04-02','2024-04-04','Guio','Tami',3,'Persons (3)',13320000.00,'DAY 1 : TANJUNG HARAPAN - BEKANTAN - NIGHT AT PONDOK AMBUN G DAY 2 : TREKKING TANJUNG HARAPAN - SUNGAI BULUH - CAMP LEAKY DAY 3 : OUT',NULL,'Flight details ETA : 07.15 by Batik Air ID6202 from Jakarta on 02 April ETD : 06.20 by Wings Air IW1809 to Semarang on 04 April Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-04-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5053488,'273','Itzell Escorcia Garcia',30783,215156,'Java Bali Overload Tour : Yogyakarta City, Mount Bromo & Ijen Crater 5D4N / A. The Phoenix Hotel - J','Confirmed','JS-JAVA05',5,'2024-04-04','2024-04-08','Guio','Tami',3,'Persons (2 / Double)',38880000.00,'Travel overland from Java all the way to Bali! This tour takes you to an amazing road trip you will never forget. From discovering the ancient wonders Borobudur and Prambanan in Yogyakarta, a city rich of authentic Javanese culture, to climbing the majestic volcanoes of Bromo and Ijen to witness the spectacular sunrises and unique blue fire, and finish on the island of the gods, Bali. You have the option of going by train from Yogyakarta until Surabaya before you reach Bromo, less tiring, more convenient but it comes at different price. On the other hand, with car you can make some stops along the way so you have a chance to see something new. It is up to you! Day 1 : Welcome to Yogyakarta Welcome to the cradle of Indonesian culture, Yogyakarta. A tourist destination for its ancient palaces, temples, batik workshops, gamelan music orchestras, court dances and wayang puppet shows. Upon your arrival in Yogyakarta a representative of come2indonesia will be waiting for you with a sign indicating your name to take you to your hotel and the rest of the day is for you. The journey from the airport should be around 2-2,5 hours. Meals : - Accommodation : A. The Phoenix Hotel - Deluxe Legacy Room Day 2 : Yogyakarta City Tour - Borobodur Temple - Prambanan Temple After breakfast, your guide will pick you up with your hotel to start exploring the city. This excursion will make you lose yourselves in the authentic magic of Yogyakarta. One of the most beautiful and complete routes of the cultural capital of Indonesia. At the scheduled time, your guide will pick you up to begin the tour of Borobudur, the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. Depending on where you stay in the city, the drive can be 1-1,5 hours to the temple. Arrival at the temple, you will walk around the garden area, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano has been producing during its history. After visiting one of the most important Buddhist temples in Southeast Asia, you will continue the journey to the heart of the city. You will visit the Keraton, or also known as the Sultan’s Palace. The palace is a complex building two centuries old. Next, you will hear the song of the “freedom” of the birds in the bird market, you will visit the “Water Castle” that occupies the highest part at the northern end of the vast complex of Taman Sari. Then, stroll around Malioboro Street, one of the main streets of Yogyakarta, with its merchants, horse carriages, taxi-bikes and markets. An incredible experience that will make the hours fly by. Finishing the tour in the centre of the city of Yogyakarta, you will head northeast towards Prambanan, the temple of Hinduists and classified as a World Heritage Site by UNESCO since 1991. This temple was completed in 856 AD to commemorate the victory of the descendant of Sanjaya dynasty, Rikai Pikatan, against the last Shailendra sovereign of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to Shiva, one of the Trimurti which is an expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the Destroyer. After this unforgettable day, you will take you to your hotel. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : A. The Phoenix Hotel - Deluxe Legacy Room Day 3 : Yogyakarta - Bromo (By Train) Ready with your suitcases, the time has come to say a farewell to this dream city. You will enjoy your breakfast at the hotel, and at the indicated time, with your guide, you will travel to Jombang / Mojokerta by train. Then by private car you will go to your hotel located on the slopes of the Bromo volcano. In total it will be about 8 hours of travel. check-in at the hotel and deserved rest. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : A. Jiwa Jawa Bromo - Deluxe Room Day 4 : Bromo - Ijen Very early, your guide and a jeep driver will be waiting for you at the hotel to attend one of the most spectacular sunrises in Indonesia. Even though you have to get up early, it will be worth it. You will climb to a high point first in full darkness and, little by little the first rays of sun are giving way to a huge and indescribable caldera that makes up the entire view of the Bromo and Semeru Natural Park. With Bromo, a volcano of great fumaroles and behind it, the Semeru Volcano with explosions every 20 minutes exactly, will make you have one of the most rewarding experiences ever. After enjoying the sunset, by jeep, we will go to the slopes of the volcano where you can go to the Bromo volcano and after climbing some stairs you can reach the very edge of its crater and see the impressive activity it has. We return to the hotel to cool off and enjoy your breakfast. At the agreed time, we will leave for our next destination, the Ijen volcano. This section lasts about 7-8 hours by car where we will make a stop to eat. Take this trip to rest. Arriving in Ijen, we will leave you at your hotel, check in and enjoy your deserved rest. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : A. Ijen Resort - Villa\'s Deluxe Day 5 : Ijen Tour - Ketapang - Bali The day has finally come to visit one of the most attractive volcanoes in Indonesia! One of the last open pit sulfur mines that survive on the planet. For this climb you can choose between two schedules; leave very early at 1 AM to see the blue fire (please not that it is not always visible, for example during rainy days) or leave more quietly at 4 AM only for the sunrise. You can decide later when you meet the guide. Once we pick you up at your hotel, you will head towards the village of Licin to reach the slope of the volcano to begin the steep climb to the crater of the volcano. During this trek, your guide will give you double filter masks to protect you from the natural chemicals of sulfur. At an altitude of 2883 meters and when dawn begins, an incredible contrast of colors will open before your eyes. A yellow earth scene and a large turquoise blue lake inside the crater that contrast with a suspended white cloud that is continuously expelling the volcano. In turn, among so much beauty you will see the local miners do what is said to be one of the toughest jobs in the world. These miners go down to the crater of the volcano to load 80 to 100 kilos of sulfur on their shoulders and then sell it. After this amazing experience on the edge of Ijen volcano crater, we begin the descent with an incredible panoramic view of the mountains that make up the national park. We will take you to your hotel to cool off and have breakfast and we start the journey to Bali for about 5 hours at least, depending on where you stay in Bali. To do this, we will go first to the port of Banyuwangi where we will take the ferry to cross to Bali. It is a journey of only 30 minutes, but remember to adjust your watch by an hour due to the time zone change. Welcome to the island of the Gods. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Flight details ETA : 15.05 by Wings Air IW1801 from Pangkalan Bun on 04 Apr 2024 Drop off Point : The Vira Bali Boutique Hotel & Suite Jl. Kartika Plaza No.127, Kuta, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Phone: (0361) 765700','{\"date\": \"2024-04-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5053508,'273','Itzell Escorcia Garcia',30783,215156,'Java Bali Overload Tour : Yogyakarta City, Mount Bromo & Ijen Crater 5D4N / A. The Phoenix Hotel - J','Confirmed','JS-JAVA05',5,'2024-04-04','2024-04-08','Guio','Tami',1,'Person (1)',3612000.00,'Travel overland from Java all the way to Bali! This tour takes you to an amazing road trip you will never forget. From discovering the ancient wonders Borobudur and Prambanan in Yogyakarta, a city rich of authentic Javanese culture, to climbing the majestic volcanoes of Bromo and Ijen to witness the spectacular sunrises and unique blue fire, and finish on the island of the gods, Bali. You have the option of going by train from Yogyakarta until Surabaya before you reach Bromo, less tiring, more convenient but it comes at different price. On the other hand, with car you can make some stops along the way so you have a chance to see something new. It is up to you! Day 1 : Welcome to Yogyakarta Welcome to the cradle of Indonesian culture, Yogyakarta. A tourist destination for its ancient palaces, temples, batik workshops, gamelan music orchestras, court dances and wayang puppet shows. Upon your arrival in Yogyakarta a representative of come2indonesia will be waiting for you with a sign indicating your name to take you to your hotel and the rest of the day is for you. The journey from the airport should be around 2-2,5 hours. Meals : - Accommodation : A. The Phoenix Hotel - Deluxe Legacy Room Day 2 : Yogyakarta City Tour - Borobodur Temple - Prambanan Temple After breakfast, your guide will pick you up with your hotel to start exploring the city. This excursion will make you lose yourselves in the authentic magic of Yogyakarta. One of the most beautiful and complete routes of the cultural capital of Indonesia. At the scheduled time, your guide will pick you up to begin the tour of Borobudur, the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. Depending on where you stay in the city, the drive can be 1-1,5 hours to the temple. Arrival at the temple, you will walk around the garden area, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano has been producing during its history. After visiting one of the most important Buddhist temples in Southeast Asia, you will continue the journey to the heart of the city. You will visit the Keraton, or also known as the Sultan’s Palace. The palace is a complex building two centuries old. Next, you will hear the song of the “freedom” of the birds in the bird market, you will visit the “Water Castle” that occupies the highest part at the northern end of the vast complex of Taman Sari. Then, stroll around Malioboro Street, one of the main streets of Yogyakarta, with its merchants, horse carriages, taxi-bikes and markets. An incredible experience that will make the hours fly by. Finishing the tour in the centre of the city of Yogyakarta, you will head northeast towards Prambanan, the temple of Hinduists and classified as a World Heritage Site by UNESCO since 1991. This temple was completed in 856 AD to commemorate the victory of the descendant of Sanjaya dynasty, Rikai Pikatan, against the last Shailendra sovereign of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to Shiva, one of the Trimurti which is an expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the Destroyer. After this unforgettable day, you will take you to your hotel. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : A. The Phoenix Hotel - Deluxe Legacy Room Day 3 : Yogyakarta - Bromo (By Train) Ready with your suitcases, the time has come to say a farewell to this dream city. You will enjoy your breakfast at the hotel, and at the indicated time, with your guide, you will travel to Jombang / Mojokerta by train. Then by private car you will go to your hotel located on the slopes of the Bromo volcano. In total it will be about 8 hours of travel. check-in at the hotel and deserved rest. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : A. Jiwa Jawa Bromo - Deluxe Room Day 4 : Bromo - Ijen Very early, your guide and a jeep driver will be waiting for you at the hotel to attend one of the most spectacular sunrises in Indonesia. Even though you have to get up early, it will be worth it. You will climb to a high point first in full darkness and, little by little the first rays of sun are giving way to a huge and indescribable caldera that makes up the entire view of the Bromo and Semeru Natural Park. With Bromo, a volcano of great fumaroles and behind it, the Semeru Volcano with explosions every 20 minutes exactly, will make you have one of the most rewarding experiences ever. After enjoying the sunset, by jeep, we will go to the slopes of the volcano where you can go to the Bromo volcano and after climbing some stairs you can reach the very edge of its crater and see the impressive activity it has. We return to the hotel to cool off and enjoy your breakfast. At the agreed time, we will leave for our next destination, the Ijen volcano. This section lasts about 7-8 hours by car where we will make a stop to eat. Take this trip to rest. Arriving in Ijen, we will leave you at your hotel, check in and enjoy your deserved rest. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : A. Ijen Resort - Villa\'s Deluxe Day 5 : Ijen Tour - Ketapang - Bali The day has finally come to visit one of the most attractive volcanoes in Indonesia! One of the last open pit sulfur mines that survive on the planet. For this climb you can choose between two schedules; leave very early at 1 AM to see the blue fire (please not that it is not always visible, for example during rainy days) or leave more quietly at 4 AM only for the sunrise. You can decide later when you meet the guide. Once we pick you up at your hotel, you will head towards the village of Licin to reach the slope of the volcano to begin the steep climb to the crater of the volcano. During this trek, your guide will give you double filter masks to protect you from the natural chemicals of sulfur. At an altitude of 2883 meters and when dawn begins, an incredible contrast of colors will open before your eyes. A yellow earth scene and a large turquoise blue lake inside the crater that contrast with a suspended white cloud that is continuously expelling the volcano. In turn, among so much beauty you will see the local miners do what is said to be one of the toughest jobs in the world. These miners go down to the crater of the volcano to load 80 to 100 kilos of sulfur on their shoulders and then sell it. After this amazing experience on the edge of Ijen volcano crater, we begin the descent with an incredible panoramic view of the mountains that make up the national park. We will take you to your hotel to cool off and have breakfast and we start the journey to Bali for about 5 hours at least, depending on where you stay in Bali. To do this, we will go first to the port of Banyuwangi where we will take the ferry to cross to Bali. It is a journey of only 30 minutes, but remember to adjust your watch by an hour due to the time zone change. Welcome to the island of the Gods. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5053512,'274','Frederic TRUBLIN',30671,200626,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-29','2024-04-30','Rendy','Eddy',1,'Double',1120000.00,'Deluxe Room with a room area of 28 square meters each, there are 2 types of bed, king and twin bed with a size of 28 square meters each.',NULL,'Check-in time 14.00 Check-out time 12.00 Flights information ETA: 15.25 by Qatar Airways QR956 from Doha on 29 Apr ETD: 00.10 by Garuda Indonesia GA682 to Sorong on 30 Apr','{\"date\": \"2024-04-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5053547,'273','Itzell Escorcia Garcia',30571,202567,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-08','2024-04-09','Guio','Tami',2,'Double',2580000.00,'Located at the Second Floor, 35 sqm comfort living with a touch of Balinese style featuring completed fitting, Cable TV, a fancy bathroom comprises rain shower and good quality amenities. Also dedicated Wi-Fi Access to complete your day.',NULL,'Flight details ETD 08.05 by Batik Air ID6333 to Labuan Bajo on 09 April','{\"date\": \"2024-04-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5053548,'275','MARCO DE SILVESTRI',30719,201080,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-16','2024-04-17','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Twin',952000.00,'Swiss-Belhotel Sorong boast 126 guest rooms in Sorong with all the comforts you would expect from an international chain of four-star hotels in Sorong. Enjoy 37-inch LED TVs, cable channels, high-speed internet access and a full range of other amenities that will make your stay here the most comfortable one possible.',NULL,'Check-in time 14.00 Check-out time 12.00 Early check-in is subject to availability upon arrival.','{\"date\": \"2024-04-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5053550,'275','MARCO DE SILVESTRI',30719,201085,'Airport transfer with Innova','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-17','2024-04-17','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Per Car',224000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5053552,'275','MARCO DE SILVESTRI',30680,205339,'Day Use - Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-17','2024-04-17','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Twin',560000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Day-use is valid for maximum 6 hours with earliest check-in at 10.00 and latest check-out at 18.00.','{\"date\": \"2024-04-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5053554,'273','Itzell Escorcia Garcia',31083,212374,'3D2N LOB Rinca - Padar - Komodo Island Tour (Medium Standard Boat)','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-04-09','2024-04-11','Guio','Tami',3,'Persons (2-3)',40874400.00,'TOUR ITINERARY Highlights: Menjarite, Kelor, Strawberry Rock, Kalong, Rinca, Padar, Komodo Island, Pink Beach, Taka Makassar, Manta Point, Kanawa, B.Cermin Mirror Cave DAY 1 : DENPASAR - LABUAN BAJO - MENJARITE - KELOR - KALONG ISLAND Arrival at Komodo Airport in Labuan Bajo west Flores, meeting service with our tour guide and transfer to the pier of Labuan Bajo for Rinca Island. It’s about 2 hours sail to the island of Komodo Dragon, stop at Menjarite island for snorkeling then continue to Rinca island-the Island of Komodo dragon, you will find not just e Dragons but also many wild animals like, deer, wild buffalo, long-tailed macaque and wild pig also numerous of birds. Keep your eyes look up as sometime you will find the young Komodo dragons on the trees. A local ranger will lead you through this natural preservation. Late afternoon sailing directly to Kalong Rinca Island to see the hundreds of fling foxes set out from the mangrove tree at 06-07pm, the lovely sunset from the boat trip really enjoyable. Lunch and dinner on boat. Meals : Lunch - Dinner DAY 2 : KALONG - PADAR - KOMODO - PINK BEACH - MANTA POINT - TAKA MAKASSAR - SEBAYUR After having breakfast in your boat, heading to Padar Island, taking trek to Padar Island until having the top view point to get breathtaking scenery of three bays around, Padar Island hike in Komodo has some of the most amazing views in Indonesia, trek to downhill and back to the Boat for sailing directly to Loh Liang – the Ranger station in Komodo Island. By passing through many small islands, After registering start to take basic trekking to see the GIANT RIZARD / KOMODO DRAGON and other wild animals as: Timor deer, wild pig, wild chicken and many variously of tropical bird. Please keep your look at any directions as sometimes you will also find young Komodo dragon hanging over the trees. A local ranger will be led you during the trek. Return to the boat on to Pink beach for snorkeling, swimming and relaxing. It is really spectacular and unspoiled coral reef and many color fish. This is one of best side for snorkeling diving. Sail toward MANTA POINT to exploring Huge Mantas by snorkeling even watching from your boat trip (can’t be guaranteed if weather is not good, like wave and current are strongly) visit also the taka Makassar its really tiny island with white sand beach really enjoyable to relaxing or beach walking then heading to Sebayur island, overnight dinner on boat. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner DAY 3 : SEBAYUR - KANAWA ISLANDS - LABUAN BAJO - DENPASAR After breakfast on the boat, taking swimming, snorkeling and relaxing as well at seraya and Kanawa. Then back to Labuan Bajo to continue your next excursion with visiting the Batu Cermin (Mirror Stone) Cave. The grotto is 75 by 75 meters large, and contains stalactites and stalagmites. Some tunnels are narrow and dark but in others sunlight falls. Then local market before taking you to the airport for flight to Denpasar. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Attention: The itinerary is subject to change due to the weather, tide level and operating conditions without prior notice.',NULL,'Flight details ETA : 09.20 by Batik Air ID6333 from Denpasar on 09 April ETD: 15.25 by Garuda Indonesia GA0453 to Jakarta on 11 April','{\"date\": \"2024-04-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5053559,'273','Itzell Escorcia Garcia',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-11','2024-04-12','Guio','Tami',2,'Double',1568000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Flight details ETA : 16.45 by Garuda Indonesia GA0453 from Labuan Bajo on 11 April ETD: 05.50 by Citilink QG910 to Kuala Namu on 12 April Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel.','{\"date\": \"2024-04-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5053584,'273','Itzell Escorcia Garcia',30662,213274,'3D2N Medan - Leuser National Park Tracking','Confirmed','RVL-3D Boh-Lst',3,'2024-04-12','2024-04-14','Guio','Tami',3,'Persons (2-3 / Double)',13356000.00,'DAY 01 : MEDAN - BUKIT LAWANG Arrival at Kuala Namu Int airport Airport Medan drive to Bukit Lawang with stop at several Plantation for rubber and Palm oil. After that arrival at Bukit Lawang check in to hotel. Meals : - Accommodation : Bukit Lawang Cottages or Rindu Alam Hotel DAY 02 : BUKIT LAWANG - FULL DAY TRACKING LEUSER PARK After breakfast walking to the jungle to start a jungle tracking to explore the nature of Leuser National park with their flora and fauna, the possibility to see Orang Utan on their own habitat and other kind of animal such as Thomas leaf monkeys, long tail macaque, gibbon, black gibbon and other kind of flora and fauna of tropical rain forest. This fullday tracking will finish in the afternoon and then return back to hotel. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Accommodation : Bukit Lawang Cottages or Rindu Alam Hotel DAY 03 : BUKIT LAWANG - MEDAN / AIRPORT After breakfast free at own leisure for swimming or walking and then drive to Medan arrival in Medan directly transfer to airport. Meals : Breakfast',NULL,'Flight details ETA: 08.10 by Citilink QG910 from Jakarta on 12 April ETD: 14.00 by Super Air Jet IU949 to Jakarta on 14 April','{\"date\": \"2024-04-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5054660,'276','FLORENCE SAUVE',30671,200626,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-05-05','2024-05-06','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Twin',1120000.00,'Deluxe Room with a room area of 28 square meters each, there are 2 types of bed, king and twin bed with a size of 28 square meters each.',NULL,'Check-in time 14.00 Check-out time 12.00 Flights information ETA: 13.10 by Cathay Pacific CX777 from Hong Kong on 05 May ETD: 02.00 by Batik Air ID6540 to Kupang on 06 May','{\"date\": \"2024-05-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5054664,'276','FLORENCE SAUVE',31158,204270,'Meet & Greet Domestic Flight Departure - for CGK','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-05-05','2024-05-05','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Person (1)',898240.00,'Meet and greet service specializes in pick-up services for flight arrivals which includes arranging a meeting between the customer and the Hotel Representative / Hotel Transportation Staff./Pick-Up. For domestic departure. Meet & Greet Domestic Airport: - Meet guests at the specified location at the entrance to the area Departure - Greet by using the guests name board. - Accompanying guests through security checks at the entrance. - Accompanying and assisting in the process of validating vaccine certificate documents and checking other documents needed at the airport. - Accompany and help for the Check-in process. - Accompanying and assisting guests for Airport Tax / Passenger Service Fee payments. - Accompanying and assisting guests to the departure lounge determined.',NULL,'Flight information ETD: 02.00 by Batik Air ID6540 to Kupang on 06 May','{\"date\": \"2024-05-05\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in hotel lobby\", \"time\": \"23:50\", \"locality\": \"Anara Airport Hotel Jakarta\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5054665,'271','WILLY VANHEULENBERGHE',31158,204270,'Meet & Greet Domestic Flight Departure - for CGK','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-02','2024-11-02','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Person (1)',898240.00,'Meet and greet service specializes in pick-up services for flight arrivals which includes arranging a meeting between the customer and the Hotel Representative / Hotel Transportation Staff./Pick-Up. For domestic departure. Meet & Greet Domestic Airport: - Meet guests at the specified location at the entrance to the area Departure - Greet by using the guests name board. - Accompanying guests through security checks at the entrance. - Accompanying and assisting in the process of validating vaccine certificate documents and checking other documents needed at the airport. - Accompany and help for the Check-in process. - Accompanying and assisting guests for Airport Tax / Passenger Service Fee payments. - Accompanying and assisting guests to the departure lounge determined.',NULL,'Flight information ETD: 09.50 by Batik Air ID6526 to Labuan Bajo on 02 Nov','{\"date\": \"2024-11-02\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in hotel lobby\", \"time\": \"07:00\", \"locality\": \"Anara Airport Hotel Jakarta\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5054667,'277','Jori Haank',30508,202897,'Uluwatu Temple and Kecak Dance','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-03','2024-04-03','Rendy','Rendy',8,'Persons (7-10)',4800000.00,'This half-day tour, is an exciting tour package to visit Padang-Padang Beach, Uluwatu Temple, the famous Balinese Hindu Temple in south part of Bali with breathtaking view of sunset and Indian Ocean. Uluwatu Temple is one of Balinese Hindu Temples located right on the petrifying hill with the crevasse exist in the right and left side. Uluwatu Temple is one of Sad Khayangan (6 biggest temple in Bali) owns magnificent view of the Indian Ocean and sunset as a backdrop. This temple is very amazing where the location is right on the narrow peninsula with deep seawater under it. This tour package is combined with the spectacular Balinese traditional dance performance of Kecak Dance. Balinese Kecak Dance is a spectacular traditional dance with the group of people playing this dance with fire game. It is very exciting and unique dance due to the sound of gamelan is not using the normal gamelan but use their mouth. The dancers make the compact choir with the exquisite dance movement that is one of this dance features. After the dance we returned back to the hotel or seafood restaurant in Jimbaran.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-03\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in the lobby\", \"time\": \"15:00\", \"locality\": \"Grand Cliff Nusa Dua\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Grand Cliff Nusa Dua\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5054669,'277','Jori Haank',30508,202884,'1D Snorkeling to Nusa Lembongan','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-05','2024-04-05','Rendy','Rendy',8,'Persons (6-8)',8544000.00,'At the agreed time, we will pick you up at your hotel in Bali and transfer to Sanur harbor where we will embark on speedboats to neighboring Nusa Lembongan, which together with Nusa Penida has one of the most complete reefs on the planet. After about 30 minutes at high speed we will arrive at this small paradise island in the Southeast of Bali where you will enjoy snorkeling on beaches with crystal clear waters and the marine life of the inhabitants of the area. The guide will take you to places incredibly covered with corals and where the amount of reef fish will leave you speechless. The guides in the area are very professional and fun, which will make the trip a safe and enjoyable trip. We will also visit the most representative places on the island such as the Devil Tears, the seaweed, Dream Beach and Yelow Bridge. If you want to take advantage of the day doing only snorkeling and leave the island for another occasion, we can go to another point different from the many on the island to continue enjoying the seabed. After spending the day in Nusa Lembongan, we will transfer you to the port to take the boat back to Bali and transfer to the hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5054670,'277','Jori Haank',30508,207268,'Nusa Dua to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-08','2024-04-08','Rendy','Rendy',8,'Persons (7-10)',7680000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-08\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in the lobby\", \"time\": \"10:00\", \"locality\": \"Grand Cliff Nusa Dua\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-08\", \"text\": \"ETD: 13.05 by Singapore Airlines SQ939 to Singapore on 08 Apr\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Denpasar Airport\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5055211,'278','LIONEL PEYROUTOU',30671,200626,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-27','2024-04-28','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Double',1120000.00,'Deluxe Room with a room area of 28 square meters each, there are 2 types of bed, king and twin bed with a size of 28 square meters each.',NULL,'Check-in time 14.00 Check-out time 12.00','{\"date\": \"2024-04-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5055631,'279','FRANCIS GRIFFON',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-05-13','2024-05-14','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Double',784000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel.','{\"date\": \"2024-05-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5055646,'279','FRANCIS GRIFFON',31703,208681,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-05-22','2024-05-24','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Double',2089920.00,'We offer 42 cozy superior rooms with a floor area of 25 square meters. Choose from double bed or twin single beds, with maximum capacity for 2 adults and 1 child. In-room dining is available round the clock. This room are equipped with individually controlled air-conditioning, IDD telephone, LCD TV with international channels, high-speed internet access, personal in-room safety box, coffee and tea making facilities, mini-bar, hairdryer, shower, and many more.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-05-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5056140,'281','Jennifer Robin McKenzie',30683,203329,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-03','2024-06-04','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Double',1116000.00,'Feel at home in one of our Superior Rooms - warm colors giving an inviting feel and ambiance. Although you are in the heart of Soekarno - Hatta Airport you can find a small oasis of relaxation where you will leave the hustle and bustle of traveling far behind spacious 24 square meters. Superior room with a king or twin beds offering comfortable stay equipped with modern facilities such as air conditioning, arm chair, work desk & chair, flat screen TV with cable and satellite channels, free access internet & Wi-Fi, in room safe, coffee/tea maker, mini cooler, private bathroom with shower and hair dryer, and many more.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel.','{\"date\": \"2024-06-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5056252,'280','Gianluigi Bravi',32660,216222,'Super Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-27','2024-09-28','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Double',840000.00,'Rooms with international standard quality facilities. Modern and elegant design provides unforgettable comfort. Equipped with facilities such as: Hot and Cool Water, Coffee and Tea Maker, Amenities, Linen and Bed with star hotel standard quality.',NULL,'Check-in time 12.00 Check-out time 14.00','{\"date\": \"2024-09-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5056260,'281','Jennifer Robin McKenzie',30683,203330,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-03','2024-06-04','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Twin',1116000.00,'Step into one of our comfortable and spacious Deluxe Rooms. Here you can kick back and relax at ease and prepare for your next flight or meeting. Spacious 24 square meters deluxe room with a king or twin beds offering comfortable stay equipped with modern facilities such as air conditioning, arm chair, work desk & chair, flat screen TV with cable and satellite channels, free access internet & Wi-Fi, in room safe, coffee/tea maker, mini cooler, private bathroom with shower and hair dryer, and many more.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel.','{\"date\": \"2024-06-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5057708,'283','ANGELA AMBROSI',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-22','2024-04-23','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Single',784000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel.','{\"date\": \"2024-04-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5060255,'284','Wolfgang Christian Praun',30662,212912,'(Journaway) 7D6N Medan - Bukit Lawang - Brastagi - Lake Toba','Confirmed',NULL,7,'2024-04-26','2024-05-02','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Persons (2-3 / Double)',21268800.00,'Day-01 : AIRPORT/MEDAN - BUKIT LAWANG Arrival at Kualanamu International Airport Medan meet by our tour guide and then drive to Bukit Lawang with enroute stop at several plantations for rubber and oil palm. Arriving in Bukit Lawang check-in to hotel. Meals : - • Overnight at : Eco-lodge Bukit Lawang Cottages - Standard Room Day-02 : BUKIT LAWANG - LEUSER PARK TREKKING (B,L,D) After breakfast walking to the jungle to start a jungle trekking to explore the nature of Leuser National Park with its rich flora and fauna, there will be chances to see Orangutans on their own natural habitat and other kinds of animal such as Thomas-leaf monkeys, long tail macaque, gibbon, black gibbon and other kind of flora and fauna of this tropical rain-forest. Lunch and dinner provided. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner • Overnight at : Tent or Shelter in the jungle Day-03 : CONTINUE TREKKING - RETURN TO BUKIT LAWANG (TUBING) (B,L) After breakfast prepared by tour guide continue trekking, today is full day walking and explore the rain tropical forest with its wildlife living in their natural habitat. In mid-afternoon, we will make our way back by tubing in the river. At the end, we will return to the hotel for check-in. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch • Overnight at : Eco-lodge Bukit Lawang Cottages - Standard Room Day-04 : BUKIT LAWANG - BERASTAGI (B) After breakfast drive to Berastagi with enroute stop at Sembahe river, arriving in Berastagi visiting Lumbhini Park to see the replica of the Shwedagon pagoda, and visit at Fruit Market. In mid-afternoon check-in to hotel. Meals : Breakfast • Overnight at : Mikie Holiday Resort - Superior Room • Alternative : Hotel Sinabung Hills - Superior Room Day-05 : SIBAYAK VOLCANO HIKING - TRANSFER TO SAMOSIR/LAKE TOBA (B) At early morning (take away your Breakfast Box) and transferred to the slope of Sibayak Volcano and then start hiking to the top of the Sibayak Volcano, to go and back will spend about 3 hours. Arriving on its peak enjoy the scenic panorama of its surroundings and the sunrise (weather depends). After take a rest and enjoy its view, start trekking back to Berastagi and then continuing the drive head for Samosir Island in Lake Toba via TELE. En-route stop at : • Dokan (to see the traditional village of the Batak Karo tribe) • Sipisopiso Waterfall (from here you can admire the scenic view of the Lake Toba from its northern tip combined with the slender 90 meters high waterfall) • Tele (a nice place for over-viewing the lake from its western part) • Efrata (another beautiful waterfall found on the way to Samosir Island) • Lumban Suhi-suhi (to see the Tobanase traditional houses where we could observe also the women doing the weaving) In mid-afternoon arriving at Tuktuk area on Samosir and check-in to hotel. Meals : Breakfast • Overnight at : Tabo Cottages - Deluxe Room • Alternative : Samosir Villa - Deluxe Room Day-06: SAMOSIR EXCURSION - AIRPORT/MEDAN CITY (B) After breakfast we start for our fullday excursion by car in the interior of Samosir Island with en-route visits at : • Ambarita (to see the stone chairs and tables where once used as the execution site by the ancient tribal chieftains) • Aek Natonang (here we can see the small lake found of the top of Samosir Island and its panorama view) • Tomok (to see the old sarcophages belonged to former Sidabutar Kings and his descendants) At mid-day, we will return to the harbor to catch the 1 PM ferry back to Parapat (1 hour sailing duration). Arriving at Parapat harbour continue the driving directly to Medan via Pematang Siantar and Tebing Tinggi (about 5 hours driving time). We will drop you off at the airport for overnight at airport hotel and be ready for morning flight departure. Meals : Breakfast Overnight: Hotel Horison Sky Kualanamu - Deluxe Room Day-07 : DEPARTURE After an early breakfast, you will continue to the departure terminal for your flight. TOUR ENDS. Meals : Breakfast','- All the above prices are not valid during Super High Season period for Idul Fitri (01-20 April 2024), Christmas & New Year festive season (18 December 2024 - 08 January 2025). - Surcharge to be advised','Per confirmed program: Day-01: AIRPORT/MEDAN – BUKIT LAWANG Day-02: BUKIT LAWANG – GUNUNG LEUSER NATIONAL PARK TREKKING Day-03: CONTINUE TREKKING – RETURN TO BUKIT LAWANG Day-04: BUKIT LAWANG – BERASTAGI Day-05: SIBAYAK VOLCANO HIKING – TRANSFER TO SAMOSIR/LAKE TOBA Day-06: SAMOSIR EXCURSION – AIRPORT/MEDAN CITY Day-07: DEPARTURE MEDAN Accommodation based on 1 Double Room: 2 Nights at Bukit Lawang Eco-Lodge – Butterfly Room 1 Night in Tent/shelter 1 Night Mikie Holiday Resort – Deluxe Room 1 Night Tabo Cottages – Deluxe Room 1 Night at Hotel Anara Sky Kualanamu - Deluxe Room Flights information ETA: 15.00 by Malaysia Airlines MH864 from Kuala Lumpur on 26 Apr ETD: 08.45 by Singapore Airlines SQ991 to Singapore on 02 May','{\"date\": \"2024-04-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5060597,'285','Sascha Caballero',32195,214479,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-05-15','2024-05-17','Rendy','Rendy',4,'Double + Twin',7374080.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-05-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5060598,'285','Sascha Caballero',32195,215077,'One-way Airport Transfer','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-05-15','2024-05-15','Rendy','Rendy',3,'Per Car',672000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-05-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5060600,'285','Sascha Caballero',32195,215077,'One-way Airport Transfer','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-05-17','2024-05-17','Rendy','Rendy',3,'Per Car',672000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-05-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5061886,'277','Jori Haank',30508,212289,'Airport to Nusa Dua','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-02','2024-04-02','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Persons (7-10)',960000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,'Guests will make a stop for lunch at Ikan Restaurant at The Westin Resort Nusa Dua','{\"date\": \"2024-04-02\", \"text\": \"ETA: 11.55 by Singapore Airlines SQ938 from Singapore on 02 Apr\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Denpasar Airport\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Grand Cliff Nusa Dua\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5061904,'277','Jori Haank',30508,202894,'Kehen Temple - Tukad Cepung Waterfall','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-06','2024-04-06','Rendy','Rendy',8,'Persons (7-10)',4176000.00,'Our wonderful tour starts from Kehen Temple. It is an ancient Hindu temple complex boasting unique architectural features. The staircases reaching from the ground to temple courtyard are carved sandstone mythical animal and Balinese folklore figure statues and also the central vestibule. The temple’s walls are also ornate with Chinese porcelain plates, which are a tribute to the historical relations between the local Bali kingdom and China. Afterwards, we continue to Penglipuran, a village that succeeded in preserving its 75-hectare bamboo forest located in the northern part of the village. Members of this village have a strong commitment to the system of \'Ayahan Desa\' - a philosophy committed to respecting the land on which the village stands. To concludes the day, we stop by at Tukad Cepung Waterfall. Well-guarded by the circular cliffs, this waterfall is difficult to locate for the first time visitor. The circular cliffs give you the feeling of being in a cave, while the open sky right from where the waterfall emerges, gives you the most enchanting view. The sunlight falls on the glistering waterfall creating a rainbow, which feels as though it is projected right up to you. If you have never seen water flowing from the sky, then this would be your chance! After spending your time there, we go back to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-06\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in the lobby\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"Grand Cliff Nusa Dua\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Grand Cliff Nusa Dua\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5062770,'286','Joyce LIPSKI',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-04-20','2024-04-22','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Double',1680000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. Please consult your departure airport transfer upon check-in.','{\"date\": \"2024-04-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5062771,'286','Joyce LIPSKI',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-04-22','2024-04-24','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Persons (2)',10800000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board. Flights information ETA: 07.15 by Batik Air ID6202 from Jakarta on 22 Apr ETD: 08.50 by Batik Air ID6134 to Surabaya on 24 Apr','{\"date\": \"2024-04-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5062793,'286','Joyce LIPSKI',30508,212287,'Airport to Sanur','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-24','2024-04-24','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Persons (1-3)',300000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-24\", \"text\": \"ETA: 14.35 by Lion Air JT922 from Surabaya on 24 Apr\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Denpasar Airport\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Puri Santrian Resort Sanur\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5062794,'286','Joyce LIPSKI',30805,202689,'CGK-PKN','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-22','2024-04-22','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Person',3520000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5062795,'286','Joyce LIPSKI',30805,213516,'PKN-DPS','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-24','2024-04-24','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Person',7040000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5062796,'286','Joyce LIPSKI',30720,202970,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,5,'2024-04-24','2024-04-29','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Double',11100000.00,'Styled for personal comfort and convenience, the Superior room category is an inviting space that captures the essence of Bali. At 35 sqm of room area, with double / twin bed capacity of 2A 1C or 3A with extra bed. Set amidst tropical landscape, this air-conditioned room comes with a private balcony, flat-screen cable TV and a safety deposit box. En suite bathroom comes with bath and shower facilities.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5062797,'286','Joyce LIPSKI',30508,202864,'Ubud and Surrounding Tour','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-25','2024-04-25','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Persons (2)',1812000.00,'We will be picking you up from your hotel to enjoy the wealth of art in Ubud. First we will visit Monkey Forest; the Ubud Monkey Forest is a nature reserve and temple complex in Ubud, Bali. It houses approximately 340 Crab-eating Macaque (Macacafas cicularis) monkeys. The Monkey Forest contains the Pura Dalem Agung Padangtegal temple as well as a \"Holy Spring\" bathing temple and another temple used for cremation ceremonies. Next we go to Ubud Traditional Art Market where the existence is not far different from other markets available in the tourism area. This market as a society economics center of Ubud and it is apposite to the existence of Ubud Empire that is called Puri Saren. Our last destination is Gua Gajah (Elephant Cave). This cave is built at crevasse edge from the federation of 2 rills that is called Pangkung River, where the irrigation is mixed with Petanu River flow. The word of Gua Gajah is anticipated coming from the word of Lwa Gajah, the name of Buddhist Temple or hermitage for Buddhist monk. There is a relief which is almost looking like the form of mountain on the entrance of this cave. It was carved many designed on the relief like grove with the stick, close leaf, animal for example forest pig, tortoise and specters. The cave mouth is decorated by the bas-relief with the eye turn around to the right or west side. At the end of tour we will transferred back you to the hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-25\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in hotel lobby\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": \"Puri Santrian Resort Sanur\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Puri Santrian Resort Sanur\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5062801,'286','Joyce LIPSKI',30508,207269,'Sanur to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-29','2024-04-29','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Persons (1-3)',600000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-29\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in hotel lobby\", \"time\": \"05:30\", \"locality\": \"Puri Santrian Resort Sanur\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-29\", \"text\": \"ETD: 08.05 by Batik Air ID6333 to Labuan Bajo on 29 Apr\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Denpasar Airport\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5062803,'286','Joyce LIPSKI',30805,202739,'DPS-LBJ','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-29','2024-04-29','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Person',3300000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5062804,'286','Joyce LIPSKI',30805,202740,'LBJ-DPS','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-05-01','2024-05-01','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Person',3520000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-05-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5062814,'286','Joyce LIPSKI',31083,212380,'3D2N Komodo Padar Tour (1N Boat, 1N Hotel)','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-04-29','2024-05-01','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Persons (2-3)',25764000.00,'TOUR ITINERARY Highlights: Menjarite, Kelor, Kalong, Rinca, Padar, Komodo island, Pink Beach, Taka Makassar, Manta Point, Kanawa, Batu Cermin Mirror Cave DAY 1 : DENPASAR - LABUAN BAJO - MENJARITE - PADAR - KELOR - KALONG ISLAND Arrival at Komodo Airport in Labuan Bajo west Flores, meeting service with our tour guide and transfer to the pier of Labuan Bajo for Rinca Island. It’s about 2 hours sail to the island of Komodo Dragon, stop at Menjarite island for snorkeling then continue to Rinca island-the Island of Komodo dragon, you will find not just e Dragons but also many wild animals like, deer, wild buffalo, long-tailed macaque and wild pig also numerous of birds. Keep your eyes look up as sometime you will find the young Komodo dragons on the trees. A local ranger will lead you through this natural preservation. Late afternoon sailing directly to Kalong Rinca Island to see the hundreds of fling foxes set out from the mangrove tree at 06-07 pm, the lovely sunset from the boat trip really enjoyable here. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Boat Cabin Air Conditioning DAY 2 : KALONG - PADAR - KOMODO - PINK BEACH - MANTA POINT - TAKA MAKASSAR - LABUAN BAJO After having breakfast in your boat, heading to Padar Island, taking trek to Padar Island until having the top view point to get breathtaking scenery of three bays around, Padar Island hike in Komodo has some of the most amazing views in Indonesia, trek to downhill and back to the Boat for sailing directly to Loh Liang – the Ranger station in Komodo Island. By passing through many small islands, After registering start to take basic trekking to see the GIANT RIZARD / KOMODO DRAGON and other wild animals as: Timor deer, wild pig, wild chicken and many variously of tropical bird. Please keep your look at any directions as sometimes you will also find young Komodo dragon hanging over the trees. A local ranger will be led you during the trek. Return to the boat on to Pink beach for snorkeling, swimming and relaxing. It is really spectacular and unspoiled coral reef and many color fish. This is one of best side for snorkeling diving. Sail toward MANTA POINT to exploring Huge Mantas by snorkeling even watching from your boat trip (can’t be guaranteed if weather is not good, like wave and current are strongly) visit also the taka Makaasar its really tiny island with white sand beach really enjoyable to relaxing or beach walking then heading to Labuan bajo for overnight and dinner at above hotel list option. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner DAY 3 : LABUAN BAJO - DENPASAR After breakfast taking your next excursion with visiting local marke and Batu Cermin (Mirror Stone) Cave. The grotto is 75 by 75 meters large, and contains stalactites and stalagmites. Some tunnels are narrow and dark but in others sunlight falls, then process to the airport for flight to Denpasar or to your next destination. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Attention: The itinerary is subject to change due to the weather, tide level and operating conditions without prior notice.',NULL,'Itinerary: 29 Apr: Bali – Labuan Bajo – Menjarite – Kalong Island 30 Apr: Padar Island – Komodo Island – Pink Beach – Labuan Bajo 01 May: Labuan Bajo – Bali Flights information ETA: 09.20 by Batik Air ID6333 from Denpasar on 29 Apr ETD: 10.00 by Batik Air ID6332 to Denpasar on 01 May','{\"date\": \"2024-04-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5064156,'287','Andrea Mitterhuber',32195,214479,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-10-07','2024-10-09','Rendy','Rendy',3,'Double',6048000.00,NULL,NULL,'Check-in time 14.00 Check-out time 12.00 Early check-in is subject to availability and may be charged at additional cost.','{\"date\": \"2024-10-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5064157,'287','Andrea Mitterhuber',32195,215077,'One-way Airport Transfer','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-07','2024-10-07','Rendy','Rendy',3,'Per Car',672000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5064160,'287','Andrea Mitterhuber',32195,215077,'One-way Airport Transfer','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-09','2024-10-09','Rendy','Rendy',3,'Per Car',672000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5064166,'287','Andrea Mitterhuber',31591,207373,'3D2N Tangkoko','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-10-23','2024-10-25','Rendy','Rendy',6,'Persons (6)',16128000.00,'Day 1 : MANADO - TANGKOKO - The expedition begins The adventure begins with meeting your guide at the Manado airport. Then you will start the journey of about 2 and a half hours by car to the Tangkoko Forest where you will do the check in at your Homestay or Lodge. Upon arrival, you will have a talk about what you will see and preparations for the trekking. Meals : Dinner Accommodation : Bird House Homestay or Similar Days 02 : Tangkoko Nature Reserve These days will be dedicated to exploring the jungle in search of animals and bird watching. You will start the trekking that will take you to Tangkok National Park. In just 40 minutes by boat, you will reach the Batuangus beach where you will then climb Mount Tangkoko (1500 m). The dense and virgin jungle is home to some unique animal species in North Sulawesi such as the crested black macaque and the tarsier spectrum that has become known as \"the smallest primate in the world\". As you will be trekking through the lush jungle, you will probably see and hear the red gnarled hornbill as well as the Maleo which is a Megapod Bird that lays eggs on large mounds it builds on the black sand. You can also find couscous, which is a relative of the Australian koala. The forest ranger will accompany you all the way to the top of Tangkoko Mountain. In the afternoon you will return to the station. Alternatively, you can have three hours of trekking in the lowland jungle or swimming on the black sand beach of Tangkoko Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Bird House Homestay or Similar Day 03 : Tangkoko - Manado After breakfast, you can spend the morning in the surroundings of the National Park and at the agreed time, with your guide, you will have the transfer to Manado. Thank you for exploring this unique jungle with us. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Flights information ETA: 15.15 by Wings Air IW1171 from Morotai on 23 Oct ETD: 14.00 by Singapore Airlines SQ8469/TR217 to Singapore on 25 Oct','{\"date\": \"2024-10-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5064545,'288','Alba & Sergio',31083,212380,'3D2N LOB Rinca - Padar - Komodo Island Tour (Medium Standard B. - Purisari, etc)','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-06-17','2024-06-19','Melysa','Tami',2,'Persons (2-3)',25764000.00,'TOUR ITINERARY Highlights: Menjarite, Kelor, Kalong, Rinca, Padar, Komodo island, Pink Beach, Taka Makassar, Manta Point, Kanawa, Batu Cermin Mirror Cave DAY 1 : DENPASAR - LABUAN BAJO - MENJARITE - PADAR - KELOR - KALONG ISLAND Arrival at Komodo Airport in Labuan Bajo west Flores, meeting service with our tour guide and transfer to the pier of Labuan Bajo for Rinca Island. It’s about 2 hours sail to the island of Komodo Dragon, stop at Menjarite island for snorkeling then continue to Rinca island-the Island of Komodo dragon, you will find not just e Dragons but also many wild animals like, deer, wild buffalo, long-tailed macaque and wild pig also numerous of birds. Keep your eyes look up as sometime you will find the young Komodo dragons on the trees. A local ranger will lead you through this natural preservation. Late afternoon sailing directly to Kalong Rinca Island to see the hundreds of fling foxes set out from the mangrove tree at 06-07 pm, the lovely sunset from the boat trip really enjoyable here. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Boat Cabin Air Conditioning DAY 2 : KALONG - PADAR - KOMODO - PINK BEACH - MANTA POINT - TAKA MAKASSAR - LABUAN BAJO After having breakfast in your boat, heading to Padar Island, taking trek to Padar Island until having the top view point to get breathtaking scenery of three bays around, Padar Island hike in Komodo has some of the most amazing views in Indonesia, trek to downhill and back to the Boat for sailing directly to Loh Liang – the Ranger station in Komodo Island. By passing through many small islands, After registering start to take basic trekking to see the GIANT RIZARD / KOMODO DRAGON and other wild animals as: Timor deer, wild pig, wild chicken and many variously of tropical bird. Please keep your look at any directions as sometimes you will also find young Komodo dragon hanging over the trees. A local ranger will be led you during the trek. Return to the boat on to Pink beach for snorkeling, swimming and relaxing. It is really spectacular and unspoiled coral reef and many color fish. This is one of best side for snorkeling diving. Sail toward MANTA POINT to exploring Huge Mantas by snorkeling even watching from your boat trip (can’t be guaranteed if weather is not good, like wave and current are strongly) visit also the taka Makaasar its really tiny island with white sand beach really enjoyable to relaxing or beach walking then heading to Labuan bajo for overnight and dinner at above hotel list option. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner DAY 3 : LABUAN BAJO - DENPASAR After breakfast taking your next excursion with visiting local marke and Batu Cermin (Mirror Stone) Cave. The grotto is 75 by 75 meters large, and contains stalactites and stalagmites. Some tunnels are narrow and dark but in others sunlight falls, then process to the airport for flight to Denpasar or to your next destination. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Attention: The itinerary is subject to change due to the weather, tide level and operating conditions without prior notice.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-17\", \"text\": \"Kawasan Marina, Jl. Soekarno Hatta, Labuan Bajo, Kec. Komodo, Kabupaten Manggarai Barat, Nusa Tenggara Tim. 86711\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Meruorah Komodo Labuan Bajo\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-19\", \"text\": \"ETD 10.00 by Batik Air ID6332 to Denpasar on 19 June 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Labuan Bajo Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5064555,'289','Andrea Piasentin',30680,205339,'Day Use - Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-04','2024-04-04','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Double',560000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Day-use is valid for maximum 6 hours with earliest check-in at 10.00 and latest check-out at 18.00.','{\"date\": \"2024-04-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5064723,'290','Ms. Raquel Munoz Garcia & Mr. Antonio Jose Munoz Ruiz',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-17','2024-04-17','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (1-3)',784000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-17\", \"text\": \"ETA : 23.10 by Qatar Airways QR960 from Doha on 17 April 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Airport Ngurah Rai\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-17\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"PERTIWI BISMA 2 UBUD\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5064727,'290','Ms. Raquel Munoz Garcia & Mr. Antonio Jose Munoz Ruiz',30620,200813,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-04-17','2024-04-21','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',3808000.00,'24 units (10 twin bed and 14 double bed) of 35 sqm each deluxe rooms with garden view are modern‐minimalism designed. Advance, facilities such as LCD TV, coffee/tea maker, balcony/terrace, safety deposit box, minibar, and complete bathroom facilities.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5064742,'290','Ms. Raquel Munoz Garcia & Mr. Antonio Jose Munoz Ruiz',30508,207379,'Ubud to Padang Bai','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-21','2024-04-21','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (1-3)',1120000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 2 Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-21\", \"text\": \"ETD : 08.30 AM by Gili Gili Fastboat from Padangbai to Gili Air\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Padangbai Harbour\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5064788,'291','Giovanni FALLA',30683,203335,'Mini-stay Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-22','2024-04-22','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Double',1120000.00,'Feel at home in one of our Superior Rooms - warm colors giving an inviting feel and ambiance. Although you are in the heart of Soekarno - Hatta Airport you can find a small oasis of relaxation where you will leave the hustle and bustle of traveling far behind Spacious 24 square meters Superior room with a king or twin beds offering comfortable stay equipped with modern facilities such as air conditioning, arm chair, work desk & chair, flat screen TV with cable and satellite channels, free access internet & Wi-Fi, in room safe, coffee/tea maker, mini cooler, private bathroom with shower and hair dryer, and many more.','Room usage for up to 6 hours Earliest check-in time 09.00 Latest check-out time 23.00 Including transfer between terminals','Flights information ETA: 11.05 by Scoot TR276 from Singapore on 22 Apr ETD: ETD: 00.30 by Batik Air ID7797 to Sorong on 23 Apr','{\"date\": \"2024-04-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5065445,'286','Joyce LIPSKI',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-26','2024-04-26','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Persons (2)',1872000.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-26\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in hotel lobby\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": \"Puri Santrian Resort Sanur\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Puri Santrian Resort Sanur\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5065482,'292','Belen Diaz Sanchez',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-23','2024-04-23','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (1-3)',672000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-23\", \"text\": \"ETA 16.55 by IB7968 from Doha on 23 Apr\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Tejaprana Bisma\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5065483,'292','Belen Diaz Sanchez',30623,200585,'Forest Villa','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-04-23','2024-04-27','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',10752000.00,'The Sawah View Villas offer a perfect retreat. These one-bedroom villas offer a spacious floor area of 100 m2, with a King-sized bed, air conditioning, private bathroom with bathtub, and a beautiful view of the garden and paddy rice field surrounding the villa. Unwind in the private outdoor space in the gazebo on the personal terrace, laze in the infinity plunge pool, or simply lay back in the outdoor natural stone bathtub.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5065484,'292','Belen Diaz Sanchez',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-24','2024-04-24','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',1747200.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-24\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Tejaprana Bisma\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5065488,'292','Belen Diaz Sanchez',32677,216345,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-04-27','2024-04-29','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',2912000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5065489,'292','Belen Diaz Sanchez',30508,202897,'Uluwatu Temple and Kecak Dance','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-29','2024-04-29','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',1836000.00,'This half-day tour, is an exciting tour package to visit Padang-Padang Beach, Uluwatu Temple, the famous Balinese Hindu Temple in south part of Bali with breathtaking view of sunset and Indian Ocean. Uluwatu Temple is one of Balinese Hindu Temples located right on the petrifying hill with the crevasse exist in the right and left side. Uluwatu Temple is one of Sad Khayangan (6 biggest temple in Bali) owns magnificent view of the Indian Ocean and sunset as a backdrop. This temple is very amazing where the location is right on the narrow peninsula with deep seawater under it. This tour package is combined with the spectacular Balinese traditional dance performance of Kecak Dance. Balinese Kecak Dance is a spectacular traditional dance with the group of people playing this dance with fire game. It is very exciting and unique dance due to the sound of gamelan is not using the normal gamelan but use their mouth. The dancers make the compact choir with the exquisite dance movement that is one of this dance features. After the dance we returned back to the hotel or seafood restaurant in Jimbaran.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-29\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bhuana Sari, Wanagiri Kec. Sukasada, Kab. Buleleng, Bali 81161\", \"time\": \"12:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Giriwood Hotel & Villa\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-29\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bangbang Metuug, Pecatu, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Green Escape Eco Resort, Uluwatu\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5065490,'292','Belen Diaz Sanchez',30930,202592,'One Bedroom Bungalow','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-04-29','2024-05-01','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',5760000.00,'Room size : 37 sqm. Our One-Bedroom Bungalow is a unique Romantic Eco-Boho Bungalow nestles in Green Escape Resort. You will stay in a sumptuous air-conditioned bungalow that has been handcrafted using recycled wood and tastefully decorated to offer you an authentic Balinese getaway. It\'s the very epitome of a tranquil escape. This Bungalow offers a deluxe king-size bed and a daybed to relax. It offers a comfy mattress, as we know the benefits of a good night’s sleep. The semi-outdoor bathroom with a rain shower will help you revive yourself. Enjoy the comfy sofa on your private terrace which opens onto the exotic garden & pool. The daybed can be used to extend the sleeping capacity of your private bungalow.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5065491,'292','Belen Diaz Sanchez',30508,212552,'Uluwatu to Padang Bai','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-05-01','2024-05-01','Guio','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',560000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-05-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"05:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Green Escape Eco Resort\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-01\", \"text\": \"ETD 08.30 from Padang Bai to Gili Air by Gili Gili Fast Boat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Padang Bai Harbour\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5065493,'292','Belen Diaz Sanchez',31308,205333,'One-Bedroom Signature Bungalow with Private Pool','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-05-01','2024-05-04','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',8064000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-05-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5065495,'292','Belen Diaz Sanchez',30508,207383,'Padang Bai to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-05-04','2024-05-04','Guio','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',560000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-05-04\", \"text\": \"ETA 12.30 from Gili Air by Gili Gili Fast Boat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Padang Bai Harbour\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-04\", \"text\": \"ETD 01.05 by IB7967 to Doha on 05 May\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5065661,'294','Paul Cyriel F De Keere',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-16','2024-04-17','Melysa','Tami',5,'Double + Twin',4200000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel.','{\"date\": \"2024-04-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5065663,'294','Paul Cyriel F De Keere',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-04-17','2024-04-19','Melysa','Tami',8,'Persons (8)',25440000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-04-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5065666,'294','Paul Cyriel F De Keere',31147,204193,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-22','2024-04-23','Melysa','Tami',5,'Double',3660000.00,'Swiss-Belhotel Superior rooms offer all the facilities a modern traveler demands with style and comfort. The Superior rooms is 24 sqm furnished with king sized bed near from the lift. This room is suitable for solo travelers or shared room with a colleague while doing business in town.',NULL,'Flight details ETD : 08.15 by Wings Air IW1350 to Palopo on 23 Apr','{\"date\": \"2024-04-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5065669,'294','Paul Cyriel F De Keere',31015,203232,'3D2N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Ijen Tour Package drop Bali','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-04-28','2024-04-30','Melysa','Tami',8,'Persons (8)',16200000.00,NULL,NULL,'Flight details ETA 14.50 by Super Air Jet IU545 from Makassar on 28 Apr','{\"date\": \"2024-04-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5065670,'294','Paul Cyriel F De Keere',30685,200875,'Deluxe Double/Twin Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-28','2024-04-29','Melysa','Tami',5,'Double + Twin',5625000.00,NULL,'The rate including service charge and government tax.',NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"202