ed, king and twin bed with a size of 28 square meters each.',NULL,'Check-in time 14.00 Check-out time 12.00','{\"date\": \"2024-05-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5095287,'340','JEAN FRANCOIS TOUILLAUD',31275,216413,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-05-19','2024-05-20','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Double',840000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-05-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5095306,'340','JEAN FRANCOIS TOUILLAUD',31275,216414,'One-Way Airport Transfer','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-05-19','2024-05-19','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Per Car',140000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-05-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5095307,'340','JEAN FRANCOIS TOUILLAUD',31275,216414,'One-Way Airport Transfer','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-05-20','2024-05-20','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Per Car',0.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-05-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5095747,'341','Natalia Rey Pelaez',32766,216810,'3D2N Open Trip Komodo - Lady Grace / Deluxe Cabin','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-05-17','2024-05-19','Guio','Komang',4,'Per Person (Min. 2 Person)',25680000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-05-17\", \"text\": \"Gio\'s Place (Jl pasar batu cermin, Gang koperasi Suka damai Desa Batu cermin, 86754, Indonesia).\", \"time\": \"09:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Labuan Bajo\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-19\", \"text\": \"ETD: 15.25h by Garuda Indonesia GA453 to CGL 19 May 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Labuan Bajo Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5097154,'320','Laure Goudon Bechet',30508,207379,'Ubud to Padang Bai','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-05-03','2024-05-03','Yuli','Febrina',1,'Persons (4-6)',1064000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,'Transfer Ubud - Padang Bai Harbor Boat detail: ETD 09:00 by Ekajaya Fast Ferry','{\"date\": \"2024-05-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Alaya Ubud Resort\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ekajaya Fast Ferry Office\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5097560,'343','Patricia Lozano Martinez',30783,215162,'Java Bali Overload Tour : Yogyakarta City, Mount Bromo & Ijen Crater 5D4N / C. Adhisthana Hotel - Br','Confirmed','JS-JAVA05',5,'2024-08-05','2024-08-09','Nicholas','Febrina',2,'Persons (2 / Double)',20730000.00,'Travel overland from Java all the way to Bali! This tour takes you to an amazing road trip you will never forget. From discovering the ancient wonders Borobudur and Prambanan in Yogyakarta, a city rich of authentic Javanese culture, to climbing the majestic volcanoes of Bromo and Ijen to witness the spectacular sunrises and unique blue fire, and finish on the island of the gods, Bali. You have the option of going by train from Yogyakarta until Surabaya before you reach Bromo, less tiring, more convenient but it comes at different price. On the other hand, with car you can make some stops along the way so you have a chance to see something new. It is up to you! Day 1 : Welcome to Yogyakarta Welcome to the cradle of Indonesian culture, Yogyakarta. A tourist destination for its ancient palaces, temples, batik workshops, gamelan music orchestras, court dances and wayang puppet shows. Upon your arrival in Yogyakarta a representative of come2indonesia will be waiting for you with a sign indicating your name to take you to your hotel and the rest of the day is for you. The journey from the airport should be around 2-2,5 hours. Meals : - Accommodation : C. Adhisthana Hotel - Superior Room Day 2 : Yogyakarta City Tour - Borobodur Temple - Prambanan Temple After breakfast, your guide will pick you up with your hotel to start exploring the city. This excursion will make you lose yourselves in the authentic magic of Yogyakarta. One of the most beautiful and complete routes of the cultural capital of Indonesia. At the scheduled time, your guide will pick you up to begin the tour of Borobudur, the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. Depending on where you stay in the city, the drive can be 1-1,5 hours to the temple. Arrival at the temple, you will walk around the garden area, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano has been producing during its history. After visiting one of the most important Buddhist temples in Southeast Asia, you will continue the journey to the heart of the city. You will visit the Keraton, or also known as the Sultan’s Palace. The palace is a complex building two centuries old. Next, you will hear the song of the “freedom” of the birds in the bird market, you will visit the “Water Castle” that occupies the highest part at the northern end of the vast complex of Taman Sari. Then, stroll around Malioboro Street, one of the main streets of Yogyakarta, with its merchants, horse carriages, taxi-bikes and markets. An incredible experience that will make the hours fly by. Finishing the tour in the centre of the city of Yogyakarta, you will head northeast towards Prambanan, the temple of Hinduists and classified as a World Heritage Site by UNESCO since 1991. This temple was completed in 856 AD to commemorate the victory of the descendant of Sanjaya dynasty, Rikai Pikatan, against the last Shailendra sovereign of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to Shiva, one of the Trimurti which is an expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the Destroyer. After this unforgettable day, you will take you to your hotel. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : C. Adhisthana Hotel - Superior Room Day 3 : Yogyakarta - Bromo (By Train) Ready with your suitcases, the time has come to say a farewell to this dream city. You will enjoy your breakfast at the hotel, and at the indicated time, with your guide, you will travel to Jombang / Mojokerta by train. Then by private car you will go to your hotel located on the slopes of the Bromo volcano. In total it will be about 8 hours of travel. check-in at the hotel and deserved rest. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : C. Bromo Terrace - Deluxe Room Day 4 : Bromo - Ijen Very early, your guide and a jeep driver will be waiting for you at the hotel to attend one of the most spectacular sunrises in Indonesia. Even though you have to get up early, it will be worth it. You will climb to a high point first in full darkness and, little by little the first rays of sun are giving way to a huge and indescribable caldera that makes up the entire view of the Bromo and Semeru Natural Park. With Bromo, a volcano of great fumaroles and behind it, the Semeru Volcano with explosions every 20 minutes exactly, will make you have one of the most rewarding experiences ever. After enjoying the sunset, by jeep, we will go to the slopes of the volcano where you can go to the Bromo volcano and after climbing some stairs you can reach the very edge of its crater and see the impressive activity it has. We return to the hotel to cool off and enjoy your breakfast. At the agreed time, we will leave for our next destination, the Ijen volcano. This section lasts about 7-8 hours by car where we will make a stop to eat. Take this trip to rest. Arriving in Ijen, we will leave you at your hotel, check in and enjoy your deserved rest. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : C. Ketapang Indah Hotel - Deluxe Room Day 5 : Ijen Tour - Ketapang - Bali The day has finally come to visit one of the most attractive volcanoes in Indonesia! One of the last open pit sulfur mines that survive on the planet. For this climb you can choose between two schedules; leave very early at 1 AM to see the blue fire (please not that it is not always visible, for example during rainy days) or leave more quietly at 4 AM only for the sunrise. You can decide later when you meet the guide. Once we pick you up at your hotel, you will head towards the village of Licin to reach the slope of the volcano to begin the steep climb to the crater of the volcano. During this trek, your guide will give you double filter masks to protect you from the natural chemicals of sulfur. At an altitude of 2883 meters and when dawn begins, an incredible contrast of colors will open before your eyes. A yellow earth scene and a large turquoise blue lake inside the crater that contrast with a suspended white cloud that is continuously expelling the volcano. In turn, among so much beauty you will see the local miners do what is said to be one of the toughest jobs in the world. These miners go down to the crater of the volcano to load 80 to 100 kilos of sulfur on their shoulders and then sell it. After this amazing experience on the edge of Ijen volcano crater, we begin the descent with an incredible panoramic view of the mountains that make up the national park. We will take you to your hotel to cool off and have breakfast and we start the journey to Bali for about 5 hours at least, depending on where you stay in Bali. To do this, we will go first to the port of Banyuwangi where we will take the ferry to cross to Bali. It is a journey of only 30 minutes, but remember to adjust your watch by an hour due to the time zone change. Welcome to the island of the Gods. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'5D4N Semarang - Yogyakarta - Bromo - Ijen - Drop off in Bali, include Train Accommodation : 05-07 Aug 2024/2N Adhisthana Hotel - 1 Double Superior Room 07-08 Aug 2024/1N Bromo Terrace Hotel - 1 Double Deluxe Room 08-09 Aug 2024/1N Ketapang Indah Hotel - 1 Double Superior Room Guide : Spanish speaking guide D1 / 05 Aug 2024: Pick up in Semarang Airport - Yogyakarta D2 / 06 Aug 2024: Yogyakarta City Tour - Borobudur Temple - Pramabanan Temple (B) D3 / 07 Aug 2024: Yogyakarta - Bromo by Train (B) D4 / 08 Aug 2024: Bromo Sunrise Tour by Jeep - Ijen (B) D5 / 09 Aug 2024: Ijen Tour with Blue Fire - Transfer to Bali by Ferry (B) Flight details: ETA in Semarang at 11:25 by Batik Air ID6303 from Pangkalan Bun on 05 Aug Drop Off in Bali: Angkul Angkul Segara Beach Kuta','{\"date\": \"2024-08-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5098233,'263','Danny Van Belle 20235019',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-16','2024-11-17','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Double',784000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Early check-in at 08.00. Check-out time is 12:00.','{\"date\": \"2024-11-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5098235,'263','Danny Van Belle 20235019',30683,203329,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-28','2024-11-29','Rendy','Rendy',4,'Double + Twin',3920000.00,'Feel at home in one of our Superior Rooms - warm colors giving an inviting feel and ambiance. Although you are in the heart of Soekarno - Hatta Airport you can find a small oasis of relaxation where you will leave the hustle and bustle of traveling far behind spacious 24 square meters. Superior room with a king or twin beds offering comfortable stay equipped with modern facilities such as air conditioning, arm chair, work desk & chair, flat screen TV with cable and satellite channels, free access internet & Wi-Fi, in room safe, coffee/tea maker, mini cooler, private bathroom with shower and hair dryer, and many more.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel.','{\"date\": \"2024-11-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5098236,'263','Danny Van Belle 20235019',30683,203329,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-12-12','2024-12-13','Rendy','Rendy',4,'Double + Twin',3920000.00,'Feel at home in one of our Superior Rooms - warm colors giving an inviting feel and ambiance. Although you are in the heart of Soekarno - Hatta Airport you can find a small oasis of relaxation where you will leave the hustle and bustle of traveling far behind spacious 24 square meters. Superior room with a king or twin beds offering comfortable stay equipped with modern facilities such as air conditioning, arm chair, work desk & chair, flat screen TV with cable and satellite channels, free access internet & Wi-Fi, in room safe, coffee/tea maker, mini cooler, private bathroom with shower and hair dryer, and many more.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel.','{\"date\": \"2024-12-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-12-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5098336,'344','Muriel GUILLOTTE',30508,202890,'Batur Sunrise 4X4 with Black Lava + Trekking to Summit + Hotspring','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-05-02','2024-05-02','Rendy','Rendy',3,'Persons (3)',2587200.00,'Enjoy trek or climb Mount Batur and see the sunrise from the top of Batur Volcano. The Batur Volcano is one of the sacred mountain according to Hindu believe. We will get in ahead of schedule morning around 02.00 am depend the area of you stay, and afterward we specifically going to Mount Batur starting point. Starting in the dark under starlight sky, you will be guided to ascend the slope of Mount Batur. You will approach the peak of Mount Batur (1717 meters) at about 06.00 am. While waiting for the sunrise you will have a simple breakfast and hot coffee or tea served by your guide in Mount Batur. Witness the breathtaking sunrise overlooking the majestic view of Lake Batur and Mount Rinjani. After witnessing the sunrise, continue for our descent, at about 9 am, you will be arriving at the finishing point.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-05-02\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in hotel lobby\", \"time\": \"03:00\", \"locality\": \"Kastara Resort and Spa Ubud\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Kastara Resort and Spa Ubud\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5098337,'345','Marie Louise Dieringer (April 2024)',30508,202897,'Uluwatu Temple and Kecak Dance','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-23','2024-04-23','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Person (1)',1446000.00,'This half-day tour, is an exciting tour package to visit Padang-Padang Beach, Uluwatu Temple, the famous Balinese Hindu Temple in south part of Bali with breathtaking view of sunset and Indian Ocean. Uluwatu Temple is one of Balinese Hindu Temples located right on the petrifying hill with the crevasse exist in the right and left side. Uluwatu Temple is one of Sad Khayangan (6 biggest temple in Bali) owns magnificent view of the Indian Ocean and sunset as a backdrop. This temple is very amazing where the location is right on the narrow peninsula with deep seawater under it. This tour package is combined with the spectacular Balinese traditional dance performance of Kecak Dance. Balinese Kecak Dance is a spectacular traditional dance with the group of people playing this dance with fire game. It is very exciting and unique dance due to the sound of gamelan is not using the normal gamelan but use their mouth. The dancers make the compact choir with the exquisite dance movement that is one of this dance features. After the dance we returned back to the hotel or seafood restaurant in Jimbaran.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-23\", \"text\": \"ETA: 14.35 by Garuda Indonesia GA408 from Jakarta on 23 Apr\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Denpasar Airport\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Puri Santrian Resort Sanur\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5098338,'345','Marie Louise Dieringer (April 2024)',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-24','2024-04-24','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Person (1)',1650000.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-24\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in hotel lobby\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"Puri Santrian Resort Sanur\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Puri Santrian Resort Sanur\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5098339,'345','Marie Louise Dieringer (April 2024)',30508,202895,'East Bali Tour','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-25','2024-04-25','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Person (1)',1626000.00,'In this part of the trip, we set off along the East Coast of the island. The first site visit will be the Kusamba Village, a fishing village where colorful Prahu in the black sand beaches. We will announce the salt making process by traditional method. We continue our journey on the east coast to reach Goa Lawah, Gua Lawah or Bat Cave is one of favorite places of interest in Bali and it is located near of hilly bank so it is called reef of Middle hill. We continue our trip to Tenganan Village, Tenganan Village is one of the oldest Balinese Traditional located in Karangasem Regency, east part of Bali. This village is much referred by cultural literature science of Tenganan Pegringsingan, which is very famous in the island. It owns very unique local community life pattern which is one example of Bali Aga Village cultures (Hindu Prehistoric) and different with other countryside in plain of Bali. From here, we go to Amlapura to visit the Royal Palace, The town of Amlapura is the capital of Karangasem (\'East Bali\'). The palace of the former kings of the region is located here, and their descendants have opened parts of the complex to the public. We will finish our trip with visit heaven of Tirta Gangga, Tirta Gangga is a beautiful park with the huge water fountain. At the end of tour we will transfer you back to the hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-25\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in hotel lobby\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"Puri Santrian Resort Sanur\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Puri Santrian Resort Sanur\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5098341,'347','Vicente Carrion Medrano',32766,216808,'3D2N Open Trip Komodo - Lady Grace / Junior Suite','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-07-19','2024-07-21','Jacob','Eddy',2,'Per Person (Min. 2 Person)',16440000.00,NULL,NULL,'DAY 01 : Kelor Island - Manjerite Island - Kalong Island DAY 02 : Padar Island - Long/ Pink Beach - Komodo Island - Manta Point - Taka Makasar DAY 03 : Kanawa Island Pick up time between In Hotel : 9.00-9.30 AM Excluded : Local Donation, Komodo National Park Fees & Rangee Fees * Foreigh/ KITAS Guest: IDR 600.000/Person/ Trips','{\"date\": \"2024-07-19\", \"text\": \"ETA: Elang Hillside Bamboo Villas Address : Jl. Elang Barat No.1, Labuan Bajo, Kec. Komodo, Kabupaten Manggarai Barat, Nusa Tenggara Tim. Phone : 0813-3706-6664\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-21\", \"text\": \"ETD: 21 JULY 17:30 QZ647 By AirAsia\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"AIRPORT LABUAN BAJO\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5099173,'348','Frederick Mason MORGAN JR',30680,200921,'Junior Suite Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-22','2024-04-23','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Double',2016000.00,'For those who are looking for an added touch of personal service, the finest amenities and extra space Junior Suite is right place to stay. Our spacious 60 sqm offer modern design with touches of comfort. An oversized spa bathroom featuring a hot and cold shower and jacuzzi bathtub further enhances your experience. This room equipped with LED TV 55\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, bathrobe, and hairdryer. Free access to our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel.','{\"date\": \"2024-04-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5099191,'348','Frederick Mason MORGAN JR',31158,204472,'VIP Service Fast Track International Arrival by Galih','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-22','2024-04-22','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Person (1)',3024000.00,'Arrival International: Pick up at before immigration area.',NULL,'MEETING POINT: Your personal assistant will be waiting for you holding a sign of your name, at the nearest point to the plane, usually at the end of jetbridge, or near the VOA counter. They will assist you through VOA purchase, immigration with fast track service, baggage claim and customs until the arrival hall exit. SPECIAL REQUEST: Escort the clients to meet up with transfer for FM7 Hotel (+62811-8815-053)','{\"date\": \"2024-04-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5100145,'349','Benjamin Schillig',30680,200914,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-05-27','2024-05-28','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Single',0.00,'Enjoy our spacious elegant deluxe room with 40 m2 of room size. Enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, hot and cold shower, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel.','{\"date\": \"2024-05-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5100146,'349','Benjamin Schillig',30806,202002,'4D3N Borneo Orangutan & Reforestation Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO7',4,'2024-05-28','2024-05-31','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Person (1)',10360000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN – KUMAI PORT – TANJUNG HARAPAN Your “Orangutan & Reforestation Tour” begins upon arrival at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan is Cape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : TANJUNG HARAPAN VILLAGE – PROBOSCIS TOUR – CAMP LEAKEY After an extraordinary breakfast, you go to visit the village inside the national park, named Tanjung Harapan Village. Here you will see the activities of the locals. After the visit, you will return to the klotok cruise up to the Sekonyer River. You will see nice vegetation around the river bank, including Nipa Palm, Pandanus, and some kinds of trees that are growing up around the river. See some wildlifes such as birds, Macaques, Proboscis Monkeys and Orangutans. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large monitor lizards. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. Note: The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. Meals : Breakfast – Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : PONDOK TANGGUI – CAMP LEAKEY – BOAT After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continue to add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After lunch, you will have the opportunity to repeat feeding camp at Camp Leaky. It is a unique opportunity to dedicate more time to your observation and to discover more wild animals, along with the Orangutans. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note: If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast – Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 4 : KUMAI PORT – PANGKALAN BUN Today we end our stay in the jungles of Borneo. Our “Orangutan & Reforestation Tour” is about to finish. In the early morning we will have breakfast on the boat, to then go to the port and in turn, be transferred to the airport. The boat departure will be at the latest at 10am, but we adapt to your flights if your flight leaves earlier in the morning. If you decide to take an afternoon flight, we can take you directly to the airport at 10 or if you want a city tour in the Arut village to drop you off at the airport later, it could be arranged at extra cost. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-05-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-31\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5100147,'349','Benjamin Schillig',30805,202689,'CGK-PKN','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-05-28','2024-05-28','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Person',1712000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-05-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5100148,'349','Benjamin Schillig',30684,200640,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-05-31','2024-06-01','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Single',1528800.00,'Equipped with either a king size or deluxe twin beds, our Deluxe Rooms are designed for modern travellers who seek comfort while staying in Bromo.',NULL,'Please send the guarantee letter/voucher following procedure below: - 30 (thirty) days reservation notice prior to the arrival date for Normal Period. - 45 (forty-five) days reservation notice prior to the arrival date for High Season (June 1th to August 31st) and Peak Season (D-3 to D+4 Idul Fitri (April 18 - 25th, 2023 and December 21st, 2023 to January 5th, 2024) period. - Otherwise, the cancellation policy will be applied.','{\"date\": \"2024-05-31\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5100149,'349','Benjamin Schillig',30805,212272,'PKN-SUB','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-05-31','2024-05-31','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Person',1819000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-05-31\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-31\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5100150,'349','Benjamin Schillig',30679,200582,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-01','2024-06-02','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Single',1677060.00,'Stylish, spacious and bright with an open-concept bedroom and bathroom, and a private balcony with daybed. Room includes a desk, a small sofa and a floor-to-ceiling window for maximum natural light.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5100151,'349','Benjamin Schillig',31015,203232,'3D2N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Ijen Tour Package drop Bali','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-05-31','2024-06-02','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Person (1)',0.00,NULL,NULL,'Arrival Surabaya Airport by Flight : ETA 10.00 by Batik Air ID 6134 from Pangkalan Bun on 31 May 2024 Hotel in Bromo : JIWA JAWA BROMO Hotel in Ijen : DIALOOG Hotel Banyuwangi Drop off Hotel in Bali :TEJAPRANA RESORT & Spa Ubud','{\"date\": \"2024-05-31\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5100166,'350','MARTA OTERO MAYAN',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-06-06','2024-06-08','Jacob','Eddy',1,'Persons (2)',5400000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-06-06\", \"text\": \"ETA 06 JUN 2024 | 07.15 / ID6202 BY BATIK AIR FROM JAKARTA\", \"time\": \"07:15\", \"locality\": \"AIRPORT PANGKALAN BUN\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-08\", \"text\": \"ETD: 08 JUN 2024 | 0730 / IN195 BY NAM AIR / TO (SRG) Semarang\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"AIRPORT PANGKALAN BUN\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5100173,'350','MARTA OTERO MAYAN',30783,214611,'3D2N Semarang - Yogyakarta / C. Adhisthana*3 (Superior Room)','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-06-08','2024-06-10','Jacob','Eddy',2,'Persons (2 / Double)',8100000.00,'D1 : Arrival at Semarang Airport - Borobudur Temple tour incl. Mendut and Pawon - Transfer to Jogja Welcome to the cradle of Indonesian culture, Yogyakarta. A tourist destination for its ancient palaces, temples, batik workshops, gamelan music orchestras, court dances and wayang puppet shows. Upon your arrival in Semarang airport a representative of come2indonesia will be waiting for you with a sign indicating your name to start exploring this special city. We will start by heading towards Borobudur Temple (Candi Borobudur), the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. We will tour around the temple, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano has been producing during its history. After visiting one of the most important Buddhist temples in Southeast Asia, we continue our journey to the Mendut temple and Pawon temple. And then, we will take you to Jogjakarta. D2 : Jogjakarta City Tour visit Sultan Palace, Watercastle and Bird Market - Visit Prambanan Temple You will enjoy a well-deserved breakfast at the hotel and we will start by heading towards Keraton known as the Sultan’s Palace. The palace is a complex building two centuries old, located in the heart of the city. You will hear the song of the “freedom” of the birds in the bird market, we will visit the “Water Castle” that occupies the highest part at the northern end of the vast complex of Taman Sari, Malioboro Street, main street of Yogyakarta, with its merchants, horse carriages, taxi-bikes and markets. After this visit we go to Candi Prambanan, the temple of the Hinduists and classified as a World Heritage Site by Unesco since 1991. The built of this temple was finished around the year 856 to commemorate the victory of the descendant Sanjaya of Siva, Rikai Pikatan on the last sovereign Sailendra of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to the Trimurti, the expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the destroyer. An incredible experience that will make the hours fly by. After this unforgettable day, we will take you back to your hotel. D3 : Transfer to Yogyakarta International Airport You will enjoy a well-deserved breakfast at the hotel and according to the time of your flight, we will pick you up to take you to the airport and take the flight to your next destination. End of our services. Thank you very much for exploring Yogyakarta by the hand of Come2indonesia.',NULL,'0608 Día 03: Semarang Airport – Templo Borobudur – Yogyakarta 0609 Día 04: Yogyakarta Tour – Templo Prambanan 0610 Día 05: Yogyakarta – Airport','{\"date\": \"2024-06-08\", \"text\": \"ETA: 08 JUN 2024 | 0840 / IN195 BY NAM AIR / FROM (PKN) PANGKALAN BUN\", \"time\": \"08:40\", \"locality\": \"AIRPORT SEMARANG\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-10\", \"text\": \"ETD: 10 JUN 2024 | 1400 / JT566 BY LION AIR / TO (DPS) DENPASAR\", \"time\": \"14:00\", \"locality\": \"AIRPORT YOGYAKARTA\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5100182,'350','MARTA OTERO MAYAN',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-10','2024-06-10','Jacob','Eddy',1,'Persons (1-3)',420000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-10\", \"text\": \"ETA: 10 JUN 2024 | 1625 / JT566 BY LION AIR / FROM (YIA) Yogyakarta\", \"time\": \"16:25\", \"locality\": \"AIRPORT DENPASAR\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-10\", \"text\": \"PERTIWI BISMA 2 JALAN RAYA BISMA, UBUD, GIANYAR, BALI 80571, INDONESIA +62361 981386\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5100184,'350','MARTA OTERO MAYAN',30620,200813,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,6,'2024-06-10','2024-06-16','Jacob','Eddy',1,'Double',6120000.00,'24 units (10 twin bed and 14 double bed) of 35 sqm each deluxe rooms with garden view are modern‐minimalism designed. Advance, facilities such as LCD TV, coffee/tea maker, balcony/terrace, safety deposit box, minibar, and complete bathroom facilities.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5100189,'351','Alvaro Gonzalez Gimenez',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-21','2024-06-22','Jacob','Tami',1,'Double',784000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel.','{\"date\": \"2024-06-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5100223,'351','Alvaro Gonzalez Gimenez',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-25','2024-06-25','Jacob','Tami',2,'Persons (1-3)',784000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-25\", \"text\": \"ETA 18.30 by Citilink QG694 from Surabaya on 25 June\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"I Gusti Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-25\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bangkiang Sidem, Keliki, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Kastara Resort and Spa\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5100281,'351','Alvaro Gonzalez Gimenez',31625,216846,'Royal Suite','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-06-25','2024-06-29','Jacob','Tami',1,'Double',17920000.00,'With room size of 85 m2, Royal Suite room is very comfortable not only for the New Honey moon couple but also those who would be celebrating an Anniversary Wedding. The facilities of this room are basically similar than the Deluxe one, in term of completely interior and facilities , luxury and stylist teak wood furniture, splendid jungle view visible, suitable space for having romantic dinner, but however the only one point of view that is private infinity pool, as the different. The infinity pool would be totally upgraded and elevated you’re experience and maximize the quality of time for having togetherness while on holiday. It is not necessary for having rusty time to be at main pool as your admiral, and for having floating breakfast or dinner would be also available by having certain charge. Through to an International experience Chef all the food with the diverse flavor east met west nor event traditional Balinese food will pumper your taste buds.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5100330,'312','JOAN TUTUSAUS SOLE MR / ANABEL TRIGUEROS ANDUJAR MRS.',30508,202892,'FD Tour Taman Ayun Temple - Jatiluwih - Tanah Lot','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-05-26','2024-05-26','Igo','Eddy',2,'Persons (2)',1747200.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-05-26\", \"text\": \"Merusaka Nusa Dua Alamat: Kawasan Wisata Nusa Dua Lot S-3, Benoa, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80363\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-05-26\", \"text\": \"Merusaka Nusa Dua Alamat: Kawasan Wisata Nusa Dua Lot S-3, Benoa, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80363\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5100515,'351','Alvaro Gonzalez Gimenez',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-27','2024-06-27','Jacob','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',1747200.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-27\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bangkiang Sidem, Keliki, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Kastara Resort and Spa\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5100519,'351','Alvaro Gonzalez Gimenez',30508,202894,'Kehen Temple - Pengelipuran - Tukad Cepung Waterfall','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-28','2024-06-28','Jacob','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',1568000.00,'Our wonderful tour starts from Kehen Temple. It is an ancient Hindu temple complex boasting unique architectural features. The staircases reaching from the ground to temple courtyard are carved sandstone mythical animal and Balinese folklore figure statues and also the central vestibule. The temple’s walls are also ornate with Chinese porcelain plates, which are a tribute to the historical relations between the local Bali kingdom and China. Afterwards, we continue to Penglipuran, a village that succeeded in preserving its 75-hectare bamboo forest located in the northern part of the village. Members of this village have a strong commitment to the system of \'Ayahan Desa\' - a philosophy committed to respecting the land on which the village stands. To concludes the day, we stop by at Tukad Cepung Waterfall. Well-guarded by the circular cliffs, this waterfall is difficult to locate for the first time visitor. The circular cliffs give you the feeling of being in a cave, while the open sky right from where the waterfall emerges, gives you the most enchanting view. The sunlight falls on the glistering waterfall creating a rainbow, which feels as though it is projected right up to you. If you have never seen water flowing from the sky, then this would be your chance! After spending your time there, we go back to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-28\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bangkiang Sidem, Keliki, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Kastara Resort and Spa\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5100621,'351','Alvaro Gonzalez Gimenez',30508,213032,'Ubud to Kusamba','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-29','2024-06-29','Jacob','Tami',2,'Persons (1-3)',784000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-29\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bangkiang Sidem, Keliki, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Kastara Resort and Spa\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-29\", \"text\": \"ETD 08.00 by The Angkal Fast Boat to Nusa Penida\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Kusamba Harbour\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5100668,'351','Alvaro Gonzalez Gimenez',30829,216854,'Snorkeling Package Sharing','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-29','2024-06-29','Jacob','Tami',2,'Person (1)',1276800.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-29\", \"text\": \"ETA 08.30 from Kusamba on 29 Jun 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sampalan Harbour Nusa Penida\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-29\", \"text\": \"Jalan Gamat Bay, Nusa Penida Island, Klungkung, Bali, Indonesia\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Māua Nusa Penida\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5100681,'351','Alvaro Gonzalez Gimenez',30582,203387,'One Bedroom Luxury Villas','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-29','2024-06-30','Jacob','Tami',1,'Double',3744000.00,'Each One Bedroom Luxury Villa is designed with a private infinity pool, scenic view across the Gamat Bay or garden view, and some have a small private garden. Every villas features the following: An integrated universal power outlet, Room safe (suitable for storing laptops), Cable TV with international news and movie channels, Eco-friendly bathroom amenities, Coffee and tea-making facilities.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5100809,'351','Alvaro Gonzalez Gimenez',30661,215777,'Lotus One Bedroom','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-06-30','2024-07-03','Jacob','Tami',1,'Double',10710000.00,'Are you looking for a romantic getaway, just the two of you? Then our one bedroom villa is exactly what you are looking for. Your own private spot in paradise will easily set the right atmosphere to share many precious and love filled moments together. You’ll be able to enjoy a morning tea or coffee with your loved one, a dip in your own private swimming pool or a romantic movie to end your day. And with food and drinks from the restaurant just one phone call away, you can forget about any distractions and completely focus on each other. Your quality time spent together at Jivana will turn into memories that will bring a smile to your face every single time.',NULL,'The original voucher issued by travel agent must back up guest check in. The voucher should clearly specify all instructions and required services.','{\"date\": \"2024-06-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5102038,'353','Howard Peters',30683,203336,'Mini-stay Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-25','2024-04-25','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Single',560000.00,'Step into one of our comfortable and spacious Deluxe Rooms. Here you can kick back and relax at ease and prepare for your next flight or meeting. Spacious 24 square meters deluxe room with a king or twin beds offering comfortable stay equipped with modern facilities such as air conditioning, arm chair, work desk & chair, flat screen TV with cable and satellite channels, free access internet & Wi-Fi, in room safe, coffee/tea maker, mini cooler, private bathroom with shower and hair dryer, and many more.','Room usage for up to 6 hours Earliest check-in time 09.00 Latest check-out time 23.00 Including transfer between terminals',NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-04-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5102056,'309','Cal McIlwaine',30959,213942,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-05-30','2024-06-02','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Single',2923200.00,'Specially designed for savvy travelers seeking comfort and style at 48 sqm of room size. Available in King and Double bet with the option of an extra bed for an additional fee. The room features a cozy living room with a comfortable sofa, LED wall-mounted TV, complimentary high-speed Wi-Fi, and in-room amenities to ensure a relaxing stay experience.',NULL,'Check-in time 14.00 Check-out time 12.00 Guaranteed early check-in on 31 May 2024','{\"date\": \"2024-05-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5102072,'354','CATIA CANCIALLI',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-04','2024-08-05','Rendy','Ayu',1,'Double',840000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. - Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK–IN','{\"date\": \"2024-08-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5102183,'21','Jambix Test',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-04-02','2024-04-03','Rahayu','Rahayu',2,'Double',1680000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. - Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK–IN','{\"date\": \"2024-04-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-04-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5102324,'356','Amanda Milani',30806,202007,'5D4N Borneo Orangutan Tour & Dayak Tribe','Confirmed',NULL,5,'2024-06-03','2024-06-07','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Persons (2)',23940000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN – KUMAI PORT – TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan is Cape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY – CAMP LEAKEY After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continue to add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note: The Birute Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. Meals : Breakfast – Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT – PANGKALAN BUN – DAYAK VILLAGE After breakfast, you make a final sail towards Kumai, where you will approach the car and go to Dayak village. On the way, you will go through indigenous villages, river workers, and people making their living near the river. You will pass some rapids with caution. You will stop on the way to be able to have lunch. Upon reaching the Dayak village, our guide will take you to the Long House (they are the typical houses of the Dayak tribes in Borneo – very long houses where almost a village lives inside). Upon arrival, you will realize the kindness of the town. Normally, they celebrate that people from outside come to visit them, because for them, it is a source of pride that people from so far away travel so much to be able to keep them company. Due to that, on arrival, it is normal to celebrate this visit with dances and some other local liquor! After walking around, the communal dinner with the whole tribe arrives, and then they will ring the bell, with which the whole town will gather to do dances and enjoy the night with what they call Pesta Menarik Horn Bill (Horn Festival Bill). Note: The guest house will be based on the basic house of local people, where you can experience their lives and get closer to their culture, with very standard facilities, a shared bathroom, and a shared house with other guests. Meals : Breakfast – Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Basic Guest House in the Village Day 4 : DAYAK VILLAGE – PANGKALAN BUN In the morning, you can visit the surroundings of the village, share stories with them, and help them in their daily tasks. You can also take the opportunity to see the manual work they do and usually take to the city to sell, such as masks, carpets, statues, etc. After packing everything, start the way back to Pangkalan Bun. On the way, you can stop at the Kotawaringin Palace and take pictures around. Lunch will be on the way, with an arrival in the afternoon at Pangkalan Bun. Transfer to the hotel, and the rest of the afternoon is free. Meals : Breakfast – Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Arsela Hotel or similar Day 5 : HOTEL – PANGKALAN BUN AIRPORT After breakfast, transfer to the airport. End of our services. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board. Flights information ETA:','{\"date\": \"2024-06-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5103107,'359','Rachel Jones',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-07-25','2024-07-27','Rendy','Tami',2,'Double',3360000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. - Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR