,15400000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5103157,'359','Rachel Jones',30805,207116,'MDC-DPS','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-05','2024-08-05','Rendy','Tami',4,'Person',9680000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5103160,'359','Rachel Jones',30805,202739,'DPS-LBJ','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-06','2024-08-06','Rendy','Tami',4,'Person',7040000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5103164,'359','Rachel Jones',30805,212510,'LBJ-CGK','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-10','2024-08-10','Rendy','Tami',4,'Person',10560000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5103175,'359','Rachel Jones',30662,213242,'4D3N Explore The Nature of Leuser National Park Sumatra Elephant & Sumatra Orang Utan','Confirmed','RVL 04D ENLNP SE',4,'2024-07-27','2024-07-30','Rendy','Tami',4,'Persons (4-5 / Double)',21360000.00,'DAY 01 : MEDAN - CITY TOUR - TANGKAHAN Upon arrival at Kualanamu International Airport pick up by our tour guide and then drive to Tangkahan via Binjai and Batang Serangan. Afternoon arrival at Tangkahan check-in at MEGA INN. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Mega In Lodge DAY 02 : TANGKAHAN - ELEPHANT WASHING & RIVER SAFARI - BUKIT LAWANG After breakfast walking to the elephant station and then join with the Mahout during washing the Elephant, and then feed the elephant, after feeding the Elephant enjoying tubing through the river and stop will be made at Fantastic Buluh Waterfall where you may enjoy the waterfall where you can take nature shower and then you can enjoy sun bathing and swimming on the river and enjoying picnic lunch on the beach of the river. Afternoon arrival at the village you can get in touch with local people, where you can see the daily activities of the local people and then return to guest house by walking, after short rest drive to Bukit Lawang by car passing plantation and jungle raod, on the way stop at Plantation and several interesting places (school) for enjoying the panorama and witness the activities of the local people. Upon arrival at Bukit Lawang check-in to hotel and afternoon free at own leisure to enjoy the nature of Bukit Lawang. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Accommodation : Ecolodge Bukit Lawang Cottage or Rindu Alam Hotel DAY 03 : BUKIT LAWANG - JUNGLE TRACKING / VISIT ORANG UTAN After breakfast walking to the jungle to start a jungle tracking to explore the nature of Leuser National park with their flora and fauna, the possibility to see Orang Utan on their own habitat and other kind of animal such as Thomas leaf monkeys, long tail macaque, gibbon, black gibbon and other kind of flora and fauna of tropical rain forest. This tracking will take about 03 hours, after tracking return to hotel. Afternoon free at own leisure to enjoy the nature of Bukit Lawang where you can also walking to the village around the hotel. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Ecolodge Bukit Lawang Cottage or Rindu Alam Hotel DAY 04 : BUKIT LAWANG - MEDAN / AIRPORT After breakfast drive Medan via Binjai, on the way visiting traditional market at Kuala, arrival in Medan directly transfer to Kuala Namu Int airport for your flight to next destination. Meals : Breakfast',NULL,'Allergies Note: Tony: Diabetic Rachel and Camille: Do not eat red meat.','{\"date\": \"2024-07-27\", \"text\": \"ETA 09.30 by Garuda Indonesia GA0182 from Jakarta on 27 Jul\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Kuala Namu International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-30\", \"text\": \"ETD 15.30 by Lion Air JT385 to Jakarta on 30 Jul\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5103176,'359','Rachel Jones',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-30','2024-07-31','Rendy','Tami',2,'Double + Twin',1680000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. - Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK–IN','{\"date\": \"2024-07-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-31\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5103177,'359','Rachel Jones',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-07-31','2024-08-02','Rendy','Tami',4,'Persons (4)',14880000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Allergies Note: Tony: Diabetic Rachel and Camille: Do not eat red meat. Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-07-31\", \"text\": \"ETA 07.15 by Batik Air ID6202 from Jakarta on 31 Jul\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pangkalan Bun Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-02\", \"text\": \"ETD 07.55 by Batik Air ID6203 to Jakarta on 02 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5103179,'359','Rachel Jones',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-02','2024-08-03','Rendy','Tami',2,'Double + Twin',1680000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. - Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK–IN','{\"date\": \"2024-08-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5103214,'359','Rachel Jones',31591,207373,'3D2N Tangkoko','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-03','2024-08-05','Rendy','Tami',4,'Persons (4-6 / Double)',10800000.00,'Day 1 : MANADO - TANGKOKO - The expedition begins The adventure begins with meeting your guide at the Manado airport. Then you will start the journey of about 2 and a half hours by car to the Tangkoko Forest where you will do the check in at your Homestay or Lodge. Upon arrival, you will have a talk about what you will see and preparations for the trekking. Meals : Dinner Accommodation : Bird House Homestay or Similar Days 02 : Tangkoko Nature Reserve These days will be dedicated to exploring the jungle in search of animals and bird watching. You will start the trekking that will take you to Tangkok National Park. In just 40 minutes by boat, you will reach the Batuangus beach where you will then climb Mount Tangkoko (1500 m). The dense and virgin jungle is home to some unique animal species in North Sulawesi such as the crested black macaque and the tarsier spectrum that has become known as \"the smallest primate in the world\". As you will be trekking through the lush jungle, you will probably see and hear the red gnarled hornbill as well as the Maleo which is a Megapod Bird that lays eggs on large mounds it builds on the black sand. You can also find couscous, which is a relative of the Australian koala. The forest ranger will accompany you all the way to the top of Tangkoko Mountain. In the afternoon you will return to the station. Alternatively, you can have three hours of trekking in the lowland jungle or swimming on the black sand beach of Tangkoko Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Bird House Homestay or Similar Day 03 : Tangkoko - Manado After breakfast, you can spend the morning in the surroundings of the National Park and at the agreed time, with your guide, you will have the transfer to Manado. Thank you for exploring this unique jungle with us. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Allergies Note: Tony: Diabetic Rachel and Camille: Do not eat red meat.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-03\", \"text\": \"ETA 12.25 by Batik Air ID6280 from Jakarta on 03 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Manado International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-05\", \"text\": \"ETD 11.25 by Lion Air JT743 to Denpasar on 05 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5103215,'359','Rachel Jones',30571,202567,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-05','2024-08-06','Rendy','Tami',2,'Double + Twin',2940000.00,'Located at the Second Floor, 35 sqm comfort living with a touch of Balinese style featuring completed fitting, Cable TV, a fancy bathroom comprises rain shower and good quality amenities. Also dedicated Wi-Fi Access to complete your day.',NULL,'Flight information ETA 15.40 by Lion Air JT743 from Manado on 05 Aug ETD 08.00 by Batik Air ID6333 to Labuan Bajo on 06 Aug','{\"date\": \"2024-08-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5103225,'359','Rachel Jones',30701,207536,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-08-08','2024-08-10','Rendy','Tami',2,'Double + Twin',4320000.00,'Our Deluxe Room at 44 sqm of room area, equipped with AC, Western toilet and shower with hot & cold water, desk, seating area, and many more. Breakfast is included in the room rate. Featuring a balcony or terrace, guests can enjoy spectacular views of the garden, pool or the sea.',NULL,'Allergies Note: Tony: Diabetic Rachel and Camille: Do not eat red meat.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5103227,'359','Rachel Jones',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-10','2024-08-11','Rendy','Tami',2,'Double + Twin',1680000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. - Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK–IN','{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5103232,'359','Rachel Jones',32156,212197,'3D2N Leisure Package','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-06','2024-08-08','Rendy','Tami',1,'(1-4 Persons) /boat',57600000.00,'Jofiel Komodo Liveaboard reserves the right to change the itinerary and particular services if required due to unforeseen or unavoidable circumstances. Jofiel Komodo Liveaboard will make every effort to offer equivalent alternatives of a comparable standard. Jofiel Komodo Liveaboard will inform the agent or individual client of such changes at the earliest possible date and the effect they will have on price. Day 1: Kelor Island, Menjerite Island, Rinca Kalong Day 2: Padar Island, Pink Beach, Komodo Island, Taka Makassar, Manta Point Day 3: Sebayur Island, Kanawa/Bidadari Island, Labuan bajo Specification - Name of vessel : KLM Jofiel - Flag : Indonesia - Type : Phinisi Buginesse Schooner - Year Built : 2017 - Made of : Iron wood - Built in : Labuan Bajo - Length : 20 m - Breadth : 4 m - Depth : 1,9 m - Gross Tonnage : 41 - Cruising Speed : +/- 8 knots - Water capacity : +/- 2.000 liters - Fuel capacity : +/- 1.000 liters - Number of cabins : 3 - Number of bathrooms : 4 - Crew : 6',NULL,'Allergies Note: Tony: Diabetic Rachel and Camille: Do not eat red meat.','{\