eady on hotel Lobby for pickup at 16.30','{\"date\": \"2024-06-30\", \"text\": \"Bali Niksoma Jl. Padma Utara Jl. Raya Legian, Legian, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Telepon: (0361) 751946\", \"time\": \"16:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Seminyak\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-30\", \"text\": \"ETD : 21.20 PM by Turkish Airlines TK67 to Istanbul on 30 June 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5136169,'436','SERGIO SHOR JINICH',30508,207262,'Ubud to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-04','2024-08-04','Nicholas','Eddy',3,'Persons (1-3)',1260000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-04\", \"text\": \"Green Field Resort Ubud Address : Jl. Raya Pengosekan, MAS, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : (0361) 9085030\\\"\", \"time\": \"04:30\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-04\", \"text\": \"ETD : 04AUG - 0800 To Labuan Bajo ID6333 by Batik Air\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"AIPRORT DENPASAR\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5136173,'436','SERGIO SHOR JINICH',30508,212288,'Airport to Seminyak','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-06','2024-08-06','Nicholas','Eddy',1,'Persons (1-3)',300000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-06\", \"text\": \"ETA : 06AUG - 1455 From Labuan Bajo ID6330 by Batik Air\", \"time\": \"14:55\", \"locality\": \"AIRPORT DENPASAR\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-06\", \"text\": \"Bali Niksoma Boutique Beach Resort Address : Jl. Padma Utara Jl. Raya Legian, Legian, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Phone : (0361) 751946\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5136174,'436','SERGIO SHOR JINICH',30596,201103,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-06','2024-08-09','Nicholas','Eddy',1,'Double',9000000.00,'Experience timeless elegance in our Deluxe Room. Perfect for couples or solo travelers seeking a spacious single/double bed. Our room offers premium linens, plush pillows, and a peaceful ambiance. Enjoy high-speed internet, a flat-screen TV, coffee and tea-making facilities, and an in-room safe deposit box, ensuring a convenient and enjoyable stay. Unwind on the balcony overlooking the pool, to recharge after a day of activities.',NULL,'1 (DBL) Deluxe Room + 1 Extra Bed','{\"date\": \"2024-08-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5136176,'436','SERGIO SHOR JINICH',30508,202897,'Uluwatu Temple and Kecak Dance','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-08','2024-08-08','Nicholas','Eddy',3,'Persons (3)',2106000.00,'This half-day tour, is an exciting tour package to visit Padang-Padang Beach, Uluwatu Temple, the famous Balinese Hindu Temple in south part of Bali with breathtaking view of sunset and Indian Ocean. Uluwatu Temple is one of Balinese Hindu Temples located right on the petrifying hill with the crevasse exist in the right and left side. Uluwatu Temple is one of Sad Khayangan (6 biggest temple in Bali) owns magnificent view of the Indian Ocean and sunset as a backdrop. This temple is very amazing where the location is right on the narrow peninsula with deep seawater under it. This tour package is combined with the spectacular Balinese traditional dance performance of Kecak Dance. Balinese Kecak Dance is a spectacular traditional dance with the group of people playing this dance with fire game. It is very exciting and unique dance due to the sound of gamelan is not using the normal gamelan but use their mouth. The dancers make the compact choir with the exquisite dance movement that is one of this dance features. After the dance we returned back to the hotel or seafood restaurant in Jimbaran.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": \"Bali Niksoma Boutique Beach Resort Address : Jl. Padma Utara Jl. Raya Legian, Legian, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Phone : (0361) 751946\", \"time\": \"13:00\", \"locality\": \"MEET AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": \"Bali Niksoma Boutique Beach Resort Address : Jl. Padma Utara Jl. Raya Legian, Legian, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Phone : (0361) 751946\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5136177,'436','SERGIO SHOR JINICH',30508,207270,'Seminyak to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-09','2024-08-09','Nicholas','Eddy',1,'Persons (1-3)',300000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": \"Bali Niksoma Boutique Beach Resort Address : Jl. Padma Utara Jl. Raya Legian, Legian, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Phone : (0361) 751946\", \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": \"MEET AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": \"ETD : 09AUG - 10:20 to singapore SQ935 by Singapore Airlines\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"AIRPORT DENPASAR\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5136179,'436','SERGIO SHOR JINICH',30508,202894,'Tegalalang – Tirta Empul – Templo Kehen – Penglipuran Village','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-07','2024-08-07','Nicholas','Eddy',3,'Persons (3)',1872000.00,'Our wonderful tour starts from Kehen Temple. It is an ancient Hindu temple complex boasting unique architectural features. The staircases reaching from the ground to temple courtyard are carved sandstone mythical animal and Balinese folklore figure statues and also the central vestibule. The temple’s walls are also ornate with Chinese porcelain plates, which are a tribute to the historical relations between the local Bali kingdom and China. Afterwards, we continue to Penglipuran, a village that succeeded in preserving its 75-hectare bamboo forest located in the northern part of the village. Members of this village have a strong commitment to the system of \'Ayahan Desa\' - a philosophy committed to respecting the land on which the village stands. To concludes the day, we stop by at Tukad Cepung Waterfall. Well-guarded by the circular cliffs, this waterfall is difficult to locate for the first time visitor. The circular cliffs give you the feeling of being in a cave, while the open sky right from where the waterfall emerges, gives you the most enchanting view. The sunlight falls on the glistering waterfall creating a rainbow, which feels as though it is projected right up to you. If you have never seen water flowing from the sky, then this would be your chance! After spending your time there, we go back to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-07\", \"text\": \"Bali Niksoma Boutique Beach Resort Address : Jl. Padma Utara Jl. Raya Legian, Legian, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Phone : (0361) 751946\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"MEET AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-07\", \"text\": \"Bali Niksoma Boutique Beach Resort Address : Jl. Padma Utara Jl. Raya Legian, Legian, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Phone : (0361) 751946\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5136459,'146','Noelia GAZQUEZ',30508,207382,'Sanur to Padang Bai','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-19','2024-06-19','Rendy','Agus',1,'Persons (1-3)',560000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,'Pick up time : 05.30 AM at Hotel Lobby ( Sudamala Resort Sanur ) Drop off : GIli Gili Fastboat Office Padang Bai ETD 08.30 AM from Padang Bai to Gili Trawangan','{\"date\": \"2024-06-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5136487,'146','Noelia GAZQUEZ',31242,205019,'One-Bedroom Villa with Private Pool','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-06-19','2024-06-22','Rendy','Agus',1,'Twin',9996000.00,'Majo Private Villas is a resort ideally located on the island of Gili Trawangan. We offer high-end luxury accommodation and fine food in our on-site restaurant. Our private villas can accommodate 2 to 3 persons, and offer a fusion between top french design and traditional balinese style. Each of our 9 villas is around 125 sqm, has a private swimming pool, a comfortable outside area, outdoor shower and is designed with a particular attention to detail. We pride ourselves to offer an excellent guest service, and the whole concept of Majo Private villas has been entirely built about offering all of our guests an experience they will never forget, both through the details of the infrastructure and the quality of service. We can organize snorkelling trips, boat trips, massages and much more, please do not hesitate to ask us for any quotation if you require a service not mentioned in this contract.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5136489,'432','Mrs. Mariza Samara Grundmann',30852,202033,'Villa Surya - One Bedroom Private Pool and Tropical Garden','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-07-07','2024-07-11','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',15680000.00,'Our cozy one bed Villa Surya is perfect for a solo traveler or a romantic getaway at 150 sqm private property. The spacious bedroom features a king-size bed with an extra thick mattress with 100% cotton linen, ensuring a blissful sleep. With high-ceilings, large windows, and a pivoting door onto your patio, the space is able to breathe whilst being basked in a beautiful, natural light. The ensuite bathroom, equipped with a bespoke basin area, rainfall shower, quality toiletries and 100% cotton towels leads out to the real star of this villa, the indulgent open-air bathtub. Large enough for two, with views of your private pool and tropical garden, while away hours in pure relaxation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5136501,'251','MORENA CELASCHI',30928,202550,'Deluxe Studio','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-16','2024-06-17','Rendy','Wiwik',2,'Double',3326400.00,'Offering views of the garden, this studio is fitted with air conditioning, a flat-screen TV and a personal safe. Private bathroom has a walk-in shower and is stocked with a hairdryer, slippers and free toiletries.',NULL,'please noted: Mrs. ARIANNA PAGANINI ---> She is a celiac, cannot eat gluten','{\"date\": \"2024-06-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5136505,'251','MORENA CELASCHI',30572,202004,'Deluxe Garden Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-17','2024-06-18','Rendy','Wiwik',2,'Double',4895520.00,'Deluxe Rooms are dressed in warm colors with contemporary Balinese interior and exterior that made up the cozy interior, with size room 30 m2 and the bed type One Double bed or Two Single bed, one crib on request. Complemented with balcony or terrace overlooking garden, located in the two-story building.',NULL,'Please noted: Mrs. ARIANNA PAGANINI ---> She is a celiac, cannot eat gluten','{\"date\": \"2024-06-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5136508,'251','MORENA CELASCHI',30711,200830,'Bisma Suite Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-18','2024-06-19','Rendy','Wiwik',2,'Double',6283200.00,'Spacious one-bedroom suite of 88 sqm with private balcony for a sophisticated Ubud getaway. Interiors feature extensive use of wood and fine Indonesian textiles and art, lending an understated elegance to the space. Featuring a private balcony, this room includes a flat-screen TV and an en-suite bathroom with a bathtub and a shower, and many more.',NULL,'Please noted: Mrs. ARIANNA PAGANINI ---> She is a celiac, cannot eat gluten','{\"date\": \"2024-06-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5136585,'98','Simon Camenzuli',30508,212411,'Ubud to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-22','2024-06-22','Ayu','Ayu',2,'Persons (1-3)',784000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,'Return transfer drop off and pick up The Kayon Resort Ubud to Mason Adventure for Rafting. Meeting point at 09.00 AM at Mason Adventure Centre in Jalan Raya Kedewatan','{\"date\": \"2024-06-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"The Kayon Resort Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"The Kayon Resort Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5136859,'251','MORENA CELASCHI',30508,207262,'Ubud to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-19','2024-06-19','Rendy','Wiwik',1,'Persons (4-6)',784000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,'Pick Up Time: 07.30 AM Flight Detail: ETD: 11.45 by Batik Air ID6331 to Labuan Bajo on 19 June 2024 Pick Up Point: KOMANEKA BISMA Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone: (0361) 971933','{\"date\": \"2024-06-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5136981,'437','Mr. Malcolm Dean Hynds',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-18','2024-08-18','Melysa','Praba',1,'Persons (4)',840000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": \"ETA 11:00AM by SQ936 from Singapore\", \"time\": \"11:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": \"Arkamara Dijiwa Ubud Jl. Katik Lantang Singakerta 80571 Ubud Bali\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5136995,'437','Mr. Malcolm Dean Hynds',30508,202883,'Ubud Electric Bike Tour','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-19','2024-08-19','Melysa','Praba',4,'Persons (4)',2400000.00,'We offer the best way to experience a bike tour Ubud. Electric bike! A mix between riding a motorcycle and a bicycle, the electric bicycle is the best of both worlds. easily while pedaling through the hills, magnificent rice terraces and villages. Our local guides will give you knowledge of Bali more than just landscapes. We will have 2 hours of cycling trip out of the busy center of Ubud through the village of Mambal, where you can see the unique Subak at work and stroll around the rustic and lush surroundings. While you ride your bike you will see beautiful rice fields, dams and waterfalls, we make a stop on the Ayung River, go through the Bali Green School and go through small villages. Our local guides have an intimate knowledge about the entire route. After your bike ride, a healthy lunch is served in a traditional Balinese house.','Afternoon Sesion',NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": \"Arkamara Dijiwa Ubud Jl. Katik Lantang Singakerta 80571 Ubud Bali\", \"time\": \"14:15\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": \"Arkamara Dijiwa Ubud Jl. Katik Lantang Singakerta 80571 Ubud Bali\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5137006,'437','Mr. Malcolm Dean Hynds',30508,202864,'Ubud and Surrounding Tour','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-20','2024-08-20','Melysa','Praba',4,'Persons (4)',2712000.00,'We will be picking you up from your hotel to enjoy the wealth of art in Ubud. First we will visit Monkey Forest; the Ubud Monkey Forest is a nature reserve and temple complex in Ubud, Bali. It houses approximately 340 Crab-eating Macaque (Macacafas cicularis) monkeys. The Monkey Forest contains the Pura Dalem Agung Padangtegal temple as well as a \"Holy Spring\" bathing temple and another temple used for cremation ceremonies. Next we go to Ubud Traditional Art Market where the existence is not far different from other markets available in the tourism area. This market as a society economics center of Ubud and it is apposite to the existence of Ubud Empire that is called Puri Saren. Our last destination is Gua Gajah (Elephant Cave). This cave is built at crevasse edge from the federation of 2 rills that is called Pangkung River, where the irrigation is mixed with Petanu River flow. The word of Gua Gajah is anticipated coming from the word of Lwa Gajah, the name of Buddhist Temple or hermitage for Buddhist monk. There is a relief which is almost looking like the form of mountain on the entrance of this cave. It was carved many designed on the relief like grove with the stick, close leaf, animal for example forest pig, tortoise and specters. The cave mouth is decorated by the bas-relief with the eye turn around to the right or west side. At the end of tour we will transferred back you to the hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-20\", \"text\": \"Arkamara Dijiwa Ubud Jl. Katik Lantang Singakerta 80571 Ubud Bali\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-20\", \"text\": \"Arkamara Dijiwa Ubud Jl. Katik Lantang Singakerta 80571 Ubud Bali\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5137015,'437','Mr. Malcolm Dean Hynds',30508,207262,'Ubud to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-21','2024-08-21','Melysa','Praba',1,'Persons (4)',840000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": \"Arkamara Dijiwa Ubud Jl. Katik Lantang Singakerta 80571 Ubud Bali\", \"time\": \"04:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": \"ETD 08:00 by ID6333 to Labuan Bajo\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5137022,'438','Lucia de Lanzagorta',31015,203232,'3D2N - Bali Ijen Mount Bromo drop Surabaya Package','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-06-30','2024-07-02','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',8880000.00,NULL,NULL,'Hotel in Ijen : Ijen Resort Randu Agung RT.01/RW.01, Krajan, Kluncing, Kec. Licin, Kabupaten Banyuwangi, Jawa Timur 68454 Telepon: 0877-5796-3021 Hotel in Bromo : Jiwa Jawa Bromo Jl. Raya Bromo, Wonotoro, Kec. Sukapura, Kabupaten Probolinggo, Jawa Timur 67254 Telepon: 0822-7202-6000','{\"date\": \"2024-06-30\", \"text\": \"The Kanyon Valley Resort Br. Nagi, Petulu, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 9080770\", \"time\": \"10:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-02\", \"text\": \"ETD : 15.10h by Batik Air ID6401 to Jakarta on 02 July\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Surabaya Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5137045,'438','Lucia de Lanzagorta',30684,200640,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-01','2024-07-02','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',1890000.00,'Designed to embody fresher and younger ambience, our Deluxe Room is a convenient stay for those who plan a relatively shorter stay in Semarang. The room is provided with either a king size or deluxe twin beds.',NULL,'Please send the guarantee letter/voucher following procedure below: - 30 (thirty) days reservation notice prior to the arrival date for Normal Period. - 45 (forty-five) days reservation notice prior to the arrival date for High Season (June 1th to August 31st) and Peak Season (D-3 to D+4 Idul Fitri (April 18 - 25th, 2023 and December 21st, 2023 to January 5th, 2024) period. - Otherwise, the cancellation policy will be applied.','{\"date\": \"2024-07-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5137057,'438','Lucia de Lanzagorta',30682,200893,'Villa\'s Deluxe','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-30','2024-07-01','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',2418000.00,'Villa Deluxe with 42 sqm room area. 23 rooms available (13 double + 10 twin), single and twin beds available with a capacity of 2 people per room. see the greatest view in Ijen Mountain. See the magic of the blue fire at night. Sophisticated design in Ijen Resort and Villas, in Banyuwangi, East Java. You can see the best view from your room, the rice field, mountains.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5137073,'438','Lucia de Lanzagorta',31083,212380,'3D2N LOB Rinca - Padar - Komodo Island Tour (Medium Standard B. - Purisari, etc)','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-07-09','2024-07-11','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2-3)',25764000.00,'TOUR ITINERARY Highlights: Menjarite, Kelor, Kalong, Rinca, Padar, Komodo island, Pink Beach, Taka Makassar, Manta Point, Kanawa, Batu Cermin Mirror Cave DAY 1 : DENPASAR - LABUAN BAJO - MENJARITE - PADAR - KELOR - KALONG ISLAND Arrival at Komodo Airport in Labuan Bajo west Flores, meeting service with our tour guide and transfer to the pier of Labuan Bajo for Rinca Island. It’s about 2 hours sail to the island of Komodo Dragon, stop at Menjarite island for snorkeling then continue to Rinca island-the Island of Komodo dragon, you will find not just e Dragons but also many wild animals like, deer, wild buffalo, long-tailed macaque and wild pig also numerous of birds. Keep your eyes look up as sometime you will find the young Komodo dragons on the trees. A local ranger will lead you through this natural preservation. Late afternoon sailing directly to Kalong Rinca Island to see the hundreds of fling foxes set out from the mangrove tree at 06-07 pm, the lovely sunset from the boat trip really enjoyable here. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Boat Cabin Air Conditioning DAY 2 : KALONG - PADAR - KOMODO - PINK BEACH - MANTA POINT - TAKA MAKASSAR - LABUAN BAJO After having breakfast in your boat, heading to Padar Island, taking trek to Padar Island until having the top view point to get breathtaking scenery of three bays around, Padar Island hike in Komodo has some of the most amazing views in Indonesia, trek to downhill and back to the Boat for sailing directly to Loh Liang – the Ranger station in Komodo Island. By passing through many small islands, After registering start to take basic trekking to see the GIANT RIZARD / KOMODO DRAGON and other wild animals as: Timor deer, wild pig, wild chicken and many variously of tropical bird. Please keep your look at any directions as sometimes you will also find young Komodo dragon hanging over the trees. A local ranger will be led you during the trek. Return to the boat on to Pink beach for snorkeling, swimming and relaxing. It is really spectacular and unspoiled coral reef and many color fish. This is one of best side for snorkeling diving. Sail toward MANTA POINT to exploring Huge Mantas by snorkeling even watching from your boat trip (can’t be guaranteed if weather is not good, like wave and current are strongly) visit also the taka Makaasar its really tiny island with white sand beach really enjoyable to relaxing or beach walking then heading to Labuan bajo for overnight and dinner at above hotel list option. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner DAY 3 : LABUAN BAJO - DENPASAR After breakfast taking your next excursion with visiting local marke and Batu Cermin (Mirror Stone) Cave. The grotto is 75 by 75 meters large, and contains stalactites and stalagmites. Some tunnels are narrow and dark but in others sunlight falls, then process to the airport for flight to Denpasar or to your next destination. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Attention: The itinerary is subject to change due to the weather, tide level and operating conditions without prior notice.',NULL,'3D2N Komodo Padar Tour 1 Night on the Medium Boat 1 Night at Puri Sari Hotel','{\"date\": \"2024-07-09\", \"text\": \"ETA : 08.20 by Citilink QZ644 from Denpasar on 09 July 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Airport Labuan Bajo\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-11\", \"text\": \"ETD : 13.30 by Citilink QG633 to Jakarta on 11 July 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Airport Labuan Bajo\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5137085,'437','Mr. Malcolm Dean Hynds',31708,217261,'Arkamara Suite Jungle','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-18','2024-08-21','Melysa','Praba',2,'Double + Twin',18396000.00,NULL,'1 Double + 1 Twin',NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5138110,'439','BEATRIZ MAYER GONZALEZ',30783,201490,'3D2N Yogyakarta - Drop Semarang / B. Gallery Prawirotaman*4 (Deluxe Room)','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-06-16','2024-06-18','Melysa','Wiwik',2,'Persons (2 / Double)',8280000.00,'D1 : Arrival at Semarang Airport - Borobudur Temple tour incl. Mendut and Pawon - Transfer to Jogja Welcome to the cradle of Indonesian culture, Yogyakarta. A tourist destination for its ancient palaces, temples, batik workshops, gamelan music orchestras, court dances and wayang puppet shows. Upon your arrival in Semarang airport a representative of come2indonesia will be waiting for you with a sign indicating your name to start exploring this special city. We will start by heading towards Borobudur Temple (Candi Borobudur), the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. We will tour around the temple, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano has been producing during its history. After visiting one of the most important Buddhist temples in Southeast Asia, we continue our journey to the Mendut temple and Pawon temple. And then, we will take you to Jogjakarta. D2 : Jogjakarta City Tour visit Sultan Palace, Watercastle and Bird Market - Visit Prambanan Temple You will enjoy a well-deserved breakfast at the hotel and we will start by heading towards Keraton known as the Sultan’s Palace. The palace is a complex building two centuries old, located in the heart of the city. You will hear the song of the “freedom” of the birds in the bird market, we will visit the “Water Castle” that occupies the highest part at the northern end of the vast complex of Taman Sari, Malioboro Street, main street of Yogyakarta, with its merchants, horse carriages, taxi-bikes and markets. After this visit we go to Candi Prambanan, the temple of the Hinduists and classified as a World Heritage Site by Unesco since 1991. The built of this temple was finished around the year 856 to commemorate the victory of the descendant Sanjaya of Siva, Rikai Pikatan on the last sovereign Sailendra of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to the Trimurti, the expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the destroyer. An incredible experience that will make the hours fly by. After this unforgettable day, we will take you back to your hotel. D3 : Transfer to Yogyakarta International Airport You will enjoy a well-deserved breakfast at the hotel and according to the time of your flight, we will pick you up to take you to the airport and take the flight to your next destination. End of our services. Thank you very much for exploring Yogyakarta by the hand of Come2indonesia.',NULL,'\"PLEASE NOTED THEY\'RE HONEYMOONER\" Flight Detail: ETA: 12.10 by Batik Air ID6344 from Jakarta on 16 June 2024 Program: D1. Pick Up Yogyakarta Airport - Prambanan Temple D2. Village Tour Prambanan - Candi Ijo D3. City Tour - Borobudur Temple - Drop Semarang','{\"date\": \"2024-06-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Artotel Gajah Mada Semarang on 18 June 2024\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5138114,'439','BEATRIZ MAYER GONZALEZ',30805,212255,'CGK-YIA','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-16','2024-06-16','Melysa','Wiwik',2,'Person',2860000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5138116,'439','BEATRIZ MAYER GONZALEZ',30672,200737,'Studio 25 (Superior) Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-18','2024-06-19','Melysa','Wiwik',1,'Double',684000.00,'Studio 25 (Superior) room with 25 sqm sized room and with exclusive ARTOTEL bedding collection, some facilities in this room is 43\" inch lcd tv, 24 hours in-room service, high speed internet wi-fi, safety deposit box and hair dryer.',NULL,'\"PLEASE NOTED THEY\'RE HONEYMOONER\" Flight Detail: ETD: 08.30 by Batik Air ID6302 to Pangkalan Bun on 19 June 2024 \"Please consult your departure time transfer upon check in\"','{\"date\": \"2024-06-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5138122,'439','BEATRIZ MAYER GONZALEZ',30672,215075,'Airport Transfer - One Way','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-19','2024-06-19','Melysa','Wiwik',1,'Per Car',180000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5138165,'439','BEATRIZ MAYER GONZALEZ',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-06-19','2024-06-21','Melysa','Wiwik',2,'Persons (2)',10800000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'\"PLEASE NOTED THEY\'RE HONEYMOONER\" Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-06-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"ETA: 09.30 by batik Air ID6302 from Semarang on 19 June 2024\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"ETD: 08.50 by Batik Air ID6134 to Surabaya Connect Denpasar on 21 June 2024\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5138169,'439','BEATRIZ MAYER GONZALEZ',30805,213516,'PKN-DPS','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-21','2024-06-21','Melysa','Wiwik',2,'Person',7040000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5138173,'439','BEATRIZ MAYER GONZALEZ',30571,202567,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-21','2024-06-22','Melysa','Wiwik',1,'Double',1290000.00,'Located at the Second Floor, 35 sqm comfort living with a touch of Balinese style featuring completed fitting, Cable TV, a fancy bathroom comprises rain shower and good quality amenities. Also dedicated Wi-Fi Access to complete your day.',NULL,'\"PLEASE NOTED THEY\'RE HONEYMOONER\" Flight Detail: ETA: 14.35 by lion Air JT922 from Surabaya on 21 June 2024 ETD: 08.00 by Batik Air ID6333 to Labuan Bajo on 22 June 2024 Please consult your departure time transfer upon check in','{\"date\": \"2024-06-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5138175,'439','BEATRIZ MAYER GONZALEZ',30805,202739,'DPS-LBJ','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-22','2024-06-22','Melysa','Wiwik',2,'Person',3520000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5138179,'439','BEATRIZ MAYER GONZALEZ',30805,207346,'LBJ-LOP','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-24','2024-06-24','Melysa','Wiwik',2,'Person',5280000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5138182,'439','BEATRIZ MAYER GONZALEZ',30883,214202,'One Bedroom Pool Villa Room','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-06-24','2024-06-27','Melysa','Wiwik',1,'Double',11880000.00,'For those wanting the ultimate secluded getaway our intimate private pool villas are the ideal choice. Modern with traditional touches the villas are beautifully furnished providing a bright and airy environment. Each villa includes a sizeable pool, decking area and spacious living areas to enjoy, they also have direct access to all other resort facilities. Spend your time enjoying the resort and island before retiring back to your own small piece of paradise.',NULL,'\"Please noted for Honeymoon Complementary\"','{\"date\": \"2024-06-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5138185,'439','BEATRIZ MAYER GONZALEZ',32156,212195,'2D1N Leisure Package','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-06-22','2024-06-23','Melysa','Wiwik',1,'(1-4 Persons) /boat',38400000.00,'Jofiel Komodo Liveaboard reserves the right to change the itinerary and particular services if required due to unforeseen or unavoidable circumstances. Jofiel Komodo Liveaboard will make every effort to offer equivalent alternatives of a comparable standard. Jofiel Komodo Liveaboard will inform the agent or individual client of such changes at the earliest possible date and the effect they will have on price. Day 1: Kelor Island, Menjerite Island, Rinca Kalong Day 2: Padar Island, Pink Beach, Komodo Island, Taka Makassar, Manta Point, Labuan Bajo Specification - Name of vessel : KLM Jofiel - Flag : Indonesia - Type : Phinisi Buginesse Schooner - Year Built : 2017 - Made of : Iron wood - Built in : Labuan Bajo - Length : 20 m - Breadth : 4 m - Depth : 1,9 m - Gross Tonnage : 41 - Cruising Speed : +/- 8 knots - Water capacity : +/- 2.000 liters - Fuel capacity : +/- 1.000 liters - Number of cabins : 3 - Number of bathrooms : 4 - Crew : 6',NULL,'\"PLEASE NOTED THEY\'RE HONEYMOONER\" Flight Detail: ETA: 09.10 by Batik Air ID6333 from Denpasar on 22 June 2024','{\"date\": \"2024-06-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Puri Sari Hotel on 23 June 2024\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5138268,'439','BEATRIZ MAYER GONZALEZ',30701,207546,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-23','2024-06-24','Melysa','Wiwik',1,'Double',900000.00,'Our Superior Room at 38 sqm of room area, equipped with AC, Western toilet and shower with hot & cold water, desk, seating area, and many more. Breakfast is included in the room rate. Featuring a balcony or terrace, guests can enjoy spectacular views of the garden, pool or the sea.',NULL,'Flight Detail: ETD: 09.50 by Batik Air ID6332 to Denpasar Connect Lombok on 24 June 2024 \"Please consult your departure time transfer upon check in\"','{\"date\": \"2024-06-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5138274,'439','BEATRIZ MAYER GONZALEZ',30508,207384,'Padang Bai to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-27','2024-06-27','Melysa','Wiwik',1,'Persons (1-3)',600000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"12:30\", \"locality\": \"Padang Bai Harbour (Office GiliGili Fast Boat)\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Tejaprana Bisma\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5138277,'439','BEATRIZ MAYER GONZALEZ',30623,200589,'Valley Villa','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-06-27','2024-06-30','Melysa','Wiwik',1,'Double',10080000.00,'The Valley Villas are situated on the lowest levels of the hotel, ensuring guests a clear view of the jungle valley below. With a floor area of 100 m², these one-bedroom villas are well-equipped with a king-size bed, air conditioning, a private bathroom featuring a rainfall showerhead, a beautiful view of the jungle valley, and other various amenities for a comfortable stay. Escape to the peaceful seclusion of the villa’s private outdoor sanctuary, where you can find respite in the cozy confines of the gazebo, unwind in the refreshing plunge pool, or immerse yourself in blissful repose within the outdoor natural stone bathtub.',NULL,'\"Please noted for Honeymoon Complementary\"','{\"date\": \"2024-06-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5138282,'439','BEATRIZ MAYER GONZALEZ',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route (Taman Ayun-Jatiluwih-Ulundanu Beratan-Tanah Lot)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-28','2024-06-28','Melysa','Wiwik',2,'Persons (2)',1872000.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"Tejaprana Bisma\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Tejaprana Bisma\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5138285,'439','BEATRIZ MAYER GONZALEZ',30508,207262,'Ubud to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-30','2024-06-30','Melysa','Wiwik',1,'Persons (1-3)',420000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-30\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 6207070\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": \"Tejaprana Bisma\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-30\", \"text\": \"ETD: 12.15 by Citilink QG667 to Jakarta on 30 June 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Airport Ngurah Rai (Domestic)\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5138286,'439','BEATRIZ MAYER GONZALEZ',30805,207114,'DPS-CGK','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-30','2024-06-30','Melysa','Wiwik',2,'Person',4180000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5138384,'440','Mr. Jan Thomas Henrik Casswall',32766,216811,'3D2N Open Trip Komodo - Lamborajo 1 / Sharing Cabin','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-06-21','2024-06-23','Sondang','Tami',1,'Per Person (Min. 2 Person)',5520000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-21\", \"text\": \"Jl. Soekarno Hatta, Kampung tengah, Labuan Bajo\", \"time\": \"09:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Hotel Deja\'vu 2.0 Labuan Bajo, Flores\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-23\", \"text\": \"Jalan Golo No.Silatey, Labuan Bajo, Kec. Komodo, Kabupaten Manggarai Barat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"La Cecile Komodo Hotel and Cafe\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5138418,'441','ANNA KATHERINE LUKEMAN',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-06-21','2024-06-23','Nicholas','Wiwik',2,'Double + Twin',3360000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Flight Detail: ETA: 19.00 by QF 41 from Sydney on 21 June 2024 ETD: 06.00 by Batik Air ID6203 to Pangkalan Bun on 23 June 2024 \"Please noted: There is one vegetarian in our group (no meat or fish) and one who doesn’t eat fish\" Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. - Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK–IN','{\"date\": \"2024-06-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5138424,'440','Mr. Jan Thomas Henrik Casswall',30700,204108,'Deluxe Double Sea View Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-23','2024-06-24','Sondang','Tami',1,'Double',1080000.00,NULL,NULL,'Flight information ETD : 10.20 by Wings Air IW1961 to Maumere on 24 Jun PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK–IN','{\"date\": \"2024-06-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5138432,'441','ANNA KATHERINE LUKEMAN',30805,202689,'CGK-PKN','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-23','2024-06-23','Nicholas','Wiwik',4,'Person',7040000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5138438,'440','Mr. Jan Thomas Henrik Casswall',31083,213614,'5D4N Flores Highlights','Confirmed',NULL,5,'2024-06-24','2024-06-28','Sondang','Tami',1,'Person (1)',18300000.00,'TOUR ITINERARY DAY 1 : DENPASAR - MAUMERE / ENDE - MONI Upon arrival in MAUMERE meet and greet with our Tour Guide and driving directly to Moni. Visit Sikka Village to see the oldest Portuguese church heritage and ikat weaving, also Stop at Paga Beach and Koka beach for relaxing and beach-walking. On arrival at Moni checking in at Kelimutu Ecolodge / Kelimutu Paradiso Resort. Lunch en route, dinner at local restaurant in Moni. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Kelimutu Ecolodge DAY 2 : MONI - KELIMUTU - BAJAWA It’s worth to experience the sun rise at Kelimutu three colored crater lakes, you will begin your day early in the morning (start about 04.00 o’clock). Last update: 15 Jul 2013, typical eruption style: Explosive, Kelimutu volcano eruptions: 1968, 1938, and 1865. Kelimutu (Keli Mutu) volcano in central Flores, Indonesia, is famous for its 3 colorful acid crater lakes, where different salts and oxides in suspension or solution give the lakes varying colors ranging from blue and dark green to intense red. In historic times, few small phreatic explosions have been the only activity at the volcano. The scenic craters with their lakes are popular tourist destinations. Background: The western lake, Tiwu Ata Mbupu (Lake of Old People) is commonly blue. Tiwu Nua Muri Kooh Tai (Lake of Young Men and Maidens) and Tiwu Ata Polo (Bewitched, or Enchanted Lake), which share a common crater wall, are commonly green- and red-coloured, respectively, although lake colours vary periodically. During the dry season reduction processes let Ba, Cu, and As minerals precipitate, in the wet season, the oxidation and precipitation of iron minerals (ferric oxide: Fe2O3) produces intense red colors. Active upwelling occurs at the two eastern lakes and is probably fed by subaqueous fumaroles. Kelimutu volcano is flanked by the older cones of Kelido and Kelibara 3 km to the north and 2 km to the south, respectively (Source: GVP) On the way you will experience the dramatic change in both nature pattern and ethnicity. You could be found yourself in the Lio ethnic’s environment – pay at call to their village Wologai and try to comprehend the locals daily life or just having closer look into their work of architectures. Lunch will be served at a local restaurant in Ende. Continue drive to Bajawa with Stop at Penggajawa Blue stone beach, here you could see local woman collect the stones to sell and building the house of garden. Before checking at hotel, drive to Soa hot spring, then checking at Virgo / Edelways Hotel. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Virgo Hotel or Edelways Hotel DAY 3 : BAJAWA - RUTENG Breakfast at hotel. Explore traditional village of Bajawa tribes. Visit Bena -a megalithic village where people do preserve their ancestral spirits believed and way of life-, which can be seen in their \"Ngadhu\" and \"Bhaga\". Ngadhu and Bhaga are conical thatched roof huts symbolized their Male and Female ancestral spirits. On the way stop on the slope of Inerie active volcano for taking pictures. Lunch will be provided enroute, then continue overland to Ruteng. Stops will be made at Aimere village to see \"arak\" distillation and fresh palm juice tapping and at \"Ranamese\" Lake, and snapshot at magnificent peak of Mt. Inerie -an active volcano-. Continue overland to Ruteng -cool and small town as the capital city of Manggarai Regency- where major Manggarainese tribe dwelt. On arrival direct check into spring hill hotel. Afternoon visit “Liang Bua” the home of Homo Florensies. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Spring Hill or Sindha or Revaya Hotel DAY 4 : RUTENG - LABUAN BAJO Breakfast at hotel. Driving to Labuan Bajo -the Western tip of Flores Island-. On the way stops will be made at Lembor or Cancar area to see the unexposed world wonder “Lingko” –The spider web shape rice fields–. It’s probably the only such a rice field ever exist on earth, then continue to Tengku lese to enjoy the fantastic Water fall, and other places according to local happenings. Lunch will be served at Local restaurant at Labuan bajo, Dinner and overnight at Puri Sari or La Cecile. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Seastra or Golo Hilltop or Puri Sari or La Cecile DAY 5 : LABUAN BAJO - DENPASAR After breakfast, taking short city sight seeing with visiting the Amelia sea view point Then local market before taking you to the airport for flight to Denpasar. Meals : Breakfast Attention: The itinerary is subject to change due to the weather, tide level and operating conditions without prior notice.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-24\", \"text\": \"ETA 11.15 by Wings Air IW1961 from Labuan Bajo on 24 Jun\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Maumere Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-28\", \"text\": \"ETD 17.30 by Air Asia QZ647 to Denpasar on 28 Jun\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Labuan Bajo Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5138440,'441','ANNA KATHERINE LUKEMAN',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-06-23','2024-06-25','Nicholas','Wiwik',4,'Persons (4)',14880000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Flight Detail: ETA: 07.15 by Batik Air ID6202 from Jakarta on 23 June 2024 ETD: 07.30 by Nam Air IN195 to Semarang on 25 June 2024 \"Please noted: There is one vegetarian in our group (no meat or fish) and one who doesn’t eat fish\" Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-06-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5138552,'360','Thomas Ronald Arrowsmith',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-19','2024-06-20','Rendy','Tami',1,'Double',840000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. - Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK–IN','{\"date\": \"2024-06-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5139537,'360','Thomas Ronald Arrowsmith',30508,207272,'Seminyak to Nusa Dua','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-29','2024-06-29','Rendy','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',300000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-29\", \"text\": \"Jl. Kayu Aya, Pantai Seminyak, Kuta, Seminyak, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali\", \"time\": \"12:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"The Seminyak Beach Resort & Spa\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-29\", \"text\": \"Jl. Pratama No.74, Tanjung, Benoa, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Grand Mirage Resort & Thalasso Bali\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5139602,'441','ANNA KATHERINE LUKEMAN',30825,217370,'Jakarta City Tour','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-22','2024-06-22','Nicholas','Wiwik',4,'Persons (2-4)',4320000.00,NULL,NULL,'Pick Up Time: 09.00 AM Pick up/Drop Off: FM& Hotel Jakarta \"Please noted: There is one vegetarian in our group (no meat or fish) and one who doesn’t eat fish\"','{\"date\": \"2024-06-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5139610,'441','ANNA KATHERINE LUKEMAN',30783,217376,'5D4N Yogyakarta Merapi-Bromo By Train / C. Adhisthana (Superior) & Bromo Terrace (Deluxe)','Confirmed',NULL,5,'2024-06-25','2024-06-29','Nicholas','Wiwik',4,'Persons (4)',34920000.00,'D1. Pick Up Semarang - Yogyakarta D2. Borobudur - Village tour with Batik - Merapi D3. Jogja City Tour - Prambanan D4. Jogja - Bromo by Train D5. Bromo Tour - Surabaya Airport',NULL,'Pick Up Semarang Airport: ETA: 08.40 by Nam Air IN195 from Pangkalan Bun on 25 June 2024 Flight at Surabaya Airport: ETD: 15.05 by Lion Air JT910 to Denpasar on 29 June 2024 \"Please noted: There is one vegetarian in our group (no meat or fish) and one who doesn’t eat fish\"','{\"date\": \"2024-06-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5139614,'441','ANNA KATHERINE LUKEMAN',30805,202685,'SUB-DPS','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-29','2024-06-29','Nicholas','Wiwik',4,'Person',4400000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5139615,'441','ANNA KATHERINE LUKEMAN',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-29','2024-06-29','Nicholas','Wiwik',1,'Persons (4-6)',840000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,'Flight Detail: ETA: 17.05 by Lion Air JT910 from Surabaya on 29 June 2024 Drop Off: Adiwana Svarga Loka Jalan Raya Penestanan Kelod, Sayan, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone: (0361) 979279','{\"date\": \"2024-06-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5139618,'441','ANNA KATHERINE LUKEMAN',30544,201961,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,7,'2024-06-29','2024-07-06','Nicholas','Wiwik',2,'Double',21840000.00,'Located at the top of the resort and ideal for single travelers or shorter stays, these 38m2 private deluxe rooms provide the perfect environment to relax in the tranquility of our peaceful surroundings. Each with an outdoor seating area, our deluxe rooms are situated on both the ground floors and first floors (with balcony).',NULL,'\"Please noted: There is one vegetarian in our group (no meat or fish) and one who doesn’t eat fish\"','{\"date\": \"2024-06-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5139642,'441','ANNA KATHERINE LUKEMAN',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route (Taman Ayun-Jatiluwih-Ulundanu Beratan-Tanah Lot)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-30','2024-06-30','Nicholas','Wiwik',4,'Persons (4)',2832000.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"Adiwana Svarga Loka\", \"location\": \"Jalan Raya Penestanan Kelod, Sayan, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Adiwana Svarga Loka\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5139644,'441','ANNA KATHERINE LUKEMAN',30508,202895,'Tenganan Village - Virgin Beach - Lempuyang Temple','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-01','2024-07-01','Nicholas','Wiwik',4,'Persons (4)',3000000.00,'In this part of the trip, we set off along the East Coast of the island. The first site visit will be the Kusamba Village, a fishing village where colorful Prahu in the black sand beaches. We will announce the salt making process by traditional method. We continue our journey on the east coast to reach Goa Lawah, Gua Lawah or Bat Cave is one of favorite places of interest in Bali and it is located near of hilly bank so it is called reef of Middle hill. We continue our trip to Tenganan Village, Tenganan Village is one of the oldest Balinese Traditional located in Karangasem Regency, east part of Bali. This village is much referred by cultural literature science of Tenganan Pegringsingan, which is very famous in the island. It owns very unique local community life pattern which is one example of Bali Aga Village cultures (Hindu Prehistoric) and different with other countryside in plain of Bali. From here, we go to Amlapura to visit the Royal Palace, The town of Amlapura is the capital of Karangasem (\'East Bali\'). The palace of the former kings of the region is located here, and their descendants have opened parts of the complex to the public. We will finish our trip with visit heaven of Tirta Gangga, Tirta Gangga is a beautiful park with the huge water fountain. At the end of tour we will transfer you back to the hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"ADIWANA SVARGA LOKA\", \"location\": \"Jalan Raya Penestanan Kelod, Sayan, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"ADIWANA SVARGA LOKA\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5139649,'441','ANNA KATHERINE LUKEMAN',30508,207262,'Ubud to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-06','2024-07-06','Nicholas','Wiwik',1,'Persons (4-6)',840000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,'Flight Detail: ETD: 07.10 by Air Asia QZ644 to Labuan Bajo on 06 july 2024','{\"date\": \"2024-07-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"04:30\", \"locality\": \"Adiwana Svarga Loka Jalan Raya Penestanan Kelod, Sayan, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone: (0361) 979279\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5139651,'441','ANNA KATHERINE LUKEMAN',30805,202739,'DPS-LBJ','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-06','2024-07-06','Nicholas','Wiwik',4,'Person',7040000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5139661,'441','ANNA KATHERINE LUKEMAN',31083,212380,'3D2N LOB Rinca - Padar - Komodo Island Tour (Medium Standard B. - Purisari)','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-07-06','2024-07-08','Nicholas','Wiwik',4,'Persons (4-5)',41688000.00,'TOUR ITINERARY Highlights: Menjarite, Kelor, Kalong, Rinca, Padar, Komodo island, Pink Beach, Taka Makassar, Manta Point, Kanawa, Batu Cermin Mirror Cave DAY 1 : DENPASAR - LABUAN BAJO - MENJARITE - PADAR - KELOR - KALONG ISLAND Arrival at Komodo Airport in Labuan Bajo west Flores, meeting service with our tour guide and transfer to the pier of Labuan Bajo for Rinca Island. It’s about 2 hours sail to the island of Komodo Dragon, stop at Menjarite island for snorkeling then continue to Rinca island-the Island of Komodo dragon, you will find not just e Dragons but also many wild animals like, deer, wild buffalo, long-tailed macaque and wild pig also numerous of birds. Keep your eyes look up as sometime you will find the young Komodo dragons on the trees. A local ranger will lead you through this natural preservation. Late afternoon sailing directly to Kalong Rinca Island to see the hundreds of fling foxes set out from the mangrove tree at 06-07 pm, the lovely sunset from the boat trip really enjoyable here. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Boat Cabin Air Conditioning DAY 2 : KALONG - PADAR - KOMODO - PINK BEACH - MANTA POINT - TAKA MAKASSAR - LABUAN BAJO After having breakfast in your boat, heading to Padar Island, taking trek to Padar Island until having the top view point to get breathtaking scenery of three bays around, Padar Island hike in Komodo has some of the most amazing views in Indonesia, trek to downhill and back to the Boat for sailing directly to Loh Liang – the Ranger station in Komodo Island. By passing through many small islands, After registering start to take basic trekking to see the GIANT RIZARD / KOMODO DRAGON and other wild animals as: Timor deer, wild pig, wild chicken and many variously of tropical bird. Please keep your look at any directions as sometimes you will also find young Komodo dragon hanging over the trees. A local ranger will be led you during the trek. Return to the boat on to Pink beach for snorkeling, swimming and relaxing. It is really spectacular and unspoiled coral reef and many color fish. This is one of best side for snorkeling diving. Sail toward MANTA POINT to exploring Huge Mantas by snorkeling even watching from your boat trip (can’t be guaranteed if weather is not good, like wave and current are strongly) visit also the taka Makaasar its really tiny island with white sand beach really enjoyable to relaxing or beach walking then heading to Labuan bajo for overnight and dinner at above hotel list option. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner DAY 3 : LABUAN BAJO - DENPASAR After breakfast taking your next excursion with visiting local marke and Batu Cermin (Mirror Stone) Cave. The grotto is 75 by 75 meters large, and contains stalactites and stalagmites. Some tunnels are narrow and dark but in others sunlight falls, then process to the airport for flight to Denpasar or to your next destination. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Attention: The itinerary is subject to change due to the weather, tide level and operating conditions without prior notice.',NULL,'Flight Detail: ETA: 08.20 by Air Asia QZ644 from Denpasar on 06 July 2024 ETD: 13.35 by Batik Air ID6330 to Denpasar on 08 July 2024 \"Please noted: There is one vegetarian in our group (no meat or fish) and one who doesn’t eat fish\"','{\"date\": \"2024-07-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5139663,'441','ANNA KATHERINE LUKEMAN',30805,202740,'LBJ-DPS','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-08','2024-07-08','Nicholas','Wiwik',4,'Person',7040000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5139668,'441','ANNA KATHERINE LUKEMAN',30598,201358,'Deluxe Pool Room','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-07-08','2024-07-11','Nicholas','Wiwik',2,'Double + Twin',8841600.00,'The 7 Deluxe Pool Rooms are all on the ground floor. Each is 40sqm and offers direct private access to the 30m blue-tiled IZE Pool, which is reserved for the use of Deluxe Pool Room guests only. Into this pool falls a graceful stainless steel water cascade. These Deluxe Pool Rooms are perfect if you need to totally chill out during your stay, luxuriating in the cool pool and relaxing in your own in-room Jacuzzi. They also carry a few other little extras such as DVD player and Bluetooth speaker.',NULL,'\"Please noted: There is one vegetarian in our group (no meat or fish) and one who doesn’t eat fish\"','{\"date\": \"2024-07-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5139679,'441','ANNA KATHERINE LUKEMAN',30508,207270,'Seminyak to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-11','2024-07-11','Nicholas','Wiwik',1,'Persons (4-6)',720000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,'Flight Detail: ETD: 22.10 by ID 6015 to Canberra on 11 July 2024','{\"date\": \"2024-07-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"18:00\", \"locality\": \"IZE Seminyak\", \"location\": \"Jl. Kayu Aya No.68, Seminyak, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Telepon: (0361) 8466999\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5139736,'446','Mrs. Marta Benito Romera',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-26','2024-06-27','Jacob','Tami',1,'Double',840000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. - Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK–IN','{\"date\": \"2024-06-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5139753,'446','Mrs. Marta Benito Romera',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-06-27','2024-06-29','Jacob','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',10800000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-06-27\", \"text\": \"ETA 07.15 by Batik Air ID6202 from Jakarta on 27 Jun\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pangkalan Bun Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-29\", \"text\": \"ETD 10.25 by Batik Air ID6303 to Semarang on 29 Jun\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5139767,'446','Mrs. Marta Benito Romera',30783,217376,'5D4N Yogyakarta Bromo By Train / C. Adhisthana (Superior) & Bromo Terrace (Deluxe)','Confirmed',NULL,5,'2024-06-29','2024-07-03','Jacob','Tami',2,'Persons (2-3 / Double)',20760000.00,'D1. Pick Up Semarang - Yogyakarta D2. Borobudur - Village tour with Batik - Merapi D3. Jogja City Tour - Prambanan D4. Jogja - Bromo by Train D5. Bromo Tour - Surabaya Airport',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-29\", \"text\": \"ETA 11.25 by Batik Air ID6303 from Pangkalan Bun on 29 Jun\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Jenderal Ahmad Yani International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-03\", \"text\": \"Visesa Ubud, Bentuyung Sakti, Jl. Suweta, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Desa Visesa Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5139778,'441','ANNA KATHERINE LUKEMAN',30508,212288,'Airport to Seminyak','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-08','2024-07-08','Nicholas','Wiwik',1,'Persons (4-6)',720000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,'Flight Detail: ETA: 14.55 by Batik Air ID6330 from Labuan Bajo on 08 July 2024','{\"date\": \"2024-07-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"IZE Seminyak\", \"location\": \"Jl. Kayu Aya No.68, Seminyak, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Telepon: (0361) 8466999\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5139853,'446','Mrs. Marta Benito Romera',30985,212180,'River Valley Suite with Private Jacuzzi','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-07-03','2024-07-07','Jacob','Tami',1,'Double',16080000.00,'From its elevated vantage point, our River Valley Suite provides unspoiled lush tropical greenery. This room category simply lends itself to relaxation with well-designed areas to sleep, unwind and soak in hot water in an outdoor style. The highlight of this room category is the private outdoor Jacuzzi overlooking the serene river valley. River Valley Suite is the perfect place to have a unique opportunity to immerse yourself in nature while still enjoying all the comforts of modern living.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5139866,'446','Mrs. Marta Benito Romera',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-05','2024-07-05','Jacob','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',1872000.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-05\", \"text\": \"Visesa Ubud, Bentuyung Sakti, Jl. Suweta, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Visesa Ubud Resort\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5139870,'446','Mrs. Marta Benito Romera',30508,202894,'Kehen Temple - Pengelipuran - Tukad Cepung Waterfall','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-06','2024-07-06','Jacob','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',1680000.00,'Our wonderful tour starts from Kehen Temple. It is an ancient Hindu temple complex boasting unique architectural features. The staircases reaching from the ground to temple courtyard are carved sandstone mythical animal and Balinese folklore figure statues and also the central vestibule. The temple’s walls are also ornate with Chinese porcelain plates, which are a tribute to the historical relations between the local Bali kingdom and China. Afterwards, we continue to Penglipuran, a village that succeeded in preserving its 75-hectare bamboo forest located in the northern part of the village. Members of this village have a strong commitment to the system of \'Ayahan Desa\' - a philosophy committed to respecting the land on which the village stands. To concludes the day, we stop by at Tukad Cepung Waterfall. Well-guarded by the circular cliffs, this waterfall is difficult to locate for the first time visitor. The circular cliffs give you the feeling of being in a cave, while the open sky right from where the waterfall emerges, gives you the most enchanting view. The sunlight falls on the glistering waterfall creating a rainbow, which feels as though it is projected right up to you. If you have never seen water flowing from the sky, then this would be your chance! After spending your time there, we go back to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-06\", \"text\": \"Visesa Ubud, Bentuyung Sakti, Jl. Suweta, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Visesa Ubud Resort\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5140582,'446','Mrs. Marta Benito Romera',30508,207379,'Ubud to Padang Bai','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-07','2024-07-07','Jacob','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',600000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-07\", \"text\": \"Visesa Ubud, Bentuyung Sakti, Jl. Suweta, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali\", \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Visesa Ubud Resort\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-07\", \"text\": \"ETD 08.30 to Gili Air by Gili Gili Fast Boat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Padang Bai Harbour\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5140588,'446','Mrs. Marta Benito Romera',30649,204187,'One Bedroom Pool Lagoon','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-07-07','2024-07-10','Jacob','Tami',1,'Double',4500000.00,'This room is perfect for travelers or business people! With a room area of ​​25m2 and equipped with a double / single bed, air conditioning controller, LED TV and high speed internet access. This modern designed bathroom is also equipped with a shower and toiletries to complete your needs during your stay at our hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5140598,'446','Mrs. Marta Benito Romera',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-10','2024-07-11','Jacob','Tami',1,'Double',840000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. - Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK–IN','{\"date\": \"2024-07-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5140684,'301','Dive Worldwide Group',31119,214055,'Queen Suite Room','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-06-11','2024-06-14','Rendy','Tami',1,'Double',6972000.00,'Our Queen Suites are tastefully decorated. Within you will find a large bed draped with a mosquito net, a living area for kicking back, a private balcony perfect for taking in the beauty of the rainforest, and a bathroom fitted with a refreshing shower. The suites are 20 square meters and feature a queen bed, air conditioning, and room amenities.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5140898,'447','SANDRA LLANO PAJARES',30783,201477,'2D1N Semarang - Yogyakarta / A. The Phoenix (Deluxe Legacy Room)','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-06-17','2024-06-18','Jacob','Praba',1,'Persons (2 / Double)',3750000.00,'D1 : Arrival Semarang airport - Borobudur Temple tour incl. Mendut and Pawon - overnight in Yogyakarta Welcome to the cradle of Indonesian culture, Yogyakarta. A tourist destination for its ancient palaces, temples, batik workshops, gamelan music orchestras, court dances and wayang puppet shows. Upon your arrival in Semarang airport a representative of come2indonesia will be waiting for you with a sign indicating your name to start exploring this special city. We will start by heading towards Borobudur Temple (Candi Borobudur), the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. We will tour around the temple, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano has been producing during its history. After visiting one of the most important Buddhist temples in Southeast Asia, we continue our journey to the Mendut temple and Pawon temple. And then, we will take you to your Jogjakarta D2 : Morning visit Prambanan Temple - City Tour Yogyakarta visit Sultan Palace, Watercastle and Bird Market - Transfer to Yogyakarta International Airport You will enjoy a well-deserved breakfast at the hotel and we will start by heading towards Candi Prambanan, the temple of the Hinduists and classified as a World Heritage Site by Unesco since 1991. The built of this temple was finished around the year 856 to commemorate the victory of the descendant Sanjaya of Siva, Rikai Pikatan on the last sovereign Sailendra of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to the Trimurti, the expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the destroyer. After this visit we go to the Keraton known as the Sultan’s Palace. The palace is a complex building two centuries old, located in the heart of the city. You will hear the song of the “freedom” of the birds in the bird market, we will visit the “Water Castle” that occupies the highest part at the northern end of the vast complex of Taman Sari, Malioboro Street, main street of Yogyakarta, with its merchants, horse carriages, taxi-bikes and markets. An incredible experience that will make the hours fly by. According to the time of your flight, we will pick you up to take you to the airport and take the flight to your next destination. End of our services. Thank you very much for exploring Yogyakarta by the hand of Come2indonesia.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-17\", \"text\": \"ETA 14:30PM BY ID6360 FROM JAKARTA\", \"time\": \"14:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"YOGYAKARTA INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-18\", \"text\": \"ARTOTEL GAJAHMADA SEMARANG Jl. Gajahmada No.101, Miroto, Kec. Semarang Tengah, Kota Semarang, Jawa Tengah\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"SEMARANG\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5141010,'447','SANDRA LLANO PAJARES',30672,200747,'Studio 30 (Deluxe) Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-18','2024-06-19','Jacob','Praba',1,'Double',804000.00,'Studio 30 (Deluxe) room with 25 sqm sized room, and exclusive ARTOTEL bedding collection, with facilities 43\" inch lcd tv, 24 hours in-room service, high speed internet wi-fi, safety deposit box, hair dryer.',NULL,'- Airport Transfer on 19 June 2024, ETD 08:30 by ID6302 to Pangkalan Bun','{\"date\": \"2024-06-19\", \"text\": \"ARTOTEL GAJAH MADA SEMARANG Jl. Gajahmada No.101, Miroto, Kec. Semarang Tengah, Kota Semarang, Jawa Tengah\", \"time\": \"05:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"SEMARANG\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-19\", \"text\": \"ETD 08:30 by ID6302 to Pangkalan Bun\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"BANDAR UDARA JENDRAL AHMAD YANI\"}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5141036,'447','SANDRA LLANO PAJARES',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-06-19','2024-06-21','Jacob','Praba',2,'Persons (2)',10800000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-06-19\", \"text\": \"ETA 09:30AM BY ID6302 FROM SEMARANG\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"BANDAR UDARA ISKANDAR PANGKALAN BUN\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-21\", \"text\": \"ETD 08:50AM BY ID6134 TO SURABAYA\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"BANDAR UDARA ISKANDAR PANGKALAN BUN\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5141041,'447','SANDRA LLANO PAJARES',31015,203230,'2D1N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Tour','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-06-21','2024-06-22','Jacob','Praba',2,'Persons (2)',4800000.00,'2D1N Surabaya - Tumpak Sewu - Bromo - Sunrise Point at Seruni - Surabaya',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-21\", \"text\": \"ETA 10:00 BY ID6134 FROM PANGKALAN BUN\", \"time\": \"10:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"JUANDA INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-22\", \"text\": \"ETD 16:55 BY JT920 TO DENPASAR\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"JUANDA INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5141043,'447','SANDRA LLANO PAJARES',30684,200640,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-21','2024-06-22','Jacob','Praba',1,'Double',1890000.00,'Designed to embody fresher and younger ambience, our Deluxe Room is a convenient stay for those who plan a relatively shorter stay in Semarang. The room is provided with either a king size or deluxe twin beds.',NULL,'Please send the guarantee letter/voucher following procedure below: - 30 (thirty) days reservation notice prior to the arrival date for Normal Period. - 45 (forty-five) days reservation notice prior to the arrival date for High Season (June 1th to August 31st) and Peak Season (D-3 to D+4 Idul Fitri (April 18 - 25th, 2023 and December 21st, 2023 to January 5th, 2024) period. - Otherwise, the cancellation policy will be applied.','{\"date\": \"2024-06-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5141772,'448','Mr. Demetrio Costantino',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-03','2024-07-03','Guio','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',392000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-03\", \"text\": \"ETA 22.40 by Qatar Airways QR960 from Doha on 03 Jul\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-03\", \"text\": \"Jl. Hanoman, Ubud, Kec. Gianyar, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Alaya Resort Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5141788,'448','Mr. Demetrio Costantino',30611,201418,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,5,'2024-07-03','2024-07-08','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',13440000.00,'The Deluxe Room provides a restful environment to unwind after a busy day spent exploring the sights of Ubud. It is a cozy base featuring clean-line furnishings, a smart en-suite bathroom and a decorative wall that showcases Bali’s creative legacy. A private terrace or balcony blends seamlessly into the outdoors providing extra space to sit and relax.',NULL,'HONEYMOONERS','{\"date\": \"2024-07-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5141798,'447','SANDRA LLANO PAJARES',30696,202104,'Kelimutu Deluxe Suite','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-27','2024-06-28','Jacob','Praba',1,'Double',3540000.00,'Opening the aura of relaxation while connecting with the beauty of nature. Restoring a sense of longing for a soul-soothing green landscape is the main reason this suite was built. A rustic themed room with a minimalist touch. Aura of relaxation is felt once you first open the two-panel wooden door wide enough to let that tropical wind roll into the room. Directly facing the opposite of the wide balcony, the green landscape is ready to calm your soul. Our Kelimutu Deluxe Suite has 32 units, 16 lower level suites (44 sqm), overlooking to the garden from private terrace and 16 upper level suite (40 sqm) with private balcony and tropical garden view. This suite is equipped with luxurious king-sized and twin bed, efficient and sustainable air-conditioning, 43\" smart TV, complimentary wireless internet, safe deposit box, water heater, private bathroom with bathroom amenities, hairdryer, bathrobe, daily turndown service, and many more.',NULL,'1X AIRPORT TRANSFER ON 27 JUNE 2024 ETA 09:1