oom','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-07-14','2024-07-18','Jacob','Komang',1,'Double',4286400.00,'There’s so much to do in Seminyak, and further afield across the great island of Bali, but you need that cool haven to come back to after shopping, sightseeing or enjoying Seminyak’s legendary nightlife – that’s what an IZE Seminyak Deluxe Room provides. Enjoy calming Scandinavian-inspired decor, rainforest shower, flat-screen TV, sofa/day-bed, small balcony and more. Kick back, unwind and recharge for your next Seminyak adventure.',NULL,'\"No need spicy food\"','{\"date\": \"2024-07-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5149851,'473','Alessia Atzori & Charlon Tabone',30508,207270,'Seminyak to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-25','2024-09-25','Ayu','Eddy',1,'Persons (1-3)',280000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-25\", \"text\": \"Hotel Indigo Bali Seminyak Beach Address : Jl. Camplung Tanduk No.10, Seminyak, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Phone : (0361) 2099999\", \"time\": \"05:00\", \"locality\": \"MEET AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-25\", \"text\": \"ETD 09.00 by Air Asia QZ504 to Singapore on 25 September 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5149866,'475','BLANCA LLES BARUQUER',30508,207270,'Seminyak to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-18','2024-07-18','Jacob','Komang',1,'Persons (1-3)',300000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,'Please ready at hotel lobby for transfer at 08.00','{\"date\": \"2024-07-18\", \"text\": \"Ize Seminyak Hotel, Jalan Kayu Aya No. 68, Seminyak - Bali - Indonesia T: +62361 8466 999\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Seminyak\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-18\", \"text\": \"ETD : 11.45 by Batik AIr ID6331 to Labuan Bajo on 18 July 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5149870,'475','BLANCA LLES BARUQUER',31658,208111,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-18','2024-07-19','Jacob','Komang',1,'Double',840000.00,'This room featured Air Conditioning, telephone, hot and cold water, satellite TV on 32 LCD screen. Bathroom amenities; Hair dryer, Bathrobe, Towels, Free toiletries, Guest toilet, Cleaning products, Body soap, Hair conditioner, Shampoo, Tooth brush, Toilet paper. Facilities inside the room are coffee/tea maker, mini bar, wake up service.',NULL,'\"No need spicy food\"','{\"date\": \"2024-07-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5149873,'473','Alessia Atzori & Charlon Tabone',30527,200579,'Valley View Villa','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-09-15','2024-09-19','Ayu','Eddy',1,'Double',11648000.00,'The Valley View Villas are located on the lowest level of the hotel grounds. This ensures guests have a clear view of the jungle valley below and complete privacy. The bedroom features a King-sized bed, and the 70 m2 floor area gives guests lots of space inside, in addition to the beautiful outdoor area. Lounge on a chair on the personal terrace with gazebo, take a plunge in the infinity pool, or let the daily worries of life drift away in the outdoor natural stone bathtub. Air conditioning and a private bathroom with bathtub, along with many other amenities, add to the comfort level of these villas.',NULL,'HONEYMOON','{\"date\": \"2024-09-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5149876,'475','BLANCA LLES BARUQUER',32766,216810,'3D2N Open Trip Komodo - Lady Grace / Deluxe Cabin','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-07-19','2024-07-21','Jacob','Komang',2,'Per Person (Min. 2 Person)',12840000.00,NULL,NULL,'pickup time between : 09.00 - 09.30','{\"date\": \"2024-07-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5150160,'476','Mr. Alberto Trujillo Cuesta',30805,202689,'CGK-PKN','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-08','2024-08-08','Melysa','Febrina',3,'Person',5280000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5150165,'476','Mr. Alberto Trujillo Cuesta',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-08-08','2024-08-10','Melysa','Febrina',3,'Persons (3)',12600000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'3D2N Borneo Orangutan Tour based on Private Standard Klotok, with Spanish speaking guide Flight details: ETA 07:15 by Batik Air ID6202 from Jakarta on 08 Aug ETD 07:30 by Nam Air IN195 to Semarang on 10 Aug Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5150168,'476','Mr. Alberto Trujillo Cuesta',30805,212246,'PKN-SRG','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-10','2024-08-10','Melysa','Febrina',3,'Person',8580000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5150176,'476','Mr. Alberto Trujillo Cuesta',30783,216543,'4D3N Semarang-Jogja-Bromo-Surabaya Incl. Train / B. Gallery Prawirotaman (Deluxe Room) & Lereng Brom','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-08-10','2024-08-13','Melysa','Febrina',3,'Persons (3 / Triple-extra bed)',26910000.00,'D1 : Arrival Yogyakarta International Airport – Visit Prambanan Temple – Transfer to hotel D2 : Borobudur temple incl. Mendut and Pawon ,Yogyakarta City Tour Visit Sultan Palace, Watercastle and Bird/Traditional Market D3 : Jogja – Mojokerto by Train then continue drive to Bromo – overnight in Bromo D4 : Sunrise and Mt. Bromo crater tour incl. Jeep ( Horse rise Exclude ) – Transfer to Surabaya airport',NULL,'4D3N Semarang - Yogyakarta - Bromo Tour - Drop off in Surabaya, with English speaking guide D1/10 Aug 2024: Arrival in Semarang - Prambanan Temple D2/11 Aug 2024: Kraton - Taman Sari - Candirejo Village Tour - Borobudur Temple (B) D3/12 Aug 2024: Yogyakarta - Bromo by train (B) D4/13 Aug 2024: Bromo Tour - Transfer to Surabaya Airport (B) Flight details: ETA in Semarang at 08:40 by Nam Air IN195 from Pangkalan Bun on 10 Aug ETD from Surabaya at 15:25 by Lion Air JT920 to Denpasar on 13 Aug','{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5150186,'476','Mr. Alberto Trujillo Cuesta',30805,202685,'SUB-DPS','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-13','2024-08-13','Melysa','Febrina',3,'Person',3300000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5150197,'476','Mr. Alberto Trujillo Cuesta',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-13','2024-08-13','Melysa','Febrina',1,'Persons (1-3)',420000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": \"ETA 17:25 by Lion Air JT920 from Surabaya on 13 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Denpasar Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": \"Jl. Raya Pengosekan, Ubud, Gianyar, Bali Phone: +62361 972385 / +62812-3900-9373\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"The Artini Dijiwa Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5150202,'476','Mr. Alberto Trujillo Cuesta',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-14','2024-08-14','Melysa','Febrina',3,'Persons (3)',2160000.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,'FD Tour Taman Ayun - Jatiluwih - Ulun Danu Beratan Temple - Tanah Lot, with Spanish speaking guide','{\"date\": \"2024-08-14\", \"text\": \"Jl. Raya Pengosekan, Ubud, Gianyar, Bali Phone: +62361 972385 / +62812-3900-9373\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"The Artini Dijiwa Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-14\", \"text\": \"Jl. Raya Pengosekan, Ubud, Gianyar, Bali Phone: +62361 972385 / +62812-3900-9373\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"The Artini Dijiwa Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5150213,'476','Mr. Alberto Trujillo Cuesta',30508,213032,'Ubud to Kusamba','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-17','2024-08-17','Melysa','Febrina',1,'Persons (1-3)',420000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,'Boat details: ETD 08:00 by The Angkal Fast Boat','{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": \"Jl. Raya Pengosekan, Ubud, Gianyar, Bali Phone: +62361 972385 / +62812-3900-9373\", \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"The Artini Dijiwa Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Kusamba Harbor\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5150232,'476','Mr. Alberto Trujillo Cuesta',30508,207112,'1D Nusa Penida West Tour','Confirmed','C2I-BALI19',1,'2024-08-17','2024-08-17','Melysa','Febrina',3,'Persons (3)',1080000.00,'Today, embark on a unique adventure as you explore the enchanting Nusa Penida, a neighboring island of Bali. Your day begins with a convenient hotel pick-up, followed by a journey to the Sanur port where a fast boat awaits to transport you to Nusa Penida in just 30 minutes. Nusa Penida, located in the southeast of Bali, is a true paradise waiting to be discovered. Upon your arrival, a friendly driver will be ready to guide you through the day\'s captivating itinerary. Your first destination is the mesmerizing Angel\'s Billabong, a natural wonder resembling a pristine pool nestled in the heart of nature. Take a refreshing swim, but exercise caution on the steps and heed your driver\'s recommendations. Next, we head to Broken Beach, a charming bay that was once a cave, now open to the sky, offering a unique and captivating scenery. Although inaccessible by land, the view from above is nothing short of breathtaking. Keep an eye out for the possibility of spotting giant manta rays gracefully gliding on the water\'s surface. Our journey continues to the renowned Kelingking Beach, famous for its stunning cliffs and the iconic hand-shaped mountain. This beach is not only one of the island\'s most famous attractions but also a favorite subject for photographers. We conclude the day at the pristine Crystal Beach, where white sands meet turquoise waters in perfect harmony. As the sun sets, you\'ll have the opportunity to relax and savor the beauty that surrounds you. This unforgettable experience concludes with a return boat trip to Bali from the Toya Pakeh port at 16:30, followed by a comfortable transfer to your hotel.',NULL,'1 Day Nusa Penida West Tour Visit: Angel\'s Billabong - Broken Beach - Kelingking Beach - Crystal Beach with English speaking driver (No guide)','{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": \"Boat details ETA 08:30 from Kusamba by The Angkal Fast Boat\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sampalan Harbor\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": \"Jl. Batu Nunggal-Suana, Suana, Nusa Penida, Klungkung, Bali Phone: +62851 57708617 / +62822 10130068\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"The Angkal Resort Nusa Penida\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5150237,'477','ENRIQUE MARTINEZ ESTEBARANZ',30680,200914,'Deluxe Room + Extra Bed','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-25','2024-06-26','Melysa','Wiwik',1,'Double',1380000.00,'Enjoy our spacious elegant deluxe room with 40 m2 of room size. Enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, hot and cold shower, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Flight Detail: ETA: 21.35 by QR954 from Doha ETD: 06.00 by ID6202 to Pangkalan Bun Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. - Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK–IN','{\"date\": \"2024-06-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5150243,'478','Mrs. Victhoritha Pinontoan',30508,212305,'Kuta to Sanur','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-08','2024-06-08','Rendy','Tami',5,'Persons (4-6)',3600000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-08\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bypass Ngurah Rai No.1, Kuta, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361\", \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Harris Hotel Kuta Galeria\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-08\", \"text\": \"ETD 07.30 to Nusa Penida by Maruti Fast Boat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sanur Harbour\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5150246,'477','ENRIQUE MARTINEZ ESTEBARANZ',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-06-26','2024-06-28','Melysa','Wiwik',3,'Persons (3)',12600000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Flight detail: ETA: 07.15 by Batik Air ID6202 from Jakarta ETD: 10.25 by Batik Air ID6303 to Semarang Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-06-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5150249,'478','Mrs. Victhoritha Pinontoan',30508,207112,'1D Nusa Penida West Tour','Confirmed','C2I-BALI19',1,'2024-06-08','2024-06-08','Rendy','Tami',5,'Persons (5-6)',1800000.00,'Today, embark on a unique adventure as you explore the enchanting Nusa Penida, a neighboring island of Bali. Your day begins with a convenient hotel pick-up, followed by a journey to the Sanur port where a fast boat awaits to transport you to Nusa Penida in just 30 minutes. Nusa Penida, located in the southeast of Bali, is a true paradise waiting to be discovered. Upon your arrival, a friendly driver will be ready to guide you through the day\'s captivating itinerary. Your first destination is the mesmerizing Angel\'s Billabong, a natural wonder resembling a pristine pool nestled in the heart of nature. Take a refreshing swim, but exercise caution on the steps and heed your driver\'s recommendations. Next, we head to Broken Beach, a charming bay that was once a cave, now open to the sky, offering a unique and captivating scenery. Although inaccessible by land, the view from above is nothing short of breathtaking. Keep an eye out for the possibility of spotting giant manta rays gracefully gliding on the water\'s surface. Our journey continues to the renowned Kelingking Beach, famous for its stunning cliffs and the iconic hand-shaped mountain. This beach is not only one of the island\'s most famous attractions but also a favorite subject for photographers. We conclude the day at the pristine Crystal Beach, where white sands meet turquoise waters in perfect harmony. As the sun sets, you\'ll have the opportunity to relax and savor the beauty that surrounds you. This unforgettable experience concludes with a return boat trip to Bali from the Toya Pakeh port at 16:30, followed by a comfortable transfer to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-08\", \"text\": \"ETA 08.00 from Sanur by Maruti Fast Boat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Toya Pakeh Harbour\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-08\", \"text\": \"ETD 16.30 to Sanur by Maruti Fast Boat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5150251,'476','Mr. Alberto Trujillo Cuesta',30508,207337,'Snorkeling to Nusa Penida (from Nusa Penida) (Private Trip)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-18','2024-08-18','Melysa','Febrina',3,'Persons (3)',1620000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": \"Jl. Batu Nunggal-Suana, Suana, Nusa Penida, Klungkung, Bali Phone: +62851 57708617 / +62822 10130068\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"The Angkal Resort Nusa Penida\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": \"Jl. Batu Nunggal-Suana, Suana, Nusa Penida, Klungkung, Bali Phone: +62851 57708617 / +62822 10130068\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"The Angkal Resort Nusa Penida\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5150253,'478','Mrs. Victhoritha Pinontoan',30508,212491,'Sanur to Kuta','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-08','2024-06-08','Rendy','Tami',5,'Persons (4-6)',3600000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-06-08\", \"text\": \"ETA 17.00 from Nusa Penida by Maruti Fast Boat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sanur Harbour\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-08\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bypass Ngurah Rai No.1, Kuta, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"HARRIS Hotel Kuta Galleria - Bali\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5150358,'477','ENRIQUE MARTINEZ ESTEBARANZ',30884,217082,'Grand Deluxe (Double + Extra Bed)','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-07-02','2024-07-04','Melysa','Wiwik',1,'Double',3897600.00,'Our Grand Deluxe features a uniquely classy and bright atmosphere, simple yet pristine, as its name suggests. Inside, it impresses with a light-flooded interior. Each room overlooks the lush green nature and the main swimming pool with its balcony. It is exclusively designed to discover the true meaning of peace in the brisk of pure silence. Bathroom offers are exclusively indoor for true relaxation and separate showers, complete with our signature amenities for guests to devour.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5150362,'477','ENRIQUE MARTINEZ ESTEBARANZ',30508,202895,'Cascada Tegenungan - Tirta Empul - Kintamani – Templo Besakih','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-03','2024-07-03','Melysa','Wiwik',3,'Persons (3)',2286000.00,'In this part of the trip, we set off along the East Coast of the island. The first site visit will be the Kusamba Village, a fishing village where colorful Prahu in the black sand beaches. We will announce the salt making process by traditional method. We continue our journey on the east coast to reach Goa Lawah, Gua Lawah or Bat Cave is one of favorite places of interest in Bali and it is located near of hilly bank so it is called reef of Middle hill. We continue our trip to Tenganan Village, Tenganan Village is one of the oldest Balinese Traditional located in Karangasem Regency, east part of Bali. This village is much referred by cultural literature science of Tenganan Pegringsingan, which is very famous in the island. It owns very unique local community life pattern which is one example of Bali Aga Village cultures (Hindu Prehistoric) and different with other countryside in plain of Bali. From here, we go to Amlapura to visit the Royal Palace, The town of Amlapura is the capital of Karangasem (\'East Bali\'). The palace of the former kings of the region is located here, and their descendants have opened parts of the complex to the public. We will finish our trip with visit heaven of Tirta Gangga, Tirta Gangga is a beautiful park with the huge water fountain. At the end of tour we will transfer you back to the hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-03\", \"text\": \"Address: Banjar Junjungan, Jl. Tirta Tawar, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone: (0361) 9000496\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"Korurua Dijiwa Ubud\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-03\", \"text\": \"Address: Banjar Junjungan, Jl. Tirta Tawar, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone: (0361) 9000496\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Korurua Dijiwa Ubud\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5150367,'477','ENRIQUE MARTINEZ ESTEBARANZ',30508,202897,'Uluwatu Temple and Kecak Dance','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-04','2024-07-04','Melysa','Wiwik',3,'Persons (3)',3186000.00,'This half-day tour, is an exciting tour package to visit Padang-Padang Beach, Uluwatu Temple, the famous Balinese Hindu Temple in south part of Bali with breathtaking view of sunset and Indian Ocean. Uluwatu Temple is one of Balinese Hindu Temples located right on the petrifying hill with the crevasse exist in the right and left side. Uluwatu Temple is one of Sad Khayangan (6 biggest temple in Bali) owns magnificent view of the Indian Ocean and sunset as a backdrop. This temple is very amazing where the location is right on the narrow peninsula with deep seawater under it. This tour package is combined with the spectacular Balinese traditional dance performance of Kecak Dance. Balinese Kecak Dance is a spectacular traditional dance with the group of people playing this dance with fire game. It is very exciting and unique dance due to the sound of gamelan is not using the normal gamelan but use their mouth. The dancers make the compact choir with the exquisite dance movement that is one of this dance features. After the dance we returned back to the hotel or seafood restaurant in Jimbaran.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-04\", \"text\": \"Address: Banjar Junjungan, Jl. Tirta Tawar, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone: (0361) 9000496\", \"time\": \"13:00\", \"locality\": \"Korurua Dijiwa Ubud\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-04\", \"text\": \"Address: Jl. Danau Tamblingan No.33, Sanur, Denpasar Selatan, Kota Denpasar, Bali 80228 Phone: (0361) 288427\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Respati Beach Hotel\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5150369,'476','Mr. Alberto Trujillo Cuesta',30805,208054,'LOP-CGK','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-23','2024-08-23','Melysa','Febrina',3,'Person',5940000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5150868,'475','BLANCA LLES BARUQUER',30508,215968,'1D Bali Tour (Lempuyang-Tirta Gangga-Tenganan-Goa Lawah)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-16','2024-07-16','Jacob','Komang',2,'Person (1)',2040000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-16\", \"text\": \"Ize Seminyak Hotel, Jalan Kayu Aya No. 68, Seminyak - Bali - Indonesia T: +62361 8466 999\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Seminyak\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-16\", \"text\": \"Ize Seminyak Hotel, Jalan Kayu Aya No. 68, Seminyak - Bali - Indonesia T: +62361 8466 999\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Seminyak\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5150870,'474','Emilio Spreafico',31106,216966,'Pick up at Airport by Innova','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-26','2024-06-26','Ayu','Eddy',1,'Per Car',392000.00,NULL,NULL,'Flight Information: ETA 11.55 by JT891 from Gorontalo on 26 June 2024','{\"date\": \"2024-06-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5150871,'474','Emilio Spreafico',31106,216970,'Drop off at Airport by Innova','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-06-27','2024-06-27','Ayu','Eddy',1,'Per Car',392000.00,NULL,NULL,'Flight Information: ETD 09.05 by JT742 to Manado on 27 June 2024','{\"date\": \"2024-06-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-06-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5150872,'477','ENRIQUE MARTINEZ ESTEBARANZ',30508,212455,'Sanur Hotel to Sanur Harbour','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-05','2024-07-05','Melysa','Wiwik',1,'Persons (1-3)',300000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-05\", \"text\": \"Address: Jl. Danau Tamblingan No.33, Sanur, Denpasar Selatan, Kota Denpasar, Bali 80228 Phone: (0361) 288427\", \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": \"Respati Beach Hotel\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-05\", \"text\": \"ETD: 07.30 AM to Nusa Penida\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Office Maruti Fast Boat\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5150874,'477','ENRIQUE MARTINEZ ESTEBARANZ',30508,207112,'1D Nusa Penida West Tour','Confirmed','C2I-BALI19',1,'2024-07-05','2024-07-05','Melysa','Wiwik',3,'Persons (3)',1080000.00,'Today, embark on a unique adventure as you explore the enchanting Nusa Penida, a neighboring island of Bali. Your day begins with a convenient hotel pick-up, followed by a journey to the Sanur port where a fast boat awaits to transport you to Nusa Penida in just 30 minutes. Nusa Penida, located in the southeast of Bali, is a true paradise waiting to be discovered. Upon your arrival, a friendly driver will be ready to guide you through the day\'s captivating itinerary. Your first destination is the mesmerizing Angel\'s Billabong, a natural wonder resembling a pristine pool nestled in the heart of nature. Take a refreshing swim, but exercise caution on the steps and heed your driver\'s recommendations. Next, we head to Broken Beach, a charming bay that was once a cave, now open to the sky, offering a unique and captivating scenery. Although inaccessible by land, the view from above is nothing short of breathtaking. Keep an eye out for the possibility of spotting giant manta rays gracefully gliding on the water\'s surface. Our journey continues to the renowned Kelingking Beach, famous for its stunning cliffs and the iconic hand-shaped mountain. This beach is not only one of the island\'s most famous attractions but also a favorite subject for photographers. We conclude the day at the pristine Crystal Beach, where white sands meet turquoise waters in perfect harmony. As the sun sets, you\'ll have the opportunity to relax and savor the beauty that surrounds you. This unforgettable experience concludes with a return boat trip to Bali from the Toya Pakeh port at 16:30, followed by a comfortable transfer to your hotel.',NULL,'Visit: Angel\'s Billabong - Broken Beach - Kelingking Beach - Crystal Beach','{\"date\": \"2024-07-05\", \"text\": \"ETA Fast Boat 08.00 from Sanur by Maruti fast Boat\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": \"Banjar Nyuh Harbour\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-05\", \"text\": \"Address: Banjar Angkal, Suana, Kec. Nusa Penida, Kabupaten Klungkung, Bali 80771 Phone: (0366) 5582389\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"The Angkal Resort\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5151124,'342','Sara Perez de Armas',31015,203232,'3D2N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Ijen Tour Package drop Bali','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-09-30','2024-10-02','Eddy','Eddy',2,'Persons (2)',8880000.00,NULL,NULL,'HOTEL PERIOD STAY : 30 SEP - 01 OCT 2024 / JIWA JAWA BROMO 01 - 02 OCT 2024 / IJEN RESORT','{\"date\": \"2024-09-30\", \"text\": \"ETA : Arrived at 10 