L,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5151709,'477','ENRIQUE MARTINEZ ESTEBARANZ',30805,202739,'DPS-LBJ','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-07','2024-07-07','Melysa','Wiwik',3,'Person',5280000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5151714,'477','ENRIQUE MARTINEZ ESTEBARANZ',30805,212510,'LBJ-CGK','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-09','2024-07-09','Melysa','Wiwik',3,'Person',7920000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5152502,'480','Isabelle ABADIE',30508,212287,'Airport to Sanur','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-02','2024-11-02','Melysa','Komang',7,'Persons (7-10)',6272000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-11-02\", \"text\": \"ETA : 15.20h by BR255 from Taipei (TPE) on 02 November 2024\", \"time\": \"15:20\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-02\", \"text\": \"Hotel Puri Santrian Sanur, Jl. Cemara No.35, Sanur, Denpasar Selatan, Kota Denpasar, Bali 80228 Telepon: (0361) 288009\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sanur\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5152518,'480','Isabelle ABADIE',30508,207269,'Sanur to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-09','2024-11-09','Melysa','Komang',7,'Persons (7-10)',6272000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,'Pease ready on hotel lobby for pickup at 13.30','{\"date\": \"2024-11-09\", \"text\": \"Hotel Puri Santrian Sanur, Jl. Cemara No.35, Sanur, Denpasar Selatan, Kota Denpasar, Bali 80228 Telepon: (0361) 288009\", \"time\": \"13:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sanur\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-09\", \"text\": \"ETD : 16.30h by BR256 to Taipe (TPE) on 09 November 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"International Ngurah Rai Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5152690,'481','Dennis Chung',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-02','2024-07-03','Ayu','Wiwik',3,'2 Double + 1 Twin',2520000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Flight Detail as below: Arrival flight (2 pax): Mr. Fong Leo Lee & Mrs. Karlai Chan Lee ETA: 20.45 by Air Asia AK353 from Kuala Lumpur on 02 July 2024 Mr. Dennis Chi Keung Chung & Mrs. Shu Fen Chung (own arrangement) Mr. David Siegel & Mrs. Wei-Li Pai (own arrangement) Departure flight (6 pax): ETD 06.00 by Batik Air ID6202 to Pangkalan bun on 03 July 2024 Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. - Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK–IN','{\"date\": \"2024-07-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5152773,'481','Dennis Chung',30806,202003,'4D3N Great Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO6',4,'2024-07-03','2024-07-06','Ayu','Wiwik',6,'Persons (6)',30960000.00,'In this Great Borneo Orangutan Tour, you will navigate the Sekonyer River looking for life that approaches the waters, enjoy the passage of the proboscis monkeys in front of the Klotok, see orangutans and macaques, and even with luck, you will see how some crocodile approaches the surface to take a breath before to dive in or out of the dark waters. Get ready to spend a magical night in the camping jungle. Take the opportunity to hike around the Leakey camp, Pondok Tangguy, and Pesalat, visit the feeding platforms of different centers, and walk at night in the forests of Borneo. NOTE FOR THIS TRIP: Due to the possible rains during the wet season in Indonesia and the fact that the jungle floor can have many wetlands for camping, we can do this trip between the months of April to October. 4D3N GREAT BORNEO ORANGUTAN TOUR Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN – KUMAI PORT – TANJUNG HARAPAN TREKKING Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan is Cape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. After visiting the feeding camp, you will do the planting of the trees and then continue trekking inside the jungle for about an hour. It is an opportunity to enjoy more intensely the endemics of the area, the orangutans, the sounds of the night, the vegetation, etc. Once the camps are assembled, you will have dinner, and, if you want, you can do some hiking at night to see the nocturnal fauna with your guide. Meals : Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Camping in the jungle Day 2 : TANJUNG HARAPAN VILLAGE – CAMP LEAKEY TREKKING After tidying up the tent, you will continue our trekking to the river, where the motor canoe will pick us up and take us to the boat. You will cruise the river with a motor canoe, and then you will have breakfast and freshen up on the boat. Take a rest a bit, then you go to visit the village inside the national park, named Tanjung Harapan Village. Here you will see the activities of the locals. After the visit, you continue the journey to Camp Leakey feeding camp. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. Note: The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. Meals : Breakfast – Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : PONDOK TANGGUI TREKKING – PROBOSCIS TOUR After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continue to add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok cruise up to the Sekonyer River. You will see nice vegetation around the river bank, including Nipa Palm, Pandanus, and some kinds of trees that are growing up around the river. See some wildlifes such as birds, Macaques, Proboscis Monkeys and Orangutans. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note: If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast – Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 4 : KUMAI PORT – PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Flight Detail: ETA: 07.15 by Batik Air ID6202 from Jakarta on 03 July 2024 ETD: 07.30 by Nam Air IN195 to Semarang on 06 July 2024 Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-07-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5152793,'481','Dennis Chung',30805,202689,'CGK-PKN','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-03','2024-07-03','Ayu','Wiwik',6,'Person',10560000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5152795,'481','Dennis Chung',30805,212246,'PKN-SRG','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-06','2024-07-06','Ayu','Wiwik',6,'Person',17160000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5152823,'481','Dennis Chung',30783,201524,'4D3N Yogyakarta - Mt. Merapi with Jeep / B. Gallery Prawirotaman (Deluxe Room - 2 Double + 1 Twin)','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-07-06','2024-07-09','Ayu','Wiwik',6,'Persons (4-6 / Double)',28980000.00,'D1 Arrival Yogyakarta International Airport – Transfer to hotel: Welcome to the cradle of Indonesian culture, Yogyakarta. A tourist destination for its ancient palaces, temples, batik workshops, gamelan music orchestras, court dances and wayang puppet shows. Upon your arrival in Yogyakarta a representative of come2indonesia will be waiting for you with a sign indicating your name to take you to your hotel and the rest of the day is for you. D2 Borobudur temple – Candirejo Village Tour by Horse cart / bicycle – Merapi lava tour Including Jeep: You will have your deserved breakfast at the hotel. Today’s tour will make you enjoy the authentic Javanese essence. You will start your route in the direction of with the Borobudur Temple (Candi Borobudur), the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. We will tour around the temple, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano has been producing during its history. After visiting one of the most important Buddhist temples in Southeast Asia, and in a horse carriage (Andong) we will visit the villages that surround this temple. These are authentic Javanese villages where culture and tradition are the protagonists. As you spend your days in this country and go around the different islands, you will realize how different Indonesians are among them in terms of clothing, food, architecture and even language. Today we will learn about and share these Javanese places. Then we will go to Kaliurang / Kalidalem to see Mount Merapi in constant activity. Here in a 4x4 jeep driven by specialized drivers, we will climb its skirt to see the remains of the 2010 eruption such as houses buried by ashes, a multitude of objects paralyzed by lava, etc. In addition, an open-air tribute museum presided over by the clock that marks the time just when the lava passed through it has been improvised. Accompanied by photos of the rescue, it will make us feel very closely the experiences of that fateful day. After finishing this day full of emotions, we will take you back to your hotel. D3 City Tour Jogjakarta Visit Sultan Palace, Watercastle and Bird Market – Prambanan Temple: After breakfast and at the indicated time we will head towards the heart of the city. We will visit the Keraton known as the Sultan’s Palace. The palace is a complex building two centuries old, located in the heart of the city. You will hear the song of the “freedom” of the birds in the bird market, we will visit the “Water Castle” that occupies the highest part at the northern end of the vast complex of Taman Sari, Malioboro Street, main street of Yogyakarta, with its merchants, horse carriages, taxi-bikes and markets. An incredible experience that will make the hours fly by. After finishing the tour in the center of the city of Yogyakarta, we will go to the northeast direction Candi Prambanan, the temple of the Hinduists and classified as a World Heritage Site by Unesco since 1991. The built of this temple was finished around the year 856 to commemorate the victory of the descendant Sanjaya of Siva, Rikai Pikatan on the last sovereign Sailendra of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to the Trimurti, the expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the Destroyer. After this unforgettable day, we will take you to your hotel. D4 Transfer out Yogyakarta International airport: Today our adventure ends at the cradle of Indonesian culture. Depending on the time of your flight, we will pick you up to take you to the airport and take the flight to your next destination. End of our services. Thank you very much for exploring Yogyakarta by the hand of Come2indonesia.',NULL,'Program details: 06 July. Arrive Semarang - Candirejo Village - Borobudur Temple - Yogyakarta 07 July. Keraton Yogyakarta - Merapi - Prambanan Temple 08 July. Taman Sari - Bird Market/Traditional Market 09 July. Departure Yogyakarta Flight Detail: ETA: 08.40 by Nam Air IN195 from Pangkalan Bun on 06 July 2024 ETD: 13.30 by Garuda Indonesia GA0252 to Denpasar on 09 July 2024','{\"date\": \"2024-07-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5152845,'481','Dennis Chung',30805,207117,'YIA-DPS','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-09','2024-07-09','Ayu','Wiwik',6,'Person',9240000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5152851,'481','Dennis Chung',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-09','2024-07-09','Ayu','Wiwik',1,'Persons (4-6)',840000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-09\", \"text\": \"ETA: 16.05 by Garuda Indonesia GA0252 from Yogyakarta on 09 July 2024\", \"time\": \"16:05\", \"locality\": \"Ngurah Rai Airport (Domestic)\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-09\", \"text\": \"Address: Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone: (0361) 6202008\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Adiwana Bisma\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5152903,'481','Dennis Chung',30538,201914,'Adiwana Rice Field Room','Confirmed',NULL,6,'2024-07-09','2024-07-15','Ayu','Wiwik',3,'2 Double + 1 Twin',68040000.00,'Come face to face with nature from a luxuriously sophisticated abode. Our beautifully designed Rice Field View room gives you front-row seats to a beloved icon of Ubud – a flourishing, productive rice field. Just steps away from your bed, lush stalks of paddy wave in the breeze. Relax on your spacious private terrace and watch the farmers at work or the ducks as they frolic and play. Reflecting the island’s unique heritage and Ubud’s reputation as the center of arts and culture, the room is appointed with a natural woven headboard, creating beautiful depth and texture against the cool of the marble floor enhanced with premium stones and hardwood furnishing. Behind a door, in the all-marble bathroom, there is a bathtub that overlooks the outdoors from behind wooden slats. His and hers vanity offers much-needed space and a standing rain shower is illuminated by soft yellow lighting.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5152918,'481','Dennis Chung',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route (Taman Ayun-Jatiluwih-Ulundanu Beratan-Tanah Lot)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-10','2024-07-10','Ayu','Wiwik',6,'Persons (5-6)',4176000.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-10\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone: (0361) 6202008\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"Adiwana Bisma\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Adiwana Bisma\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5152930,'481','Dennis Chung',30508,202882,'Kusamba-Goa Lawah-Besakih-Kertagosha','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-11','2024-07-11','Ayu','Wiwik',6,'Persons (5-6)',4104000.00,'The first destination is Kusamba Beach, it is one of the favorite places of interest in Bali which is famous with the beautiful beach, we can also meet a fish market in this place which is usually held between 10 am until 4 pm. Then we go to Goa Lawah, this is one of the favourite place to be visited, because here is a nature cave dwelt by thousands of tail bat located at north side from Jeroan/center of Goa Lawah Temple. Next we go to Bukit Jambul, it is strategically located beside of the main road from Denpasar to Besakih Temple and it is one of the tourist destinations that visited on Besakih Tour. It is situated in the plateau area which is blessed with the beautiful panorama of rice terrace and green coconuts three unfolding to the sea. After visit Bukit Jambul, we’ll continue to Besakih Temple is the biggest Hindu temple in Bali which the local people call Pura Besakih. It owns beautiful view from the top of temple area where we can see the wide nature panorama until to the ocean so that’s why this temple is many visited by tourists from all over the world. Then go to Kertagosa, This place also owns Taman Gili, a building floating or sees like floating because it is intentionally founded in the middle of a fish pond.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-11\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone: (0361) 6202008\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"Adiwana Bisma\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Adiwana Bisma\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5152943,'481','Dennis Chung',30508,207262,'Ubud to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-15','2024-07-15','Ayu','Wiwik',1,'Persons (4-6)',840000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-15\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone: (0361) 6202008\", \"time\": \"04:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-15\", \"text\": \"ETD: 08.00 by Batik Air ID6333 to Labuan Bajo on 15 July 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Airport Ngurah Rai (Domestic)\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5152959,'481','Dennis Chung',30805,202739,'DPS-LBJ','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-15','2024-07-15','Ayu','Wiwik',6,'Person',10560000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5152975,'481','Dennis Chung',31083,212381,'3D2N LOB Rinca - Padar - Komodo Island Tour (Medium Standard B. - Bintang Flores, Deluxe Room)','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-07-15','2024-07-17','Ayu','Wiwik',6,'Persons (6-7)',50508000.00,'TOUR ITINERARY Highlights: Menjarite, Kelor, Kalong, Rinca, Padar, Komodo island, Pink Beach, Taka Makassar, Manta Point, Kanawa, Batu Cermin Mirror Cave DAY 1 : DENPASAR - LABUAN BAJO - MENJARITE - PADAR - KELOR - KALONG ISLAND Arrival at Komodo Airport in Labuan Bajo west Flores, meeting service with our tour guide and transfer to the pier of Labuan Bajo for Rinca Island. It’s about 2 hours sail to the island of Komodo Dragon, stop at Menjarite island for snorkeling then continue to Rinca island-the Island of Komodo dragon, you will find not just e Dragons but also many wild animals like, deer, wild buffalo, long-tailed macaque and wild pig also numerous of birds. Keep your eyes look up as sometime you will find the young Komodo dragons on the trees. A local ranger will lead you through this natural preservation. Late afternoon sailing directly to Kalong Rinca Island to see the hundreds of fling foxes set out from the mangrove tree at 06-07 pm, the lovely sunset from the boat trip really enjoyable here. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Boat Cabin Air Conditioning DAY 2 : KALONG - PADAR - KOMODO - PINK BEACH - MANTA POINT - TAKA MAKASSAR - LABUAN BAJO After having breakfast in your boat, heading to Padar Island, taking trek to Padar Island until having the top view point to get breathtaking scenery of three bays around, Padar Island hike in Komodo has some of the most amazing views in Indonesia, trek to downhill and back to the Boat for sailing directly to Loh Liang – the Ranger station in Komodo Island. By passing through many small islands, After registering start to take basic trekking to see the GIANT RIZARD / KOMODO DRAGON and other wild animals as: Timor deer, wild pig, wild chicken and many variously of tropical bird. Please keep your look at any directions as sometimes you will also find young Komodo dragon hanging over the trees. A local ranger will be led you during the trek. Return to the boat on to Pink beach for snorkeling, swimming and relaxing. It is really spectacular and unspoiled coral reef and many color fish. This is one of best side for snorkeling diving. Sail toward MANTA POINT to exploring Huge Mantas by snorkeling even watching from your boat trip (can’t be guaranteed if weather is not good, like wave and current are strongly) visit also the taka Makaasar its really tiny island with white sand beach really enjoyable to relaxing or beach walking then heading to Labuan bajo for overnight and dinner at above hotel list option. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner DAY 3 : LABUAN BAJO - DENPASAR After breakfast taking your next excursion with visiting local marke and Batu Cermin (Mirror Stone) Cave. The grotto is 75 by 75 meters large, and contains stalactites and stalagmites. Some tunnels are narrow and dark but in others sunlight falls, then process to the airport for flight to Denpasar or to your next destination. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Attention: The itinerary is subject to change due to the weather, tide level and operating conditions without prior notice.',NULL,'Flight Detail: ETA: 09.10 by Batik Air ID6333 from Denpasar on 15 July 2024 ETD: 09.50 by Batik Air ID6332 to Denpasar connect Lombok on 17 July 2024','{\"date\": \"2024-07-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5152996,'481','Dennis Chung',30805,212441,'LBJ-DPS-LOP','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-17','2024-07-17','Ayu','Wiwik',6,'Person',16500000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5153012,'481','Dennis Chung',30650,208425,'Private Pool Villa','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-07-17','2024-07-20','Ayu','Wiwik',3,'Double',27000000.00,'Each villa embraces calmness, comfort and privacy in a simple and elegant setting. Guests can relax while peacefully sipping drinks in an inviting plunge pool surrounded by a lush tropical garden and at an old-wooden deck. At 85 m2 room size, this villa\'s special feature is the private pool. The air-conditioned villa features 1 bedroom and 1 bathroom with a shower and a hairdryer. The villa provides a mini-bar, a tea and coffee maker, a seating area as well as a terrace with garden views. The unit offers 1 bed.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5153021,'481','Dennis Chung',30508,207385,'Padang Bai to Nusa Dua','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-20','2024-07-20','Ayu','Wiwik',1,'Persons (4-6)',1140000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-20\", \"text\": \"ETA Fast Boat 12.30 from Gili Air by GiliGili Fast Boat\", \"time\": \"12:30\", \"locality\": \"Padang Bai Harbour\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-20\", \"text\": \"Kawasan Wisata Nusa Dua Lot S-3, Benoa, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80363 Telepon: (0361) 2002900\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Merusaka Nusa Dua\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5153034,'481','Dennis Chung',30914,202449,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-07-20','2024-07-23','Ayu','Wiwik',3,'2 Double + 1 Twin',21060000.00,'The room is spacious at 48 sqm with king and twin size beds capacity of 2 (two) adults and 2 (two) child below 12 years old, decked with combination of Balinese-modern contemporary elements, immaculately designed to characterize each of Seven Balinese Goddesses. Located on a higher level of each Puri, the room is equipped with every amenity that could possibly be required, making it ideal for a single traveler or couples.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5153037,'481','Dennis Chung',30508,207268,'Nusa Dua to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-23','2024-07-23','Ayu','Wiwik',1,'Persons (4-6)',720000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-23\", \"text\": \"Kawasan Wisata Nusa Dua Lot S-3, Benoa, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80363 Telepon: (0361) 2002900\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"Merusaka Nusa Dua\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-23\", \"text\": \"ETD: 12.00 by Garuda Indonesia GA0407 to Jakarta on 23 July 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Ngurah Rai Airport (Domestic)\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5153042,'481','Dennis Chung',30805,207114,'DPS-CGK','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-23','2024-07-23','Ayu','Wiwik',6,'Person',12540000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5154062,'455','Mrs. Katrin Rottmann',30662,213209,'13D12N (Explore Sumatra) Medan - Tangkahan - Bukit Lawang - Lake Toba - Bukittinggi - Tour Plus','Confirmed','RVL-13D Exsum',13,'2024-07-18','2024-07-30','Yuli','Yuli',4,'Persons (4-5 / Double)',57120000.00,'DAY 01 : ARRIVAL IN MEDAN Upon arrival at Kualanamu International Airport pick up by our tour guide and then Transfer to hotel, afternoon free at own leisure. Meals : - Accommodation : Emerald Garden Hotel or Le Polonia Hotel or Similar Hotel DAY 02 : MEDAN - CITY TOUR - TANGKAHAN After breakfast city tour visiting Sultan Palace, Great Mosque, Chinese Temple and then drive to Tangkahan via Binjai and Batang Serangan. Afternoon arriving at Tangkahan check into simple Mega Inn Lodge. Meals : - Accommodation : Mega Inn Lodge DAY 03 : TANGKAHAN - ELEPHANT WASHING & RIVER SAFARI After breakfast walking to the elephant station and then join with the Mahout during washing the Elephant, help feeding the elephants, after feeding the Elephant enjoying Tubing through the river and stop will be made at fantastic Buluh Waterfall where you may enjoy the waterfall, take your natural shower and then you can enjoy sun bathing or swimming on the river while enjoying picnic lunch on the beach of the river. Afternoon arrival at the village you can get in touch with local people, where you can see the daily activities of the local people and then return to guest house by walking, arrival at guest house you can take a rest or visit hot springs and waterfall near the guest house. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Accommodation : Mega Inn Lodge DAY 04 : TANGKAHAN - BUKIT LAWANG After breakfast leave Tangkahan for Bukit Lawang by car passing plantation and jungle road, on the way stop at plantation and several interesting places for enjoying the panorama and witness the activities of the local people. Upon arrival at Bukit Lawang check in to hotel. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Bukit Lawang Cottage or Rindu Alam Hotel DAY 05 : BUKIT LAWANG - TRACKING After breakfast walking to the jungle to start a jungle tracking to explore the nature of Leuser National Park with their flora and fauna, there will be possibility to see Orang Utan in their own natural habitat and other kind of animals such as Thomas leaf monkeys, long tail macaque, gibbon, black gibbon and other kind of flora and fauna of tropical rain forest. This tracking will take about 03 hours, after tracking return to hotel. Afternoon free at own leisure to enjoy the nature of Bukit Lawang where you can also walking to the village around the hotel. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Bukit Lawang Cottage or Rindu Alam Hotel DAY 06 : BUKIT LAWANG - BRASTAGI After breakfast drive to Brastagi via new road passing several village such as Namu Ukur, Rumah Galuh and Simpang Kuta Buluh, on the way you can enjoying the panorama of Sinabung Volcano, afternoon arrival in Brastagi visiting Lhumbini Park with its duplicate of Shwedagon pagoda, fruit market, and Gundaling hill, and afternoon check in to hotel. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Sinabung Hotel or Mikie Holiday Hotel DAY 07 : BRASTAGI - SAMOSIR / LAKE TOBA After breakfast drive head for Samosir Island in Lake Toba via TELE. En-route stop at : - Dokan (to see the traditional village of the Batak Karo tribe) - Sipisopiso Waterfall (from here you can admire the scenic view of the Lake Toba from its northern tip combined with the slender 90 meters high waterfall) - Tele (a nice place for over-viewing the lake from its western part) - Efrata (another beautiful waterfall found on the way to Samosir Island) - Lumban Suhi-Suhi (to see the Tobanase traditional houses where we could observe also the women doing the weaving) In mid afternoon arriving at Tuktuk area on Samosir and check-in to hotel. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Tabo Cottage or Samosir Villa or Toledo Inn DAY 08 : SAMOSIR EXCURSION BY CAR After breakfast we start for our full day excursion by car in the interior of Samosir island and en-route visiting : - Ambarita (to see the stone chairs and tables where once used as the execution site by the ancient tribal chieftains) - Aek Natonang (here we can see the small lake found of the top of Samosir Island and its panorama view) - Tomok (to see the old sarcophages belonged to former Sidabutar Kings and his descendants) In afternoon return back to hotel and free at leisure. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Tabo Cottage or Samosir Villa or Toledo Inn DAY 09 : SAMOSIR – PADANG SIDEMPUAN After breakfast crossing back to Parapat and arrival at Parapat drive to Padang Sidempuan, on the way stop at pineapple, clove, and coffee plantation and visiting traditional market at Balige Sigur-gur and Sipoholon Hot Springs. Before arrival at Padang Sidempuan, enjoy the nature by walking at the bank of Sarulla river, the ricefield-terraces and arrival at Padang Sidempuan check in to hotel. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Mega Permata or Mutiara Hotel DAY 10 : PADANG SIDEMPUAN – BUKITTINGGI Leave Padang Sidempuan for Bukittinggi by passing rain tropical forest of Rimba Panti and visit pepper, vanilla, cardamon and cinnamon garden, and crossing the equator line at Bonjol, afternoon arrival at Bukittinggi -the charming town ofMinangkabaupeople- directly check-in to hotel. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Santika Bukittinggi or Royal Denai Hotel DAY 11 : BUKITTINGGI – MINANGKABAU TOUR After breakfast drive to Batusangkar via Tabek Patah, on the way stop at Rao-Rao to visit Minangkabau traditional village and stop to see traditional coffee milling, arrival at Batusangkar drive to Pagaruyung to visit the duplicate of the Palace of Minangkabau Kingdom, afternoon return to Bukittinggi via Padang Panjang and visit Pandai Sikat village to see Minangkabau traditional hand weaving and wood carving, arrival at Bukittinggi city tour visiting Sianok Canyon (from thepanorama point), Fort-De-Kock, Museum and Market. Afternoon return to hotel. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Santika Bukittinggi or Royal Denai Hotel DAY 12 : VILLAGE TOUR BY BICYCLE After breakfast drive to Panampuang village, it will take about 30 minutes driving from your hotel in Bukittinggi, arrival at Panampuang village visiting traditional embroidery and then start the trip with bicycle to explore the villages where you will stop at rice field to see the farmer working on rice field traditionally during planting the rice or harvest time, you may also try and join with the farmer during working at rice field, then continue by bicycle to visit school in the village and keep in touch with local peoples in the village during their daily activities such as making traditional handy craft or snack, you can also stop at coffee shop in the village to try traditional coffee and get in touch with the villagers at coffee shop, since coffeeshop is used by the villagers for social contact. Afternoon return to hotel in Bukittinggi. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Santika Bukittinggi or Royal Denai Hotel DAY 13 : BUKITTINGGI – PADANG / AIRPORT After brekfast drive to Padang via Anai Valley, on the way stop at Anai Waterfall, arrival at Padang directly transfer to Airport. Meals : Breakfast',NULL,'Based on 2 Rooms (1 Double + 1 Twin Bed), Side by side English speaking guide DAY 01, 18 JULY : ARRIVE IN MEDAN Accommodation: Emerald Garden Hotel - Superior Room DAY 02, 19 JULY : MEDAN – CITY TOUR – TANGKAHAN (B) Accommodation: Mega Inn Lodge - Standard Room DAY 03, 20 JULY : TANGKAHAN ECOTOURISM – ELEPHANT WASHING & RIVER SAFARI (B,L) Accommodation: Mega Inn Lodge - Standard Room DAY 04, 21 JULY : TANGKAHAN – BUKIT LAWANG (B) Accommodation: Wisma Leuser Sibayak - River View Room DAY 05, 22 JULY : FULL DAY LEUSER NATIONAL PARK TRACKING (B,L) Accommodation: Wisma Leuser Sibayak - River View Room DAY 06, 23 JULY : BUKIT LAWANG – BRASTAGI (B) Accommodation: Mikie Holiday Resort - Deluxe Room DAY 07, 24 JULY : BRASTAGI – SAMOSIR / LAKE TOBA (B) Accommodation: Samosir Villa Resort - Deluxe room DAY 08, 25 JULY : SAMOSIR EXCURSION BY CAR (B) Accommodation: Samosir Villa Resort - Deluxe room DAY 09, 26 JULY : SAMOSIR – PADANG SIDEMPUAN (B) Accommodation: Mega Permata Hotel - Deluxe Room DAY 10, 27 JULY : PADANG SIDEMPUAN – BUKITTINGGI (B) Accommodation: Santika Hotel - Deluxe Room DAY 11, 28 JULY : BUKITTINGGI – MINANGKABAU TOUR (B) Accommodation: Santika Hotel - Deluxe Room DAY 12, 29 JULY : VILLAGE TOUR BY BICYCLE (B)Accommodation: Santika Hotel - Deluxe Room DAY 13, 30 JULY : BUKITTINGGI – PADANG – JOGJAKARTA (B) Flight details: ETA from Singapore at 19:20 by Lufthansa LH7238 on 18 July ETD to Jakarta at 12:00 by Garuda Indonesia GA149 on 30 July','{\"date\": \"2024-07-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5154081,'455','Mrs. Katrin Rottmann',30783,201524,'4D3N Yogyakarta - Mt. Merapi with Jeep','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-07-30','2024-08-02','Yuli','Yuli',4,'Persons (4-6 / Double)',18704000.00,'D1 Arrival Yogyakarta International Airport – Transfer to hotel: Welcome to the cradle of Indonesian culture, Yogyakarta. A tourist destination for its ancient palaces, temples, batik workshops, gamelan music orchestras, court dances and wayang puppet shows. Upon your arrival in Yogyakarta a representative of come2indonesia will be waiting for you with a sign indicating your name to take you to your hotel and the rest of the day is for you. D2 Borobudur temple – Candirejo Village Tour by Horse cart / bicycle – Merapi lava tour Including Jeep: You will have your deserved breakfast at the hotel. Today’s tour will make you enjoy the authentic Javanese essence. You will start your route in the direction of with the Borobudur Temple (Candi Borobudur), the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. We will tour around the temple, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano has been producing during its history. After visiting one of the most important Buddhist temples in Southeast Asia, and in a horse carriage (Andong) we will visit the villages that surround this temple. These are authentic Javanese villages where culture and tradition are the protagonists. As you spend your days in this country and go around the different islands, you will realize how different Indonesians are among them in terms of clothing, food, architecture and even language. Today we will learn about and share these Javanese places. Then we will go to Kaliurang / Kalidalem to see Mount Merapi in constant activity. Here in a 4x4 jeep driven by specialized drivers, we will climb its skirt to see the remains of the 2010 eruption such as houses buried by ashes, a multitude of objects paralyzed by lava, etc. In addition, an open-air tribute museum presided over by the clock that marks the time just when the lava passed through it has been improvised. Accompanied by photos of the rescue, it will make us feel very closely the experiences of that fateful day. After finishing this day full of emotions, we will take you back to your hotel. D3 City Tour Jogjakarta Visit Sultan Palace, Watercastle and Bird Market – Prambanan Temple: After breakfast and at the indicated time we will head towards the heart of the city. We will visit the Keraton known as the Sultan’s Palace. The palace is a complex building two centuries old, located in the heart of the city. You will hear the song of the “freedom” of the birds in the bird market, we will visit the “Water Castle” that occupies the highest part at the northern end of the vast complex of Taman Sari, Malioboro Street, main street of Yogyakarta, with its merchants, horse carriages, taxi-bikes and markets. An incredible experience that will make the hours fly by. After finishing the tour in the center of the city of Yogyakarta, we will go to the northeast direction Candi Prambanan, the temple of the Hinduists and classified as a World Heritage Site by Unesco since 1991. The built of this temple was finished around the year 856 to commemorate the victory of the descendant Sanjaya of Siva, Rikai Pikatan on the last sovereign Sailendra of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to the Trimurti, the expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the Destroyer. After this unforgettable day, we will take you to your hotel. D4 Transfer out Yogyakarta International airport: Today our adventure ends at the cradle of Indonesian culture. Depending on the time of your flight, we will pick you up to take you to the airport and take the flight to your next destination. End of our services. Thank you very much for exploring Yogyakarta by the hand of Come2indonesia.',NULL,'Based on 2 Rooms (1 Double + 1 Twin Bed), Connecting room / Side by side English speaking guide DAY 01, 30 JULY : ARRIVE IN YOGYAKARTA Accommodation: GAIA Cosmo - Deluxe Room DAY 02, 31 JULY : : JOGJAKARTA CITY TOUR – PRAMBANAN TEMPLE – MERAPI LAVA TOUR (B) Accommodation: GAIA Cosmo - Deluxe Room DAY 03, 01 AUG : BOROBUDUR TEMPLE – CANDIREJO VILLAGE – SEMARANG (B) Accommodation: Aston Inn Pandanaran Semarang - Superior Room DAY 04, 02 AUG : TRANSFER OUT TO SEMARANG AIRPORT (B) Flight details: ETA in Yogyakarta at 16:05 by Garuda Indonesia GA212 from Jakarta on 30 July ETD from Semarang at 08:30 by Batik Air ID6302 to Pangkalan Bun on 02 Aug','{\"date\": \"2024-07-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5154097,'482','Javier Hernandez Ayerra',31015,203232,'3D2N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Ijen Tour Package drop Bali','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-07-13','2024-07-15','Jacob','Praba',4,'Persons (4)',11520000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-13\", \"text\": \"ETA 10:00AM by Batik Air ID6134 from Pangkalan Bun\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Juanda International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-15\", \"text\": \"Bambu Lokha Guest House Kemenuh, Kec. Sukawati, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5154103,'482','Javier Hernandez Ayerra',31196,204658,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-13','2024-07-14','Jacob','Praba',2,'Double',3690000.00,'Room type deluxe, with spacious room 3,41 m x 6,09 m and have type bed king size or twin bed. This type of room is available on the 2nd, 3rd and 4th floors and has of the hills view.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5154109,'482','Javier Hernandez Ayerra',30803,202852,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-14','2024-07-15','Jacob','Praba',2,'Double + Twin',1680000.00,'At 25 sqm of room size with 46 rooms available. This smart room category is more contemporary in appearance and comes with its own terrace or balcony. Minimalist furnishings are balanced by a neutral decor to soothe the senses and ensure restful slumber. Including a double bed (king or queen) or 2 single beds (twin) with maximum capacity of 2 adults + 1 child or 3 adults. The en-suite bathroom features a modern shower cubicle enclosed in glass together with a marble vanity.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5154117,'455','Mrs. Katrin Rottmann',30806,202007,'5D4N Borneo Orangutan Tour & Dayak Tribe','Confirmed',NULL,5,'2024-08-02','2024-08-06','Yuli','Yuli',4,'Persons (4)',37856000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN – KUMAI PORT – TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan is Cape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY – CAMP LEAKEY After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continue to add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note: The Birute Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. Meals : Breakfast – Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT – PANGKALAN BUN – DAYAK VILLAGE After breakfast, you make a final sail towards Kumai, where you will approach the car and go to Dayak village. On the way, you will go through indigenous villages, river workers, and people making their living near the river. You will pass some rapids with caution. You will stop on the way to be able to have lunch. Upon reaching the Dayak village, our guide will take you to the Long House (they are the typical houses of the Dayak tribes in Borneo – very long houses where almost a village lives inside). Upon arrival, you will realize the kindness of the town. Normally, they celebrate that people from outside come to visit them, because for them, it is a source of pride that people from so far away travel so much to be able to keep them company. Due to that, on arrival, it is normal to celebrate this visit with dances and some other local liquor! After walking around, the communal dinner with the whole tribe arrives, and then they will ring the bell, with which the whole town will gather to do dances and enjoy the night with what they call Pesta Menarik Horn Bill (Horn Festival Bill). Note: The guest house will be based on the basic house of local people, where you can experience their lives and get closer to their culture, with very standard facilities, a shared bathroom, and a shared house with other guests. Meals : Breakfast – Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Basic Guest House in the Village Day 4 : DAYAK VILLAGE – PANGKALAN BUN In the morning, you can visit the surroundings of the village, share stories with them, and help them in their daily tasks. You can also take the opportunity to see the manual work they do and usually take to the city to sell, such as masks, carpets, statues, etc. After packing everything, start the way back to Pangkalan Bun. On the way, you can stop at the Kotawaringin Palace and take pictures around. Lunch will be on the way, with an arrival in the afternoon at Pangkalan Bun. Transfer to the hotel, and the rest of the afternoon is free. Meals : Breakfast – Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Arsela Hotel or similar Day 5 : HOTEL – PANGKALAN BUN AIRPORT After breakfast, transfer to the airport. End of our services. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Flight Details: ETA 09:30 by Batik Air ID6302 from Semarang on 02 Aug ETD 08:50 by Batik Air ID6134 to Surabaya on 06 Aug Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5154168,'455','Mrs. Katrin Rottmann',32900,217798,'Premium Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-05','2024-08-06','Yuli','Yuli',2,'Double + Twin',2162899.20,NULL,NULL,'Premium Superior - Connecting Rooms','{\"date\": \"2024-08-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5154223,'484','Ms. Lidia Margalef Garcia',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-09-05','2024-09-07','Nicholas','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',10800000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visit