Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-07-15\", \"text\": \"ETA: 07.15 by Batik Air ID6202 from Jakarta on 15 July 2024\", \"time\": \"07:15\", \"locality\": \"BANDAR UDARA ISKANDAR (PANGKALAN BUN)\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-17\", \"text\": \"ETD: 10.25 by Batik Air ID6303 to Semarang on 17 July 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"BANDAR UDARA ISKANDAR (PANGKALAN BUN)\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5167120,'515','OSCAR BUSTOS',30783,201490,'3D2N Semarang - Yogyakarta / B. Gallery Prawirotaman (DOUBEL Superior Room + Extra Bed)','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-07-17','2024-07-19','Guio','Wiwik',3,'Persons (3 / Triple-extra bed)',11700000.00,'D1 : Arrival at Semarang Airport - Borobudur Temple tour incl. Mendut and Pawon - Transfer to Jogja Welcome to the cradle of Indonesian culture, Yogyakarta. A tourist destination for its ancient palaces, temples, batik workshops, gamelan music orchestras, court dances and wayang puppet shows. Upon your arrival in Semarang airport a representative of come2indonesia will be waiting for you with a sign indicating your name to start exploring this special city. We will start by heading towards Borobudur Temple (Candi Borobudur), the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. We will tour around the temple, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano has been producing during its history. After visiting one of the most important Buddhist temples in Southeast Asia, we continue our journey to the Mendut temple and Pawon temple. And then, we will take you to Jogjakarta. D2 : Jogjakarta City Tour visit Sultan Palace, Watercastle and Bird Market - Visit Prambanan Temple You will enjoy a well-deserved breakfast at the hotel and we will start by heading towards Keraton known as the Sultan’s Palace. The palace is a complex building two centuries old, located in the heart of the city. You will hear the song of the “freedom” of the birds in the bird market, we will visit the “Water Castle” that occupies the highest part at the northern end of the vast complex of Taman Sari, Malioboro Street, main street of Yogyakarta, with its merchants, horse carriages, taxi-bikes and markets. After this visit we go to Candi Prambanan, the temple of the Hinduists and classified as a World Heritage Site by Unesco since 1991. The built of this temple was finished around the year 856 to commemorate the victory of the descendant Sanjaya of Siva, Rikai Pikatan on the last sovereign Sailendra of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to the Trimurti, the expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the destroyer. An incredible experience that will make the hours fly by. After this unforgettable day, we will take you back to your hotel. D3 : Transfer to Yogyakarta International Airport You will enjoy a well-deserved breakfast at the hotel and according to the time of your flight, we will pick you up to take you to the airport and take the flight to your next destination. End of our services. Thank you very much for exploring Yogyakarta by the hand of Come2indonesia.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-17\", \"text\": \"ETA: 11.25 by Batik Air ID6303 from Pangkalan Bun on 17 July 2024\", \"time\": \"11:25\", \"locality\": \"Bandar Udara Jenderal Ahmad Yani (Semarang)\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-19\", \"text\": \"ETD: 14.00 by Lion Air JT566 to Denpasar on 19 July 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Bandar Udara Internasional Yogyakarta\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5167133,'515','OSCAR BUSTOS',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-19','2024-07-19','Guio','Wiwik',1,'Persons (1-3)',420000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-19\", \"text\": \"ETA: 16.25 by Lion Air JT566 from Yogyakarta on 19 July 2024\", \"time\": \"16:25\", \"locality\": \"Airport Ngurah Rai (Domestic)\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-19\", \"text\": \"Jl. Suweta, Bentuyung Sakti, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571, Phone: (0361) 2091788\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Visesa Ubud Resort\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5167135,'514','Mr. Chetan Dalichand Fulchand Shah',31015,203230,'2D1N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Tour','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-07-12','2024-07-13','Melysa','Praba',5,'Persons (5)',7440000.00,NULL,NULL,'Food Restriction: All the guest is Vegetarian, they also don’t eat Eggs or Fish','{\"date\": \"2024-07-12\", \"text\": \"12 July 2024 ETA 10:00AM by ID6134 from Pangkalan Bun\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Juanda International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-13\", \"text\": \"13 July 2024 ETD 15:25PM by JT910 to Denpasar\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Juanda International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5167146,'515','OSCAR BUSTOS',30985,203055,'Two Bedroom Pool Villa','Confirmed',NULL,5,'2024-07-19','2024-07-24','Guio','Wiwik',1,'Double + Twin',29700000.00,'This villa has one master bedroom plus a second bedroom. It comes with a generous living and dining area, shadowed by pergolas overlooking the infinity pools. Guests enjoy a flat-screen cable TV, an iPod dock, a minibar, a coffee machine and a personal safe. It\'s furnished with a desk, a sofa and a dining table. The bathroom comes with a bath, a shower, a hairdryer and free toiletries. Guests enjoy free daily permaculture course of making soil bed, composting and planting. Guests enjoy 30% discount on spa treatments',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5167148,'515','OSCAR BUSTOS',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route (Taman Ayun-Jatiluwih-Ulundanu Beratan-Tanah Lot)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-20','2024-07-20','Guio','Wiwik',3,'Persons (3)',2160000.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-20\", \"text\": \"Jl. Suweta, Bentuyung Sakti, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571, Phone: (0361) 2091788\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"Visesa Ubud Resort\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Visesa Ubud Resort\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5167153,'515','OSCAR BUSTOS',30508,202894,'Kehen Temple - Pengelipuran - Kintamani','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-21','2024-07-21','Guio','Wiwik',3,'Persons (3)',1872000.00,'Our wonderful tour starts from Kehen Temple. It is an ancient Hindu temple complex boasting unique architectural features. The staircases reaching from the ground to temple courtyard are carved sandstone mythical animal and Balinese folklore figure statues and also the central vestibule. The temple’s walls are also ornate with Chinese porcelain plates, which are a tribute to the historical relations between the local Bali kingdom and China. Afterwards, we continue to Penglipuran, a village that succeeded in preserving its 75-hectare bamboo forest located in the northern part of the village. Members of this village have a strong commitment to the system of \'Ayahan Desa\' - a philosophy committed to respecting the land on which the village stands. To concludes the day, we stop by at Tukad Cepung Waterfall. Well-guarded by the circular cliffs, this waterfall is difficult to locate for the first time visitor. The circular cliffs give you the feeling of being in a cave, while the open sky right from where the waterfall emerges, gives you the most enchanting view. The sunlight falls on the glistering waterfall creating a rainbow, which feels as though it is projected right up to you. If you have never seen water flowing from the sky, then this would be your chance! After spending your time there, we go back to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-21\", \"text\": \"Jl. Suweta, Bentuyung Sakti, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571, Phone: (0361) 2091788\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"Visesa Ubud Resort\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Visesa Ubud Resort\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5167209,'514','Mr. Chetan Dalichand Fulchand Shah',30673,200559,'Deluxe Room + 1 Extra Bed','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-12','2024-07-13','Melysa','Praba',2,'Double + Twin',3360000.00,'Designed to capture nature vibes. Slide open the door to your private terrace to let in the fresh mountain air and relax.',NULL,'Food Restriction: All the guest is Vegetarian, they also don’t eat Eggs or Fish','{\"date\": \"2024-07-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5167210,'516','Mr. Alberto Gil Miron',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-26','2024-07-27','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',784000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. - Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK–IN','{\"date\": \"2024-07-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5167216,'516','Mr. Alberto Gil Miron',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-07-27','2024-07-29','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',10080000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-07-27\", \"text\": \"ETA 07.15 by Batik Air ID6202 from Jakarta on 27 Jul\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pangkalan Bun Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-29\", \"text\": \"ETD 10.25 by Batik Air ID6303 to Semarang on 29 Jul\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5167224,'516','Mr. Alberto Gil Miron',30783,214536,'3D2N Semarang - Yogyakarta / C. Ayaartta (Deluxe Room)','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-07-29','2024-07-31','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2 / Double)',7560000.00,'D1 : Arrival at Semarang Airport - Borobudur Temple tour incl. Mendut and Pawon - Transfer to Jogja Welcome to the cradle of Indonesian culture, Yogyakarta. A tourist destination for its ancient palaces, temples, batik workshops, gamelan music orchestras, court dances and wayang puppet shows. Upon your arrival in Semarang airport a representative of come2indonesia will be waiting for you with a sign indicating your name to start exploring this special city. We will start by heading towards Borobudur Temple (Candi Borobudur), the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. We will tour around the temple, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano has been producing during its history. After visiting one of the most important Buddhist temples in Southeast Asia, we continue our journey to the Mendut temple and Pawon temple. And then, we will take you to Jogjakarta. D2 : Jogjakarta City Tour visit Sultan Palace, Watercastle and Bird Market - Visit Prambanan Temple You will enjoy a well-deserved breakfast at the hotel and we will start by heading towards Keraton known as the Sultan’s Palace. The palace is a complex building two centuries old, located in the heart of the city. You will hear the song of the “freedom” of the birds in the bird market, we will visit the “Water Castle” that occupies the highest part at the northern end of the vast complex of Taman Sari, Malioboro Street, main street of Yogyakarta, with its merchants, horse carriages, taxi-bikes and markets. After this visit we go to Candi Prambanan, the temple of the Hinduists and classified as a World Heritage Site by Unesco since 1991. The built of this temple was finished around the year 856 to commemorate the victory of the descendant Sanjaya of Siva, Rikai Pikatan on the last sovereign Sailendra of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to the Trimurti, the expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the destroyer. An incredible experience that will make the hours fly by. After this unforgettable day, we will take you back to your hotel. D3 : Transfer to Yogyakarta International Airport You will enjoy a well-deserved breakfast at the hotel and according to the time of your flight, we will pick you up to take you to the airport and take the flight to your next destination. End of our services. Thank you very much for exploring Yogyakarta by the hand of Come2indonesia.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-29\", \"text\": \"ETA 11.25 by Batik Air ID6303 from Pangkalan Bun on 29 Jul\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Semarang Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-31\", \"text\": \"ETD 13.30 by Garuda Indonesia GA0252 to Denpasar on 31 Jul\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Yogyakarta International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5167225,'515','OSCAR BUSTOS',30508,207379,'Ubud to Padang Bai','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-24','2024-07-24','Guio','Wiwik',1,'Persons (1-3)',600000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-24\", \"text\": \"Jl. Suweta, Bentuyung Sakti, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone: (0361) 2091788\", \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": \"Desa Visesa Ubud\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-24\", \"text\": \"ETD: 08.00 to Gili Air\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Office Bluewater Express\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5167227,'514','Mr. Chetan Dalichand Fulchand Shah',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-13','2024-07-13','Melysa','Praba',5,'Persons (5)',4200000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-13\", \"text\": \"13 July 2024 ETA 17:25PM by JT910 from Surabaya\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-13\", \"text\": \"Rama Phala Resort & Spa Jl.Raya Pengosekan, Ubud Bali\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5167233,'516','Mr. Alberto Gil Miron',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-31','2024-07-31','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (1-3)',672000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-31\", \"text\": \"ETA 16.05 by Garuda Indonesia GA0252 on 31 Jul\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-31\", \"text\": \"Jl. Suweta, Bentuyung Sakti, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Visesa Ubud Resort\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5167239,'514','Mr. Chetan Dalichand Fulchand Shah',31298,205278,'Deluxe Room + 1 Extra Bed','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-07-13','2024-07-15','Melysa','Praba',2,'Double + Twin',5520000.00,'Our deluxe rooms at Rama Phala are setting with the garden picturesque views. Take a moment on your verandah as we put the Ubud’s flora on full display. Enjoy the nonchalance of Ubud from your authentic Ubud resort ambiance and airy deluxe room. Not to mention, you’ll find our curated eco-friendly amenities, signature scent, Tumanggal fabric on your bed and balinese artwork that reminds you of Ubud.',NULL,'Food restriction: All the guest is Vegetarian, they also don’t eat Eggs or Fish A valid voucher is required prior to guest’s arrival or upon guest’s check in. Failure to provide a valid voucher before guest’s departure will be automatically switched to normal published rate and payment will be on guest personal account.','{\"date\": \"2024-07-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5167250,'514','Mr. Chetan Dalichand Fulchand Shah',31298,205278,'Deluxe Room + 1 Extra Bed','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-07-15','2024-07-18','Melysa','Praba',2,'Double + Twin',9360000.00,'Our deluxe rooms at Rama Phala are setting with the garden picturesque views. Take a moment on your verandah as we put the Ubud’s flora on full display. Enjoy the nonchalance of Ubud from your authentic Ubud resort ambiance and airy deluxe room. Not to mention, you’ll find our curated eco-friendly amenities, signature scent, Tumanggal fabric on your bed and balinese artwork that reminds you of Ubud.',NULL,'Food restriction: All the guest is Vegetarian. They also don\'t eat Eggs or Fish A valid voucher is required prior to guest’s arrival or upon guest’s check in. Failure to provide a valid voucher before guest’s departure will be automatically switched to normal published rate and payment will be on guest personal account.','{\"date\": \"2024-07-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29');
INSERT INTO `booked_products` VALUES (5167268,'514','Mr. Chetan Dalichand Fulchand Shah',30508,202864,'Ubud and Surrounding Tour','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-14','2024-07-14','Melysa','Praba',5,'Persons (5)',3330000.00,'We will be picking you up from your hotel to enjoy the wealth of art in Ubud. First we will visit Monkey Forest; the Ubud Monkey Forest is a nature reserve and temple complex in Ubud, Bali. It houses approximately 340 Crab-eating Macaque (Macacafas cicularis) monkeys. The Monkey Forest contains the Pura Dalem Agung Padangtegal temple as well as a \"Holy Spring\" bathing temple and another temple used for cremation ceremonies. Next we go to Ubud Traditional Art Market where the existence is not far different from other markets available in the tourism area. This market as a society economics center of Ubud and it is apposite to the existence of Ubud Empire that is called Puri Saren. Our last destination is Gua Gajah (Elephant Cave). This cave is built at crevasse edge from the federation of 2 rills that is called Pangkung River, where the irrigation is mixed with Petanu River flow. The word of Gua Gajah is anticipated coming from the word of Lwa Gajah, the name of Buddhist Temple or hermitage for Buddhist monk. There is a relief which is almost looking like the form of mountain on the entrance of this cave. It was carved many designed on the relief like grove with the stick, close leaf, animal for example forest pig, tortoise and specters. The cave mouth is decorated by the bas-relief with the eye turn around to the right or west side. At the end of tour we will transferred back you to the hotel.',NULL,'Ubud Market - Puri Ubud - Monkey Forest Food restriction: All the guest is Vegetarian, they also don’t eat Eggs or Fish','{\"date\": \"2024-07-14\", \"text\": \"Rama Phala Resort & Spa Jl.Raya Pengosekan, Ubud Bali\", \"time\": \"13:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-14\", \"text\": \"Rama Phala Resort & Spa Jl.Raya Pengosekan, Ubud Bali\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5167277,'516','Mr. Alberto Gil Miron',30985,212179,'Jungle Suite Room with Private Balcony','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-07-31','2024-08-03','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',7560000.00,'Escape the hustle and bustle of everyday life and immerse yourself in the beauty of nature with our Jungle Suite with Private Balcony. Located in the heart of the lush tropical rainforest, this Suite offers a unique opportunity to immerse yourself in nature while still enjoying all the comforts of modern living. The real highlight of this room category is the private balcony overlooking the jungle canopy. Relax in your own personal paradise as you listen to the sounds of nature, watch the birds playing in the trees, and breathe in the fresh air while taking in the breathtaking views.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-31\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5167283,'514','Mr. Chetan Dalichand Fulchand Shah',30508,202891,'Contact with Nature Tour (Pura Luhur Batukaru - Lake Buyan - Munduk Waterfall(','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-16','2024-07-16','Melysa','Praba',5,'Persons (5)',3450000.00,'Deferent than the other tours! This tour will quietly finding you in the fullness of nature. First we will explore Pura Luhur Batukaru. Pura Luhur Batukaru Temple is one of the six directional temples on Bali that are believed to protect the island and its people from evil spirits. Pura Luhur Batukaru protects Bali from the West and was originally built in the 11th century. Pura Luhur Batukaru is one of Bali’s biggest Hindu temples, but because it is off the main tourist trail, sees fewer visitors than many of the other temples. Its peaceful setting amid rainforest at the foot of Mount Batukaru enhances its stunning Balinese architecture. We continue to reach the terrace rice fields Jatiluwih. Jatiluwih is a favorite tourist destination in Bali famous with the beautiful rice terrace unfolding from the foot of mountain until the coastal side. With the beautiful view as according to its name from Jati and Luwih, where Jati mean really and Luwih meaning especial, good, and beautiful or the equivalent. The local paddies are planted in this place look typically of the high relative size plant if it is compared with other pre-eminent paddy planted by most farmers in Bali. You’ll get to explore different parts of the terraces, jump over rivers. We continue our way to the Lake Buyan. We will see one of the most beautiful nature and vegetation scenery on the island. Buyan Lake is a smallest lake in Bali located in the plateau area with cool weather covers it. It is situated in the high land with hill and rain forest surrounds it. Since the location in the plateau area, the fog is usually blanketing the area. This lake can be seen from the top of hill which is called Asah Gobleg. The western end of Lake Buyan, we will start to see the sister lake of Buyan, the Lake Tamblingan. If we follow the road it will bring us closer and closer to Lake Tamblingan, or if we take direction to the right at the following junction at the end of the road, we will arrive in Munduk village, a village rich with coffee plantations. And our final destination is Munduk Waterfalls. This waterfall is a beautiful tourist destination in north part of Bali. Waterfall voice around the charming nature was amazing and it was the separate attraction which can be enjoyed by each visitor who comes to visit. In order to visit the waterfall, all visitors will follow the walkway down until the spot point.',NULL,'1D Pura Luhur Batukaru - Lake Buyan - Munduk Waterfall Food Restriction: All the guest is Vegetarian, they also don’t eat Eggs or Fish','{\"date\": \"2024-07-16\", \"text\": \"Rama Phala Resort & Spa Jl.Raya Pengosekan, Ubud Bali\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-16\", \"text\": \"Rama Phala Resort & Spa Jl.Raya Pengosekan, Ubud Bali\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5167284,'514','Mr. Chetan Dalichand Fulchand Shah',30508,207262,'Ubud to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-18','2024-07-18','Melysa','Praba',5,'Persons (5)',4200000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-18\", \"text\": \"Rama Phala Resort & Spa Jl.Raya Pengosekan, Ubud Bali\", \"time\": \"04:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-18\", \"text\": \"ETD 08:00AM by ID6333 to Labuan Bajo\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5167437,'516','Mr. Alberto Gil Miron',30508,202881,'Jatiluwih Rice Terrace - Banyumala Twin Waterfall - Wanagiri Hidden Hill','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-01','2024-08-01','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',1579200.00,'We begin the tour from a beautiful rice terrace of Jatiluwih. Unfolding from the foot of mountain until the coastal side, it is one of places in Bali with the beautiful view, as according to its name “Jati” and “Luwih”, where Jati mean really and Luwih meaning especial, good, and beautiful or the equivalent. The local paddies are planted in this place look typically of the high relative size plant if it is compared with other pre-eminent paddy planted by most farmers in Bali. Stroll around the area for a while and take a nice pictures, before we continue to Banyumala Twin Waterfall. The waterfall is special in that there are two flows of water to be seen, hence the name ‘twin’. Water cascades down steep rocks with gorgeous greenery surrounding them. Here you can take a refreshing dip in the plunge pool at the bottom - dunk your head and listen to the sounds of the water crashing down. After the refreshment, we conclude our day by heading to Wanagiri Hidden Hill. This hill has a charm of beauty that can make anyone who saw her feel hypnotized and fell in love Beautiful natural paintings depicting the beautiful mountains, the beautiful green trees, and the expanse of the lake can be seen clearly from this place. In addition to the panoramic view, cool and fresh air is also an added value that makes this tourist area worth visiting. Take photos and enjoy the scenery and then we head back to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-01\", \"text\": \"Jl. Suweta, Bentuyung Sakti, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Visesa Ubud Resort\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5167445,'516','Mr. Alberto Gil Miron',30508,202889,'Tamblingan Jungle Trek - Ulun Danu Temple','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-02','2024-08-02','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',2105600.00,'Today we will explore the nature of Buyan and Tamblingan lake in our lovely village, it will help you to escape from the crowds and fell the Nature atmosphere of the real jungle of Bali. We will pick you at your hotel at 07:30 AM and we drive to Tamblingan lake. Arrive in the trekking start point, we will have an explanation about the trekking. We will start the trek by entering a lush protected rain-forest area with giant old tress, animal such as macaque, black giant squirrel, birds and old legend temple inside in the Jungle. You will then walk along the shore of this lake situated in the caldera of an extinct Jungle Mountain. Our trekking guide will explain more detail about plants and living creatures in the jungle. This tour also combine with a session of thirty five minutes exploring the Tamblingan lake by dugout canoe to finishing point. Finish with trekking we will drop you to your hotel but we will make a stop at Ulun Danu Temple. Ulun Danu Temple Bratan, the famous temple stands on a small promontory located in the shore of Lake Bratan and has beautiful scenery with this lake and the mountains as backdrop sight.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-02\", \"text\": \"Jl. Suweta, Bentuyung Sakti, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"07:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Visesa Ubud Resort\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5167448,'516','Mr. Alberto Gil Miron',30508,215968,'Git Git Waterfall - Tanah Lot Temple','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-03','2024-08-03','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',1792000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Visesa Ubud Resort\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-03\", \"text\": \"Gg. Mertasari, Pecatu, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sal Secret Spot\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5167451,'516','Mr. Alberto Gil Miron',30508,202897,'Uluwatu Temple and Kecak Dance','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-04','2024-08-04','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',2556000.00,'This half-day tour, is an exciting tour package to visit Padang-Padang Beach, Uluwatu Temple, the famous Balinese Hindu Temple in south part of Bali with breathtaking view of sunset and Indian Ocean. Uluwatu Temple is one of Balinese Hindu Temples located right on the petrifying hill with the crevasse exist in the right and left side. Uluwatu Temple is one of Sad Khayangan (6 biggest temple in Bali) owns magnificent view of the Indian Ocean and sunset as a backdrop. This temple is very amazing where the location is right on the narrow peninsula with deep seawater under it. This tour package is combined with the spectacular Balinese traditional dance performance of Kecak Dance. Balinese Kecak Dance is a spectacular traditional dance with the group of people playing this dance with fire game. It is very exciting and unique dance due to the sound of gamelan is not using the normal gamelan but use their mouth. The dancers make the compact choir with the exquisite dance movement that is one of this dance features. After the dance we returned back to the hotel or seafood restaurant in Jimbaran.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-04\", \"text\": \"Gg. Mertasari, Pecatu, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361\", \"time\": \"16:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sal Secret Spot\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5167460,'516','Mr. Alberto Gil Miron',30621,200788,'Standard Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-08-03','2024-08-05','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',3215520.00,'The standard rooms in main Sal building are an oasis of tranquility, with garden and pool views they will offer you the comfort and eclectic beauty of Indonesian and Mediterranean inspired features. With comfortable beds and lovely mosquito nets, large bathrooms the charming standard rooms represent a great option for your stay. Room amenities; Wireless Internet Access, Air-conditioning, Mini Bar, Safety Box. Located in the stunning Bukit region, this intimate eco boutique resort is one of the best kept secrets in Bali, offering you the best service and beautiful amenities such as our gorgeous swimming pools.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5167462,'516','Mr. Alberto Gil Miron',30508,216161,'Uluwatu to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-05','2024-08-05','Guio','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',392000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-05\", \"text\": \"Gg. Mertasari, Pecatu, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361\", \"time\": \"05:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sal Secret Spot\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-05\", \"text\": \"ETD 08.00 by Batik Air ID6333 to Labuan Bajo on 05 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5167470,'516','Mr. Alberto Gil Miron',31083,212375,'3D2N LOB Rinca - Padar - Komodo Island Tour (Superior Standard Boat)','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-05','2024-08-07','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2-3)',39569600.00,'TOUR ITINERARY Highlights: Menjarite, Kelor, Strawberry Rock, Kalong, Rinca, Padar, Komodo Island, Pink Beach, Taka Makassar, Manta Point, Kanawa, B.Cermin Mirror Cave DAY 1 : DENPASAR - LABUAN BAJO - MENJARITE - KELOR - KALONG ISLAND Arrival at Komodo Airport in Labuan Bajo west Flores, meeting service with our tour guide and transfer to the pier of Labuan Bajo for Rinca Island. It’s about 2 hours sail to the island of Komodo Dragon, stop at Menjarite island for snorkeling then continue to Rinca island-the Island of Komodo dragon, you will find not just e Dragons but also many wild animals like, deer, wild buffalo, long-tailed macaque and wild pig also numerous of birds. Keep your eyes look up as sometime you will find the young Komodo dragons on the trees. A local ranger will lead you through this natural preservation. Late afternoon sailing directly to Kalong Rinca Island to see the hundreds of fling foxes set out from the mangrove tree at 06-07pm, the lovely sunset from the boat trip really enjoyable. Lunch and dinner on boat. Meals : Lunch - Dinner DAY 2 : KALONG - PADAR - KOMODO - PINK BEACH - MANTA POINT - TAKA MAKASSAR - SEBAYUR After having breakfast in your boat, heading to Padar Island, taking trek to Padar Island until having the top view point to get breathtaking scenery of three bays around, Padar Island hike in Komodo has some of the most amazing views in Indonesia, trek to downhill and back to the Boat for sailing directly to Loh Liang – the Ranger station in Komodo Island. By passing through many small islands, After registering start to take basic trekking to see the GIANT RIZARD / KOMODO DRAGON and other wild animals as: Timor deer, wild pig, wild chicken and many variously of tropical bird. Please keep your look at any directions as sometimes you will also find young Komodo dragon hanging over the trees. A local ranger will be led you during the trek. Return to the boat on to Pink beach for snorkeling, swimming and relaxing. It is really spectacular and unspoiled coral reef and many color fish. This is one of best side for snorkeling diving. Sail toward MANTA POINT to exploring Huge Mantas by snorkeling even watching from your boat trip (can’t be guaranteed if weather is not good, like wave and current are strongly) visit also the taka Makassar its really tiny island with white sand beach really enjoyable to relaxing or beach walking then heading to Sebayur island, overnight dinner on boat. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner DAY 3 : SEBAYUR - KANAWA ISLANDS - LABUAN BAJO - DENPASAR After breakfast on the boat, taking swimming, snorkeling and relaxing as well at seraya and Kanawa. Then back to Labuan Bajo to continue your next excursion with visiting the Batu Cermin (Mirror Stone) Cave. The grotto is 75 by 75 meters large, and contains stalactites and stalagmites. Some tunnels are narrow and dark but in others sunlight falls. Then local market before taking you to the airport for flight to Denpasar. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Attention: The itinerary is subject to change due to the weather, tide level and operating conditions without prior notice.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-05\", \"text\": \"ETA 09.10 by Batik Air ID6333 from Denpasar on 05 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Komodo International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-07\", \"text\": \"ETD 13.35 by Batik Air ID6330 to Denpasar on 07 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5167494,'516','Mr. Alberto Gil Miron',30571,202567,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-07','2024-08-08','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',1372000.00,'Located at the Second Floor, 35 sqm comfort living with a touch of Balinese style featuring completed fitting, Cable TV, a fancy bathroom comprises rain shower and good quality amenities. Also dedicated Wi-Fi Access to complete your day.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5167507,'516','Mr. Alberto Gil Miron',30508,212305,'Kuta to Sanur','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-08','2024-08-08','Guio','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',280000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": \"Jl. Kartika Plaza No.127, Kuta, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361\", \"time\": \"07:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"The Vira Bali Boutique Hotel & Suite\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": \"ETD 09.00 to Nusa Penida by Maruti Fast Boat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sanur Harbour\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5167530,'516','Mr. Alberto Gil Miron',32964,218226,'Deluxe Suite Room','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-08-08','2024-08-12','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',9552063.36,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5167553,'516','Mr. Alberto Gil Miron',30508,207269,'Sanur to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-12','2024-08-12','Guio','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',280000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-12\", \"text\": \"ETA 08.00 by Maruti Fast Boat from Nusa Penida\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sanur Harbour\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-12\", \"text\": \"ETD 12.15 by Citilink QG667 to Jakarta on 12 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5167586,'464','Eric Olalla & party',30714,200657,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-18','2024-07-19',NULL,'Eddy',2,'Double + Double',3326400.00,'Room area : 24 square meters. Our Deluxe Rooms are designed for modern travellers who seek comfort on a short stay in Ijen area. With its spacious rooms of 24 meters square with either a king size or deluxe twin beds, maximum occupancy is 2 adults. Equipped with one shower bathroom, LED TV 32\" with satelite channel, and air conditioning.',NULL,'Please send the guarantee letter/voucher following procedure below: - 30 (thirty) days reservation notice prior to the arrival date for Normal Period. - 45 (forty-five) days reservation notice prior to the arrival date for High Season (June 1th to August 31st) and Peak Season (D-3 to D+4 Idul Fitri (April 18 - 25th, 2023 and December 21st, 2023 to January 5th, 2024) period. - Otherwise, the cancellation policy will be applied.','{\"date\": \"2024-07-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5168260,'514','Mr. Chetan Dalichand Fulchand Shah',31083,214905,'Padar & Komodo Jurassic Adventure 3D2N / A. Traditional Boat (Standard Cabin - Superior)','Confirmed','SEB-FLORES2',3,'2024-07-18','2024-07-20','Melysa','Praba',5,'Persons (5)',63915000.00,'Explore the islands of Padar and Komodo on this amazing adventure! Welcome to the ultimate adventure tour that will transport you back in time to the prehistoric era, where ancient creatures roam the Earth and untamed landscapes captivated the imagination. Get ready for the Jurassic Adventure of Padar and Komodo, a 3-day, 2-night journey that will leave you in awe and excited. We\'ll take you in search of the star of the park, the Komodo dragons. During the tour, we\'ll also make a stop at Padar Island, where we\'ll enjoy spectacular views from the highest point, where you can see the three crescent-shaped beaches that surround the island. You\'ll sleep the 2 nights on the boat so make sure you don\'t get seasick. Also, don\'t forget to take lots of photos so that you will be the envy of all your friends! DAY 1 : LABUAN BAJO - MENJARITE - KELOR - KALONG ISLAND Welcome to the Island of Flores! Arrival at Komodo Airport in Labuan Bajo in the West of Flores Island. Our team will be waiting for you to start this adventure. After a drive of only 15 minutes, we\'ll board one of our traditional wooden boats from Komodo National Park. During this first day aboard a traditional boat, we\'ll visit the stunning islands of Menjarite and Kalong. First, we will sail through crystal clear waters for about 3 hours, towards Menjarite Island, where we will be able to snorkel and relax. Get your snorkeling gear ready and dive into an underwater world full of colors and life! In the afternoon, we will sail to the mysterious Kalong Island, known as the home of the flying foxes. Here you will see thousands of flying foxes that come out of the mangroves at sunset time in search of food on the Island of Flores. Just at sunset they will take flight overtaking the boats of the National Park, a true spectacle of nature. The sunset in Komodo is perhaps one of the most beautiful in Indonesia and you can enjoy it on board your boat. We\'ll end the day enjoying a delicious dinner prepared by the crew and spend the night on the boat. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : A. Traditional Boat ( Standard Cabin - Superior ) DAY 2 : PADAR - KOMODO - PINK BEACH - MANTA POINT - SEBAYUR ISLAND After breakfast on board, we set sail for Padar Island. Get your trekking boots ready for a hike to the famous view of the three bays, a panorama that will take your breath away. After enjoying this postcard image, we\'ll continue directly to Loh Liang, the Ranger station on Komodo Island. We will pass around many small islands and after a period of sailing, we will arrive at the pier of Komodo Island. After checking in, we will do a gentle trek to see the Komodo dragon and other wildlife such as: Timor deer, wild boar, wild chicks and many species of tropical birds. A local ranger will guide you during the hike. Back at the boat, we\'ll sail to the iconic Pink Beach. Here you can dive into its crystal-clear waters to enjoy a spectacular underwater world, with pristine coral reefs and a variety of multicolored fish. It is also an ideal place to relax, sunbathe and swim. We will then sail to Manta Point to explore giant mantas by snorkeling, even seeing them from the boat (the encounter with the mantas cannot be guaranteed if the weather is not good or there are strong waves and currents). Lunch will be provided on board. In the late afternoon, we will sail to the island of Sebayur where we can relax after this day on board. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : A. Traditional Boat ( Standard Cabin - Superior ) DAY 3 : KANAWA ISLAND - LABUAN BAJO - AIRPORT Komodo National Park is much more than dragons. You will be amazed by the clarity of its waters and beaches of white sand and corals. After breakfast on the boat, we will sail to Kanawa to snorkel and relax by sunbathing on the beach. Then, we continue to Labuan Bajo airport to take the flight to your next destination. Thank you for enjoying this tour of Padar and Komodo with Come2Indonesia. We look forward to seeing you on another excursion with us. Sampai Jumpa! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Food Restriction: All the guest is Vegetarian, they also don’t eat Eggs or Fish','{\"date\": \"2024-07-18\", \"text\": \"18 July 2024 ETA 09:10AM by ID6333 from Denpasar\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Labuan Bajo\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-20\", \"text\": \"Bintang Flores Hotel Jl. Pantai Pede Labuan Bajo - Manggarai Barat - NTT\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Labuan Bajo\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5168282,'514','Mr. Chetan Dalichand Fulchand Shah',30699,203281,'Deluxe Room + 1 Extra Bed + 1 Way Airport Transfer','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-20','2024-07-21','Melysa','Praba',2,'Double',4800000.00,'The hotel offers 92 Deluxe Rooms with 32 square meters of room size overlooking the garden and the beach. This room features stylish furniture, individual controlled air- conditioning, standing shower with hot and cold water, tea and coffee making facilities, safe deposit box, IDD telephone and cable TV, Free Wi-Fi internet in all room categories and hotel\'s public areas.',NULL,'Exchange vouchers will be honored only if booking agent has established and maintain approved credit facilities with Bintang Flores Hotel. Food Restriction: All the guest is Vegetarian, they also don’t eat Eggs or Fish','{\"date\": \"2024-07-20\", \"text\": \"Bintang Flores Hotel Jl. Pantai Pede Labuan Bajo - Manggarai Barat - NTT\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Labuan Bajo\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-21\", \"text\": \"ETD 09:50AM by ID6332 to Denpasar\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Airport Komodo\"}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5168312,'514','Mr. Chetan Dalichand Fulchand Shah',31007,203162,'Suite 1 Bedroom Villa Private Pool + Extra Bed','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-07-21','2024-07-25','Melysa','Praba',2,'Double',23296000.00,'At 30 square meters with 4 units available. This suite has a electric kettle, private pool and cable TV.',NULL,'Food Restriction: All the guest is Vegetarian, they also don’t eat Eggs or Fish','{\"date\": \"2024-07-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5168322,'519','Mrs. Tanit Solana',30783,213061,'Transfer from Semarang Airport to Yogyakarta Hotel with Stop in Borobudur','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-14','2024-07-14','Jacob','Praba',1,'Per Car',960000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-14\", \"text\": \"ETA 14:20PM by IN197 from Pangkalan Bun\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Bandar Udara Jendra Ahmad Yani\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-14\", \"text\": \"Puri Pangeran Hotel Jl. Masjid No.7, Purwokinanti, Pakualaman, Kota Yogyakarta, Daerah Istimewa Yogyakarta\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Yogyakarta\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5168709,'520','ANA MIGUEZ X2',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-15','2024-10-15','Guio','Eddy',1,'Persons (1-3)',392000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-15\", \"text\": \"Arrival / 150ct2024 / 22:20 from DUBAI EK 398 BY Emirates\", \"time\": \"22:20\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-15\", \"text\": \"THE ARTINI DIJIWA UBUD \\\"ADDRESS : Jl. Raya Pengosekan Ubud, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : (0361) 972385\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5168719,'520','ANA MIGUEZ X2',30705,201147,'Premier Room Garden View','Confirmed',NULL,5,'2024-10-15','2024-10-20','Guio','Eddy',1,'Double',6244000.00,'Get back to nature in one of our Premier Garden View suites. These spacious, light-filled rooms have beautiful Balinese double doors that can be closed to create a cool air-conditioned space or opened to merge indoor and outdoor living. The balconies overlook the resort’s lush gardens, which are awash in tropical flowers and foliage.',NULL,'HONEYMOON','{\"date\": \"2024-10-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5168752,'520','ANA MIGUEZ X2',30508,202881,'Taman Ayun,Jatiluwih Rice Terrace,Ulun danu Bratan,Pura luhur batukaru','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-16','2024-10-16','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (2)',1579200.00,'We begin the tour from a beautiful rice terrace of Jatiluwih. Unfolding from the foot of mountain until the coastal side, it is one of places in Bali with the beautiful view, as according to its name “Jati” and “Luwih”, where Jati mean really and Luwih meaning especial, good, and beautiful or the equivalent. The local paddies are planted in this place look typically of the high relative size plant if it is compared with other pre-eminent paddy planted by most farmers in Bali. Stroll around the area for a while and take a nice pictures, before we continue to Banyumala Twin Waterfall. The waterfall is special in that there are two flows of water to be seen, hence the name ‘twin’. Water cascades down steep rocks with gorgeous greenery surrounding them. Here you can take a refreshing dip in the plunge pool at the bottom - dunk your head and listen to the sounds of the water crashing down. After the refreshment, we conclude our day by heading to Wanagiri Hidden Hill. This hill has a charm of beauty that can make anyone who saw her feel hypnotized and fell in love Beautiful natural paintings depicting the beautiful mountains, the beautiful green trees, and the expanse of the lake can be seen clearly from this place. In addition to the panoramic view, cool and fresh air is also an added value that makes this tourist area worth visiting. Take photos and enjoy the scenery and then we head back to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-16\", \"text\": \"THE ARTINI DIJIWA UBUD \\\"ADDRESS : Jl. Raya Pengosekan Ubud, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : (0361) 972385\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"MEET AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-16\", \"text\": \"THE ARTINI DIJIWA UBUD \\\"ADDRESS : Jl. Raya Pengosekan Ubud, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : (0361) 972385\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5168776,'520','ANA MIGUEZ X2',30508,202894,'Tirta Empul -Templo Kehen - Pengeliburan - Cascada Tukad Cepung','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-17','2024-10-17','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (2)',1568000.00,'Our wonderful tour starts from Kehen Temple. It is an ancient Hindu temple complex boasting unique architectural features. The staircases reaching from the ground to temple courtyard are carved sandstone mythical animal and Balinese folklore figure statues and also the central vestibule. The temple’s walls are also ornate with Chinese porcelain plates, which are a tribute to the historical relations between the local Bali kingdom and China. Afterwards, we continue to Penglipuran, a village that succeeded in preserving its 75-hectare bamboo forest located in the northern part of the village. Members of this village have a strong commitment to the system of \'Ayahan Desa\' - a philosophy committed to respecting the land on which the village stands. To concludes the day, we stop by at Tukad Cepung Waterfall. Well-guarded by the circular cliffs, this waterfall is difficult to locate for the first time visitor. The circular cliffs give you the feeling of being in a cave, while the open sky right from where the waterfall emerges, gives you the most enchanting view. The sunlight falls on the glistering waterfall creating a rainbow, which feels as though it is projected right up to you. If you have never seen water flowing from the sky, then this would be your chance! After spending your time there, we go back to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-17\", \"text\": \"THE ARTINI DIJIWA UBUD \\\"ADDRESS : Jl. Raya Pengosekan Ubud, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : (0361) 972385\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"MEET AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-17\", \"text\": \"THE ARTINI DIJIWA UBUD \\\"ADDRESS : Jl. Raya Pengosekan Ubud, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : (0361) 972385\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5168792,'520','ANA MIGUEZ X2',30508,202896,'Bali Village Tour - Templo Tanah Lot','Confirmed','C2I-BALI05',1,'2024-10-18','2024-10-18','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (2)',2441600.00,'At 08.00 am, we pick you up from your hotel and start our journey to Tunjuk Village in Tabanan district. Upon arrival, you will be greeted with open arms and with the warm smiles of the locals you meet along the way. You\'ll meet in the outer courtyard of the village temple and meet your local guides. Throughout the hike you will meet people from the village involved in the tasks that keep their lives busy day in and day out. You can choose to observe or participate in them to gain a better understanding of village life. The mighty water buffalo is still used to drag the plough through the muddy rice paddies and prepare the land for planting. Or maybe you want to help with planting or harvesting, depending on the time of year. When you complete the tour in the rice paddies, you\'ll follow your guide on a path through lush gardens where villagers go about their daily chores. There are women who beat the rice with heavy mallets to remove the hooves. After lunch we leave Tunjuk Village and continue our journey to visit THE TANAH LOT. We\'ll close the visit by watching the sunset at the most famous and photographed temple in Bali. Torn from the earth on a stone pedestal sculpted by the incoming tides, the solitary black towers of Tanah Lot and the plumes of foliage spilling over the precipices, recall the delicacy of Chinese painting. The Pura Tanah Lot or the Earth Temple in the middle of the sea was built in the 16th century. At the end of the day, you\'ll be transferred to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-18\", \"text\": \"THE ARTINI DIJIWA UBUD \\\"ADDRESS : Jl. Raya Pengosekan Ubud, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : (0361) 972385\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": \"MEET AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-18\", \"text\": \"THE ARTINI DIJIWA UBUD \\\"ADDRESS : Jl. Raya Pengosekan Ubud, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : (0361) 972385\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5168812,'520','ANA MIGUEZ X2',30508,202893,'Tenganan - Tiirta Gangga -Temolo Lempuyang - Goa Lawah','Confirmed','C2I-BALI11',1,'2024-10-19','2024-10-19','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (2)',1792000.00,'At the agreed time, our guide will pick you up to start the tour in the eastern part of Bali. The first place you will visit is Goa Lawah Temple. Goa Lawah Temple consists of two names, \"Goa\" which means cave and \"Lawah\" which means bat. Several thousand bats are flying in the cave as the name suggests. With the lights fading as you go deeper inside the cave, it gives off a very strange atmosphere. From Goa Lawah, we continue our way to Lempuyang Temple. Upon arrival, the temple will greet you with its gratifying panorama that extends into infinity. On a clear, sunny day, you\'ll be able to gaze out over the mountains, Amlapura city, and Mount Agung, an incredibly magnificent sight that\'s beautiful beyond words. This portrait of heaven is beautifully framed by the Gapura Candi Bentar (the gate of the temple). Our journey continues to visit Tirta Gangga. The site is a paradise surrounded by water, with all the pools decorated with unusual statues. With its seclusion and a view of the surrounding rice paddies, Tirta Gangga is a wonderful place. At the end of the trip we go to Tenganan Village, the most famous Bali Agas (the “original” Bali people) in the city. With its characteristics, the city village is arranged in parallel along the wide main road paved with rows of cobblestones. In Tenganan, women still weave the famous Kamben Geringsing, or \"burnt cloth,\" which has the power to immunize the wearer against evil. We take a close look at what they do in their daily lives in a traditional lifestyle. From Tenganan, we will transfer you to the hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-19\", \"text\": \"THE ARTINI DIJIWA UBUD \\\"ADDRESS : Jl. Raya Pengosekan Ubud, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : (0361) 972385\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": \"MEET AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-19\", \"text\": \"THE ARTINI DIJIWA UBUD \\\"ADDRESS : Jl. Raya Pengosekan Ubud, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : (0361) 972385\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5168835,'520','ANA MIGUEZ X2',30508,202881,'Banyumala Twin Waterfall - Brahma Vihara Budha - Lovina','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-20','2024-10-20','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (2)',1579200.00,'We begin the tour from a beautiful rice terrace of Jatiluwih. Unfolding from the foot of mountain until the coastal side, it is one of places in Bali with the beautiful view, as according to its name “Jati” and “Luwih”, where Jati mean really and Luwih meaning especial, good, and beautiful or the equivalent. The local paddies are planted in this place look typically of the high relative size plant if it is compared with other pre-eminent paddy planted by most farmers in Bali. Stroll around the area for a while and take a nice pictures, before we continue to Banyumala Twin Waterfall. The waterfall is special in that there are two flows of water to be seen, hence the name ‘twin’. Water cascades down steep rocks with gorgeous greenery surrounding them. Here you can take a refreshing dip in the plunge pool at the bottom - dunk your head and listen to the sounds of the water crashing down. After the refreshment, we conclude our day by heading to Wanagiri Hidden Hill. This hill has a charm of beauty that can make anyone who saw her feel hypnotized and fell in love Beautiful natural paintings depicting the beautiful mountains, the beautiful green trees, and the expanse of the lake can be seen clearly from this place. In addition to the panoramic view, cool and fresh air is also an added value that makes this tourist area worth visiting. Take photos and enjoy the scenery and then we head back to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-20\", \"text\": \"THE ARTINI DIJIWA UBUD \\\"ADDRESS : Jl. Raya Pengosekan Ubud, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : (0361) 972385\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"MEET AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-20\", \"text\": \"FRANGIPANI BEACH HOTEL \\\"Address: Jl. Kartika 99, Kalibukbuk, Anturan, Kec. Buleleng, Singaraja, Bali 81151 Phone: (0362) 3435764\\\"\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5168845,'514','Mr. Chetan Dalichand Fulchand Shah',31973,218244,'Balinese Cooking Experience (Mebat)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-15','2024-07-15','Melysa','Praba',5,'Persons (5)',2400000.00,NULL,NULL,'Vegetarian Cooking Class Food Restriction: All the guest is Vegetarian, they also don’t eat Eggs or Fish','{\"date\": \"2024-07-15\", \"text\": \"Rama Phala Resort & Spa Jl. Raya Pengosekan, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-15\", \"text\": \"Rama Phala Resort & SpaJl. Raya Pengosekan, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5169012,'520','ANA MIGUEZ X2',30554,202023,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-21','2024-10-22','Guio','Eddy',1,'Double',985600.00,'Ground floor room with modern Balinese interior with sea view. Option of king size bed or twin beds.',NULL,'HONEYMOON','{\"date\": \"2024-10-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5169027,'520','ANA MIGUEZ X2',30508,207264,'Candidasa to Padangbai','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-22','2024-10-22','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (1-3)',1232000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-22\", \"text\": \"HOTEL GENGGONG BALI \\\"ADDRESS : Jl.Puri Bagus, Candidasa, Sengkidu, Kec. Manggis, Kabupaten Karangasem, Bali 80871 Phone : +62 (0363) 4381005\\\"\", \"time\": \"10:30\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-22\", \"text\": \"22 Oct 2024 Padang Bai (12:15) ~ Gili Trawangan (13:45)\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"PADANG BAY PORT\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5169040,'520','ANA MIGUEZ X2',31007,203159,'Grand Deluxe Room With Private Balcony','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-10-22','2024-10-25','Guio','Eddy',1,'Double',3612000.00,'At 20 square meters of room size with 10 units available. This twin/double room features a balcony, electric kettle and air conditioning.',NULL,'HONEYMOON','{\"date\": \"2024-10-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5169050,'520','ANA MIGUEZ X2',30692,204751,'Double Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-10-25','2024-10-27','Guio','Eddy',1,'Double',1680000.00,'This 36sqm room features refrigerator, coffee/tea maker, air conditioning, desk, in-room safety, television, complimentary bottled water. Bathroom amenities such as; shower, free toiletries, private bathroom and hot water. The bedroom is a double room with queen bed type. Guest can see pool from the terrace.',NULL,'HONEYMOON','{\"date\": \"2024-10-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5169090,'518','Simon Patrick ERNST',30662,212912,'(Journaway) 7D6N Medan - Bukit Lawang - Brastagi - Lake Toba','Confirmed',NULL,7,'2024-07-14','2024-07-20','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Person (1)',19829600.00,'Day-01 : AIRPORT/MEDAN - BUKIT LAWANG Arrival at Kualanamu International Airport Medan meet by our tour guide and then drive to Bukit Lawang with enroute stop at several plantations for rubber and oil palm. Arriving in Bukit Lawang check-in to hotel. Meals : - • Overnight at : Eco-lodge Bukit Lawang Cottages - Standard Room Day-02 : BUKIT LAWANG - LEUSER PARK TREKKING (B,L,D) After breakfast walking to the jungle to start a jungle trekking to explore the nature of Leuser National Park with its rich flora and fauna, there will be chances to see Orangutans on their own natural habitat and other kinds of animal such as Thomas-leaf monkeys, long tail macaque, gibbon, black gibbon and other kind of flora and fauna of this tropical rain-forest. Lunch and dinner provided. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner • Overnight at : Tent or Shelter in the jungle Day-03 : CONTINUE TREKKING - RETURN TO BUKIT LAWANG (TUBING) (B,L) After breakfast prepared by tour guide continue trekking, today is full day walking and explore the rain tropical forest with its wildlife living in their natural habitat. In mid-afternoon, we will make our way back by tubing in the river. At the end, we will return to the hotel for check-in. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch • Overnight at : Eco-lodge Bukit Lawang Cottages - Standard Room Day-04 : BUKIT LAWANG - BERASTAGI (B) After breakfast drive to Berastagi with enroute stop at Sembahe river, arriving in Berastagi visiting Lumbhini Park to see the replica of the Shwedagon pagoda, and visit at Fruit Market. In mid-afternoon check-in to hotel. Meals : Breakfast • Overnight at : Mikie Holiday Resort - Superior Room • Alternative : Hotel Sinabung Hills - Superior Room Day-05 : SIBAYAK VOLCANO HIKING - TRANSFER TO SAMOSIR/LAKE TOBA (B) At early morning (take away your Breakfast Box) and transferred to the slope of Sibayak Volcano and then start hiking to the top of the Sibayak Volcano, to go and back will spend about 3 hours. Arriving on its peak enjoy the scenic panorama of its surroundings and the sunrise (weather depends). After take a rest and enjoy its view, start trekking back to Berastagi and then continuing the drive head for Samosir Island in Lake Toba via TELE. En-route stop at : • Dokan (to see the traditional village of the Batak Karo tribe) • Sipisopiso Waterfall (from here you can admire the scenic view of the Lake Toba from its northern tip combined with the slender 90 meters high waterfall) • Tele (a nice place for over-viewing the lake from its western part) • Efrata (another beautiful waterfall found on the way to Samosir Island) • Lumban Suhi-suhi (to see the Tobanase traditional houses where we could observe also the women doing the weaving) In mid-afternoon arriving at Tuktuk area on Samosir and check-in to hotel. Meals : Breakfast • Overnight at : Tabo Cottages - Deluxe Room • Alternative : Samosir Villa - Deluxe Room Day-06: SAMOSIR EXCURSION - AIRPORT/MEDAN CITY (B) After breakfast we start for our fullday excursion by car in the interior of Samosir Island with en-route visits at : • Ambarita (to see the stone chairs and tables where once used as the execution site by the ancient tribal chieftains) • Aek Natonang (here we can see the small lake found of the top of Samosir Island and its panorama view) • Tomok (to see the old sarcophages belonged to former Sidabutar Kings and his descendants) At mid-day, we will return to the harbor to catch the 1 PM ferry back to Parapat (1 hour sailing duration). Arriving at Parapat harbour continue the driving directly to Medan via Pematang Siantar and Tebing Tinggi (about 5 hours driving time). We will drop you off at the airport for overnight at airport hotel and be ready for morning flight departure. Meals : Breakfast Overnight: Hotel Horison Sky Kualanamu - Deluxe Room Day-07 : DEPARTURE After an early breakfast, you will continue to the departure terminal for your flight. TOUR ENDS. Meals : Breakfast','- All the above prices are not valid during Super High Season period for Idul Fitri (01-20 April 2024), Christmas & New Year festive season (18 December 2024 - 08 January 2025). - Surcharge to be advised','Per confirmed program: Day-01: AIRPORT/MEDAN – BUKIT LAWANG Day-02: BUKIT LAWANG – GUNUNG LEUSER NATIONAL PARK TREKKING Day-03: CONTINUE TREKKING – RETURN TO BUKIT LAWANG Day-04: BUKIT LAWANG – BERASTAGI Day-05: SIBAYAK VOLCANO HIKING – TRANSFER TO SAMOSIR/LAKE TOBA Day-06: SAMOSIR EXCURSION – AIRPORT/MEDAN CITY Day-07: DEPARTURE MEDAN Accommodation based on 1 Double Room: 2 Nights at Bukit Lawang Eco-Lodge – Orangutan Room 1 Night in Tent/shelter 1 Night Mikie Holiday Resort – Deluxe Room 1 Nights at Tabo Cottages – Deluxe Room 1 Night at Hotel Anara Sky Kualanamu – Deluxe Room Flights information: ETA: 15.00 by Malaysia Airlines MH864 from Kuala Lumpur on 14 Jul ETD: 08.45 by Singapore Airlines SQ991 to Singapore on 20 Jul','{\"date\": \"2024-07-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5169094,'520','ANA MIGUEZ X2',30508,207386,'Padang Bai to Seminyak','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-27','2024-10-27','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (2)',1120000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-27\", \"text\": \"Arrival Padang Bai (Central Bali) 27 Oct 2024, 13:55 By Blue Water\", \"time\": \"13:55\", \"locality\": \"P BAY PORT\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-27\", \"text\": \"\\\"KAYUMAS SEMINYAK RESORT \\\" \\\"ADDRESS : Jl. Pura Telaga Waja No.18a, Kerobokan Kelod, Kec. Kuta Utara, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361, Indonesia P: +62361 9348348\\\"\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5169106,'520','ANA MIGUEZ X2',30798,201630,'One Bedroom Suite Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-10-27','2024-10-29','Guio','Eddy',1,'Double',2598400.00,'The two-story, 45 sqm One Bedroom Suite features an natural and airy interior, complemented with modern furnishings and views overlooking to the private terrace with a plunge pool. Floor-to-ceiling glass doors provide generous natural lighting and a dynamic ambience. Plush linens and a marble bathroom surround guests in elegance.',NULL,'HONEYMOON','{\"date\": \"2024-10-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5169122,'520','ANA MIGUEZ X2',30508,207270,'Seminyak to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-29','2024-10-29','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (2)',560000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-29\", \"text\": \"\\\"KAYUMAS SEMINYAK RESORT \\\" \\\"ADDRESS : Jl. Pura Telaga Waja No.18a, Kerobokan Kelod, Kec. Kuta Utara, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361, Indonesia P: +62361 9348348\\\"\", \"time\": \"12:30\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-29\", \"text\": \"DEPARTURE / 29 OCT 2024 / 16:20 TO DUBAI EK 369 BY Emirates\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"AIRPORT DENPASAR\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5169682,'521','SHEREE RENEE KELLEY',30508,212287,'Airport to Sanur','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-01','2024-11-01','Melysa','Komang',1,'Persons (1-3)',300000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-11-01\", \"text\": \"ETA : 15.20 by Eva Airways BR27 from San Francisco on 01 November 2024\", \"time\": \"15:20\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"International Ngurah Rai Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-01\", \"text\": \"Puri Santrian Sanur, Jl. Cemara No.35, Sanur, Denpasar Selatan, Kota Denpasar, Bali 80228 Telepon: (0361) 288009\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sanur\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5169692,'521','SHEREE RENEE KELLEY',30720,202970,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-11-01','2024-11-03','Melysa','Komang',1,'Double',3960000.00,'Styled for personal comfort and convenience, the Superior room category is an inviting space that captures the essence of Bali. At 35 sqm of room area, with double / twin bed capacity of 2A 1C or 3A with extra bed. Set amidst tropical landscape, this air-conditioned room comes with a private balcony, flat-screen cable TV and a safety deposit box. En suite bathroom comes with bath and shower facilities.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-11-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5169726,'521','SHEREE RENEE KELLEY',30508,207269,'Sanur to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-03','2024-11-03','Melysa','Komang',1,'Persons (1-3)',300000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,'Please ready on hotel lobby for pickup at 04.30','{\"date\": \"2024-11-03\", \"text\": \"Puri Santrian Sanur, Jl. Cemara No.35, Sanur, Denpasar Selatan, Kota Denpasar, Bali 80228 Telepon: (0361) 288009\", \"time\": \"04:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sanur\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-03\", \"text\": \"ETD : 07.00 by Lion Air JT746 to Makassar on 03 November 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5169777,'521','SHEREE RENEE KELLEY',30508,212289,'Airport to Nusa Dua','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-11-19','2024-11-20','Melysa','Komang',1,'Persons (1-3)',600000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-11-19\", \"text\": \"ETA : 17.45 by Super Air Jet IU736 from Jakarta on 19 November 2024\", \"time\": \"18:10\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-20\", \"text\": \"Merusaka Nusa Dua, Kawasan Wisata Nusa Dua Lot S-3, Benoa, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80363 Telepon: (0361) 2002900\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Nusa Dua\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5169788,'521','SHEREE RENEE KELLEY',30914,202449,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-11-19','2024-11-21','Melysa','Komang',1,'Double',4380000.00,'The room is spacious at 48 sqm with king and twin size beds capacity of 2 (two) adults and 2 (two) child below 12 years old, decked with combination of Balinese-modern contemporary elements, immaculately designed to characterize each of Seven Balinese Goddesses. Located on a higher level of each Puri, the room is equipped with every amenity that could possibly be required, making it ideal for a single traveler or couples.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-11-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5169792,'521','SHEREE RENEE KELLEY',30508,207268,'Nusa Dua to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-21','2024-11-21','Melysa','Komang',1,'Persons (1-3)',300000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,'Please ready on hotel lobby for pickup at 13.30','{\"date\": \"2024-11-21\", \"text\": \"Merusaka Nusa Dua, Kawasan Wisata Nusa Dua Lot S-3, Benoa, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80363 Telepon: (0361) 2002900\", \"time\": \"13:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Nusa Dua\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-21\", \"text\": \"ETD : 16.30 by Eva Airways BR256 to San Francisco on 21 Nov 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"International Ngurah Rai Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5169916,'522','ANNA WILLIAMS',32660,216222,'Super Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-27','2024-09-28','Ayu','Tami',1,'Single',840000.00,'Rooms with international standard quality facilities. Modern and elegant design provides unforgettable comfort. Equipped with facilities such as: Hot and Cool Water, Coffee and Tea Maker, Amenities, Linen and Bed with star hotel standard quality.',NULL,'Check-in time 12.00 Check-out time 14.00','{\"date\": \"2024-09-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5170027,'523','Ms. Andrea Patricia Rohrer',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-07-03','2024-07-05','Nicholas','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',10800000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note for Meals : have an intolerance for garlic and onions. Prepare the meals without these ingredients Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-07-03\", \"text\": \"ETA 08.10 by Batik Air ID6135 from Surabaya on 03 Jul\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pangkalan Bun Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-05\", \"text\": \"ETD 08.50 by Batik Air ID6134 to Surabaya on 05 Jul\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5170046,'473','Alessia Atzori & Charlon Tabone',30597,201143,'Standard Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-09-23','2024-09-25','Ayu','Eddy',1,'Double',7168000.00,'At 50 sqm room size, Standard Room an inviting hideaway in the heart of Seminyak. Tucked at the side of the resort building, this room is the perfect choice for a quiet hideaway in the heart of Seminyak. Providing an ample daylight from the private balcony with daybed, this room is eclectically designed, featuring a spa inspired ensuite bathroom. Treat your loved one to an unforgettable stay at one of the finest Seminyak beachfront resorts.',NULL,'HONEY MOON','{\"date\": \"2024-09-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5170048,'473','Alessia Atzori & Charlon Tabone',32971,218256,'One Bedroom Villa','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-09-21','2024-09-23','Ayu','Eddy',1,'Double',7822080.00,NULL,NULL,'HONEYMOON','{\"date\": \"2024-09-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5170101,'525','Ulrich Antonius Stratmann',30662,212912,'(Journaway) 7D6N Medan - Bukit Lawang - Brastagi - Lake Toba','Confirmed',NULL,7,'2024-07-28','2024-08-03','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Persons (2-3 / Double)',22348480.00,'Day-01 : AIRPORT/MEDAN - BUKIT LAWANG Arrival at Kualanamu International Airport Medan meet by our tour guide and then drive to Bukit Lawang with enroute stop at several plantations for rubber and oil palm. Arriving in Bukit Lawang check-in to hotel. Meals : - • Overnight at : Eco-lodge Bukit Lawang Cottages - Standard Room Day-02 : BUKIT LAWANG - LEUSER PARK TREKKING (B,L,D) After breakfast walking to the jungle to start a jungle trekking to explore the nature of Leuser National Park with its rich flora and fauna, there will be chances to see Orangutans on their own natural habitat and other kinds of animal such as Thomas-leaf monkeys, long tail macaque, gibbon, black gibbon and other kind of flora and fauna of this tropical rain-forest. Lunch and dinner provided. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner • Overnight at : Tent or Shelter in the jungle Day-03 : CONTINUE TREKKING - RETURN TO BUKIT LAWANG (TUBING) (B,L) After breakfast prepared by tour guide continue trekking, today is full day walking and explore the rain tropical forest with its wildlife living in their natural habitat. In mid-afternoon, we will make our way back by tubing in the river. At the end, we will return to the hotel for check-in. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch • Overnight at : Eco-lodge Bukit Lawang Cottages - Standard Room Day-04 : BUKIT LAWANG - BERASTAGI (B) After breakfast drive to Berastagi with enroute stop at Sembahe river, arriving in Berastagi visiting Lumbhini Park to see the replica of the Shwedagon pagoda, and visit at Fruit Market. In mid-afternoon check-in to hotel. Meals : Breakfast • Overnight at : Mikie Holiday Resort - Superior Room • Alternative : Hotel Sinabung Hills - Superior Room Day-05 : SIBAYAK VOLCANO HIKING - TRANSFER TO SAMOSIR/LAKE TOBA (B) At early morning (take away your Breakfast Box) and transferred to the slope of Sibayak Volcano and then start hiking to the top of the Sibayak Volcano, to go and back will spend about 3 hours. Arriving on its peak enjoy the scenic panorama of its surroundings and the sunrise (weather depends). After take a rest and enjoy its view, start trekking back to Berastagi and then continuing the drive head for Samosir Island in Lake Toba via TELE. En-route stop at : • Dokan (to see the traditional village of the Batak Karo tribe) • Sipisopiso Waterfall (from here you can admire the scenic view of the Lake Toba from its northern tip combined with the slender 90 meters high waterfall) • Tele (a nice place for over-viewing the lake from its western part) • Efrata (another beautiful waterfall found on the way to Samosir Island) • Lumban Suhi-suhi (to see the Tobanase traditional houses where we could observe also the women doing the weaving) In mid-afternoon arriving at Tuktuk area on Samosir and check-in to hotel. Meals : Breakfast • Overnight at : Tabo Cottages - Deluxe Room • Alternative : Samosir Villa - Deluxe Room Day-06: SAMOSIR EXCURSION - AIRPORT/MEDAN CITY (B) After breakfast we start for our fullday excursion by car in the interior of Samosir Island with en-route visits at : • Ambarita (to see the stone chairs and tables where once used as the execution site by the ancient tribal chieftains) • Aek Natonang (here we can see the small lake found of the top of Samosir Island and its panorama view) • Tomok (to see the old sarcophages belonged to former Sidabutar Kings and his descendants) At mid-day, we will return to the harbor to catch the 1 PM ferry back to Parapat (1 hour sailing duration). Arriving at Parapat harbour continue the driving directly to Medan via Pematang Siantar and Tebing Tinggi (about 5 hours driving time). We will drop you off at the airport for overnight at airport hotel and be ready for morning flight departure. Meals : Breakfast Overnight: Hotel Horison Sky Kualanamu - Deluxe Room Day-07 : DEPARTURE After an early breakfast, you will continue to the departure terminal for your flight. TOUR ENDS. Meals : Breakfast','- All the above prices are not valid during Super High Season period for Idul Fitri (01-20 April 2024), Christmas & New Year festive season (18 December 2024 - 08 January 2025). - Surcharge to be advised','Per confirmed program: Day-01: AIRPORT/MEDAN – BUKIT LAWANG Day-02: BUKIT LAWANG – GUNUNG LEUSER NATIONAL PARK TREKKING Day-03: CONTINUE TREKKING – RETURN TO BUKIT LAWANG Day-04: BUKIT LAWANG – BERASTAGI Day-05: SIBAYAK VOLCANO HIKING – TRANSFER TO SAMOSIR/LAKE TOBA Day-06: SAMOSIR EXCURSION – AIRPORT/MEDAN CITY Day-07: DEPARTURE MEDAN Accommodation based on 1 Double Room: 2 Nights at The Heritage Resort Hotel - Deluxe Room 1 Night in Tent/shelter 1 Night Mikie Holiday Resort – Standard Room 1 Nights at Hotel Toledo Inn – Deluxe Room 1 Night at Hotel Anara Sky Kualanamu – Deluxe Room Flights information: ETA: 10.10 by Batik Air ID7289 from Kuala Lumpur on 28 Jul ETD: 10.30 by Batik Air ID 7147 to Singapore on 03 Aug','{\"date\": \"2024-07-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5170158,'526','Mr. Ivan Pozo Duran',31015,203232,'3D2N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Surabaya','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-11','2024-08-13','Jacob','Praba',5,'Persons (5)',9840000.00,NULL,NULL,'12 Aug 2024 Drop to Swiss-Belhotel Tunjungan Surabaya 13 Aug 2024 Pick up from Swiss-Belhotel Tunjungan Surabaya and drop to Airport Surabaya','{\"date\": \"2024-08-11\", \"text\": \"11 Aug 2024 ETA 16:25PM by Super Air Jet IU727 from Labuan Bajo\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Juanda International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": \"13 Aug 2024 ETD 07:00AM by Batik Air ID6135 to Pangkalan Bun\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Juanda International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5170177,'526','Mr. Ivan Pozo Duran',31196,204658,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-11','2024-08-12','Jacob','Praba',3,'1 Double + 2 Twin',4284000.00,'Room type deluxe, with spacious room 3,41 m x 6,09 m and have type bed king size or twin bed. This type of room is available on the 2nd, 3rd and 4th floors and has of the hills view.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5170180,'526','Mr. Ivan Pozo Duran',30723,213467,'Deluxe Premium Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-12','2024-08-13','Jacob','Praba',3,'1 Double + 2 Twin',2754000.00,'Deluxe Premium Type rooms are available with Queen Beds 180 x 200, and have a room area size of 23 m2. This room is equipped with, Individually controlled air-conditioning, IDD telephone, 32 inch LCD TV with international channels, high speed internet access, 14 inch laptop size in-room safe, coffee and tea making facilities, and bathroom with shower.',NULL,'- Shall your company has Credit Facility with the hotel, Hotel will only confirm the reservations upon received your Copy of Room Voucher or Guarantee Letter prior to the guest arrival. - Should the Hotel has not received the Copy of Room Voucher or Guarantee Letter upon the Guest check-in; the Hotel shall apply Walk-in Rates to the guest (s) and should be settled by the guest upon check-out.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5170207,'526','Mr. Ivan Pozo Duran',30783,212220,'4D3N Yogyakarta via Semarang - City Tour - Borobudur - Prambanan - Mt. Merapi with Jeep / C. Adhisth','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-08-16','2024-08-19','Jacob','Praba',5,'Persons (1-5)',23400000.00,'D1 Arrival Yogyakarta International Airport – Transfer to hotel: Welcome to the cradle of Indonesian culture, Yogyakarta. A tourist destination for its ancient palaces, temples, batik workshops, gamelan music orchestras, court dances and wayang puppet shows. Upon your arrival in Yogyakarta a representative of come2indonesia will be waiting for you with a sign indicating your name to take you to your hotel and the rest of the day is for you. D2 Borobudur temple – Candirejo Village Tour by Horse cart / bicycle – Merapi lava tour Including Jeep: You will have your deserved breakfast at the hotel. Today’s tour will make you enjoy the authentic Javanese essence. You will start your route in the direction of with the Borobudur Temple (Candi Borobudur), the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. We will tour around the temple, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano has been producing during its history. After visiting one of the most important Buddhist temples in Southeast Asia, and in a horse carriage (Andong) we will visit the villages that surround this temple. These are authentic Javanese villages where culture and tradition are the protagonists. As you spend your days in this country and go around the different islands, you will realize how different Indonesians are among them in terms of clothing, food, architecture and even language. Today we will learn about and share these Javanese places. Then we will go to Kaliurang / Kalidalem to see Mount Merapi in constant activity. Here in a 4x4 jeep driven by specialized drivers, we will climb its skirt to see the remains of the 2010 eruption such as houses buried by ashes, a multitude of objects paralyzed by lava, etc. In addition, an open-air tribute museum presided over by the clock that marks the time just when the lava passed through it has been improvised. Accompanied by photos of the rescue, it will make us feel very closely the experiences of that fateful day. After finishing this day full of emotions, we will take you back to your hotel. D3 City Tour Jogjakarta Visit Sultan Palace, Watercastle and Bird Market – Prambanan Temple: After breakfast and at the indicated time we will head towards the heart of the city. We will visit the Keraton known as the Sultan’s Palace. The palace is a complex building two centuries old, located in the heart of the city. You will hear the song of the “freedom” of the birds in the bird market, we will visit the “Water Castle” that occupies the highest part at the northern end of the vast complex of Taman Sari, Malioboro Street, main street of Yogyakarta, with its merchants, horse carriages, taxi-bikes and markets. An incredible experience that will make the hours fly by. After finishing the tour in the center of the city of Yogyakarta, we will go to the northeast direction Candi Prambanan, the temple of the Hinduists and classified as a World Heritage Site by Unesco since 1991. The built of this temple was finished around the year 856 to commemorate the victory of the descendant Sanjaya of Siva, Rikai Pikatan on the last sovereign Sailendra of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to the Trimurti, the expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the Destroyer. After this unforgettable day, we will take you to your hotel. D4 Transfer out Yogyakarta International airport: Today our adventure ends at the cradle of Indonesian culture. Depending on the time of your flight, we will pick you up to take you to the airport and take the flight to your next destination. End of our services. Thank you very much for exploring Yogyakarta by the hand of Come2indonesia.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": \"16 Aug 2024 ETA 11:25AM by Batik Air ID6303 from Pangkalan Bun\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Bandar Udara Jenderal Ahmad Yani\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": \"19 Aug 2024 ETD 11:45AM by Air Asia AK347 to Kuala Lumpur\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Yogyakarta International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5170232,'527','ANTONIO SANTOS ROMAN',30680,200919,'Premier Family Room + Extra Bed','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-30','2024-07-31','Guio','Wiwik',2,'Single + Double',2880000.00,'The most important things in this world is family. Thoughtfully designed with families in mind, our Family Premier Room includes everything needed for you and your family to feel comfortable during your stay. At 43 m2 pf room size with 1 king size and 1 twin size, this room equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, hot and cold shower, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer. Free access to our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers.',NULL,'Flight Detail: ETA: 21.35 by IB7960 Qatar Airways from Doha on 30 july 2024 ETD: 12.20 by Lion Air JT126 to Tanjung Pandan Belitung on 31 July 2024 Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. - Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK–IN','{\"date\": \"2024-07-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-31\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5170997,'479','MR. SERGIO APARICIO COBO',30672,200737,'Studio 25 (Superior) Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-04','2024-10-05','Guio','Eddy',1,'Double',684000.00,'Studio 25 (Superior) room with 25 sqm sized room and with exclusive ARTOTEL bedding collection, some facilities in this room is 43\" inch lcd tv, 24 hours in-room service, high speed internet wi-fi, safety deposit box and hair dryer.',NULL,'HONEYMOON ETD : 05OCT 0830 ID6302 by Batik Air TO (PKN) Pangkalanbun','{\"date\": \"2024-10-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-05\", \"text\": \"ETD : 05OCT 0830 ID6302 by Batik Air TO (PKN) Pangkalanbun\", \"time\": \"06:30\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5171024,'479','MR. SERGIO APARICIO COBO',30806,212962,'OT3 Barco Klotok - Private Trip','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-10-05','2024-10-07','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (2)',11520000.00,'Hop on a speedboat and cruise along the Kumai River to visit the feeding camps in the national park of Tanjung Puting. On this Borneo Orangutan Tour by speedboat, see the wild orangutans in their natural environment through gentle trekking into the rainforest. Enjoying the riverside view accompanied by the proboscis monkeys hanging around the tips of the trees. This trip is prepared for those who are keen to see the wildlife from different perspectives, combining jungle adventure while also having a little private adventure with the comfort of sleeping in a hotel! Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN – KUMAI PORT – TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our speedboat. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the trip up the river in the famous Sekonyer River. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan is Cape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even see crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. A picnic lunch will be provided during the tour. After the tour, transfer to your hotel for check-in and overnight. Meals : Picnic Lunch Accommodation : A. Rimba Eco Lodge – Amethyst Beo Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY – CAMP LEAKEY After breakfast at the hotel, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continue to add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the speedboat again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. Back to your hotel and rest. Note: The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. Meals : Breakfast – Picnic Lunch Accommodation : A. Rimba Eco Lodge – Amethyst Beo Day 3 : HOTEL – PANGKALAN BUN After breakfast, depending on your flight schedule, our team will pick you up and escort you to the airport. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-10-05\", \"text\": \"ETA :05OCT 0930 From (SRG) Semarang ID6302 By Batik Air\", \"time\": \"09:30\", \"locality\": \"AIRPORT PANGKALAN BUN\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-07\", \"text\": \"ETD 07OCT 0850 To (SUB) Surabaya ID6134 By Batik Air\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"AIRPORT PANGKALAN BUN\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5171040,'479','MR. SERGIO APARICIO COBO',31015,203230,'2D1N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Tour','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-10-07','2024-10-08','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (2)',4800000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-07\", \"text\": \"ETA 07OCT 1000 From (PKN) Pangkalanbun ID6134 By Batik Air\", \"time\": \"10:00\", \"locality\": \"SURABAYA AIRPORT\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-08\", \"text\": \"ETD 08OCT 1525 To (DPS) Denpasar JT920 By Lion Air\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"SURABAYA AIRPORT\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5171041,'479','MR. SERGIO APARICIO COBO',31196,204658,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-07','2024-10-08','Guio','Eddy',1,'Double',1428000.00,'Room type deluxe, with spacious room 3,41 m x 6,09 m and have type bed king size or twin bed. This type of room is available on the 2nd, 3rd and 4th floors and has of the hills view.',NULL,'HONEYMOON','{\"date\": \"2024-10-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5171047,'479','MR. SERGIO APARICIO COBO',30711,200830,'Bisma Suite Room','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-10-08','2024-10-12','Guio','Eddy',1,'Double',13464000.00,'Spacious one-bedroom suite of 88 sqm with private balcony for a sophisticated Ubud getaway. Interiors feature extensive use of wood and fine Indonesian textiles and art, lending an understated elegance to the space. Featuring a private balcony, this room includes a flat-screen TV and an en-suite bathroom with a bathtub and a shower, and many more.',NULL,'HONEYMOON','{\"date\": \"2024-10-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5171069,'479','MR. SERGIO APARICIO COBO',30508,202896,'Bali Village Life - Tanah Lot Temple','Confirmed','C2I-BALI05',1,'2024-10-09','2024-10-09','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (2)',2616000.00,'At 08.00 am, we pick you up from your hotel and start our journey to Tunjuk Village in Tabanan district. Upon arrival, you will be greeted with open arms and with the warm smiles of the locals you meet along the way. You\'ll meet in the outer courtyard of the village temple and meet your local guides. Throughout the hike you will meet people from the village involved in the tasks that keep their lives busy day in and day out. You can choose to observe or participate in them to gain a better understanding of village life. The mighty water buffalo is still used to drag the plough through the muddy rice paddies and prepare the land for planting. Or maybe you want to help with planting or harvesting, depending on the time of year. When you complete the tour in the rice paddies, you\'ll follow your guide on a path through lush gardens where villagers go about their daily chores. There are women who beat the rice with heavy mallets to remove the hooves. After lunch we leave Tunjuk Village and continue our journey to visit THE TANAH LOT. We\'ll close the visit by watching the sunset at the most famous and photographed temple in Bali. Torn from the earth on a stone pedestal sculpted by the incoming tides, the solitary black towers of Tanah Lot and the plumes of foliage spilling over the precipices, recall the delicacy of Chinese painting. The Pura Tanah Lot or the Earth Temple in the middle of the sea was built in the 16th century. At the end of the day, you\'ll be transferred to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-09\", \"text\": \"KOMANEKA AT BISMA \\\"Address: Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone: (0361) 971933\\\"\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-09\", \"text\": \"KOMANEKA AT BISMA \\\"Address: Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone: (0361) 971933\\\"\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5171128,'479','MR. SERGIO APARICIO COBO',30578,203470,'Luxury Suite Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-10-12','2024-10-14','Guio','Eddy',1,'Double',7778880.00,'Discover our exquisite Luxury Suites, each spanning approximately 60 m² and nestled within our lush coffee plantation at various enchanting vantage points. These suites offer a personal terrace and a spacious en-suite bathroom adorned with a double sink, embodying a minimalist design that seamlessly incorporates some of the most beautiful natural elements found at MMP. Crafted with Merbau parquet flooring and adorned with Sulawesi cream marble in the bathroom, the Luxury Suites are a testament to nature\'s elegance. King-size poster beds, tropical hardwood couches, and premium cotton and linen fabrics, alongside captivating local artworks, combine to create a cozy interior ambiance. Enormous glass panel doors showcase panoramic vistas in every direction. As a luxurious touch, a generously sized hand-finished terrazzo bathtub beckons you to unwind in the soothing embrace of mountain water infused with fragrant essences, provided to enhance your tranquil experience.',NULL,'HONEYMOON','{\"date\": \"2024-10-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5171174,'479','MR. SERGIO APARICIO COBO',30508,202889,'Tamblingan Trek - Ulun Danu','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-13','2024-10-13','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (2)',2256000.00,'Today we will explore the nature of Buyan and Tamblingan lake in our lovely village, it will help you to escape from the crowds and fell the Nature atmosphere of the real jungle of Bali. We will pick you at your hotel at 07:30 AM and we drive to Tamblingan lake. Arrive in the trekking start point, we will have an explanation about the trekking. We will start the trek by entering a lush protected rain-forest area with giant old tress, animal such as macaque, black giant squirrel, birds and old legend temple inside in the Jungle. You will then walk along the shore of this lake situated in the caldera of an extinct Jungle Mountain. Our trekking guide will explain more detail about plants and living creatures in the jungle. This tour also combine with a session of thirty five minutes exploring the Tamblingan lake by dugout canoe to finishing point. Finish with trekking we will drop you to your hotel but we will make a stop at Ulun Danu Temple. Ulun Danu Temple Bratan, the famous temple stands on a small promontory located in the shore of Lake Bratan and has beautiful scenery with this lake and the mountains as backdrop sight.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-13\", \"text\": \"MUNDUK MODING PLANTATION NATURE RESORT \\\"Address: Jl. Asah Gobleg, Gobleg, Kec. Banjar, Kabupaten Buleleng, Bali 81152 Phone: (0368) 2080123\\\"\", \"time\": \"07:30\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-13\", \"text\": \"MUNDUK MODING PLANTATION NATURE RESORT \\\"Address: Jl. Asah Gobleg, Gobleg, Kec. Banjar, Kabupaten Buleleng, Bali 81152 Phone: (0368) 2080123\\\"\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5171328,'479','MR. SERGIO APARICIO COBO',30572,202004,'Deluxe Garden Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-14','2024-10-15','Guio','Eddy',1,'Double',2622600.00,'Deluxe Rooms are dressed in warm colors with contemporary Balinese interior and exterior that made up the cozy interior, with size room 30 m2 and the bed type One Double bed or Two Single bed, one crib on request. Complemented with balcony or terrace overlooking garden, located in the two-story building.',NULL,'HONEYMOON','{\"date\": \"2024-10-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5171344,'529','Rosa Maria Espinos',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-30','2024-07-31','Guio','Eddy',1,'Twin',840000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. - Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. AIPORT JAKARTA ETA : 30 JUL 2024 /14:40 EY0474 Etihad Airways From Abu Dabi AIPORT JAKARTA ETD : 31 JUL 2024/ 0600 ID6202 Batik Air To Pangkalanbun PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN','{\"date\": \"2024-07-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-31\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5171377,'529','Rosa Maria Espinos',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-07-31','2024-08-02','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (2)',10800000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board. AIPORT PANGKALANBUN ETA : 31 JUL 2024 /0715 ID6202 by Batik Air From Jakarta AIPORT PANGKALANBUN ETD : 02 AUG 2024 / 0850 ID6134 by Batik Air To Surabaya','{\"date\": \"2024-07-31\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5171396,'529','Rosa Maria Espinos',31015,203230,'2D1N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Tour','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-08-02','2024-08-03','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (2)',4800000.00,NULL,NULL,'HOTEL AT BROMO / 02 - 03 Aug 2024 1 NIGHT GUBUK NDESO HOMESTAY Address : Jl. Raya Bromo No.92, Dusun 1, Sapikerep, Kec. Sukapura, Kabupaten Probolinggo, Jawa Timur 67254 Phone: 0823-3101-1658 ETA : AIRPORT SURABAYA 02 AUG 2024 / 1000 ID6134 by Batik Air From Pangkalanbun ETD : AIRPORT SURABAYA 03 AUG 2024 / 1525 JT920 by Lion To Denpasar','{\"date\": \"2024-08-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5171410,'529','Rosa Maria Espinos',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-03','2024-08-03','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (1-3)',840000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-03\", \"text\": \"ETA : 03 AUG 2024 / 1725 JT920 by Lion From Surabaya\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"AIRPORT DENPASAR\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-03\", \"text\": \"Adi House Homestay Ubud Address : Jl. Sugriwa No.58, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : 0812-4628-584\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5171424,'479','MR. SERGIO APARICIO COBO',30852,202033,'One Bedroom Pool Villa','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-10-15','2024-10-18','Guio','Eddy',1,'Double',9720000.00,'Our cozy one bed Villa Surya is perfect for a solo traveler or a romantic getaway at 150 sqm private property. The spacious bedroom features a king-size bed with an extra thick mattress with 100% cotton linen, ensuring a blissful sleep. With high-ceilings, large windows, and a pivoting door onto your patio, the space is able to breathe whilst being basked in a beautiful, natural light. The ensuite bathroom, equipped with a bespoke basin area, rainfall shower, quality toiletries and 100% cotton towels leads out to the real star of this villa, the indulgent open-air bathtub. Large enough for two, with views of your private pool and tropical garden, while away hours in pure relaxation.',NULL,'HONEYMOON','{\"date\": \"2024-10-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5171432,'529','Rosa Maria Espinos',30508,215968,'1D Bali Tour (Kanto Lampo, Goa Gajah, Tegalalang, Tenengunan Waterfall)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-05','2024-08-05','Guio','Eddy',2,'Person (1)',0.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-05\", \"text\": \"Adi House Homestay Ubud Address : Jl. Sugriwa No.58, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : 0812-4628-584\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"MEET AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-05\", \"text\": \"Adi House Homestay Ubud Address : Jl. Sugriwa No.58, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : 0812-4628-584\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5171437,'529','Rosa Maria Espinos',30508,215968,'1D Bali Tour (Jatiluwih, Templo Ulun Danu Bratan, Leke2 waterfall)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-04','2024-08-04','Guio','Eddy',2,'Person (1)',0.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-04\", \"text\": \"Adi House Homestay Ubud Address : Jl. Sugriwa No.58, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : 0812-4628-584\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"MEET AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-04\", \"text\": \"Adi House Homestay Ubud Address : Jl. Sugriwa No.58, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : 0812-4628-584\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5171441,'529','Rosa Maria Espinos',30508,215968,'1D Bali Tour (Campuhan Ride Walk + Rafting di river + Monkey Forest)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-06','2024-08-06','Guio','Eddy',2,'Person (1)',0.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-06\", \"text\": \"Adi House Homestay Ubud Address : Jl. Sugriwa No.58, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : 0812-4628-584\", \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": \"MEET AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-06\", \"text\": \"Adi House Homestay Ubud Address : Jl. Sugriwa No.58, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : 0812-4628-584\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5171456,'529','Rosa Maria Espinos',30508,207112,'1D Nusa Penida West Tour','Confirmed','C2I-BALI19',1,'2024-08-07','2024-08-07','Guio','Eddy',2,'Persons (2)',1020000.00,'Today, embark on a unique adventure as you explore the enchanting Nusa Penida, a neighboring island of Bali. Your day begins with a convenient hotel pick-up, followed by a journey to the Sanur port where a fast boat awaits to transport you to Nusa Penida in just 30 minutes. Nusa Penida, located in the southeast of Bali, is a true paradise waiting to be discovered. Upon your arrival, a friendly driver will be ready to guide you through the day\'s captivating itinerary. Your first destination is the mesmerizing Angel\'s Billabong, a natural wonder resembling a pristine pool nestled in the heart of nature. Take a refreshing swim, but exercise caution on the steps and heed your driver\'s recommendations. Next, we head to Broken Beach, a charming bay that was once a cave, now open to the sky, offering a unique and captivating scenery. Although inaccessible by land, the view from above is nothing short of breathtaking. Keep an eye out for the possibility of spotting giant manta rays gracefully gliding on the water\'s surface. Our journey continues to the renowned Kelingking Beach, famous for its stunning cliffs and the iconic hand-shaped mountain. This beach is not only one of the island\'s most famous attractions but also a favorite subject for photographers. We conclude the day at the pristine Crystal Beach, where white sands meet turquoise waters in perfect harmony. As the sun sets, you\'ll have the opportunity to relax and savor the beauty that surrounds you. This unforgettable experience concludes with a return boat trip to Bali from the Toya Pakeh port at 16:30, followed by a comfortable transfer to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-07\", \"text\": \"07 August 2024 : Kusamba - Nusa Penida (ETA 08.20) BY THE ANGKAL\", \"time\": \"08:20\", \"locality\": \"HARBOUR SAMPALAN\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-07\", \"text\": \"07 August 2024 : Nusa Penida - SANUR (ETD 16.30 ) BY THE ANGKAL\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"HARBOUR BANJAR NYUH\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5171461,'529','Rosa Maria Espinos',30508,212455,'Sanur to Sanur','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-07','2024-08-07','Guio','Eddy',1,'Persons (1-3)',300000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-07\", \"text\": \"ETA : 07 August 2024 : Nusa Penida - SANUR (17.00) BY THE ANGKAL\", \"time\": \"17:00\", \"locality\": \"SANUR HARBOUR\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-07\", \"text\": \"Nyaman Guest House Sanur Address : Jl. Danau Tamblingan No.96, Sanur, Denpasar Selatan, Kota Denpasar, Bali 80228 Phone : (0361) 4720691\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5171561,'529','Rosa Maria Espinos',30508,207269,'Sanur to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-08','2024-08-08','Guio','Eddy',1,'Persons (1-3)',300000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": \"Nyaman Guest House Sanur Address : Jl. Danau Tamblingan No.96, Sanur, Denpasar Selatan, Kota Denpasar, Bali 80228 Phone : (0361) 4720691\", \"time\": \"07:30\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": \"ETD : 08 AUG 2024 / 1050 QZ642 by AirAsia to Labuan Bajo\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"AIRPORT DENPASAR\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5171604,'529','Rosa Maria Espinos',32766,216810,'3D2N Open Trip Komodo - Lady Grace / Deluxe Cabin','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-09','2024-08-11','Guio','Eddy',2,'Per Person (Min. 2 Person)',12840000.00,'DAY 1 : Kelor Island - Manjerite Island - Kalong Island DAY 2 : Padar Island - Long / Pick Beach - Komodo Island - Manta Point - Taka Makasar DAY 3 : Kanawa Island',NULL,'pick up time is between 09.00-09.30 am Excluded - Personal expenses - Crew gratitues - Local donation, Komodo National Park Fees & Rangee Fees Foreign/KITAS guest : IDR 600.000/person/trips Vuelo (LBJ) Labuan Bajo – (SUB) Surabaya – (LOP) Lombok IU727 LBJ-SUB 1710-173511AUG IU718 SUB-LOP 1815-201511AUG','{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": \"EL ORA HOTEL & EATERY LABUAN BAJO Address : Jl. Yohanis Sahadun No.8, Labuan Bajo, Kec. Komodo, Kabupaten Manggarai Barat, Nusa Tenggara Tim. Phone : 0851-0607-7731\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-11\", \"text\": \"ETD : 11 AUG 2024 / 1710 IU727 by Super Air Jet to Lombok\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"AIRPORT LABUAN BAJO\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5171682,'530','Marta Rey',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-15','2024-08-16','Jacob','Febrina',1,'Double',840000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Roundtrip Airport Transfer Flight details: ETA 15:25 from Doha by Iberia IB7962 on 15 Aug ETD 06:00 to Pangkalan Bun by Batik Air ID6202 on 16 Aug Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. - Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK–IN','{\"date\": \"2024-08-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5171687,'530','Marta Rey',30805,202689,'CGK-PKN','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-16','2024-08-16','Jacob','Febrina',2,'Person',3520000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5171703,'530','Marta Rey',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-08-16','2024-08-18','Jacob','Febrina',2,'Persons (2)',10800000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'3D2N Borneo Orangutan Tour based on Private Standard Klotok, with Spanish speaking guide Flight details: ETA 07:15 from Jakarta by Batik Air ID6202 on 16 Aug ETD 10:25 to Semarang by Batik Air ID6303 on 18 Aug Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5171709,'530','Marta Rey',30805,212246,'PKN-SRG','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-18','2024-08-18','Jacob','Febrina',2,'Person',5720000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5171719,'201','Claudio De Mauro',30571,202567,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-19','2024-07-20','Rendy','Tami',1,'Double',1372000.00,'Located at the Second Floor, 35 sqm comfort living with a touch of Balinese style featuring completed fitting, Cable TV, a fancy bathroom comprises rain shower and good quality amenities. Also dedicated Wi-Fi Access to complete your day.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5171723,'201','Claudio De Mauro',30571,202567,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-30','2024-07-31','Rendy','Tami',1,'Double',1372000.00,'Located at the Second Floor, 35 sqm comfort living with a touch of Balinese style featuring completed fitting, Cable TV, a fancy bathroom comprises rain shower and good quality amenities. Also dedicated Wi-Fi Access to complete your day.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-31\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5172568,'531','Robert Mackean',31169,204438,'Meet and Greet International Arrival','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-02','2024-07-02','Rendy','Rendy',3,'Person (1)',1165920.00,'Arrival Domestic: Pick up at the end of aviobridge until the client meet the driver.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5172572,'530','Marta Rey',30805,207117,'YIA-DPS','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-21','2024-08-21','Jacob','Febrina',2,'Person',3080000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5172574,'530','Marta Rey',30985,212179,'Jungle Suite Room with Private Balcony','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-08-21','2024-08-23','Jacob','Febrina',1,'Double',5400000.00,'Escape the hustle and bustle of everyday life and immerse yourself in the beauty of nature with our Jungle Suite with Private Balcony. Located in the heart of the lush tropical rainforest, this Suite offers a unique opportunity to immerse yourself in nature while still enjoying all the comforts of modern living. The real highlight of this room category is the private balcony overlooking the jungle canopy. Relax in your own personal paradise as you listen to the sounds of nature, watch the birds playing in the trees, and breathe in the fresh air while taking in the breathtaking views.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5172577,'530','Marta Rey',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-21','2024-08-21','Jacob','Febrina',1,'Persons (1-3)',420000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": \"ETA 12:15 from Yogyakarta by Lion Air JT560 on 21 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Denpasar Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": \"Jl. Suweta, Banjar Bentuyung Sakti, Ubud, Gianyar, Bali. Phone: +62361 2091788\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Desa Visesa Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5172632,'530','Marta Rey',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-22','2024-08-22','Jacob','Febrina',2,'Persons (2)',1872000.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,'FD Tour Taman Ayun - Jatiluwih - Ulun Danu Beratan Temple - Tanah Lot, with Spanish speaking guide','{\"date\": \"2024-08-22\", \"text\": \"Jl. Suweta, Banjar Bentuyung Sakti, Ubud, Gianyar, Bali. Phone: +62361 2091788\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Desa Visesa Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-22\", \"text\": \"Jl. Suweta, Banjar Bentuyung Sakti, Ubud, Gianyar, Bali. Phone: +62361 2091788\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Desa Visesa Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5172643,'530','Marta Rey',30930,202592,'One Bedroom Bungalow','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-23','2024-08-26','Jacob','Febrina',1,'Double',9360000.00,'Room size : 37 sqm. Our One-Bedroom Bungalow is a unique Romantic Eco-Boho Bungalow nestles in Green Escape Resort. You will stay in a sumptuous air-conditioned bungalow that has been handcrafted using recycled wood and tastefully decorated to offer you an authentic Balinese getaway. It\'s the very epitome of a tranquil escape. This Bungalow offers a deluxe king-size bed and a daybed to relax. It offers a comfy mattress, as we know the benefits of a good night’s sleep. The semi-outdoor bathroom with a rain shower will help you revive yourself. Enjoy the comfy sofa on your private terrace which opens onto the exotic garden & pool. The daybed can be used to extend the sleeping capacity of your private bungalow.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5172648,'530','Marta Rey',30508,212553,'Transfer Uluwatu -Padang Bai Harbor','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-26','2024-08-26','Jacob','Febrina',1,'Persons (2)',660000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-26\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bangbang Metuug, Bingin, Pecatu, Kuta Selatan, Badung, Bali. Phone: +62811 3997903\", \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Green Escape Eco & Boutique Resort\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-26\", \"text\": \"ETD 08:30 by Gili Gili Fast Boat to Gili Air.\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Padang Bai Harbor / https://goo.gl/maps/qRvTJixStazBCLAu8 (close to Serangan 1 Homestay Padangbai)\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5172652,'530','Marta Rey',30650,208425,'Private Pool Villa','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-26','2024-08-29','Jacob','Febrina',1,'Double',10800000.00,'Each villa embraces calmness, comfort and privacy in a simple and elegant setting. Guests can relax while peacefully sipping drinks in an inviting plunge pool surrounded by a lush tropical garden and at an old-wooden deck. At 85 m2 room size, this villa\'s special feature is the private pool. The air-conditioned villa features 1 bedroom and 1 bathroom with a shower and a hairdryer. The villa provides a mini-bar, a tea and coffee maker, a seating area as well as a terrace with garden views. The unit offers 1 bed.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5172687,'530','Marta Rey',30805,208054,'LOP-CGK','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-29','2024-08-29','Jacob','Febrina',2,'Person',3960000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5172705,'533','Esther Julian Montaner',31015,203232,'3D2N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Ijen Tour Package drop Bali','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-07-25','2024-07-27','Jacob','Tami',3,'Persons (3)',9360000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-25\", \"text\": \"ETA 12:00 by SJ1921\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Surabaya International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-27\", \"text\": \"Jl. Padma Utara, Legian, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Royal Tunjung Bali Hotel & Villas\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5172731,'533','Esther Julian Montaner',30673,200584,'Deluxe Twin Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-25','2024-07-26','Jacob','Tami',1,'Twin',1440000.00,'Escape the nature with family, friends, colleague and just relax.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5172739,'533','Esther Julian Montaner',30803,202852,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-26','2024-07-27','Jacob','Tami',1,'Twin',840000.00,'At 25 sqm of room size with 46 rooms available. This smart room category is more contemporary in appearance and comes with its own terrace or balcony. Minimalist furnishings are balanced by a neutral decor to soothe the senses and ensure restful slumber. Including a double bed (king or queen) or 2 single beds (twin) with maximum capacity of 2 adults + 1 child or 3 adults. The en-suite bathroom features a modern shower cubicle enclosed in glass together with a marble vanity.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5172916,'534','Jose Antonio Rivero',30680,200919,'Premier Family Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-07','2024-08-08','Guio','Tami',1,'Single + Double',1440000.00,'The most important things in this world is family. Thoughtfully designed with families in mind, our Family Premier Room includes everything needed for you and your family to feel comfortable during your stay. At 43 m2 pf room size with 1 king size and 1 twin size, this room equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, hot and cold shower, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer. Free access to our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. - Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK–IN','{\"date\": \"2024-08-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5172920,'534','Jose Antonio Rivero',30508,212291,'Airport to Jimbaran','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-08','2024-08-08','Guio','Tami',1,'Persons (4-6)',720000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": \"ETA 15.25 by Super Air Jet IU742 from Jakarta on 08 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": \"Uluwatu St, Jimbaran, South Kuta, Badung Regency, Bali 80361\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Kupu Kupu Jimbaran Hotel\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5172931,'534','Jose Antonio Rivero',31581,218316,'Family Suite','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-08-08','2024-08-10','Guio','Tami',1,'Double + Twin',9374400.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5173019,'534','Jose Antonio Rivero',30508,202897,'Uluwatu Temple and Kecak Dance','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-09','2024-08-09','Guio','Tami',4,'Persons (4)',2760000.00,'This half-day tour, is an exciting tour package to visit Padang-Padang Beach, Uluwatu Temple, the famous Balinese Hindu Temple in south part of Bali with breathtaking view of sunset and Indian Ocean. Uluwatu Temple is one of Balinese Hindu Temples located right on the petrifying hill with the crevasse exist in the right and left side. Uluwatu Temple is one of Sad Khayangan (6 biggest temple in Bali) owns magnificent view of the Indian Ocean and sunset as a backdrop. This temple is very amazing where the location is right on the narrow peninsula with deep seawater under it. This tour package is combined with the spectacular Balinese traditional dance performance of Kecak Dance. Balinese Kecak Dance is a spectacular traditional dance with the group of people playing this dance with fire game. It is very exciting and unique dance due to the sound of gamelan is not using the normal gamelan but use their mouth. The dancers make the compact choir with the exquisite dance movement that is one of this dance features. After the dance we returned back to the hotel or seafood restaurant in Jimbaran.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": \"Uluwatu St, Jimbaran, South Kuta, Badung Regency, Bali 80361\", \"time\": \"14:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Kupu Kupu Jimbaran Hotel\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5173024,'534','Jose Antonio Rivero',30508,202891,'Contact with Nature Tour','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-10','2024-08-10','Guio','Tami',4,'Persons (4)',2808000.00,'Deferent than the other tours! This tour will quietly finding you in the fullness of nature. First we will explore Pura Luhur Batukaru. Pura Luhur Batukaru Temple is one of the six directional temples on Bali that are believed to protect the island and its people from evil spirits. Pura Luhur Batukaru protects Bali from the West and was originally built in the 11th century. Pura Luhur Batukaru is one of Bali’s biggest Hindu temples, but because it is off the main tourist trail, sees fewer visitors than many of the other temples. Its peaceful setting amid rainforest at the foot of Mount Batukaru enhances its stunning Balinese architecture. We continue to reach the terrace rice fields Jatiluwih. Jatiluwih is a favorite tourist destination in Bali famous with the beautiful rice terrace unfolding from the foot of mountain until the coastal side. With the beautiful view as according to its name from Jati and Luwih, where Jati mean really and Luwih meaning especial, good, and beautiful or the equivalent. The local paddies are planted in this place look typically of the high relative size plant if it is compared with other pre-eminent paddy planted by most farmers in Bali. You’ll get to explore different parts of the terraces, jump over rivers. We continue our way to the Lake Buyan. We will see one of the most beautiful nature and vegetation scenery on the island. Buyan Lake is a smallest lake in Bali located in the plateau area with cool weather covers it. It is situated in the high land with hill and rain forest surrounds it. Since the location in the plateau area, the fog is usually blanketing the area. This lake can be seen from the top of hill which is called Asah Gobleg. The western end of Lake Buyan, we will start to see the sister lake of Buyan, the Lake Tamblingan. If we follow the road it will bring us closer and closer to Lake Tamblingan, or if we take direction to the right at the following junction at the end of the road, we will arrive in Munduk village, a village rich with coffee plantations. And our final destination is Munduk Waterfalls. This waterfall is a beautiful tourist destination in north part of Bali. Waterfall voice around the charming nature was amazing and it was the separate attraction which can be enjoyed by each visitor who comes to visit. In order to visit the waterfall, all visitors will follow the walkway down until the spot point.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": \"Uluwatu St, Jimbaran, South Kuta, Badung Regency, Bali 80361\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Kupu Kupu Jimbaran Hotel\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": \"Jl. Raya Asah Gobleg, Br. Dinas Asah, Desa Gobleg, Kec. Banjar, Munduk Bali. 81152\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Munduk Tentrem\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5173103,'521','SHEREE RENEE KELLEY',30959,213942,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-11-11','2024-11-13','Melysa','Komang',1,'Double',2088000.00,'Specially designed for savvy travelers seeking comfort and style at 48 sqm of room size. Available in King and Double bet with the option of an extra bed for an additional fee. The room features a cozy living room with a comfortable sofa, LED wall-mounted TV, complimentary high-speed Wi-Fi, and in-room amenities to ensure a relaxing stay experience.',NULL,'Check-in time 14.00 Check-out time 12.00','{\"date\": \"2024-11-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5173119,'534','Jose Antonio Rivero',31322,218317,'Deluxe Garden View Standard','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-08-10','2024-08-12','Guio','Tami',2,'Double',16800000.00,'Munduk Tentrem offers four (4) Deluxe Tentrem Room has 180 panoramic view modern replicas of the traditional Javanese styled wooden house. Every room enjoys extensive views of the surrounding hills and the bay view. Fitted with a king size master bedroom suite and two additional bedrooms with twin beds (convertible to create a king size bed). This room can accommodate up to 2 guests.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5173127,'534','Jose Antonio Rivero',30508,202889,'Tamblingan Jungle Trek - Ulun Danu Temple','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-11','2024-08-11','Guio','Tami',4,'Persons (4)',3360000.00,'Today we will explore the nature of Buyan and Tamblingan lake in our lovely village, it will help you to escape from the crowds and fell the Nature atmosphere of the real jungle of Bali. We will pick you at your hotel at 07:30 AM and we drive to Tamblingan lake. Arrive in the trekking start point, we will have an explanation about the trekking. We will start the trek by entering a lush protected rain-forest area with giant old tress, animal such as macaque, black giant squirrel, birds and old legend temple inside in the Jungle. You will then walk along the shore of this lake situated in the caldera of an extinct Jungle Mountain. Our trekking guide will explain more detail about plants and living creatures in the jungle. This tour also combine with a session of thirty five minutes exploring the Tamblingan lake by dugout canoe to finishing point. Finish with trekking we will drop you to your hotel but we will make a stop at Ulun Danu Temple. Ulun Danu Temple Bratan, the famous temple stands on a small promontory located in the shore of Lake Bratan and has beautiful scenery with this lake and the mountains as backdrop sight.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-11\", \"text\": \"Jl. Raya Asah Gobleg, Br. Dinas Asah, Desa Gobleg, Kec. Banjar, Munduk Bali. 81152\", \"time\": \"07:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Munduk Tentrem\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5173132,'534','Jose Antonio Rivero',30508,213316,'Munduk to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-12','2024-08-12','Guio','Tami',1,'Persons (4-6)',1232000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-12\", \"text\": \"Jl. Raya Asah Gobleg, Br. Dinas Asah, Desa Gobleg, Kec. Banjar, Munduk Bali. 81152\", \"time\": \"12:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Munduk Tentrem\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-12\", \"text\": \"Jl. A.A. Gede Rai No.88, Lodtunduh, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Royal Casa Ganesha Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5173137,'534','Jose Antonio Rivero',30771,213056,'2BR Pool Villa','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-12','2024-08-15','Guio','Tami',1,'Double + Twin',16632000.00,'At 140 m2 room size, a two-bedroom villa with distinctive Jogja Joglo architecture, with a private pool, kitchen, and a balcony with lush greenery views.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5173149,'534','Jose Antonio Rivero',30508,207379,'Ubud to Padang Bai','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-15','2024-08-15','Guio','Tami',1,'Persons (4-6)',1064000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-15\", \"text\": \"Jl. A.A. Gede Rai No.88, Lodtunduh, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"11:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Royal Casa Ganesha Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-15\", \"text\": \"ETD 13.30 to Gili Trawangan by Gili Gili Fast Boat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Padang Bai Harbour\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5173164,'527','ANTONIO SANTOS ROMAN',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-08-04','2024-08-06','Guio','Wiwik',5,'Persons (5)',17400000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Flight Detail: ETA: 07.15 by Batik Air ID6202 from Jakarta on 04 August 2024. ETD: 08.50 by Batik Air ID6134 to Surabaya on 06 August 2024. Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5173178,'527','ANTONIO SANTOS ROMAN',31015,203230,'2D1N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Tour','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-08-06','2024-08-07','Guio','Wiwik',5,'Persons (5)',7440000.00,NULL,NULL,'Flight Detail: ETA: 10.00 by Batik Air ID6134 from Pangkalan Bun on 06 August 2024 ETD: 14.00 by Lion Air JT642 to Lombok on 07 August 2024.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5173200,'534','Jose Antonio Rivero',31007,203170,'Melati 2 Bedroom Villa Private Pool','Confirmed',NULL,5,'2024-08-15','2024-08-20','Guio','Tami',1,'Double + Double',20100000.00,'This villa features a tea/coffee maker, tile/marble floor and private pool.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5173220,'534','Jose Antonio Rivero',30680,200919,'Premier Family Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-20','2024-08-21','Guio','Tami',1,'Single + Double',1344000.00,'The most important things in this world is family. Thoughtfully designed with families in mind, our Family Premier Room includes everything needed for you and your family to feel comfortable during your stay. At 43 m2 pf room size with 1 king size and 1 twin size, this room equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, hot and cold shower, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer. Free access to our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. - Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK–IN','{\"date\": \"2024-08-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5173245,'527','ANTONIO SANTOS ROMAN',31196,204663,'President Suite Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-06','2024-08-07','Guio','Wiwik',1,'Double',3780000.00,'Room type president suite, with spacious room 5,15 m x 7,20 m and have type bed king size and twin. This type of room is available on the 5th floors and has jacuzzi for 4 - 5 persons, living room, and hills view.',NULL,'With Extra Bed','{\"date\": \"2024-08-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5174140,'538','Nuria Catala Senra',32766,216810,'3D2N Open Trip Komodo - Lady Grace / Deluxe Cabin','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-30','2024-09-01','Jacob','Eddy',2,'Per Person (Min. 2 Person)',12840000.00,'DAY 1 : Kelor Island - Manjerite Island - Kalong Island DAY 2 : Padar Island - Long / Pick Beach - Komodo Island - Manta Point - Taka Makasar DAY 3 : Kanawa Island',NULL,'NOTE: size for fins is 38','{\"date\": \"2024-08-30\", \"text\": \"Pick up time between 09.00-10.00 World BnB, dirección: Cowang Dereng, Dasa Batu Cermin, 86754 Labuan Bajo, Indonesia\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-01\", \"text\": \"ETD: 17:30 FLIGHT\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"AIRPORT LABUAN BAJO\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5174159,'535','Enric Rovira',32766,218324,'3D2N Open Trip Komodo - Gamala / Deluxe Ocean','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-23','2024-08-25','Jacob','Eddy',3,'Per Person (Min. 2 Person)',15480000.00,'DAY 1 : Kelor Island - Manjerite Island - Kalong Island DAY 2 : Padar Island - Long / Pick Beach - Komodo Island - Manta Point - Taka Makasar DAY 3 : Kanawa Island',NULL,'Pick up TIme Between 09.00-10.00','{\"date\": \"2024-08-23\", \"text\": \"ETA: Hotel Wisata Address: Jl. Soekarno Hatta No.39, 86554 Labuan Bajo, Indonesia Phone: +62812 37547403\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-25\", \"text\": \"ETD: Hotel Wisata Address: Jl. Soekarno Hatta No.39, 86554 Labuan Bajo, Indonesia Phone: +62812 37547403\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5174163,'537','Diana Nicoli',30806,202002,'4D3N Borneo Orangutan & Reforestation Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO7',4,'2024-07-17','2024-07-20','Yuli','Yuli',5,'Persons (5)',20720000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN – KUMAI PORT – TANJUNG HARAPAN Your “Orangutan & Reforestation Tour” begins upon arrival at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan is Cape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : TANJUNG HARAPAN VILLAGE – PROBOSCIS TOUR – CAMP LEAKEY After an extraordinary breakfast, you go to visit the village inside the national park, named Tanjung Harapan Village. Here you will see the activities of the locals. After the visit, you will return to the klotok cruise up to the Sekonyer River. You will see nice vegetation around the river bank, including Nipa Palm, Pandanus, and some kinds of trees that are growing up around the river. See some wildlifes such as birds, Macaques, Proboscis Monkeys and Orangutans. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large monitor lizards. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. Note: The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. Meals : Breakfast – Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : PONDOK TANGGUI – CAMP LEAKEY – BOAT After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continue to add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After lunch, you will have the opportunity to repeat feeding camp at Camp Leaky. It is a unique opportunity to dedicate more time to your observation and to discover more wild animals, along with the Orangutans. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note: If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast – Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 4 : KUMAI PORT – PANGKALAN BUN Today we end our stay in the jungles of Borneo. Our “Orangutan & Reforestation Tour” is about to finish. In the early morning we will have breakfast on the boat, to then go to the port and in turn, be transferred to the airport. The boat departure will be at the latest at 10am, but we adapt to your flights if your flight leaves earlier in the morning. If you decide to take an afternoon flight, we can take you directly to the airport at 10 or if you want a city tour in the Arut village to drop you off at the airport later, it could be arranged at extra cost. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'4D3N Orangutan Tour based on Private Standard Klotok, with English speaking guide Day 01/17 July 2024: PANGKALAN BUN – KUMAI – TANJUNG HARAPAN (B,L,D) Day 02/18 July 2024: TANJUNG HARAPAN FOREST TREKKING & CAMP LEAKEY (B,L,D) Day 03/19 July 2024: PONDOK TANGGUY – CAMP LEAKEY (B,L,D) Day 04/20 July 2024: KUMAI – PANGKALAN BUN AIRPORT (B) Flight details: ETA 07:15 by Batik Air ID6202 from Jakarta on 17 July ETD 08:50 by Batik Air ID6134 to Surabaya on 20 July Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-07-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5174181,'536','Elio Vazquez Ambrosio',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-06','2024-07-06','Guio','Komang',1,'Persons (4-6)',784000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-06\", \"text\": \"ETA : 22.20 by Emirates EK398 from Dubai on 06 July 2024\", \"time\": \"22:20\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"International Ngurah Rai Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-06\", \"text\": \"Pertiwi Resort Ubud, Jl. Monkey Forest, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571•(0361) 975236\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5174201,'537','Diana Nicoli',31015,203230,'2D1N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Tour','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-07-20','2024-07-21','Yuli','Yuli',5,'Persons (5)',6944000.00,NULL,NULL,'2D1N Surabaya - Bromo Tour - Surabaya, with English speaking guide Day 01/20 July 2024: ARRIVAL IN SURABAYA - BROMO Day 02/21 July 2024: BROMO TOUR - TRANSFER TO SURABAYA AIRPORT Hotel in Bromo: Lereng Bromo Hotel Jl. Bromo, Ledoksari Tosari, Wonokitri, Pasuruan, Jawa Timur Phone: +62343 4020999 / +62813 36598889 Flight details: ETA 10:00 by Batik Air ID6134 from Pangkalan Bun on 20 July ETD 16:15 by Lion Air JT914 to Denpasar on 21 July','{\"date\": \"2024-07-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5174277,'536','Elio Vazquez Ambrosio',30768,201343,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-07-06','2024-07-09','Guio','Komang',2,'Double',7392000.00,'A premium room with upgraded amenities and toiletries. This 38 sqm suite comes with a walk-in shower, flat screen TV and a safe. Enjoy our complimentary daily mineral water and daily afternoon tea. With an extra space, the room can accommodate up to 3 adults with an extra bed that will come at an additional charge or guests who travel with a child.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5174286,'537','Diana Nicoli',31196,204663,'President Suite Room + 1 Extra Bed','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-20','2024-07-21','Yuli','Yuli',1,'Double + Twin',3528000.00,'Room type president suite, with spacious room 5,15 m x 7,20 m and have type bed king size and twin. This type of room is available on the 5th floors and has jacuzzi for 4 - 5 persons, living room, and hills view.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5174295,'536','Elio Vazquez Ambrosio',30508,202893,'Lempuyang Temple Tour (Tenganan - Virgin Beach - Lempuyang)','Confirmed','C2I-BALI11',1,'2024-07-08','2024-07-08','Guio','Komang',4,'Persons (4)',2732800.00,'At the agreed time, our guide will pick you up to start the tour in the eastern part of Bali. The first place you will visit is Goa Lawah Temple. Goa Lawah Temple consists of two names, \"Goa\" which means cave and \"Lawah\" which means bat. Several thousand bats are flying in the cave as the name suggests. With the lights fading as you go deeper inside the cave, it gives off a very strange atmosphere. From Goa Lawah, we continue our way to Lempuyang Temple. Upon arrival, the temple will greet you with its gratifying panorama that extends into infinity. On a clear, sunny day, you\'ll be able to gaze out over the mountains, Amlapura city, and Mount Agung, an incredibly magnificent sight that\'s beautiful beyond words. This portrait of heaven is beautifully framed by the Gapura Candi Bentar (the gate of the temple). Our journey continues to visit Tirta Gangga. The site is a paradise surrounded by water, with all the pools decorated with unusual statues. With its seclusion and a view of the surrounding rice paddies, Tirta Gangga is a wonderful place. At the end of the trip we go to Tenganan Village, the most famous Bali Agas (the “original” Bali people) in the city. With its characteristics, the city village is arranged in parallel along the wide main road paved with rows of cobblestones. In Tenganan, women still weave the famous Kamben Geringsing, or \"burnt cloth,\" which has the power to immunize the wearer against evil. We take a close look at what they do in their daily lives in a traditional lifestyle. From Tenganan, we will transfer you to the hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-08\", \"text\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 1 Ubud, Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kec. Gianyar, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 978018\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-08\", \"text\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 1 Ubud, Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kec. Gianyar, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 978018\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5174296,'523','Ms. Andrea Patricia Rohrer',31092,214371,'3D2N Banjarmasin Trip / A. Swiss-Belhotel *3','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-07-05','2024-07-07','Nicholas','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',19800000.00,'DAY 1 : AIRPORT - HOTEL - FREE PROGRAM Arrival in the afternoon at Syamsuddion Nor airport, directly transferred to hotel, check in and free program. Meals : Dinner DAY 2 : FLOATING MARKET - ALALAK ISLAND - CANAL Early morning at 05.00 boating to Lokbaintan village to visit the floating market, boating back to hotel for breakfast. Afternoon activities is boating to the Alalak island to see the boats and canoes productions and the Canals at the afternoon. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner DAY 3 : TRANSFER AIRPORT Free program till departure time to the airport. Meals : Breakfast',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-05\", \"text\": \"ETA 15.25 by Lion Air JT222 from Surabaya on 05 Jul\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Banjarmasin International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-07\", \"text\": \"ETD 09.30 by Super Air Jet IU635 to Surabaya on 07 Jul\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5174299,'536','Elio Vazquez Ambrosio',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-07','2024-07-07','Guio','Komang',4,'Persons (4)',2643200.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-07\", \"text\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 1 Ubud, Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kec. Gianyar, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 978018\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-07\", \"text\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 1 Ubud, Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kec. Gianyar, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 978018\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5174315,'536','Elio Vazquez Ambrosio',30508,212411,'Ubud to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-09','2024-07-09','Guio','Komang',1,'Persons (4-6)',784000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-09\", \"text\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 1 Ubud, Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kec. Gianyar, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 978018\", \"time\": \"12:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-09\", \"text\": \"TBA\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5174347,'539','Karin Allgoewer',30508,215968,'08D07D Banda Naira Tour','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-28','2024-08-28','Guio','Komang',2,'Person (1)',26160000.00,NULL,NULL,'Arrival Flight detail in Ambon : ETA : 15.35 by GARUDA GA646 from Jakarta on 28 August 2024 Departure Flight detail in Ambon : ETD : 16.20 by GARUDA GA647 to Jakarta on 04 September 2024','{\"date\": \"2024-08-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5174414,'541','DAVID VELICIAS MANSILLA',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-26','2024-07-26','Guio','Komang',1,'Persons (1-3)',392000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-26\", \"text\": \"ETA : 18.50 by Batik Air ID7134 from Singapore on 26 July 2024\", \"time\": \"18:50\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"International Ngurah Rai Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-26\", \"text\": \"Kamandalu Ubud, Jl. Raya Andong, Banjar Nagi, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 975825\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5174428,'540','Maria Adela Zamora Ramirez',30680,200914,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-23','2024-07-24','Igo','Tami',1,'Double',960000.00,'Enjoy our spacious elegant deluxe room with 40 m2 of room size. Enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, hot and cold shower, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. - Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK–IN','{\"date\": \"2024-07-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5174433,'540','Maria Adela Zamora Ramirez',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-07-24','2024-07-26','Igo','Tami',3,'Persons (3)',12600000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-07-24\", \"text\": \"ETA 07.15 by Batik Air ID6202 from Jakarta on 24 Jul\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pangkalan Bun Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-26\", \"text\": \"ETD 10.25 by Batik Air ID6303 to Semarang on 26 Jul\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5174439,'540','Maria Adela Zamora Ramirez',30783,212220,'4D3N Yogyakarta - Mt. Merapi with Jeep / C. Ayaartta (Deluxe Room)','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-07-26','2024-07-29','Igo','Tami',3,'Persons (2-3)',15390000.00,'D1 Arrival Yogyakarta International Airport – Transfer to hotel: Welcome to the cradle of Indonesian culture, Yogyakarta. A tourist destination for its ancient palaces, temples, batik workshops, gamelan music orchestras, court dances and wayang puppet shows. Upon your arrival in Yogyakarta a representative of come2indonesia will be waiting for you with a sign indicating your name to take you to your hotel and the rest of the day is for you. D2 Borobudur temple – Candirejo Village Tour by Horse cart / bicycle – Merapi lava tour Including Jeep: You will have your deserved breakfast at the hotel. Today’s tour will make you enjoy the authentic Javanese essence. You will start your route in the direction of with the Borobudur Temple (Candi Borobudur), the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. We will tour around the temple, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano has been producing during its history. After visiting one of the most important Buddhist temples in Southeast Asia, and in a horse carriage (Andong) we will visit the villages that surround this temple. These are authentic Javanese villages where culture and tradition are the protagonists. As you spend your days in this country and go around the different islands, you will realize how different Indonesians are among them in terms of clothing, food, architecture and even language. Today we will learn about and share these Javanese places. Then we will go to Kaliurang / Kalidalem to see Mount Merapi in constant activity. Here in a 4x4 jeep driven by specialized drivers, we will climb its skirt to see the remains of the 2010 eruption such as houses buried by ashes, a multitude of objects paralyzed by lava, etc. In addition, an open-air tribute museum presided over by the clock that marks the time just when the lava passed through it has been improvised. Accompanied by photos of the rescue, it will make us feel very closely the experiences of that fateful day. After finishing this day full of emotions, we will take you back to your hotel. D3 City Tour Jogjakarta Visit Sultan Palace, Watercastle and Bird Market – Prambanan Temple: After breakfast and at the indicated time we will head towards the heart of the city. We will visit the Keraton known as the Sultan’s Palace. The palace is a complex building two centuries old, located in the heart of the city. You will hear the song of the “freedom” of the birds in the bird market, we will visit the “Water Castle” that occupies the highest part at the northern end of the vast complex of Taman Sari, Malioboro Street, main street of Yogyakarta, with its merchants, horse carriages, taxi-bikes and markets. An incredible experience that will make the hours fly by. After finishing the tour in the center of the city of Yogyakarta, we will go to the northeast direction Candi Prambanan, the temple of the Hinduists and classified as a World Heritage Site by Unesco since 1991. The built of this temple was finished around the year 856 to commemorate the victory of the descendant Sanjaya of Siva, Rikai Pikatan on the last sovereign Sailendra of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to the Trimurti, the expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the Destroyer. After this unforgettable day, we will take you to your hotel. D4 Transfer out Yogyakarta International airport: Today our adventure ends at the cradle of Indonesian culture. Depending on the time of your flight, we will pick you up to take you to the airport and take the flight to your next destination. End of our services. Thank you very much for exploring Yogyakarta by the hand of Come2indonesia.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-26\", \"text\": \"ETA 11.25 by Batik Air ID6303 from Pangkalan Bun on 26 Jul\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Semarang International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-29\", \"text\": \"ETD 14.00 by Lion Air JT566 to Denpasar on 29 Jul\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Yogyakarta International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5174453,'540','Maria Adela Zamora Ramirez',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-29','2024-07-29','Igo','Tami',3,'Persons (1-3)',1080000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-29\", \"text\": \"ETA 16.25 by Lion Air JT566 from Yogyakarta on 29 Jul\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-29\", \"text\": \"Jl. A.A. Gede Rai No.88, Lodtunduh, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Royal Casa Ganesha Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5174455,'540','Maria Adela Zamora Ramirez',30771,201371,'Grand Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-07-29','2024-08-02','Igo','Tami',1,'Double',6000000.00,'At 31,8 m2 room size, with beautiful garden view and charming decor. It includes a seating area and a private bathroom with a shower and complimentary bathroom amenities.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5174458,'540','Maria Adela Zamora Ramirez',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-30','2024-07-30','Igo','Tami',3,'Persons (3)',2160000.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-30\", \"text\": \"Jl. A.A. Gede Rai No.88, Lodtunduh, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Royal Casa Ganesha Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5174460,'540','Maria Adela Zamora Ramirez',30508,202894,'Kehen Temple - Pengelipuran - Kintamani','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-31','2024-07-31','Igo','Tami',3,'Persons (3)',1872000.00,'Our wonderful tour starts from Kehen Temple. It is an ancient Hindu temple complex boasting unique architectural features. The staircases reaching from the ground to temple courtyard are carved sandstone mythical animal and Balinese folklore figure statues and also the central vestibule. The temple’s walls are also ornate with Chinese porcelain plates, which are a tribute to the historical relations between the local Bali kingdom and China. Afterwards, we continue to Penglipuran, a village that succeeded in preserving its 75-hectare bamboo forest located in the northern part of the village. Members of this village have a strong commitment to the system of \'Ayahan Desa\' - a philosophy committed to respecting the land on which the village stands. To concludes the day, we stop by at Tukad Cepung Waterfall. Well-guarded by the circular cliffs, this waterfall is difficult to locate for the first time visitor. The circular cliffs give you the feeling of being in a cave, while the open sky right from where the waterfall emerges, gives you the most enchanting view. The sunlight falls on the glistering waterfall creating a rainbow, which feels as though it is projected right up to you. If you have never seen water flowing from the sky, then this would be your chance! After spending your time there, we go back to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-31\", \"text\": \"Jl. A.A. Gede Rai No.88, Lodtunduh, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Royal Casa Ganesha Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-31\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5174470,'540','Maria Adela Zamora Ramirez',30508,207379,'Ubud to Padang Bai','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-02','2024-08-02','Igo','Tami',3,'Persons (1-3)',1800000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-02\", \"text\": \"Jl. A.A. Gede Rai No.88, Lodtunduh, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Royal Casa Ganesha Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-02\", \"text\": \"ETD 08.30 to Gili Air by Gili Gili Fast Boat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Padang Bai Harbour\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5174477,'540','Maria Adela Zamora Ramirez',32607,215994,'Deluxe Suite','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-02','2024-08-05','Igo','Tami',1,'Double',4680000.00,'At 38 m2 room size, welcome to the Deluxe suite with ocean view. Sleep soundly during your trip to one of Gili Islands in Lombok, West Nusa Tenggara, Indonesia in our deluxe suite room, which is designed in a modern style and features a comfortable king bed, spacious, and individually designed.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5174573,'527','ANTONIO SANTOS ROMAN',32915,217999,'Family Room + Extra Bed','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-03','2024-08-04','Guio','Wiwik',1,'Double + Double',2220000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5174835,'542','Alberto Hernandez Castillo',31083,203735,'6D5N Flores - Komodo (LOB 2D1N - Rinca - Komodo)','Confirmed',NULL,6,'2024-08-10','2024-08-15','Jacob','Tami',7,'Persons (6-7 / Double)',76650000.00,'TOUR ITINERARY DAY 1 : MAUMERE - MONI Welcome to Maumere, the capital of Flores! This is the starting point of our Flores overland tour. Meet and greet with our friendly guide at the airport, then we will drive to Moni village. We will go from East to West through the famous and only road that crosses the island. It is known among locals as the “Transflores”. It takes about 4 hours driving, but we can make some stops on the way to Moni to make the journey more bearable. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Kelimutu Ecolodge or Kelimutu Paradiso Resort DAY 2 : MONI - VOLCANO KELIMUTU - BAJAWA Today we will get up early to see sunrise on top of the Kelimutu. The Kelimutu is a large volcano, which we access practically by car, until the last 20 minutes, which will be practically a walk in the field. When reaching the top, we can see 3 craters, which have become three lakes, ofdifferent colors. One black, one yellow and one a little purple, but the great thing is that they change color, especially in the moments of dawn! Take a coat, because sometimes it is a bit cold while we wait for the sunrise. After admiring this natural wonder, we headed to Bajawa. In the vicinity of our hotel in Moni, we will be able to do some stops between the villages, where we can see how most of the women make Sarongs with the looms, in a totally traditional way. We can also pass by a waterfall in the surroundings of the town. On the way to Bajawa we will stop in the capital of Flores, an immense bay open to the Indian Ocean, the city of Ende, where we will have lunch, visit the Market, etc. On the outskirts of Ende, we will make a stop to see a cove, called the beach of the blue stones (although the stones are really green?) Where we will see dozens of workers, collecting stones and classifying them, and then be exported, due to the beauty they represent for gardens in Hong Kong and Singapore. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : New Virgo Hotel DAY 3 : BAJAWA - BENA - RUTENG Today, in the morning we will be able to have our well-deserved breakfast, and then we will go to Bena, one of the best known traditional villages of Flores, belonging to the Ngadas tribes. Tribes that despite being Christianized, they still maintain their animistic beliefs. There you can see the way of life of the Bajawa people. In the village complex they have all the houses with the doors open towards the Ngadhu and Bhaga (Man and Woman) temples. Altars that they use both to bless the town and for the harvest, as they represent their ancestors. We will also take the opportunity to stop on the slopes of the great Inerie volcano and take photos of its continuous fumaroles. After having lunch on the way, our a new long drive begins, about another 4-5 hours until we reach Ruteng. But we will stop in a traditional town, called Aimere, where we will see (or for those who want to try) how they distill the Palm liquor, called Arak. If we get to Ruteng early, we can visit the cave where the Homo Florensis was discovered. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accomodation : Spring Hill or Sinda or Revaya Hotel DAY 4 : RUTENG - LABUAN BAJO - RINCA ISLAND - KALONG ISLAND In the early morning, we continue the march to reach Labuan Bajo. On the way to Labuan Bajo, we will stop at Golo Cara, to see the giant rice pots, the only ones in the world shaped like a spider web, a wonder to behold. Upon arrival in Labuan Bajo, directly transfer to the port for in turn we will sail to Rinca Island. Today we will go to see the Komodo Dragons, for that we first go to Rinca Island, where in addition to Komodo dragons in their natural environment, we will be able to see Water buffalo, macaque monkeys, cockatoos, wild horses, etc. A trekk lasts about 2 hours around the island, from the hands of a Rangers of the national park. Then in the afternoon, the boat is anchored next to some mangroves, to see how millions of bats take flight at sunset. You will have dinner and spend the night on the boat in the Rinca Sea. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Traditional Wooden Boat DAY 5 : KOMODO ISLAND - PINK BEACH - MANTA POINT - LABUAN BAJO Today, we will sail to Loh Liang that is the ranger’s station on Komodo Island. During the sail, you will realize that the sea is like a great lake dotted with hundreds of tiny islands, most of them uninhabited, or with only a few fishermen, who moor in them to rest or spend the night. Once on the island, we have to enter the office of the rangers to register and pay the national park fee. There we will be assigned a ranger who will accompany us at all times while we are inside the island. During the trekking, in addition to Komodo dragons in their natural environment. There are other animals in the area such as Timor deer, wild pigs, sulfur cockatoos, snakes, etc. At the end of the trek, we head back to the port and continue the sail. After a short while, we will reach Pink Beach where we can do snorkeling in the middle of coral reefs full of life. Did you know that Indonesia is the most important center of marine biodiversity in the world? It is where the species of the Indian Ocean and Pacific Ocean come together with the endemic species of Indonesia. It makes Indonesia have the largest number of underwater species in the world. Well, you will be swimming in the middle of all that. Afterwards, we will go to another beautiful place. After a short navigation, we arrive at Manta Point where we have the chance to see huge “blankets” in the waters as we snorkel. Sometimes, we can even see them from the boat. Lunch is served on board.In the afternoon we go to the port of Labuan Bajo and from there to the hotel. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Puri Sari or La Cecile or Golo Hilltop DAY 6 : LABUAN BAJO - BALI - END OF TRIP Today in the morning, if the flight schedule allows us, we will go to see the cave of the mirrors, and at about noon we go to Labuan Bajo airport to take the direct flight to Bali and continue your return flight Depending on the time of your flight. End of our services. Meals : Breakfast',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": \"ETA 11.10 by Wings Air IW1952 from Labuan Bajo on 10 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ende Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-15\", \"text\": \"ETD 16.35 by Air Asia QZ861 to Jakarta on 15 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Labuan Bajo Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5175663,'543','James Melrod',30571,202570,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-28','2024-08-29','Ayu','Eddy',1,'Double',1540000.00,'Located at the Third & Fourth Floor, 38 sqm comfort living with a touch of Balinese style featuring completed fitting, Cable TV, a fancy bathroom comprises rain shower and good quality amenities. Also dedicated WiFi Access to complete your day.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5175767,'473','Alessia Atzori & Charlon Tabone',30508,213069,'Kusamba to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-16','2024-09-16','Ayu','Eddy',1,'Persons (1-3)',392000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-16\", \"text\": \"ETA 16.20 From Nusa Penida - by the Angkal\", \"time\": \"16:20\", \"locality\": \"KUSAMBA PORT\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-16\", \"text\": \"Tejaprana Resort & Spa Address : Jl. Raya Tegallalang, Banjar Sapat, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80561 Phone: (0361) 9080939\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5176199,'537','Diana Nicoli',30805,202689,'CGK-PKN','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-17','2024-07-17','Yuli','Yuli',5,'Person',8560000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5176201,'537','Diana Nicoli',30805,202689,'CGK-PKN (extra baggage 5kg)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-17','2024-07-17','Yuli','Yuli',3,'Person',750000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5176204,'537','Diana Nicoli',30805,212272,'PKN-SUB','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-20','2024-07-20','Yuli','Yuli',5,'Person',9095000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5176205,'537','Diana Nicoli',30805,212272,'PKN-SUB (extra baggage 5kg)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-20','2024-0