026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5181692,'561','RICARD CREUS PEREZ',30508,216161,'Uluwatu to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-21','2024-07-21','Melysa','Komang',1,'Persons (1-3)',420000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-21\", \"text\": \"Adila Bali Hotel Uluwatu, Jl. Pura Batu Pageh No.79, Ungasan, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80364 Telepon: 0812-4651-4895\", \"time\": \"05:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Uluwatu\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-21\", \"text\": \"ETD : 09.55 by Qatar Airways QR965 to Doha on 21 Jul 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Interational Airport Ngurah Rai\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5181714,'561','RICARD CREUS PEREZ',31849,218500,'Deluxe Sea View Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-07-19','2024-07-21','Melysa','Komang',1,'Double',3628800.00,'Bright and spacious air-conditioned rooms with view to the ocean and the pool deck. En-suite marble bathrooms with a shower and free toiletries. Guests enjoy views of the surrounding greenery and the sea beyond.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5181748,'508','Andrea Carl Brincat Dimech',30508,218503,'Bedugul to Candidasa','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-30','2024-07-30','Ayu','Ayu',1,'Persons (4-6)',1232000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"10:00\", \"locality\": \"Dusun Bedugul Hotel\", \"location\": \"Candikuning, Baturiti, Tabanan Regency, Bali 82191, Indonesia\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Nirwana Beach Resort Candidasa\", \"location\": \"Jalan Sengkidu, Jl. Raya Candidasa, Sengkidu, Kec. Manggis, Kabupaten Karangasem\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5181773,'564','Steven Edward Foldi',31591,207372,'4D3N Tangkoko','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-08-13','2024-08-16','Nicholas','Tami',2,'Persons (2-3)',9240000.00,'Day 1 : MANADO - TANGKOKO - The expedition begins The adventure begins with meeting your guide at the Manado airport. Then you will start the journey of about 2 and a half hours by car to the Tangkoko Forest where you will do the check in at your Homestay or Lodge. Upon arrival, you will have a talk about what you will see and preparations for the trekking. Meals : Dinner Accommodation : Bird House Homestay or Similar Days 02 - 03 : Tangkoko Nature Reserve These days will be dedicated to exploring the jungle in search of animals and bird watching. You will start the trekking that will take you to Tangkok National Park. In just 40 minutes by boat, you will reach the Batuangus beach where you will then climb Mount Tangkoko (1500 m). The dense and virgin jungle is home to some unique animal species in North Sulawesi such as the crested black macaque and the tarsier spectrum that has become known as \"the smallest primate in the world\". As you will be trekking through the lush jungle, you will probably see and hear the red gnarled hornbill as well as the Maleo which is a Megapod Bird that lays eggs on large mounds it builds on the black sand. You can also find couscous, which is a relative of the Australian koala. The forest ranger will accompany you all the way to the top of Tangkoko Mountain. In the afternoon you will return to the station. Alternatively, you can have three hours of trekking in the lowland jungle or swimming on the black sand beach of Tangkoko. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Bird House Homestay or Similar Day 04 : Tangkoko - Manado After breakfast, you can spend the morning in the surroundings of the National Park and at the agreed time, with your guide, you will have the transfer to Manado. Thank you for exploring this unique jungle with us. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Flight information ETA 12.25 by Batik Air ID6280 from Jakarta on 13 Aug ETD 14.00 by Scoot TR217 to Singapore on 16 Aug (Steve) ETD 14.45 by Garuda GA601 to Jakarta on 16 Aug (Nicholas)','{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5181785,'565','Maria Dolores Curras Mateo',30680,200914,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-03','2024-08-04','Nicholas','Tami',1,'Double',960000.00,'Enjoy our spacious elegant deluxe room with 40 m2 of room size. Enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, hot and cold shower, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. - Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK–IN','{\"date\": \"2024-08-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5181806,'565','Maria Dolores Curras Mateo',30783,212189,'2D1N Yogyakarta / C. Ayaartta (Deluxe Room)','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-08-04','2024-08-05','Nicholas','Tami',3,'Persons (2-3)',9450000.00,'D1 : Arrival Yogyakarta International Airport - Visit Borobudur Temple incl. Mendut and Pawon - check in hotel Welcome to the cradle of Indonesian culture, Yogyakarta. A tourist destination for its ancient palaces, temples, batik workshops, gamelan music orchestras, court dances and wayang puppet shows. Upon your arrival in Yogyakarta a representative of come2indonesia will be waiting for you with a sign indicating your name to start exploring this special city. We will start by heading towards Borobudur Temple (Candi Borobudur), the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. We will tour around the temple, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano has been producing during its history. After visiting one of the most important Buddhist temples in Southeast Asia, we continue our journey to the Mendut temple and Pawon temple. D2 : Morning visit Prambanan Temple - City Tour Yogyakarta visit Sultan Palace, Watercastle and Bird Market - Transfer to Yogyakarta International Airport You will enjoy a well-deserved breakfast at the hotel and we will start by heading towards Candi Prambanan, the temple of the Hinduists and classified as a World Heritage Site by Unesco since 1991. The built of this temple was finished around the year 856 to commemorate the victory of the descendant Sanjaya of Siva, Rikai Pikatan on the last sovereign Sailendra of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to the Trimurti, the expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the destroyer. After this visit we go to the Keraton known as the Sultan’s Palace. The palace is a complex building two centuries old, located in the heart of the city. You will hear the song of the “freedom” of the birds in the bird market, we will visit the “Water Castle” that occupies the highest part at the northern end of the vast complex of Taman Sari, Malioboro Street, main street of Yogyakarta, with its merchants, horse carriages, taxi-bikes and markets. An incredible experience that will make the hours fly by. According to the time of your flight, we will pick you up to take you to the airport and take the flight to your next destination. End of our services. Thank you very much for exploring Yogyakarta by the hand of Come2indonesia.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-04\", \"text\": \"ETA 07.10 by Batik Air ID6368 from Jakarta on 04 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Yogyakarta International Airport (YIA)\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-05\", \"text\": \"Jl. Gajahmada No.101, Miroto, Kec. Semarang Tengah, Kota Semarang, Jawa Tengah\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"ARTOTEL Gajahmada Semarang\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5181809,'565','Maria Dolores Curras Mateo',30672,200747,'Studio 30 (Deluxe) Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-05','2024-08-06','Nicholas','Tami',1,'Double',804000.00,'Studio 30 (Deluxe) room with 25 sqm sized room, and exclusive ARTOTEL bedding collection, with facilities 43\" inch lcd tv, 24 hours in-room service, high speed internet wi-fi, safety deposit box, hair dryer.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5181817,'565','Maria Dolores Curras Mateo',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-08-06','2024-08-08','Nicholas','Tami',3,'Persons (3)',12600000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-06\", \"text\": \"ETA 09.30 by Batik Air ID6302 from Semarang on 06 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pangkalan Bun Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": \"ETD 08.50 by Batik Air ID6134 to Surabaya on 08 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5181819,'565','Maria Dolores Curras Mateo',31015,203230,'2D1N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Tour','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-08-08','2024-08-09','Nicholas','Tami',3,'Persons (3)',5400000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": \"ETA 10.00 by Batik Air ID6134 from Pangkalan Bun on 08 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Surabaya International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": \"ETD 15.45 by Lion Air JT920 to Denpasar on 09 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5181822,'565','Maria Dolores Curras Mateo',31196,204658,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-08','2024-08-09','Nicholas','Tami',1,'Double',1428000.00,'Room type deluxe, with spacious room 3,41 m x 6,09 m and have type bed king size or twin bed. This type of room is available on the 2nd, 3rd and 4th floors and has of the hills view.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5181926,'565','Maria Dolores Curras Mateo',30571,202567,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-09','2024-08-10','Nicholas','Tami',1,'Double',1170000.00,'Located at the Second Floor, 35 sqm comfort living with a touch of Balinese style featuring completed fitting, Cable TV, a fancy bathroom comprises rain shower and good quality amenities. Also dedicated Wi-Fi Access to complete your day.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5181942,'565','Maria Dolores Curras Mateo',31658,208111,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-08-10','2024-08-12','Nicholas','Tami',1,'Double',1680000.00,'This room featured Air Conditioning, telephone, hot and cold water, satellite TV on 32 LCD screen. Bathroom amenities; Hair dryer, Bathrobe, Towels, Free toiletries, Guest toilet, Cleaning products, Body soap, Hair conditioner, Shampoo, Tooth brush, Toilet paper. Facilities inside the room are coffee/tea maker, mini bar, wake up service.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5181960,'565','Maria Dolores Curras Mateo',31083,203792,'Komodo Island Full Day Tour (Fast Boat - Pick Up/Drop Off Labuan Bajo)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-11','2024-08-11','Nicholas','Tami',3,'Persons (2-3)',20286000.00,'TOUR ITINERARY Highlights: Padar Island, Komodo Island, Long beach, Pink Beach, Manta Point & Kanawa. PICK UP / ARRIVE LABUAN BAJO - PADAR - KOMODO - PINK BEACH - MANTA POINT - LABUAHAN BAJO Pick up & meeting service with our tour guide and transfer to the pier of Labuan Bajo for sailing directly to Loh Liang – the Ranger station in Komodo Island. By passing through many small islands, it will be 3 hours with slow wooden boat and 1.50 hours by speed boat to reach the pier of Komodo island. After registering start to take basic trekking to see the GIANT RIZARD / KOMODO DRAGON and other wild animals as: Timor deer, wild pig, wild chicken and many variously of tropical bird. Please keep your look at any directions as sometimes you will also find young Komodo dragon hanging over the trees. A local ranger will be led you during the trek. Return to the boat on to Pink beach for snorkeling, swimming and relaxing. It is really spectacular and unspoiled coral reef and many color fish. Sail toward MANTA POINT to exploring Huge Mantas by snorkeling even watching from your boat trip (can’t be guaranteed if weather is not good, like wave and current are strongly). Lunch will be provided on board. Late in the afternoon back to Labuan Bajo harbor and transfer to your prefer Hotel for overnight and Dinner. Meals : Lunch Attention: The itinerary is subject to change due to the weather, tide level and operating conditions without prior notice.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-11\", \"text\": \"Macang Tanggar, Komodo, West Manggarai Regency, East Nusa Tenggara\", \"time\": \"07:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Luwansa Beach Resort\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5181997,'565','Maria Dolores Curras Mateo',30680,200914,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-12','2024-08-13','Nicholas','Tami',1,'Double',960000.00,'Enjoy our spacious elegant deluxe room with 40 m2 of room size. Enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, hot and cold shower, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. - Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK–IN','{\"date\": \"2024-08-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5182019,'566