s center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, hot and cold shower, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available)','{\"date\": \"2024-08-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5185404,'583','Sonia Garcia Lazaro',30544,201961,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-08','2024-08-11','Melysa','Komang',1,'Double',6120000.00,'The Deluxe Room beautifully design with Balinese contemporary which provides a comfortable space to relax in the tranquility of the resort’s peaceful surroundings.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5185407,'583','Sonia Garcia Lazaro',30508,212408,'Ubud to Uluwatu','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-11','2024-08-11','Melysa','Komang',2,'Persons (1-3)',840000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-11\", \"text\": \"Adiwana Svarga Loka, Jalan Raya Penestanan Kelod, Sayan, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 979279\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-11\", \"text\": \"Adila Villa Uluwatu,Jl. Pura Batu Pageh No.79, Ungasan, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80364 Telepon: 0812-4651-4895\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Uluwatu\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5185408,'583','Sonia Garcia Lazaro',31849,218500,'Deluxe Sea View Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-08-11','2024-08-13','Melysa','Komang',1,'Double',3888000.00,'Bright and spacious air-conditioned rooms with view to the ocean and the pool deck. En-suite marble bathrooms with a shower and free toiletries. Guests enjoy views of the surrounding greenery and the sea beyond.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5185414,'583','Sonia Garcia Lazaro',30508,216161,'Uluwatu to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-13','2024-08-13','Melysa','Komang',2,'Persons (1-3)',840000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": \"Adila Bali Uluwatu, Jl. Pura Batu Pageh No.79, Ungasan, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80364 Telepon: 0812-4651-4895\", \"time\": \"13:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Uluwatu\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": \"ETD : 17.35 by Garuda Indonesia GA 349 to Surabaya on 13 Aug 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5185430,'583','Sonia Garcia Lazaro',31365,216725,'Standard Room (Room Breakfast)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-13','2024-08-14','Melysa','Komang',1,'Double',576000.00,'This twin or double room has air conditioning, desk and a flat-screen cable TV. Private bathroom comes with a shower and free toiletries.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5185432,'583','Sonia Garcia Lazaro',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-08-14','2024-08-16','Melysa','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',10800000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5185434,'584','Marla Conley',30711,200830,'Bisma Suite Room','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-09-08','2024-09-12','Ayu','Wiwik',1,'Double',12566400.00,'Spacious one-bedroom suite of 88 sqm with private balcony for a sophisticated Ubud getaway. Interiors feature extensive use of wood and fine Indonesian textiles and art, lending an understated elegance to the space. Featuring a private balcony, this room includes a flat-screen TV and an en-suite bathroom with a bathtub and a shower, and many more.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5185435,'584','Marla Conley',30571,202567,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-12','2024-09-13','Ayu','Wiwik',1,'Double',1204000.00,'Located at the Second Floor, 35 sqm comfort living with a touch of Balinese style featuring completed fitting, Cable TV, a fancy bathroom comprises rain shower and good quality amenities. Also dedicated Wi-Fi Access to complete your day.',NULL,'Check in: 14.00 PM Check out: 12.00 Noon Flight information: ETD 00.20 by Garuda GA880 to Narita on 14 September 2024 \"PLEASE CONSULT YOUR DEPARTURE TIME TRANSFER UPON CHECK IN\"','{\"date\": \"2024-09-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5185436,'584','Marla Conley',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-08','2024-09-08','Ayu','Wiwik',1,'Persons (1-3)',392000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-08\", \"text\": \"ETA: 16.35 by Garuda GA7037 from Labuan Bajo on 08 September 2024\", \"time\": \"16:35\", \"locality\": \"Ngurah Rai Airport (Domestic)\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Komaneka Bisma Ubud\", \"location\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali.Telepon: (0361) 971933\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5185438,'583','Sonia Garcia Lazaro',30783,218000,'4D3N Jogja-Bromo-Surabaya Incl. Train / C. Ayaartta (Deluxe) & Bromo Terrace (Deluxe)','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-08-16','2024-08-19','Melysa','Komang',2,'Persons (2 / Double)',16560000.00,'D1 : Arrival Yogyakarta International Airport – Visit Prambanan Temple – Transfer to hotel D2 : Borobudur temple incl. Mendut and Pawon ,Yogyakarta City Tour Visit Sultan Palace, Watercastle and Bird/Traditional Market D3 : Jogja – Mojokerto by Train then continue drive to Bromo – overnight in Bromo D4 : Sunrise and Mt. Bromo crater tour incl. Jeep ( Horse rise Exclude ) – Transfer to Surabaya airport',NULL,'16 Aug / D1 : Arrival Semarang - Borobudur - Yogyakarta 17 Aug / D2 : Yogyakarta City Tour - Prambanan Temple 18 Aug / D3 : Yogyakarta - Bromo by Train 19 Aug / D4 : Sunrise Bromo - Dropoff Surabaya Airport Yogyakarta : Adhistana Hotel - Double Superior room Bromo : Lava View Lodge -Double Deluxe room','{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5185439,'584','Marla Conley',30508,202895,'East Bali Tour','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-10','2024-09-10','Ayu','Wiwik',1,'Person (1)',1528800.00,'In this part of the trip, we set off along the East Coast of the island. The first site visit will be the Kusamba Village, a fishing village where colorful Prahu in the black sand beaches. We will announce the salt making process by traditional method. We continue our journey on the east coast to reach Goa Lawah, Gua Lawah or Bat Cave is one of favorite places of interest in Bali and it is located near of hilly bank so it is called reef of Middle hill. We continue our trip to Tenganan Village, Tenganan Village is one of the oldest Balinese Traditional located in Karangasem Regency, east part of Bali. This village is much referred by cultural literature science of Tenganan Pegringsingan, which is very famous in the island. It owns very unique local community life pattern which is one example of Bali Aga Village cultures (Hindu Prehistoric) and different with other countryside in plain of Bali. From here, we go to Amlapura to visit the Royal Palace, The town of Amlapura is the capital of Karangasem (\'East Bali\'). The palace of the former kings of the region is located here, and their descendants have opened parts of the complex to the public. We will finish our trip with visit heaven of Tirta Gangga, Tirta Gangga is a beautiful park with the huge water fountain. At the end of tour we will transfer you back to the hotel.',NULL,'Full Day Tour visiting: East Bali Tour: Kusamba Beach – Goa Lawah Temple – Tenganan Village – Tirta Gangga','{\"date\": \"2024-09-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": \"Komaneka at Bisma Ubud\", \"location\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali. Telepon: (0361) 971933\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Komaneka at Bisma Ubud\", \"location\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali. Telepon: (0361) 971933\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5185440,'584','Marla Conley',30508,202897,'Uluwatu Temple and Kecak Dance','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-12','2024-09-12','Ayu','Wiwik',1,'Person (1)',1472800.00,'This half-day tour, is an exciting tour package to visit Padang-Padang Beach, Uluwatu Temple, the famous Balinese Hindu Temple in south part of Bali with breathtaking view of sunset and Indian Ocean. Uluwatu Temple is one of Balinese Hindu Temples located right on the petrifying hill with the crevasse exist in the right and left side. Uluwatu Temple is one of Sad Khayangan (6 biggest temple in Bali) owns magnificent view of the Indian Ocean and sunset as a backdrop. This temple is very amazing where the location is right on the narrow peninsula with deep seawater under it. This tour package is combined with the spectacular Balinese traditional dance performance of Kecak Dance. Balinese Kecak Dance is a spectacular traditional dance with the group of people playing this dance with fire game. It is very exciting and unique dance due to the sound of gamelan is not using the normal gamelan but use their mouth. The dancers make the compact choir with the exquisite dance movement that is one of this dance features. After the dance we returned back to the hotel or seafood restaurant in Jimbaran.',NULL,'Half Day Tour visiting: Padang Padang Beach - Uluwatu Temple - Kecak Dance Performance','{\"date\": \"2024-09-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"13:30\", \"locality\": \"Komaneka at Bisma Ubud\", \"location\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571. Telepon: (0361) 971933\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"The Vira Hotel Kuta\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5185445,'583','Sonia Garcia Lazaro',31150,204228,'Modern Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-08-19','2024-08-23','Melysa','Komang',1,'Double',4320000.00,'Standard guest rooms are a 12 tropical theme single room accommodation offering a queen-sized bed and twin bed, a coffee maker, mini-refrigerator, a flat-screen TV and all our signature features and amenities. The large bathrooms offer a tropical walk-in shower. Great for couple on romantic escape, our Standard Rooms are the ideal choice for an affordable stay in Gili Air.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5185446,'475','BLANCA LLES BARUQUER',30508,207278,'Full Day Tour Car & Driver (8-10 hours)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-15','2024-07-15','Jacob','Komang',1,'Persons (1-3)',0.00,NULL,NULL,'Not Include : Guide,Entrance fee, parking, ticket','{\"date\": \"2024-07-15\", \"text\": \"Ize Seminyak, Jl. Kayu Aya No.68, Seminyak, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Telepon: (0361) 8466999\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Seminyak\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-15\", \"text\": \"Ize Seminyak, Jl. Kayu Aya No.68, Seminyak, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Telepon: (0361) 8466999\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Seminyak\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5185457,'585','Sonia Casillas',30783,214536,'3D2N Semarang - Yogyakarta / C. Ayaartta (Deluxe Room)','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-07','2024-08-09','Igo','Komang',4,'Persons (2 / Double)',17760000.00,'D1 : Arrival at Semarang Airport - Borobudur Temple tour incl. Mendut and Pawon - Transfer to Jogja Welcome to the cradle of Indonesian culture, Yogyakarta. A tourist destination for its ancient palaces, temples, batik workshops, gamelan music orchestras, court dances and wayang puppet shows. Upon your arrival in Semarang airport a representative of come2indonesia will be waiting for you with a sign indicating your name to start exploring this special city. We will start by heading towards Borobudur Temple (Candi Borobudur), the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. We will tour around the temple, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano has been producing during its history. After visiting one of the most important Buddhist temples in Southeast Asia, we continue our journey to the Mendut temple and Pawon temple. And then, we will take you to Jogjakarta. D2 : Jogjakarta City Tour visit Sultan Palace, Watercastle and Bird Market - Visit Prambanan Temple You will enjoy a well-deserved breakfast at the hotel and we will start by heading towards Keraton known as the Sultan’s Palace. The palace is a complex building two centuries old, located in the heart of the city. You will hear the song of the “freedom” of the birds in the bird market, we will visit the “Water Castle” that occupies the highest part at the northern end of the vast complex of Taman Sari, Malioboro Street, main street of Yogyakarta, with its merchants, horse carriages, taxi-bikes and markets. After this visit we go to Candi Prambanan, the temple of the Hinduists and classified as a World Heritage Site by Unesco since 1991. The built of this temple was finished around the year 856 to commemorate the victory of the descendant Sanjaya of Siva, Rikai Pikatan on the last sovereign Sailendra of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to the Trimurti, the expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the destroyer. An incredible experience that will make the hours fly by. After this unforgettable day, we will take you back to your hotel. D3 : Transfer to Yogyakarta International Airport You will enjoy a well-deserved breakfast at the hotel and according to the time of your flight, we will pick you up to take you to the airport and take the flight to your next destination. End of our services. Thank you very much for exploring Yogyakarta by the hand of Come2indonesia.',NULL,'Flight Arrival in YIA : ETA : 17.05 by Air Asia AK348 from KUL on 07 August 2024 Dropoff Hotel Semarang on 09 Aug : ARTOTEL SEMARANG Program : 07 Aug / D1 : Arrival Yogyakarta - Transfer to hotel 08 Aug /D2 : Yogyakarta City Tour - Prambanan Temple 09 Aug/D3 : Borobudur Temple - Semarang - Hotel Rooming list : Mrs. Sonia Casillas Viladerrams & Mr. Jordi Villaret Codina (Double Bed) Ms. Aran Villaret Casillas & Mr. Roger Villaret Casillas (Twin Bed)','{\"date\": \"2024-08-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5185458,'585','Sonia Casillas',30672,200737,'Studio 25 (Superior) Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-09','2024-08-10','Igo','Komang',2,'Double + Twin',0.00,'Studio 25 (Superior) room with 25 sqm sized room and with exclusive ARTOTEL bedding collection, some facilities in this room is 43\" inch lcd tv, 24 hours in-room service, high speed internet wi-fi, safety deposit box and hair dryer.',NULL,'Rooming list : Mrs. Sonia Casillas Viladerrams & Mr. Jordi Villaret Codina (Double Bed) Ms. Aran Villaret Casillas & Mr. Roger Villaret Casillas (Twin Bed)','{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5185461,'585','Sonia Casillas',30806,212962,'3D2N Borneo Orangutan Tour by Speedboat / A. Rimba Eco Lodge (Amethyst Beo)','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO2',3,'2024-08-10','2024-08-12','Igo','Komang',4,'Persons (2)',23040000.00,'Hop on a speedboat and cruise along the Kumai River to visit the feeding camps in the national park of Tanjung Puting. On this Borneo Orangutan Tour by speedboat, see the wild orangutans in their natural environment through gentle trekking into the rainforest. Enjoying the riverside view accompanied by the proboscis monkeys hanging around the tips of the trees. This trip is prepared for those who are keen to see the wildlife from different perspectives, combining jungle adventure while also having a little private adventure with the comfort of sleeping in a hotel! Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN – KUMAI PORT – TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our speedboat. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the trip up the river in the famous Sekonyer River. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan is Cape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even see crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. A picnic lunch will be provided during the tour. After the tour, transfer to your hotel for check-in and overnight. Meals : Picnic Lunch Accommodation : A. Rimba Eco Lodge – Amethyst Beo Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY – CAMP LEAKEY After breakfast at the hotel, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continue to add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the speedboat again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. Back to your hotel and rest. Note: The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. Meals : Breakfast – Picnic Lunch Accommodation : A. Rimba Eco Lodge – Amethyst Beo Day 3 : HOTEL – PANGKALAN BUN After breakfast, depending on your flight schedule, our team will pick you up and escort you to the airport. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5185462,'585','Sonia Casillas',31015,203232,'3D2N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Ijen Tour Package drop Bali','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-12','2024-08-14','Igo','Komang',2,'Persons (4)',5700000.00,NULL,NULL,'Pickup & Dropoff Hotel Bromo : Lereng Bromo Hotel,Jl. Bromo, Ledok Sari, Wonokitri, Kec. Tosari, Pasuruan, Jawa Timur 67177 Telepon: 0813-3659-8889 Banyuwangi : Ketapang Indah Hotel, Jalan Gatot Subroto No.Km. 6, Lingkungan Tj., Klatak, Kec. Kalipuro, Kabupaten Banyuwangi, Jawa Timur 68421 Telepon: (0333) 422280 Bali (Ubud) : Teba Suci Suite, Jl. Raya Semana, Singakerta, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: 0821-2970-5341','{\"date\": \"2024-08-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5185463,'585','Sonia Casillas',30508,207379,'Ubud to Padang Bai','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-18','2024-08-18','Igo','Komang',1,'Persons (4-6)',1140000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": \"Teba Suci Suite,Jl. Raya Semana, Singakerta, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: 0821-2970-5341\", \"time\": \"06:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": \"ETD :09.00 by Ekajaya Fastboat to Gili Trawangan on 18 Aug 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Padang Bay Harbour\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5185466,'585','Sonia Casillas',31285,208028,'Suite Room with Ocean View','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-20','2024-08-23','Igo','Komang',2,'Double + Twin',11736000.00,'With 100 sqm of space, this suite comfortably accommodates up to 2 adults. It comes with air conditioning, a flat-screen TV with international channels, and a personal safe. The suite has a dining area and coffee/tea making facilities. Bathroom is fitted with separate toilet and shower. Fresh towels and bed linens are provided.',NULL,'Please ready on hotel lobby for transfer on 23 Aug at 11.30 AM Vouchers must be presented upon check-in and the hotel will there for invoice with in the 7 days period if credit facility has been extended by the hotel.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5185468,'585','Sonia Casillas',30508,212457,'Sanur to Nusa Dua','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-23','2024-08-23','Igo','Komang',1,'Persons (4-6)',720000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-23\", \"text\": \"ETA : 13.00 by Maruti Fastboat from Nusa Penida on 23 Aug 2024\", \"time\": \"13:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sanur harbour\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-23\", \"text\": \"The Grand Bali, Jalan Raya Nusa Dua Selatan, Jl. Nusa Dua No.8, Benoa, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80363 Telepon: (0361) 776688\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Nusa Dua\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5185469,'585','Sonia Casillas',30574,208091,'Deluxe Garden View','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-23','2024-08-24','Igo','Komang',2,'Double + Twin',3000000.00,'Be impressed by accommodating chambers - the largest discovered standard room on the island. Marble-floored bathrooms with a separate bathtub and shower are just some of the luxurious appointments in the room. The outdoors cares Balinese balcony space with tranquility view to the pool.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5185584,'586','Rafael Redondo López & Party (3)',30662,213274,'3D2N Medan - Leuser National Park Tracking','Confirmed','RVL-3D Boh-Lst',3,'2024-07-21','2024-07-23','Jacob','Eddy',3,'Persons (2-3 / Triple-extra bed)',14310000.00,'DAY 01 : MEDAN - BUKIT LAWANG Arrival at Kuala Namu Int airport Airport Medan drive to Bukit Lawang with stop at several Plantation for rubber and Palm oil. After that arrival at Bukit Lawang check in to hotel. Meals : - Accommodation : Bukit Lawang Cottages or Rindu Alam Hotel DAY 02 : BUKIT LAWANG - FULL DAY TRACKING LEUSER PARK After breakfast walking to the jungle to start a jungle tracking to explore the nature of Leuser National park with their flora and fauna, the possibility to see Orang Utan on their own habitat and other kind of animal such as Thomas leaf monkeys, long tail macaque, gibbon, black gibbon and other kind of flora and fauna of tropical rain forest. This fullday tracking will finish in the afternoon and then return back to hotel. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Accommodation : Bukit Lawang Cottages or Rindu Alam Hotel DAY 03 : BUKIT LAWANG - MEDAN / AIRPORT After breakfast free at own leisure for swimming or walking and then drive to Medan arrival in Medan directly transfer to airport. Meals : Breakfast',NULL,'0721 Día 01: Llegada A Medan – Bukit Lawang 0722 Día 02: Bukit Lawang Full Day Trekking 0723 Día 03: Bukit Lawang – Medan – Aeropuerto – Llegada A Jakarta 21 - 23 JUL (2N) AT The Heritage Hotel – Deluxe B room (DBL + Extra Bed)','{\"date\": \"2024-07-21\", \"text\": \"ETA: 21JUL 15:00 from Kuala Lumpur QR5475 by Qatar Airways\", \"time\": \"15:00\", \"locality\": \"MEDAN AIPORT\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-23\", \"text\": \"ETD: 23JUL 1700 QG883 to Jakarta by Citilink\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5185586,'586','Rafael Redondo López & Party (3)',30680,200914,'1 Deluxe Room + 1 Extra Bed','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-23','2024-07-24','Jacob','Eddy',1,'Triple',960000.00,'Enjoy our spacious elegant deluxe room with 40 m2 of room size. Enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, hot and cold shower, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.','Bed Type Base Upon Arrival At Check In Time (For Dbl or Twin bed) with 1 extra bed in 1 room','Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup & Dropoff Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available) Bed Type Base Upon Arrival At Check In Time (For Dbl or Twin bed) with 1 extra bed in 1 room','{\"date\": \"2024-07-23\", \"text\": \"ETA: 23JUL 1920 QG883 from Medan by Citilink\", \"time\": \"19:20\", \"locality\": \"AIRPORT JAKARTA\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-24\", \"text\": \"ETD: 24JUL 1320 ID6360 to Yogyakarta by Batik Air\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"AIRPORT JAKARTA\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5185588,'586','Rafael Redondo López & Party (3)',30783,212220,'4D3N Yogyakarta - Mt. Merapi with Jeep / C. Ayaartta (Deluxe Room)','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-07-24','2024-07-27','Jacob','Eddy',3,'Persons (3 / Triple-extra bed)',13950000.00,'D1 Arrival Yogyakarta International Airport – Transfer to hotel: Welcome to the cradle of Indonesian culture, Yogyakarta. A tourist destination for its ancient palaces, temples, batik workshops, gamelan music orchestras, court dances and wayang puppet shows. Upon your arrival in Yogyakarta a representative of come2indonesia will be waiting for you with a sign indicating your name to take you to your hotel and the rest of the day is for you. D2 Borobudur temple – Candirejo Village Tour by Horse cart / bicycle – Merapi lava tour Including Jeep: You will have your deserved breakfast at the hotel. Today’s tour will make you enjoy the authentic Javanese essence. You will start your route in the direction of with the Borobudur Temple (Candi Borobudur), the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. We will tour around the temple, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano has been producing during its history. After visiting one of the most important Buddhist temples in Southeast Asia, and in a horse carriage (Andong) we will visit the villages that surround this temple. These are authentic Javanese villages where culture and tradition are the protagonists. As you spend your days in this country and go around the different islands, you will realize how different Indonesians are among them in terms of clothing, food, architecture and even language. Today we will learn about and share these Javanese places. Then we will go to Kaliurang / Kalidalem to see Mount Merapi in constant activity. Here in a 4x4 jeep driven by specialized drivers, we will climb its skirt to see the remains of the 2010 eruption such as houses buried by ashes, a multitude of objects paralyzed by lava, etc. In addition, an open-air tribute museum presided over by the clock that marks the time just when the lava passed through it has been improvised. Accompanied by photos of the rescue, it will make us feel very closely the experiences of that fateful day. After finishing this day full of emotions, we will take you back to your hotel. D3 City Tour Jogjakarta Visit Sultan Palace, Watercastle and Bird Market – Prambanan Temple: After breakfast and at the indicated time we will head towards the heart of the city. We will visit the Keraton known as the Sultan’s Palace. The palace is a complex building two centuries old, located in the heart of the city. You will hear the song of the “freedom” of the birds in the bird market, we will visit the “Water Castle” that occupies the highest part at the northern end of the vast complex of Taman Sari, Malioboro Street, main street of Yogyakarta, with its merchants, horse carriages, taxi-bikes and markets. An incredible experience that will make the hours fly by. After finishing the tour in the center of the city of Yogyakarta, we will go to the northeast direction Candi Prambanan, the temple of the Hinduists and classified as a World Heritage Site by Unesco since 1991. The built of this temple was finished around the year 856 to commemorate the victory of the descendant Sanjaya of Siva, Rikai Pikatan on the last sovereign Sailendra of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to the Trimurti, the expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the Destroyer. After this unforgettable day, we will take you to your hotel. D4 Transfer out Yogyakarta International airport: Today our adventure ends at the cradle of Indonesian culture. Depending on the time of your flight, we will pick you up to take you to the airport and take the flight to your next destination. End of our services. Thank you very much for exploring Yogyakarta by the hand of Come2indonesia.',NULL,'0724 Día 04: Jakarta – Llegada a Yogjakarta 0725 Día 05: Templo de Borobudur – Visitando el Pueblo – Batik – Merapi 0726 Día 06: Jogjakarta City tour – Templo Prambanan 0727 Día 07: Yogyakarta – Airport 24 - 27 JUL (3N) at Ayaartta Hotel – Deluxe room (DBL + Extra Bed)','{\"date\": \"2024-07-24\", \"text\": \"ETA: 24JUL 1430 ID6360 from Jakarta by Batik Air\", \"time\": \"14:30\", \"locality\": \"AIRPORT JOGJA\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-27\", \"text\": \"ETD: 27JUL 0950 JT560 to Denpasar by Lion Air\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"AIRPORT JOGJA\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5185590,'586','Rafael Redondo López & Party (3)',30508,202897,'Uluwatu Temple and Kecak Dance','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-27','2024-07-27','Jacob','Eddy',3,'Persons (3)',3186000.00,'This half-day tour, is an exciting tour package to visit Padang-Padang Beach, Uluwatu Temple, the famous Balinese Hindu Temple in south part of Bali with breathtaking view of sunset and Indian Ocean. Uluwatu Temple is one of Balinese Hindu Temples located right on the petrifying hill with the crevasse exist in the right and left side. Uluwatu Temple is one of Sad Khayangan (6 biggest temple in Bali) owns magnificent view of the Indian Ocean and sunset as a backdrop. This temple is very amazing where the location is right on the narrow peninsula with deep seawater under it. This tour package is combined with the spectacular Balinese traditional dance performance of Kecak Dance. Balinese Kecak Dance is a spectacular traditional dance with the group of people playing this dance with fire game. It is very exciting and unique dance due to the sound of gamelan is not using the normal gamelan but use their mouth. The dancers make the compact choir with the exquisite dance movement that is one of this dance features. After the dance we returned back to the hotel or seafood restaurant in Jimbaran.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-27\", \"text\": \"ETD: 27JUL 1215 JT560 from Yogyakarta by Lion Air\", \"time\": \"12:15\", \"locality\": \"AIRPORT DENPASAR\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-27\", \"text\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 2 Periksa ketersediaan Address:Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : (0361) 981386\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5185592,'586','Rafael Redondo López & Party (3)',30620,200812,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-07-27','2024-07-29','Jacob','Eddy',1,'Double',2160000.00,'20 units (10 double bed and 10 twin bed) of 29 sqm each superior rooms with valley view and garden are modern‐minimalism designed. Advance facilities such as LCD TV, coffee/tea maker, balcony/terrace, safety deposit box, minibar, and complete bathroom facilities.',NULL,'1 (dbl) superior room + Extra bed','{\"date\": \"2024-07-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5185593,'586','Rafael Redondo López & Party (3)',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route (Templo Taman Ayun - Jatiluwih - Templo Ulun Danu Bratan - Tanah Lot )','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-28','2024-07-28','Jacob','Eddy',3,'Persons (3)',2160000.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-28\", \"text\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 2 Periksa ketersediaan Address:Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : (0361) 981386\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-28\", \"text\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 2 Periksa ketersediaan Address:Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : (0361) 981386\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5185594,'586','Rafael Redondo López & Party (3)',30508,213032,'Ubud to Kusamba','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-29','2024-07-29','Jacob','Eddy',3,'Persons (1-3)',1260000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-29\", \"text\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 2 Periksa ketersediaan Address:Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : (0361) 981386\", \"time\": \"05:00\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-29\", \"text\": \"Fast Boat by the angkal - One-way Fast Boat from Kusamba to Nusa Penida on 29 July 2024 (ETD 07.00)\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Kusamba Port\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5185600,'586','Rafael Redondo López & Party (3)',30508,207112,'Tour De La Isla Nusa Penida + Snorkel En Nusa Penida','Confirmed','C2I-BALI19',1,'2024-07-29','2024-07-29','Jacob','Eddy',3,'Persons (3)',1080000.00,'Today, embark on a unique adventure as you explore the enchanting Nusa Penida, a neighboring island of Bali. Your day begins with a convenient hotel pick-up, followed by a journey to the Sanur port where a fast boat awaits to transport you to Nusa Penida in just 30 minutes. Nusa Penida, located in the southeast of Bali, is a true paradise waiting to be discovered. Upon your arrival, a friendly driver will be ready to guide you through the day\'s captivating itinerary. Your first destination is the mesmerizing Angel\'s Billabong, a natural wonder resembling a pristine pool nestled in the heart of nature. Take a refreshing swim, but exercise caution on the steps and heed your driver\'s recommendations. Next, we head to Broken Beach, a charming bay that was once a cave, now open to the sky, offering a unique and captivating scenery. Although inaccessible by land, the view from above is nothing short of breathtaking. Keep an eye out for the possibility of spotting giant manta rays gracefully gliding on the water\'s surface. Our journey continues to the renowned Kelingking Beach, famous for its stunning cliffs and the iconic hand-shaped mountain. This beach is not only one of the island\'s most famous attractions but also a favorite subject for photographers. We conclude the day at the pristine Crystal Beach, where white sands meet turquoise waters in perfect harmony. As the sun sets, you\'ll have the opportunity to relax and savor the beauty that surrounds you. This unforgettable experience concludes with a return boat trip to Bali from the Toya Pakeh port at 16:30, followed by a comfortable transfer to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-29\", \"text\": \"One-way Fast Boat from Kusamba to Nusa Penida on 29 July 2024 (ETA 07.30)\", \"time\": \"07:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-29\", \"text\": \"THE ANGKAL RESORT NUSA PENIDA \\\"Address : 7HMV+6VX Banjar Angkal, Suana, Kec. Nusa Penida, Kabupaten Klungkung, Bali 80771 Phone : +62 (0366) 5582389\\\"\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5185601,'586','Rafael Redondo López & Party (3)',31040,203404,'Ocean View Bungalow Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-29','2024-07-30','Jacob','Eddy',1,'Double',1140000.00,'Room size: 55 sqm. The ocean view bungalow room has 13 units available. The rooms at this Nusa Penida hotel provide guests with high-velocity internet and a flat-screen TV with satellite channels, and comforts such as ironing facilities and air conditioning. The units are designed in a comfortable manner. Offering amenities like hair dryers and bathrobes, the bathrooms also include a walk-in shower, a separate toilet and a sink.',NULL,'1 Unit DBL Ocean View Bungalow + Extra bed','{\"date\": \"2024-07-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5185603,'586','Rafael Redondo López & Party (3)',32607,215996,'Lumbung Suite','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-07-30','2024-08-01','Jacob','Eddy',1,'Double',4680000.00,'At 64 m2 room size, welcome to the Lumbung suite with ocean view. Sleep soundly during your trip to one of Gili Islands in Lombok, West Nusa Tenggara, Indonesia in our Lumbung Suite Room, which is designed in a traditional style, two stories and features a king bed with comfortable bedding, spacious, and individually designed.',NULL,'1 (dbl) Lumbung Suite + Extra bed','{\"date\": \"2024-07-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5185607,'586','Rafael Redondo López & Party (3)',31083,203792,'Komodo Island Full Day Tour (Fast Boat - Pick Up/Drop Off Labuan Bajo)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-02','2024-08-02','Jacob','Eddy',3,'Persons (2-3)',20286000.00,'TOUR ITINERARY Highlights: Padar Island, Komodo Island, Long beach, Pink Beach, Manta Point & Kanawa. PICK UP / ARRIVE LABUAN BAJO - PADAR - KOMODO - PINK BEACH - MANTA POINT - LABUAHAN BAJO Pick up & meeting service with our tour guide and transfer to the pier of Labuan Bajo for sailing directly to Loh Liang – the Ranger station in Komodo Island. By passing through many small islands, it will be 3 hours with slow wooden boat and 1.50 hours by speed boat to reach the pier of Komodo island. After registering start to take basic trekking to see the GIANT RIZARD / KOMODO DRAGON and other wild animals as: Timor deer, wild pig, wild chicken and many variously of tropical bird. Please keep your look at any directions as sometimes you will also find young Komodo dragon hanging over the trees. A local ranger will be led you during the trek. Return to the boat on to Pink beach for snorkeling, swimming and relaxing. It is really spectacular and unspoiled coral reef and many color fish. Sail toward MANTA POINT to exploring Huge Mantas by snorkeling even watching from your boat trip (can’t be guaranteed if weather is not good, like wave and current are strongly). Lunch will be provided on board. Late in the afternoon back to Labuan Bajo harbor and transfer to your prefer Hotel for overnight and Dinner. Meals : Lunch Attention: The itinerary is subject to change due to the weather, tide level and operating conditions without prior notice.',NULL,'TOUR ITINERARY Pick up/Arrive Labuan Bajo – PADAR -KOMODO – PINK BEACH – MANTA POINT - LABUAHAN BAJO (L )','{\"date\": \"2024-08-02\", \"text\": \"La Cecile Hotel & Café \\\"Address : Jl. Golo Silatey, Kab. Manggarai Barat Komodo Indonesia Phone : 03852440 612 I Wa. 08214661 3330\\\"\", \"time\": \"07:00\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-02\", \"text\": \"La Cecile Hotel & Café \\\"Address : Jl. Golo Silatey, Kab. Manggarai Barat Komodo Indonesia Phone : 03852440 612 I Wa. 08214661 3330\\\"\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5185609,'586','Rafael Redondo López & Party (3)',31106,203994,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-04','2024-08-05','Jacob','Eddy',1,'Double',810000.00,'Discover Makassar from a very comfortable room with a king-size bed (or two single beds), a practical desk with an executive chair, and a modern bathroom with an open shower. You will also really like the welcome minibar to start your stay as you deserve. Inside the room has flat-screen TV, high speed Wi-Fi, and refrigerator.',NULL,'1 (DBL) Deluxe Room + Extrabed With one way Transfer Pick up Airport - Hotel','{\"date\": \"2024-08-04\", \"text\": \"ETA: 04AUG 1745 JT744 from Labuan Bajo by Lion Air\", \"time\": \"16:20\", \"locality\": \"AIRPORT MAKASSAR\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5185610,'586','Rafael Redondo López & Party (3)',30644,201464,'4D3N Toraja Package (3N Toraja)','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-08-05','2024-08-08','Jacob','Eddy',3,'Persons (2 / Double)',22500000.00,NULL,NULL,'0805 Día 16: Makasar (Ujung Pandang) – Toraja 0806–07 Días 17–18: Toraja Tour – El “Mundo” De Los Espíritus En La Exploración 0808 Día 19: Traslado Al Aeropuerto De Toraja. Fin De La Aventura 05 - 08 AUG (3N) at HOTEL SANTAI TORAJA – Deluxe room + Extra Bed) DOMESTIC FLIGHT 08 Aug 2024 / IW 1351 / Depart - Palopo (LLO) 09:30 hrs / Arrive Ujung Pandang (UPG) 10:25 hrs (Operated by Wings Air) -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 08 Aug 2024 / JT 891 / Ujung Pandang (UPG) 12:10 hrs / Jakarta (CGK) 13:20 hrs (Operated by Lion Air)','{\"date\": \"2024-08-05\", \"text\": \"Meliá Makassar Address: Jl. A. Mappanyukki No.17, Kunjung Mae, Kec. Mariso, Kota Makassar, Sulawesi Selatan 90134 Phone : (0411) 8055888\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": \"ETD: 08 AUG 09:30 IW1351 to Jakarta by Wings Abadi Air\", \"time\": nu