or your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": \"Indigo Hotel Seminyak\", \"location\": \"Jl. Camplung Tanduk No.10, Seminyak\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-14\", \"text\": \"ETD 08:00 to Gili Trawangan by BlueWater Express\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Serangan Harbour ( Blue Water Express Office )\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5185917,'588','Agustin Ruiz Coca',33011,218594,'Air Transfer Semarang - Karimun Jawa','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-04','2024-08-04','Jacob','Tami',10,'Person',34760000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5185921,'588','Agustin Ruiz Coca',33011,218595,'Air Transfer Karimun Jawa - Semarang','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-08','2024-08-08','Jacob','Tami',10,'Person',34760000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5185929,'588','Agustin Ruiz Coca',30681,207525,'Grand Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-08','2024-08-09','Jacob','Tami',4,'2 Double + 2 Twin',7920000.00,'Spacious 40 square meter of luxury with an elegant touch, understated modern design features, and full of comfort, located at 15th floor with amazing view of Semarang city. Along with subtle hues of natural color enhanced with black marble and accent of luxurious walnut wood. The Grand Deluxe Room is designed with business needs in mind and fully equipped with a functional work station with ergonomic executive chair, enjoy the plush comfort of bed, with luxury bed linens, cover and duvet, a high definition 42″ LED interactive TV and high speed internet access up to 400 Mbps, international power outlet, spa-inspired bathroom with separate rain shower and deep-soaking bath areas and 120 x 200 twin beds or 200 x 200 cm king bed, dressed with plush 100% cotton linen, down duvet and pillows. Guests who reserve a stay in this accommodation will enjoy enhanced benefits including exclusive access to the Tower Club Executive Lounge.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5185931,'436','SERGIO SHOR JINICH',30508,202864,'Ubud and Surrounding Tour','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-01','2024-08-01','Nicholas','Eddy',3,'Persons (3)',2070000.00,'We will be picking you up from your hotel to enjoy the wealth of art in Ubud. First we will visit Monkey Forest; the Ubud Monkey Forest is a nature reserve and temple complex in Ubud, Bali. It houses approximately 340 Crab-eating Macaque (Macacafas cicularis) monkeys. The Monkey Forest contains the Pura Dalem Agung Padangtegal temple as well as a \"Holy Spring\" bathing temple and another temple used for cremation ceremonies. Next we go to Ubud Traditional Art Market where the existence is not far different from other markets available in the tourism area. This market as a society economics center of Ubud and it is apposite to the existence of Ubud Empire that is called Puri Saren. Our last destination is Gua Gajah (Elephant Cave). This cave is built at crevasse edge from the federation of 2 rills that is called Pangkung River, where the irrigation is mixed with Petanu River flow. The word of Gua Gajah is anticipated coming from the word of Lwa Gajah, the name of Buddhist Temple or hermitage for Buddhist monk. There is a relief which is almost looking like the form of mountain on the entrance of this cave. It was carved many designed on the relief like grove with the stick, close leaf, animal for example forest pig, tortoise and specters. The cave mouth is decorated by the bas-relief with the eye turn around to the right or west side. At the end of tour we will transferred back you to the hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-01\", \"text\": \"Green Field Resort Ubud Address : Jl. Raya Pengosekan, MAS, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : (0361) 9085030\\\"\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-01\", \"text\": \"Green Field Resort Ubud Address : Jl. Raya Pengosekan, MAS, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : (0361) 9085030\\\"\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5185933,'436','SERGIO SHOR JINICH',30508,202891,'Contact with Nature Tour','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-02','2024-08-02','Nicholas','Eddy',3,'Persons (3)',2142000.00,'Deferent than the other tours! This tour will quietly finding you in the fullness of nature. First we will explore Pura Luhur Batukaru. Pura Luhur Batukaru Temple is one of the six directional temples on Bali that are believed to protect the island and its people from evil spirits. Pura Luhur Batukaru protects Bali from the West and was originally built in the 11th century. Pura Luhur Batukaru is one of Bali’s biggest Hindu temples, but because it is off the main tourist trail, sees fewer visitors than many of the other temples. Its peaceful setting amid rainforest at the foot of Mount Batukaru enhances its stunning Balinese architecture. We continue to reach the terrace rice fields Jatiluwih. Jatiluwih is a favorite tourist destination in Bali famous with the beautiful rice terrace unfolding from the foot of mountain until the coastal side. With the beautiful view as according to its name from Jati and Luwih, where Jati mean really and Luwih meaning especial, good, and beautiful or the equivalent. The local paddies are planted in this place look typically of the high relative size plant if it is compared with other pre-eminent paddy planted by most farmers in Bali. You’ll get to explore different parts of the terraces, jump over rivers. We continue our way to the Lake Buyan. We will see one of the most beautiful nature and vegetation scenery on the island. Buyan Lake is a smallest lake in Bali located in the plateau area with cool weather covers it. It is situated in the high land with hill and rain forest surrounds it. Since the location in the plateau area, the fog is usually blanketing the area. This lake can be seen from the top of hill which is called Asah Gobleg. The western end of Lake Buyan, we will start to see the sister lake of Buyan, the Lake Tamblingan. If we follow the road it will bring us closer and closer to Lake Tamblingan, or if we take direction to the right at the following junction at the end of the road, we will arrive in Munduk village, a village rich with coffee plantations. And our final destination is Munduk Waterfalls. This waterfall is a beautiful tourist destination in north part of Bali. Waterfall voice around the charming nature was amazing and it was the separate attraction which can be enjoyed by each visitor who comes to visit. In order to visit the waterfall, all visitors will follow the walkway down until the spot point.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-02\", \"text\": \"Green Field Resort Ubud Address : Jl. Raya Pengosekan, MAS, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : (0361) 9085030\\\"\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-02\", \"text\": \"Green Field Resort Ubud Address : Jl. Raya Pengosekan, MAS, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : (0361) 9085030\\\"\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5185934,'436','SERGIO SHOR JINICH',30508,202887,'Bali Rafting & The Mother Temple Besakih','Confirmed','C2I-BALI12',1,'2024-08-03','2024-08-03','Nicholas','Eddy',3,'Persons (3)',2826000.00,'This tour is meant to have a full day of Balinese fun and life. At 8:00 a.m. you will be picked up to head to Klungkung where you will go rafting on the Melanggit River with an approximate duration of 2 hours. Its steep cliffs, waterfalls, and hairpin bends make it very attractive to adventurers. This river with its pollution-free water and dense vegetation makes it a super refreshing experience within the tropical heat of Bali. It is a rafting with many jumps, some even of almost two meters, but under the helm of great professionals. After the rafting, we continue towards Besakih Mother Temple. This temple is located on the slopes of the Agung Volcano, whose last explosion was in 1963, just on the day when thousands of Balinese people celebrated one of the most important days of the Hindu calendar and which was a tragedy for the people and inhabitants of the area. Founded in the 8th century as a shrine honoring the gods of the Gunung Agung, today it comprises 22 main complexes with more than eighty small temples. At the end of the day, your driver will take you back to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-03\", \"text\": \"Green Field Resort Ubud Address : Jl. Raya Pengosekan, MAS, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : (0361) 9085030\\\"\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-03\", \"text\": \"Green Field Resort Ubud Address : Jl. Raya Pengosekan, MAS, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Phone : (0361) 9085030\\\"\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5185943,'588','Agustin Ruiz Coca',30805,212247,'SRG-PKN','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-09','2024-08-09','Jacob','Tami',10,'Person',13035000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5185948,'588','Agustin Ruiz Coca',30806,202002,'4D3N Borneo Orangutan & Reforestation Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO7',4,'2024-08-09','2024-08-12','Jacob','Tami',10,'Persons (10)',38400000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN – KUMAI PORT – TANJUNG HARAPAN Your “Orangutan & Reforestation Tour” begins upon arrival at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan is Cape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : TANJUNG HARAPAN VILLAGE – PROBOSCIS TOUR – CAMP LEAKEY After an extraordinary breakfast, you go to visit the village inside the national park, named Tanjung Harapan Village. Here you will see the activities of the locals. After the visit, you will return to the klotok cruise up to the Sekonyer River. You will see nice vegetation around the river bank, including Nipa Palm, Pandanus, and some kinds of trees that are growing up around the river. See some wildlifes such as birds, Macaques, Proboscis Monkeys and Orangutans. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large monitor lizards. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. Note: The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. Meals : Breakfast – Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : PONDOK TANGGUI – CAMP LEAKEY – BOAT After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continue to add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After lunch, you will have the opportunity to repeat feeding camp at Camp Leaky. It is a unique opportunity to dedicate more time to your observation and to discover more wild animals, along with the Orangutans. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note: If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast – Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 4 : KUMAI PORT – PANGKALAN BUN Today we end our stay in the jungles of Borneo. Our “Orangutan & Reforestation Tour” is about to finish. In the early morning we will have breakfast on the boat, to then go to the port and in turn, be transferred to the airport. The boat departure will be at the latest at 10am, but we adapt to your flights if your flight leaves earlier in the morning. If you decide to take an afternoon flight, we can take you directly to the airport at 10 or if you want a city tour in the Arut village to drop you off at the airport later, it could be arranged at extra cost. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": \"ETA 09.30 by Batik Air ID6302 from Semarang on 09 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pangkalan Bun Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-12\", \"text\": \"ETD 07.55 by Batik Air ID6203 to Jakarta on 12 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5185949,'582','GERARD BALLESTA LUENGO',30508,207278,'PRIVATE CAR (BATUR TREKK)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-10','2024-08-10','Guio','Wiwik',1,'Persons (2)',560000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"02:00\", \"locality\": \"The Sankara Resort\", \"location\": \"Jl. Cempaka, Kumbuh, Jl. Cempaka, MAS, Ubud, Gianyar Regency, Bali 80571. Phone: (0361) 8493515\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"The Sankara Resort\", \"location\": \"Jl. Cempaka, Kumbuh, Jl. Cempaka, MAS, Ubud, Gianyar Regency, Bali 80571. Phone: (0361) 8493515\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5185959,'588','Agustin Ruiz Coca',30680,200914,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-12','2024-08-13','Jacob','Tami',4,'2 Double + 2 Twin',3840000.00,'Enjoy our spacious elegant deluxe room with 40 m2 of room size. Enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, hot and cold shower, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available)','{\"date\": \"2024-08-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5185960,'582','GERARD BALLESTA LUENGO',30508,213032,'Ubud to Kusamba','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-11','2024-08-11','Guio','Wiwik',1,'Persons (1-3)',392000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": \"The Sankara resort\", \"location\": \"Jl. Cempaka, Kumbuh, Jl. Cempaka, MAS, Ubud, Gianyar Regency, Bali 80571. Phone: (0361) 8493515\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Kusamba Harbour\", \"location\": \"ETD: 08.00 to Nusa Penida (Sampalan Harbour) by The Angkal Fast Boat\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5185965,'588','Agustin Ruiz Coca',30805,212245,'PKN-CGK','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-12','2024-08-12','Jacob','Tami',10,'Person',14058000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5185972,'582','GERARD BALLESTA LUENGO',30698,205187,'Bungalow Room With Ocean View','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-08-11','2024-08-13','Guio','Wiwik',1,'Double',4256000.00,'The property is consisted of 6 units of bungalow room ocean view. Each of our bungalows has a spacious private balcony facing to swimming pool, tropical garden and ocean. Each room is facilitated with remote control system, remote control system air conditioner, refrigerator, in-room safe, tea and coffee making facility, spacious bathroom with shower, bath robe. Our Bungalow Room Ocean View has a king bed setup.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5185980,'582','GERARD BALLESTA LUENGO',30508,207337,'Snorkeling to Nusa Penida (from Nusa Penida) (Sharing Trip)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-12','2024-08-12','Guio','Wiwik',2,'Persons (2)',1232000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": \"Sea La Vie Resort - Nusa Penida\", \"location\": \"jl toya pakeh Penida, Nusa Penida island, Kabupaten Klungkung, Bali 80771. Phone: 0821-4502-8514\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Sea La Vie Resort - Nusa Penida\", \"location\": \"jl toya pakeh Penida, Nusa Penida island, Kabupaten Klungkung, Bali 80771. Phone: 0821-4502-8514\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5185995,'582','GERARD BALLESTA LUENGO',31102,203958,'One-Bedroom Villa with Pool','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-13','2024-08-16','Guio','Wiwik',1,'Double',9744000.00,'Step into a world of luxury and tranquility with our 1-Bedroom Private Pool Villas. These meticulously designed villas offer a haven of privacy and comfort, perfect for couples seeking an unforgettable escape. As you enter the villa, you\'ll be greeted by a spacious and elegantly furnished outdoor living area, adorned with tasteful decor and modern amenities. The thoughtfully curated interiors create a warm and inviting ambiance, setting the stage for a truly relaxing stay. Experience the highlight of our 1-Bedroom Private Pool Villas - the expansive bedroom featuring a plush king-size bed draped in soft linens, offering breathtaking views of lush greenery and immediate access to your sparkling private pool. Indulge in the en-suite bathroom\'s lavish rain shower, set in a tropical atmosphere, providing a rejuvenating retreat for your senses.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5186011,'582','GERARD BALLESTA LUENGO',30508,207386,'Padang Bai to Seminyak','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-16','2024-08-16','Guio','Wiwik',1,'Persons (1-3)',560000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"12:25\", \"locality\": \"Padang Bai Harbour by Bluewater Express from Gili Air\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Bali Niksoma Boutique Beach Resort\", \"location\": \"Jl. Padma Utara Jl. Raya Legian, Legian, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung. Phone: (0361) 751946\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5186015,'582','GERARD BALLESTA LUENGO',30596,201103,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-16','2024-08-17','Guio','Wiwik',1,'Double',2800000.00,'Experience timeless elegance in our Deluxe Room. Perfect for couples or solo travelers seeking a spacious single/double bed. Our room offers premium linens, plush pillows, and a peaceful ambiance. Enjoy high-speed internet, a flat-screen TV, coffee and tea-making facilities, and an in-room safe deposit box, ensuring a convenient and enjoyable stay. Unwind on the balcony overlooking the pool, to recharge after a day of activities.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5186027,'582','GERARD BALLESTA LUENGO',30508,207270,'Seminyak to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-17','2024-08-17','Guio','Wiwik',1,'Persons (1-3)',280000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"14:30\", \"locality\": \"Bali Niksoma Boutique Beach Resort\", \"location\": \"Jl. Padma Utara Jl. Raya Legian, Legian, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Telepon: (0361) 751946\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": \"ETD: 18.55 by QR963 to Doha on 17 August 2024.\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Ngurah Rai Airport (International Airport)\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5187183,'573','Elena María Duran Agosto 2024',30771,201371,'Grand Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-08-14','2024-08-18','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',6496000.00,'At 31,8 m2 room size, with beautiful garden view and charming decor. It includes a seating area and a private bathroom with a shower and complimentary bathroom amenities.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5187189,'582','GERARD BALLESTA LUENGO',30508,207112,'1D Nusa Penida West Tour','Confirmed','C2I-BALI19',1,'2024-08-11','2024-08-11','Guio','Wiwik',2,'Persons (2)',952000.00,'Today, embark on a unique adventure as you explore the enchanting Nusa Penida, a neighboring island of Bali. Your day begins with a convenient hotel pick-up, followed by a journey to the Sanur port where a fast boat awaits to transport you to Nusa Penida in just 30 minutes. Nusa Penida, located in the southeast of Bali, is a true paradise waiting to be discovered. Upon your arrival, a friendly driver will be ready to guide you through the day\'s captivating itinerary. Your first destination is the mesmerizing Angel\'s Billabong, a natural wonder resembling a pristine pool nestled in the heart of nature. Take a refreshing swim, but exercise caution on the steps and heed your driver\'s recommendations. Next, we head to Broken Beach, a charming bay that was once a cave, now open to the sky, offering a unique and captivating scenery. Although inaccessible by land, the view from above is nothing short of breathtaking. Keep an eye out for the possibility of spotting giant manta rays gracefully gliding on the water\'s surface. Our journey continues to the renowned Kelingking Beach, famous for its stunning cliffs and the iconic hand-shaped mountain. This beach is not only one of the island\'s most famous attractions but also a favorite subject for photographers. We conclude the day at the pristine Crystal Beach, where white sands meet turquoise waters in perfect harmony. As the sun sets, you\'ll have the opportunity to relax and savor the beauty that surrounds you. This unforgettable experience concludes with a return boat trip to Bali from the Toya Pakeh port at 16:30, followed by a comfortable transfer to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"08:20\", \"locality\": \"Sampalan Harbour by The Angkal fast Boat from Kusamba\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Sea La Vie Resort\", \"location\": \"jl toya pakeh Penida, Nusa Penida island, Kabupaten Klungkung. Telepon: 0821-4502-8514\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5187341,'502','Mr. David Esteso Villar',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-09-25','2024-09-27','Melysa','Praba',2,'Persons (2)',10800000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-25\", \"text\": \"ETA 07:15AM by Batik Airlines ID6202 from Jakarta\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pangkalan Bun Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-27\", \"text\": \"ETD 10:25AM by Batik Air ID6303 to Semarang\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pangkaln Bun Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5187381,'502','Mr. David Esteso Villar',30783,201474,'2D1N Semarang - Yogyakarta / B. Gallery Prawirotaman (Superior Room)','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-09-27','2024-09-28','Melysa','Praba',2,'Persons (2 / Double)',6780000.00,'D1 : Arrival Semarang airport - Borobudur Temple tour incl. Mendut and Pawon - overnight in Yogyakarta Welcome to the cradle of Indonesian culture, Yogyakarta. A tourist destination for its ancient palaces, temples, batik workshops, gamelan music orchestras, court dances and wayang puppet shows. Upon your arrival in Semarang airport a representative of come2indonesia will be waiting for you with a sign indicating your name to start exploring this special city. We will start by heading towards Borobudur Temple (Candi Borobudur), the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. We will tour around the temple, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano has been producing during its history. After visiting one of the most important Buddhist temples in Southeast Asia, we continue our journey to the Mendut temple and Pawon temple. And then, we will take you to your Jogjakarta. D2 : Morning visit Prambanan Temple - City Tour Yogyakarta visit Sultan Palace, Watercastle and Bird Market - Transfer to Yogyakarta International Airport You will enjoy a well-deserved breakfast at the hotel and we will start by heading towards Candi Prambanan, the temple of the Hinduists and classified as a World Heritage Site by Unesco since 1991. The built of this temple was finished around the year 856 to commemorate the victory of the descendant Sanjaya of Siva, Rikai Pikatan on the last sovereign Sailendra of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to the Trimurti, the expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the destroyer. After this visit we go to the Keraton known as the Sultan’s Palace. The palace is a complex building two centuries old, located in the heart of the city. You will hear the song of the “freedom” of the birds in the bird market, we will visit the “Water Castle” that occupies the highest part at the northern end of the vast complex of Taman Sari, Malioboro Street, main street of Yogyakarta, with its merchants, horse carriages, taxi-bikes and markets. An incredible experience that will make the hours fly by. According to the time of your flight, we will pick you up to take you to the airport and take the flight to your next destination. End of our services. Thank you very much for exploring Yogyakarta by the hand of Come2indonesia.',NULL,'- HONEYMOONERS Details: D1/27 Sep: Arrival Semarang - Borobudur Temple - check in Hotel Yogyakarta D2/28 Sep: Transfer out YIA','{\"date\": \"2024-09-27\", \"text\": \"ETA 11:25 by Batik Air ID6303 from Pangkalan Bun\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ahmad Yani Airport Semarang\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-28\", \"text\": \"ETD 08:05 by Lion Air JT560 to Denpasar\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Yogyakarta International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5187394,'502','Mr. David Esteso Villar',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-28','2024-09-28','Melysa','Praba',1,'Persons (2)',360000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-28\", \"text\": \"ETA 10:30 by Lion Air JT560 from Yogyakarta\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-28\", \"text\": \"Banjar Junjungan, Jl. Tirta Tawar, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Korurua Dijiwa Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5187407,'502','Mr. David Esteso Villar',30884,217082,'Grand Deluxe','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-09-28','2024-10-02','Melysa','Praba',1,'Double',7795200.00,'Our Grand Deluxe features a uniquely classy and bright atmosphere, simple yet pristine, as its name suggests. Inside, it impresses with a light-flooded interior. Each room overlooks the lush green nature and the main swimming pool with its balcony. It is exclusively designed to discover the true meaning of peace in the brisk of pure silence. Bathroom offers are exclusively indoor for true relaxation and separate showers, complete with our signature amenities for guests to devour.',NULL,'- Honeymooners','{\"date\": \"2024-09-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5187415,'502','Mr. David Esteso Villar',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route (Pura Taman Ayun - Jatiluwih Rice Terrace - Templo Ulun Danu Bratan – Pura Luhur','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-29','2024-09-29','Melysa','Praba',2,'Persons (2)',1872000.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-29\", \"text\": \"Korurua Dijiwa Ubud Banjar Junjungan, Jl. Tirta Tawar, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-29\", \"text\": \"Korurua Dijiwa Ubud Banjar Junjungan, Jl. Tirta Tawar, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5187428,'502','Mr. David Esteso Villar',30508,202896,'Bali Village Life - Tanah Lot Temple','Confirmed','C2I-BALI05',1,'2024-09-30','2024-09-30','Melysa','Praba',2,'Persons (2)',2616000.00,'At 08.00 am, we pick you up from your hotel and start our journey to Tunjuk Village in Tabanan district. Upon arrival, you will be greeted with open arms and with the warm smiles of the locals you meet along the way. You\'ll meet in the outer courtyard of the village temple and meet your local guides. Throughout the hike you will meet people from the village involved in the tasks that keep their lives busy day in and day out. You can choose to observe or participate in them to gain a better understanding of village life. The mighty water buffalo is still used to drag the plough through the muddy rice paddies and prepare the land for planting. Or maybe you want to help with planting or harvesting, depending on the time of year. When you complete the tour in the rice paddies, you\'ll follow your guide on a path through lush gardens where villagers go about their daily chores. There are women who beat the rice with heavy mallets to remove the hooves. After lunch we leave Tunjuk Village and continue our journey to visit THE TANAH LOT. We\'ll close the visit by watching the sunset at the most famous and photographed temple in Bali. Torn from the earth on a stone pedestal sculpted by the incoming tides, the solitary black towers of Tanah Lot and the plumes of foliage spilling over the precipices, recall the delicacy of Chinese painting. The Pura Tanah Lot or the Earth Temple in the middle of the sea was built in the 16th century. At the end of the day, you\'ll be transferred to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-30\", \"text\": \"Korurua Dijiwa Ubud Banjar Junjungan, Jl. Tirta Tawar, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-30\", \"text\": \"Korurua Dijiwa Ubud Banjar Junjungan, Jl. Tirta Tawar, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5187434,'592','Cesar Salazar Chaves',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-21','2024-08-22','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',784000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available)','{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5187444,'592','Cesar Salazar Chaves',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-08-22','2024-08-24','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',10080000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-22\", \"text\": \"ETA 07.15 by Batik Air ID6202 from Jakarta on 22 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pangkalan Bun Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": \"ETD 10.25 by Batik Air ID6303 to Semarang on 24 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5187446,'502','Mr. David Esteso Villar',30508,215968,'1D Bali Tour (Custom Itinerary) Tegalalang Rice Terrace - Tirta Empul - Desa Penglipuran - Air Terju','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-01','2024-10-01','Melysa','Praba',2,'Persons (2)',1920000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-01\", \"text\": \"Korurua Dijiwa Ubud Banjar Junjungan, Jl. Tirta Tawar, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-01\", \"text\": \"Korurua Dijiwa Ubud Banjar Junjungan, Jl. Tirta Tawar, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5187448,'592','Cesar Salazar Chaves',30783,218000,'4D3N Jogja-Bromo-Surabaya Incl. Train / C. Adhisthana Hotel (Superior) & Lava View Lodge (Deluxe)','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-08-24','2024-08-27','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2-3)',15456000.00,'D1 : Arrival Yogyakarta International Airport – Visit Prambanan Temple – Transfer to hotel D2 : Borobudur temple incl. Mendut and Pawon ,Yogyakarta City Tour Visit Sultan Palace, Watercastle and Bird/Traditional Market D3 : Jogja – Mojokerto by Train then continue drive to Bromo – overnight in Bromo D4 : Sunrise and Mt. Bromo crater tour incl. Jeep ( Horse rise Exclude ) – Transfer to Surabaya airport',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": \"ETA 11.25 by Batik Air ID6303 from Pangkalan Bun on 24 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Semarang International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-27\", \"text\": \"ETD 15.25 by Lion Air JT920 to Denpasar on 27 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Surabaya International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5187449,'502','Mr. David Esteso Villar',30508,213032,'Ubud to Kusamba','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-02','2024-10-02','Melysa','Praba',1,'Persons (2)',420000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-02\", \"text\": \"Korurua Dijiwa Ubud Banjar Junjungan, Jl. Tirta Tawar, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-02\", \"text\": \"ETD 08:00AM by The Angkal Fastboat to Penida\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Kusamba Port\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5187462,'592','Cesar Salazar Chaves',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-27','2024-08-27','Guio','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',336000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-27\", \"text\": \"ETA 17.25 by Lion Air JT920 from Surabaya on 27 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"I Gusti Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-27\", \"text\": \"Jl. Hanoman, Ubud, Kec. Gianyar, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Alaya Resort Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5187472,'592','Cesar Salazar Chaves',30611,201418,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-08-27','2024-08-31','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',10752000.00,'The Deluxe Room provides a restful environment to unwind after a busy day spent exploring the sights of Ubud. It is a cozy base featuring clean-line furnishings, a smart en-suite bathroom and a decorative wall that showcases Bali’s creative legacy. A private terrace or balcony blends seamlessly into the outdoors providing extra space to sit and relax.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-31\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5187478,'502','Mr. David Esteso Villar',31040,203404,'Ocean View Bungalow Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-02','2024-10-03','Melysa','Praba',1,'Double',1140000.00,'Room size: 55 sqm. The ocean view bungalow room has 13 units available. The rooms at this Nusa Penida hotel provide guests with high-velocity internet and a flat-screen TV with satellite channels, and comforts such as ironing facilities and air conditioning. The units are designed in a comfortable manner. Offering amenities like hair dryers and bathrobes, the bathrooms also include a walk-in shower, a separate toilet and a sink.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5187494,'592','Cesar Salazar Chaves',30508,215968,'Campuhan Trekk – Tegalalang – Tirta Empul – Gunung Kawi Hill – Tegenungan Waterfall','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-28','2024-08-28','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',2128000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-28\", \"text\": \"Jl. Hanoman, Ubud, Kec. Gianyar, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Alaya Resort Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5187500,'592','Cesar Salazar Chaves',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-29','2024-08-29','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',1747200.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-29\", \"text\": \"Jl. Hanoman, Ubud, Kec. Gianyar, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Alaya Resort Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5187518,'592','Cesar Salazar Chaves',30508,213032,'Ubud to Kusamba','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-31','2024-08-31','Guio','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',392000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-31\", \"text\": \"Jl. Hanoman, Ubud, Kec. Gianyar, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Alaya Resort Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-31\", \"text\": \"ETD 08:00 to Nusa Penida by The Angkal Fast Boat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Kusamba Harbour\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5187534,'502','Mr. David Esteso Villar',30805,202689,'CGK-PKN','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-25','2024-09-25','Melysa','Praba',2,'Person',3326356.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5187539,'502','Mr. David Esteso Villar',30805,212246,'PKN-SRG','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-27','2024-09-27','Melysa','Praba',2,'Person',2408384.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5187544,'502','Mr. David Esteso Villar',30805,207117,'YIA-DPS','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-28','2024-09-28','Melysa','Praba',2,'Person',2018940.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5187548,'502','Mr. David Esteso Villar',30805,208054,'LOP-CGK','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-05','2024-10-05','Melysa','Praba',2,'Person',3995552.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5187619,'592','Cesar Salazar Chaves',30508,207112,'1D Nusa Penida West Tour','Confirmed','C2I-BALI19',1,'2024-08-31','2024-08-31','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',952000.00,'Today, embark on a unique adventure as you explore the enchanting Nusa Penida, a neighboring island of Bali. Your day begins with a convenient hotel pick-up, followed by a journey to the Sanur port where a fast boat awaits to transport you to Nusa Penida in just 30 minutes. Nusa Penida, located in the southeast of Bali, is a true paradise waiting to be discovered. Upon your arrival, a friendly driver will be ready to guide you through the day\'s captivating itinerary. Your first destination is the mesmerizing Angel\'s Billabong, a natural wonder resembling a pristine pool nestled in the heart of nature. Take a refreshing swim, but exercise caution on the steps and heed your driver\'s recommendations. Next, we head to Broken Beach, a charming bay that was once a cave, now open to the sky, offering a unique and captivating scenery. Although inaccessible by land, the view from above is nothing short of breathtaking. Keep an eye out for the possibility of spotting giant manta rays gracefully gliding on the water\'s surface. Our journey continues to the renowned Kelingking Beach, famous for its stunning cliffs and the iconic hand-shaped mountain. This beach is not only one of the island\'s most famous attractions but also a favorite subject for photographers. We conclude the day at the pristine Crystal Beach, where white sands meet turquoise waters in perfect harmony. As the sun sets, you\'ll have the opportunity to relax and savor the beauty that surrounds you. This unforgettable experience concludes with a return boat trip to Bali from the Toya Pakeh port at 16:30, followed by a comfortable transfer to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-31\", \"text\": \"ETA 08.30 from Kusamba by The Angkal Fast Boat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sampalan Harbour\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-31\", \"text\": \"Banjar Angkal, Suana, Kec. Nusa Penida, Kabupaten Klungkung, Bali 80771\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"The Angkal Resort Nusa Penida Bali\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5187627,'592','Cesar Salazar Chaves',31040,203404,'Ocean View Bungalow Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-31','2024-09-01','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',1064000.00,'Room size: 55 sqm. The ocean view bungalow room has 13 units available. The rooms at this Nusa Penida hotel provide guests with high-velocity internet and a flat-screen TV with satellite channels, and comforts such as ironing facilities and air conditioning. The units are designed in a comfortable manner. Offering amenities like hair dryers and bathrobes, the bathrooms also include a walk-in shower, a separate toilet and a sink.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-31\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5187677,'592','Cesar Salazar Chaves',30650,208425,'Private Pool Villa','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-09-01','2024-09-04','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',8400000.00,'Each villa embraces calmness, comfort and privacy in a simple and elegant setting. Guests can relax while peacefully sipping drinks in an inviting plunge pool surrounded by a lush tropical garden and at an old-wooden deck. At 85 m2 room size, this villa\'s special feature is the private pool. The air-conditioned villa features 1 bedroom and 1 bathroom with a shower and a hairdryer. The villa provides a mini-bar, a tea and coffee maker, a seating area as well as a terrace with garden views. The unit offers 1 bed.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5187933,'592','Cesar Salazar Chaves',30692,204751,'Double Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-04','2024-09-05','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',840000.00,'This 36sqm room features refrigerator, coffee/tea maker, air conditioning, desk, in-room safety, television, complimentary bottled water. Bathroom amenities such as; shower, free toiletries, private bathroom and hot water. The bedroom is a double room with queen bed type. Guest can see pool from the terrace.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5188014,'594','VANESA PEREZ LAMPON',30705,201148,'Premier Room Rice Field View','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-25','2024-08-28','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',5124000.00,'Gaze out at rippling rice fields as you let your stress slip away in one of our Premier Ricefield View suites. Inside you have smooth tiles, warm wooden accents, and all the modern comforts you could ask for. Step onto the balcony and you have an airy nook where you can witness life unfold in the Balinese countryside.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5188016,'594','VANESA PEREZ LAMPON',30508,215968,'1D Bali Tour (GOA GAJAH – TAMPAK SIRING – GUNUNG KAWI SEBATU TEMPLE – TEGALALANG )','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-26','2024-08-26','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',1904000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-26\", \"text\": \"The Artini Dijiwa Ubud, Jl. Raya Pengosekan Ubud, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 972385\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-26\", \"text\": \"The Artini Dijiwa Ubud, Jl. Raya Pengosekan Ubud, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 972385\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5188022,'594','VANESA PEREZ LAMPON',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route (TAMAN AYUN-JATI LUWIH-BEDUGUL-TANAH LOT)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-27','2024-08-27','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',1747200.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"dat