ou to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-01\", \"text\": \"ETA : 12.30 by Gili Gili Fastboat from Gili Air on 01 September 2024\", \"time\": \"12:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Padang Bay\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-01\", \"text\": \"Aston Canggu Beach Resort, Jl. Pantai Batu Bolong No.99, Canggu, Kec. Kuta Utara, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80363 Telepon: (0361) 3023333\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Canggu\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5188634,'595','Elena Jalon Sebastian',30508,216161,'Uluwatu to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-26','2024-08-26','Jacob','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',392000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-26\", \"text\": \"Jl. Pemutih Jl. Labuansait, Pecatu, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361\", \"time\": \"20:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Radisson Blu Resort, Bali Uluwatu\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-26\", \"text\": \"ETD 01.05 by Qatar QR961 to Doha on 27 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"I Gusti Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5188635,'596','Mrs. Ester Roca Pardos',31015,203232,'3D2N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Ijen Tour Package drop Bali','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-15','2024-08-17','Jacob','Praba',2,'Persons (2)',8880000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-15\", \"text\": \"ETA 10:00AM by Batik Airlines ID6134 from Pangkalan Bun\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Juanda International Airport Surabaya\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": \"D\'MACHO VILLAS UBUD Jl. Raya Silungan, Lodtunduh, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5188644,'594','VANESA PEREZ LAMPON',30638,204956,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-09-01','2024-09-03','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',2395008.00,'Indulge in the cozy comforts of our 35 sqm Deluxe Room, including a private balcony. Furnished with international amenities and a seating area on the private balcony, our Deluxe Rooms provide the option of two Twin beds or one King bed. Infused with a contemporary design complemented by a touch of Balinese aesthetics, this room offers all the conveniences for a vibrant stay in Canggu, with a delightful view overlooking the garden.',NULL,'A valid voucher is required prior to the guest’s arrival or upon the guest’s check in. Failure to provide a valid voucher before the guest\'s departure will be automatically switched to the normal best available rate and payment will be on the guest personal account and non- commissionable.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5188647,'596','Mrs. Ester Roca Pardos',31196,204658,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-15','2024-08-16','Jacob','Praba',1,'Double',1428000.00,'Room type deluxe, with spacious room 3,41 m x 6,09 m and have type bed king size or twin bed. This type of room is available on the 2nd, 3rd and 4th floors and has of the hills view.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5188651,'594','VANESA PEREZ LAMPON',30508,207265,'Canggu to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-03','2024-09-03','Guio','Komang',1,'Persons (1-3)',392000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,'Please ready on hotel lobby for pickup at 20.00','{\"date\": \"2024-09-03\", \"text\": \"Aston Canggu Beach Resort, Jl. Pantai Batu Bolong No.99, Canggu, Kec. Kuta Utara, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80363 Telepon: (0361) 3023333\", \"time\": \"20:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Canggu\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-03\", \"text\": \"ETD : 01.05 by IBERIA IB7967 to Doha on 04 September 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"International Ngurah Rai Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5188652,'596','Mrs. Ester Roca Pardos',30682,200889,'Resort\'s Deluxe','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-16','2024-08-17','Jacob','Praba',1,'Double',2418000.00,'Beautiful Hotel in Banyuwangi, East Java. Ijen Resort and Villas Close with Ijen Crater, very recommended place to stay with great view from your room. You can directly enjoy the mountain view or rice field view. Also can enjoy some great facility such us swimming pool with the great view near ijen mountain, in Banyuwangi.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5188677,'597','CARLOS ROPERO',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-12','2024-08-13','Jacob','Wiwik',1,'Double',840000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'FLIGHT DETAIL: ETA: 14.20 by Etihad Airways EY474 from Abu Dhabi on 12 August 2024. ETD: 05.45 by Nam Air IN190 to Pangkalan Bun on 13 August 2024. Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available)','{\"date\": \"2024-08-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5188697,'597','CARLOS ROPERO',31371,205712,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-13','2024-08-14','Jacob','Wiwik',1,'Double',882000.00,'With a spacious 31m2 air conditioned room where you can enjoy the cozy ambiance. Offering complete facilities to comfort your stay. This room equipped with a flat screen cable TV, fridge, ensuite bathroom, offers a shower, seating area, and many more.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5188702,'597','CARLOS ROPERO',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-08-14','2024-08-16','Jacob','Wiwik',2,'Persons (2)',10800000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Flight Detail: ETA: 07.00 by Nam Air IN190 from Jakarta on 13 August 2024. ETD: 10.25 by Batik Air ID6303 to Semarang on 16 August 2024. Drop Off/Pick Up: Grand Kecubung Hotel Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5188727,'597','CARLOS ROPERO',30783,213447,'4D3N Yogyakarta - Mt. Merapi with Jeep / C. Adhisthana (Superior Room)','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-08-16','2024-08-19','Jacob','Wiwik',2,'Persons (2 / Double)',10260000.00,'D1 Arrival Yogyakarta International Airport – Transfer to hotel: Welcome to the cradle of Indonesian culture, Yogyakarta. A tourist destination for its ancient palaces, temples, batik workshops, gamelan music orchestras, court dances and wayang puppet shows. Upon your arrival in Yogyakarta a representative of come2indonesia will be waiting for you with a sign indicating your name to take you to your hotel and the rest of the day is for you. D2 Borobudur temple – Candirejo Village Tour by Horse cart / bicycle – Merapi lava tour Including Jeep: You will have your deserved breakfast at the hotel. Today’s tour will make you enjoy the authentic Javanese essence. You will start your route in the direction of with the Borobudur Temple (Candi Borobudur), the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. We will tour around the temple, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano has been producing during its history. After visiting one of the most important Buddhist temples in Southeast Asia, and in a horse carriage (Andong) we will visit the villages that surround this temple. These are authentic Javanese villages where culture and tradition are the protagonists. As you spend your days in this country and go around the different islands, you will realize how different Indonesians are among them in terms of clothing, food, architecture and even language. Today we will learn about and share these Javanese places. Then we will go to Kaliurang / Kalidalem to see Mount Merapi in constant activity. Here in a 4x4 jeep driven by specialized drivers, we will climb its skirt to see the remains of the 2010 eruption such as houses buried by ashes, a multitude of objects paralyzed by lava, etc. In addition, an open-air tribute museum presided over by the clock that marks the time just when the lava passed through it has been improvised. Accompanied by photos of the rescue, it will make us feel very closely the experiences of that fateful day. After finishing this day full of emotions, we will take you back to your hotel. D3 City Tour Jogjakarta Visit Sultan Palace, Watercastle and Bird Market – Prambanan Temple: After breakfast and at the indicated time we will head towards the heart of the city. We will visit the Keraton known as the Sultan’s Palace. The palace is a complex building two centuries old, located in the heart of the city. You will hear the song of the “freedom” of the birds in the bird market, we will visit the “Water Castle” that occupies the highest part at the northern end of the vast complex of Taman Sari, Malioboro Street, main street of Yogyakarta, with its merchants, horse carriages, taxi-bikes and markets. An incredible experience that will make the hours fly by. After finishing the tour in the center of the city of Yogyakarta, we will go to the northeast direction Candi Prambanan, the temple of the Hinduists and classified as a World Heritage Site by Unesco since 1991. The built of this temple was finished around the year 856 to commemorate the victory of the descendant Sanjaya of Siva, Rikai Pikatan on the last sovereign Sailendra of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to the Trimurti, the expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the Destroyer. After this unforgettable day, we will take you to your hotel. D4 Transfer out Yogyakarta International airport: Today our adventure ends at the cradle of Indonesian culture. Depending on the time of your flight, we will pick you up to take you to the airport and take the flight to your next destination. End of our services. Thank you very much for exploring Yogyakarta by the hand of Come2indonesia.',NULL,'Flight Detail: ETA: 11.25 by Batik Air ID6303 from Pangkalan Bun on 16 August 2024. (Semarang Airport) ETD: 14.00 by Lion Air JT566 to Denpasar on 19 August 2024.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5188747,'597','CARLOS ROPERO',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-19','2024-08-19','Jacob','Wiwik',1,'Persons (1-3)',420000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": \"ETA: 12.15 by Lion Air JT3560 from Yogyakarta.\", \"time\": \"12:15\", \"locality\": \"Airport Ngurah Rai (Domestic)\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Komaneka at Bisma\", \"location\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali. Telepon: (0361) 971933\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5188774,'502','Mr. David Esteso Villar',30508,207112,'1D Nusa Penida West Tour','Confirmed','C2I-BALI19',1,'2024-10-02','2024-10-02','Melysa','Praba',2,'Persons (2)',1020000.00,'Today, embark on a unique adventure as you explore the enchanting Nusa Penida, a neighboring island of Bali. Your day begins with a convenient hotel pick-up, followed by a journey to the Sanur port where a fast boat awaits to transport you to Nusa Penida in just 30 minutes. Nusa Penida, located in the southeast of Bali, is a true paradise waiting to be discovered. Upon your arrival, a friendly driver will be ready to guide you through the day\'s captivating itinerary. Your first destination is the mesmerizing Angel\'s Billabong, a natural wonder resembling a pristine pool nestled in the heart of nature. Take a refreshing swim, but exercise caution on the steps and heed your driver\'s recommendations. Next, we head to Broken Beach, a charming bay that was once a cave, now open to the sky, offering a unique and captivating scenery. Although inaccessible by land, the view from above is nothing short of breathtaking. Keep an eye out for the possibility of spotting giant manta rays gracefully gliding on the water\'s surface. Our journey continues to the renowned Kelingking Beach, famous for its stunning cliffs and the iconic hand-shaped mountain. This beach is not only one of the island\'s most famous attractions but also a favorite subject for photographers. We conclude the day at the pristine Crystal Beach, where white sands meet turquoise waters in perfect harmony. As the sun sets, you\'ll have the opportunity to relax and savor the beauty that surrounds you. This unforgettable experience concludes with a return boat trip to Bali from the Toya Pakeh port at 16:30, followed by a comfortable transfer to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-02\", \"text\": \"ETA 08:30AM by The Angkal Fastboat from Kusamba\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-02\", \"text\": \"The Angkal Resort Nusa Penida\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Nusa Penida\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5188816,'597','CARLOS ROPERO',30711,200830,'Bisma Suite Room','Confirmed',NULL,5,'2024-08-19','2024-08-24','Jacob','Wiwik',1,'Double',20655000.00,'Spacious one-bedroom suite of 88 sqm with private balcony for a sophisticated Ubud getaway. Interiors feature extensive use of wood and fine Indonesian textiles and art, lending an understated elegance to the space. Featuring a private balcony, this room includes a flat-screen TV and an en-suite bathroom with a bathtub and a shower, and many more.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5188825,'597','CARLOS ROPERO',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route (Taman Ayun-Jatiluwih-Ulundanu Beratan-Tanah Lot)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-20','2024-08-20','Jacob','Wiwik',2,'Persons (2)',1872000.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"Komaneka at Bisma\", \"location\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali. Phone: (0361) 971933\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Komaneka at Bisma\", \"location\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali. Phone: (0361) 971933\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5188844,'597','CARLOS ROPERO',30508,202894,'Kehen Temple - Pengelipuran - Kintamani','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-21','2024-08-21','Jacob','Wiwik',2,'Persons (2)',1680000.00,'Our wonderful tour starts from Kehen Temple. It is an ancient Hindu temple complex boasting unique architectural features. The staircases reaching from the ground to temple courtyard are carved sandstone mythical animal and Balinese folklore figure statues and also the central vestibule. The temple’s walls are also ornate with Chinese porcelain plates, which are a tribute to the historical relations between the local Bali kingdom and China. Afterwards, we continue to Penglipuran, a village that succeeded in preserving its 75-hectare bamboo forest located in the northern part of the village. Members of this village have a strong commitment to the system of \'Ayahan Desa\' - a philosophy committed to respecting the land on which the village stands. To concludes the day, we stop by at Tukad Cepung Waterfall. Well-guarded by the circular cliffs, this waterfall is difficult to locate for the first time visitor. The circular cliffs give you the feeling of being in a cave, while the open sky right from where the waterfall emerges, gives you the most enchanting view. The sunlight falls on the glistering waterfall creating a rainbow, which feels as though it is projected right up to you. If you have never seen water flowing from the sky, then this would be your chance! After spending your time there, we go back to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"Komaneka at Bisma\", \"location\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali. Phone: (0361) 971933\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Komaneka at Bisma\", \"location\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali. Phone: (0361) 971933\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5188851,'597','CARLOS ROPERO',30508,207379,'Ubud to Padang Bai','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-24','2024-08-24','Jacob','Wiwik',1,'Persons (1-3)',600000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"10:00\", \"locality\": \"Komaneka at Bisma\", \"location\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali. Phone: (0361) 971933\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Padang Bai Harbour\", \"location\": \"Fast Boat by Gili Gili to Gili Air (ETD: 13.30)\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5188872,'597','CARLOS ROPERO',31102,203958,'One-Bedroom Villa with Pool','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-24','2024-08-27','Jacob','Wiwik',1,'Double',10440000.00,'Step into a world of luxury and tranquility with our 1-Bedroom Private Pool Villas. These meticulously designed villas offer a haven of privacy and comfort, perfect for couples seeking an unforgettable escape. As you enter the villa, you\'ll be greeted by a spacious and elegantly furnished outdoor living area, adorned with tasteful decor and modern amenities. The thoughtfully curated interiors create a warm and inviting ambiance, setting the stage for a truly relaxing stay. Experience the highlight of our 1-Bedroom Private Pool Villas - the expansive bedroom featuring a plush king-size bed draped in soft linens, offering breathtaking views of lush greenery and immediate access to your sparkling private pool. Indulge in the en-suite bathroom\'s lavish rain shower, set in a tropical atmosphere, providing a rejuvenating retreat for your senses.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5188909,'597','CARLOS ROPERO',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-27','2024-08-28','Jacob','Wiwik',1,'Double',840000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Flight Detail: ETA: 18.35 by Super Air Jet IU767 from Lombok on 27 August 2024. ETD: 17.45 by Etihad Airways EY475 to Abu Dhabi on 28 August 2024. Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available)','{\"date\": \"2024-08-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5188911,'599','Isabel Garcia Rodriguez',31015,203232,'3D2N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Ijen Tour Package drop Bali','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-07-28','2024-07-30','Igo','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',8880000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-28\", \"text\": \"ETA 10.40 by Air Asia QZ321 from Kuala Lumpur on 28 Jul\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Surabaya International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-30\", \"text\": \"Jl. Sukma Kesuma No.29, Peliatan, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Inn Between Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5188915,'597','CARLOS ROPERO',30805,202689,'CGK-PKN','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-13','2024-08-13','Jacob','Wiwik',2,'Person',3520000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5188917,'597','CARLOS ROPERO',30805,212246,'PKN-SRG','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-16','2024-08-16','Jacob','Wiwik',2,'Person',5720000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5188920,'597','CARLOS ROPERO',30805,207117,'YIA-DPS','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-19','2024-08-19','Jacob','Wiwik',2,'Person',3080000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5188921,'597','CARLOS ROPERO',30805,208054,'LOP-CGK','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-27','2024-08-27','Jacob','Wiwik',2,'Person',3960000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5188925,'599','Isabel Garcia Rodriguez',30673,200584,'Deluxe Twin Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-28','2024-07-29','Igo','Tami',1,'Twin',1320000.00,'Escape the nature with family, friends, colleague and just relax.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5188928,'599','Isabel Garcia Rodriguez',30803,202852,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-29','2024-07-30','Igo','Tami',1,'Twin',840000.00,'At 25 sqm of room size with 46 rooms available. This smart room category is more contemporary in appearance and comes with its own terrace or balcony. Minimalist furnishings are balanced by a neutral decor to soothe the senses and ensure restful slumber. Including a double bed (king or queen) or 2 single beds (twin) with maximum capacity of 2 adults + 1 child or 3 adults. The en-suite bathroom features a modern shower cubicle enclosed in glass together with a marble vanity.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5188945,'600','Eric Marino',30508,202890,'Mount Batur Sunrise Trekking Tour','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-26','2024-09-26','Ayu','Wiwik',2,'Persons (2)',1120000.00,'Enjoy trek or climb Mount Batur and see the sunrise from the top of Batur Volcano. The Batur Volcano is one of the sacred mountain according to Hindu believe. We will get in ahead of schedule morning around 02.00 am depend the area of you stay, and afterward we specifically going to Mount Batur starting point. Starting in the dark under starlight sky, you will be guided to ascend the slope of Mount Batur. You will approach the peak of Mount Batur (1717 meters) at about 06.00 am. While waiting for the sunrise you will have a simple breakfast and hot coffee or tea served by your guide in Mount Batur. Witness the breathtaking sunrise overlooking the majestic view of Lake Batur and Mount Rinjani. After witnessing the sunrise, continue for our descent, at about 9 am, you will be arriving at the finishing point.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5188956,'600','Eric Marino',32338,215100,'Ubud to Tegalalang (Shared)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-27','2024-09-27','Ayu','Wiwik',2,'Person (1)',1236480.00,'For the Ubud to Tegalalang trip, we currently do two tours per day. The morning tour starts at 9 am and the afternoon tour starts at 3 pm. If your guests are requesting a different time please contact us and we will do our best to accommodate them. The tours last about 2.5 hours.','This trip is shared with other guests.','Tour: Ubud to Tegallalang Rice Terraces','{\"date\": \"2024-09-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"08:20\", \"locality\": \"Alamdini Ubud\", \"location\": \"Jl. Bisma No.49, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Alamdini Ubud\", \"location\": \"Jl. Bisma No.49, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5189081,'601','Mr. Ancor Sanchez Suarez',30662,213255,'7D6N Explore Tangkahan - Bukit Lawang - Lake Toba Tour(Double + Extra Bed)','Confirmed','07D EXTABOHTO',7,'2024-07-20','2024-07-26','Guio','Komang',3,'Persons (3)',34020000.00,'DAY 01 : AIRPORT / MEDAN - CITY TOUR - TANGKAHAN Upon arrival at Kualanamu International Airport, pick up by our tour guide and then transfer to town for city tour visiting Sultan Palace, Great Mosque, Chinese Temple and then drive to Tangkahan via Binjai and Batang Serangan. Afternoon arrival at Tangkahan check in MEGA INN. Meals : - Accommodation : Mega Inn Lodge DAY 02 : TANGKAHAN - ELEPHANT WASHING & RIVER SAFARI After breakfast walking to the elephant station and then join with the Mahout during washing the Elephant, and then feed the elephant, after feeding the Elephant enjoying tubing through the river and stop will be made at Fantastic Buluh Waterfall where you may enjoy the waterfall where you can take nature shower and then you can enjoy sun bathing and swimming on the river and enjoying picnic lunch on the beach of the river. Afternoon arrival at the village you can get in touch with local people, where you can see the daily activities of the local people and then return to guest house by walking, arrival at guest house you can take a rest or visit hot springs and waterfall near the guest house. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Accommodation : The Heritage Lodge - Deluxe DAY 03 : TANGKAHAN - BUKIT LAWANG BY JEEP After breakfast leave Tangkahan for Bukit Lawang by Jeep passing plantation and jungle raod, on the way stop at plantation and several interesting places such as school, enjoying the panorama and witness the activities of the local people. Upon arrival at Bukit Lawang check in to hotel and afternoon walking to the jungle to start a jungle tracking to explore the nature of Leuser National park with their flora and fauna, the possibility to see Orang Utan on their own habitat and other kind of animal such as Thomas leaf monkeys, long tail macaque, gibbon, black gibbon and other kind of flora and fauna of tropical rain forest. This tracking will take about 03 hours, after tracking return to hotel. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Bukit Lawang Cottages or Rindu Alam Hotel DAY 04 : BUKIT LAWANG - BRASTAGI After breakfast drive to Brastagi via new road and passing several village such as Namu Ukur, Rumah Galuh and Simpang Kuta Buluh, on the way you can enjoying the panorama of Sinabung Volcano, afternoon arrival in Brastagi visiting Lhumbini Park with its duplicate of Shwedagon pagoda, fruit market, and Gundaling hill, afternoon check in to hotel. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Accommodation : The Heritage Lodge - Deluxe DAY 05 : BRASTAGI - SAMOSIR / LAKE TOBA After breakfast drive head for Samosir Island in Lake Toba via TELE. En-route stop at : - Dokan (to see the traditional village of the Batak Karo tribe). - Sipisopiso Waterfall (from here you can admire the scenic view of the Lake Toba from its northern tip combined with the slender 90 meters high waterfall). - Tele (a nice place for over-viewing the lake from its western part). - Efrata (another beautiful waterfall found on the way to Samosir Island). - Lumban Suhi-suhi (to see the Tobanase traditional houses where we could observe also the women doing the weaving). In mid afternoon arriving at Tuktuk area on Samosir and check-in to hotel. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Samosir Villa Resort - Deluxe DAY 06 : SAMOSIR EXCURSION BY CAR After breakfast we start for our fullday excursion by car in the interior of Samosir island and en-route visiting : - Ambarita (to see the stone chairs and tables where once used as the execution site by the ancient tribal chieftains). - Aek Natonang (here we can see the small lake found of the top of Samosir Island and its panorama view). - Tomok (to see the old sarcophages belonged to former Sidabutar Kings and his descendants). In afternoon return back to hotel and free at leisure. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Anara Sky Kuala Namu - Deluxe DAY 07 : SAMOSIR - MEDAN / AIRPORT After breakfast drive back to Medan via Pematang Siantar and Tebing Tinggi, on the way stop at several plantation, and it will take about 5 hours driving. Arrival in Medan directly transfer to airport to catch the flight to next destination. Meals : Breakfast',NULL,'D1/20 Jul : Arrival Medan (Sumatra) – Tangkahan Elephant / Overnight at Mega Inn Lodge - simple & basic accommodation D2/21 Jul : Sumatra elephant – Tubing - transfer by jeep to Bukit Lawang/Overnight at The Heritage Hotel – Deluxe B room (breakfast - Lunch) D3/22 Jul : Sumatra orangutanes trekking camping / Overnight in Tent or shelter in the jungle (breakfast-Lunch-Dinner) D4/23 Jul : Sumatra trekking – Return to Bukit Lawang / Overnight at The Heritage Hotel – Deluxe B room (breakfast - Lunch) D5/24 Jul : Bukit Lawang - Brastagi - Samosir / Overnight at Samosir Villa Resort – Deluxe room (breakfast) D6/25 Jul : Sumatra Lake Toba - Medan - hotel in Medan / Overnight at Anara Sky Hotel Kualanamu – Deluxe room (breakfast) D7/26 Jul : Sumatra Out - Flight to Yogyakarta/ (Breakfast) note : Since 21 July is Sunday it is not possible to visit school, therefore once there is an opened local school en-route we stop for short visit.','{\"date\": \"2024-07-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5189119,'601','Mr. Ancor Sanchez Suarez',30806,202002,'4D3N Borneo Orangutan & Arut River','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO7',4,'2024-07-29','2024-08-01','Guio','Komang',3,'Persons (3)',16020000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN – KUMAI PORT – TANJUNG HARAPAN Your “Orangutan & Reforestation Tour” begins upon arrival at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan is Cape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : TANJUNG HARAPAN VILLAGE – PROBOSCIS TOUR – CAMP LEAKEY After an extraordinary breakfast, you go to visit the village inside the national park, named Tanjung Harapan Village. Here you will see the activities of the locals. After the visit, you will return to the klotok cruise up to the Sekonyer River. You will see nice vegetation around the river bank, including Nipa Palm, Pandanus, and some kinds of trees that are growing up around the river. See some wildlifes such as birds, Macaques, Proboscis Monkeys and Orangutans. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large monitor lizards. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. Note: The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. Meals : Breakfast – Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : PONDOK TANGGUI – CAMP LEAKEY – BOAT After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continue to add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After lunch, you will have the opportunity to repeat feeding camp at Camp Leaky. It is a unique opportunity to dedicate more time to your observation and to discover more wild animals, along with the Orangutans. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note: If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast – Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 4 : KUMAI PORT – PANGKALAN BUN Today we end our stay in the jungles of Borneo. Our “Orangutan & Reforestation Tour” is about to finish. In the early morning we will have breakfast on the boat, to then go to the port and in turn, be transferred to the airport. The boat departure will be at the latest at 10am, but we adapt to your flights if your flight leaves earlier in the morning. If you decide to take an afternoon flight, we can take you directly to the airport at 10 or if you want a city tour in the Arut village to drop you off at the airport later, it could be arranged at extra cost. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board. 29 July : Lunch - Dinner at Klotok 30 July : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner at klotok 31 July : Breakfast at klotok - lunch at local restaurant (without dinner) 01 Aug. Breakfast at hotel - Transfer Airport Pangkalan Bun','{\"date\": \"2024-07-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5189498,'587','Beatrice Tedeschi',33010,218588,'Fun Dive (Two Dives at Two Different Sites per Shift) IN GILIS','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-15','2024-08-15','Ayu','Tami',2,'Person (1)',2832000.00,'Morning shift: - Meeting time 7:15 AM at the dive center, walking by your own to the dive center (12 – 15 minutes) at DPM Diving Gili Trawangan ( Jl. Ikan Nautilus, Gili Trawangan ) - Boat departure time for 2 morning dives at 7:50 AM - Back at the dive center ~ 11:30 AM Afternoon shift: - Meeting time 12:30 PM at the dive center. - Boat departure time for 2 afternoon dives at 1 PM - Back at the dive center ~ 4:30 PM Here are the most popular dive sites and their respective highlights: - Shark Point: Shipwreck & white and black tip sharks. - Turtle Heaven: Nice coral and turtles. - Halik: Coral reef & reef sharks. - Bounty: Underwater platform, nice corals & turtles. - Turbo: beautiful coral, reef sharks & rays.',NULL,'Fun Dive (two dives at two different sites per shift) IN GILIS Morning shift: - Meeting time 7:15 AM at the dive center, walking by your own to the dive center (12 – 15 minutes) at DPM Diving Gili Trawangan (Jl. Ikan Nautilus, Gili Trawangan ) - Boat departure time for 2 morning dives at 7:50 AM - Back at the dive center ~ 11:30 AM Afternoon shift: -Meeting time 12:30 PM at the dive center. -Boat departure time for 2 afternoon dives at 1 PM -Back at the dive center ~ 4:30 PM Here are the most popular dive sites and their respective highlights: - Shark Point: Shipwreck & white and black tip sharks. - Turtle Heaven: Nice coral and turtles. - Halik: Coral reef & reef sharks. - Bounty: Underwater platform, nice corals & turtles. - Turbo: beautiful coral, reef sharks & rays.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5189500,'587','Beatrice Tedeschi',30508,207269,'Sanur to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-17','2024-08-17','Ayu','Tami',2,'Persons (1-3)',600000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"04:00\", \"locality\": \"Andaz Bali - A Concept by Hyatt\", \"location\": \"Jl. Danau Tamblingan No.89a, Sanur\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": \"ETD 07.00 by Lion Air JT3569 to Yogyakarta on 17 August 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Ngurah Rai Airport\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5189501,'587','Beatrice Tedeschi',30783,212808,'2D1N Yogyakarta / A. The Phoenix (Deluxe Legacy Room)','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-08-17','2024-08-18','Ayu','Tami',2,'Persons (1-3)',0.00,'D1 : Arrival Yogyakarta International Airport - Visit Borobudur Temple incl. Mendut and Pawon - check in hotel Welcome to the cradle of Indonesian culture, Yogyakarta. A tourist destination for its ancient palaces, temples, batik workshops, gamelan music orchestras, court dances and wayang puppet shows. Upon your arrival in Yogyakarta a representative of come2indonesia will be waiting for you with a sign indicating your name to start exploring this special city. We will start by heading towards Borobudur Temple (Candi Borobudur), the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. We will tour around the temple, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano has been producing during its history. After visiting one of the most important Buddhist temples in Southeast Asia, we continue our journey to the Mendut temple and Pawon temple. D2 : Morning visit Prambanan Temple - City Tour Yogyakarta visit Sultan Palace, Watercastle and Bird Market - Transfer to Yogyakarta International Airport You will enjoy a well-deserved breakfast at the hotel and we will start by heading towards Candi Prambanan, the temple of the Hinduists and classified as a World Heritage Site by Unesco since 1991. The built of this temple was finished around the year 856 to commemorate the victory of the descendant Sanjaya of Siva, Rikai Pikatan on the last sovereign Sailendra of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to the Trimurti, the expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the destroyer. After this visit we go to the Keraton known as the Sultan’s Palace. The palace is a complex building two centuries old, located in the heart of the city. You will hear the song of the “freedom” of the birds in the bird market, we will visit the “Water Castle” that occupies the highest part at the northern end of the vast complex of Taman Sari, Malioboro Street, main street of Yogyakarta, with its merchants, horse carriages, taxi-bikes and markets. An incredible experience that will make the hours fly by. According to the time of your flight, we will pick you up to take you to the airport and take the flight to your next destination. End of our services. Thank you very much for exploring Yogyakarta by the hand of Come2indonesia.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": \"ETA 07.25 by Lion Air JT3569 from Denpasar on 17 August 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Yogyakarta International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": \"ETD 13.40 by Garuda Indonesia GA209 to Jakarta on 18 August 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5189794,'587','Beatrice Tedeschi',30548,218660,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-16','2024-08-17','Ayu','Tami',1,'Double',8856000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5189795,'587','Beatrice Tedeschi',30508,218658,'Serangan to Sanur','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-16','2024-08-16','Ayu','Tami',2,'Persons (1-3)',600000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"14:55\", \"locality\": \"Serangan Port (Blue Water Express)\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Andaz Bali - A Concept by Hyatt\", \"location\": \"Jl. Danau Tamblingan No.89a, Sanur\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5189812,'586','Rafael Redondo López & Party (3)',30700,204108,'Deluxe Double Sea View Room','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-01','2024-08-04','Jacob','Eddy',1,'Double',3600000.00,NULL,NULL,'Deluxe Double Sea View Room + Extra Bed PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN','{\"date\": \"2024-08-01\", \"text\": \"ETD: 01 AUG 1650 ID6335 JT560 from Lombok by Batik Air\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"AIRPORT LABUAN BAJO\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-04\", \"text\": \"ETA: 01 AUG 1335 ID6330 JT560 to Ujung Pandang by Batik Air\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"AIRPORT LABUAN BAJO\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5189882,'602','Mr. Francesc Dassis Martin Cuberto',30783,214536,'3D2N Yogyakarta - Semarang / C. Ayaartta (Deluxe Room)','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-09-01','2024-09-03','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2 / Double)',8100000.00,'D1 : Arrival at Semarang Airport - Borobudur Temple tour incl. Mendut and Pawon - Transfer to Jogja Welcome to the cradle of Indonesian culture, Yogyakarta. A tourist destination for its ancient palaces, temples, batik workshops, gamelan music orchestras, court dances and wayang puppet shows. Upon your arrival in Semarang airport a representative of come2indonesia will be waiting for you with a sign indicating your name to start exploring this special city. We will start by heading towards Borobudur Temple (Candi Borobudur), the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. We will tour around the temple, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano has been producing during its history. After visiting one of the most important Buddhist temples in Southeast Asia, we continue our journey to the Mendut temple and Pawon temple. And then, we will take you to Jogjakarta. D2 : Jogjakarta City Tour visit Sultan Palace, Watercastle and Bird Market - Visit Prambanan Temple You will enjoy a well-deserved breakfast at the hotel and we will start by heading towards Keraton known as the Sultan’s Palace. The palace is a complex building two centuries old, located in the heart of the city. You will hear the song of the “freedom” of the birds in the bird market, we will visit the “Water Castle” that occupies the highest part at the northern end of the vast complex of Taman Sari, Malioboro Street, main street of Yogyakarta, with its merchants, horse carriages, taxi-bikes and markets. After this visit we go to Candi Prambanan, the temple of the Hinduists and classified as a World Heritage Site by Unesco since 1991. The built of this temple was finished around the year 856 to commemorate the victory of the descendant Sanjaya of Siva, Rikai Pikatan on the last sovereign Sailendra of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to the Trimurti, the expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the destroyer. An incredible experience that will make the hours fly by. After this unforgettable day, we will take you back to your hotel. D3 : Transfer to Yogyakarta International Airport You will enjoy a well-deserved breakfast at the hotel and according to the time of your flight, we will pick you up to take you to the airport and take the flight to your next destination. End of our services. Thank you very much for exploring Yogyakarta by the hand of Come2indonesia.',NULL,'01 Sept/ Day 1 transfer in 02 Sept/ Day 2 Candirejo village tour - Watercastle - Bird market 03 Sept/ Day 3 Prambanan - Kraton - Borobudur - drop Semarang','{\"date\": \"2024-09-01\", \"text\": \"ETA : 12.50 by Garuda Indonesia GA208 from Jakarta on 01 Sept 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Yogyakarta International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-03\", \"text\": \"Artotel Gajahmada Semarang Jl. Gajahmada No.101, Miroto, Kec. Semarang Tengah, Kota Semarang\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Semarang\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5189892,'602','Mr. Francesc Dassis Martin Cuberto',30672,200737,'Studio 25 (Superior) Room + Oneway Airport Transfer','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-03','2024-09-04','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',684000.00,'Studio 25 (Superior) room with 25 sqm sized room and with exclusive ARTOTEL bedding collection, some facilities in this room is 43\" inch lcd tv, 24 hours in-room service, high speed internet wi-fi, safety deposit box and hair dryer.',NULL,'\"please consult your transfer to the Airport upon check-in\"','{\"date\": \"2024-09-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5189901,'602','Mr. Francesc Dassis Martin Cuberto',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-09-04','2024-09-06','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',10800000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5189908,'602','Mr. Francesc Dassis Martin Cuberto',31015,203232,'3D2N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Ijen Tour Package drop Bali','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-09-06','2024-09-08','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',8880000.00,NULL,NULL,'Hotel in Bromo : Bromo Terrace Hotel Hotel in Banyuwangi : Ketapang Indah Banyuwangi Dropoff hotel in Bali : Artini Dijiwa Hotel Ubud','{\"date\": \"2024-09-06\", \"text\": \"ETA : 10.00 by Batik Air ID6134 from Pangkalan Bun on 06 Sept 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Juanda International Airport Surabaya\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-08\", \"text\": \"The Artini Dijiwa Ubud Jl. Raya Pengosekan Ubud, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5189911,'602','Mr. Francesc Dassis Martin Cuberto',30673,200559,'Deluxe Double Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-06','2024-09-07','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',1260000.00,'Designed to capture nature vibes. Slide open the door to your private terrace to let in the fresh mountain air and relax.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5189913,'602','Mr. Francesc Dassis Martin Cuberto',30803,202852,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-07','2024-09-08','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',780000.00,'At 25 sqm of room size with 46 rooms available. This smart room category is more contemporary in appearance and comes with its own terrace or balcony. Minimalist furnishings are balanced by a neutral decor to soothe the senses and ensure restful slumber. Including a double bed (king or queen) or 2 single beds (twin) with maximum capacity of 2 adults + 1 child or 3 adults. The en-suite bathroom features a modern shower cubicle enclosed in glass together with a marble vanity.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5189915,'602','Mr. Francesc Dassis Martin Cuberto',30705,201148,'Premier Room Rice Field View','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-09-08','2024-09-12','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',7320000.00,'Gaze out at rippling rice fields as you let your stress slip away in one of our Premier Ricefield View suites. Inside you have smooth tiles, warm wooden accents, and all the modern comforts you could ask for. Step onto the balcony and you have an airy nook where you can witness life unfold in the Balinese countryside.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5189920,'602','Mr. Francesc Dassis Martin Cuberto',30508,202894,'Kintamani - Kehen Temple - Pengelipuran - Tukad Cepung Waterfall','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-09','2024-09-09','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',1680000.00,'Our wonderful tour starts from Kehen Temple. It is an ancient Hindu temple complex boasting unique architectural features. The staircases reaching from the ground to temple courtyard are carved sandstone mythical animal and Balinese folklore figure statues and also the central vestibule. The temple’s walls are also ornate with Chinese porcelain plates, which are a tribute to the historical relations between the local Bali kingdom and China. Afterwards, we continue to Penglipuran, a village that succeeded in preserving its 75-hectare bamboo forest located in the northern part of the village. Members of this village have a strong commitment to the system of \'Ayahan Desa\' - a philosophy committed to respecting the land on which the village stands. To concludes the day, we stop by at Tukad Cepung Waterfall. Well-guarded by the circular cliffs, this waterfall is difficult to locate for the first time visitor. The circular cliffs give you the feeling of being in a cave, while the open sky right from where the waterfall emerges, gives you the most enchanting view. The sunlight falls on the glistering waterfall creating a rainbow, which feels as though it is projected right up to you. If you have never seen water flowing from the sky, then this would be your chance! After spending your time there, we go back to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-09\", \"text\": \"The Artini Dijiwa Ubud Jl. Raya Pengosekan Ubud, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-09\", \"text\": \"The Artini Dijiwa Ubud Jl. Raya Pengosekan Ubud, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5189931,'602','Mr. Francesc Dassis Martin Cuberto',30508,202893,'Lempuyang Temple Tour (Tenganan - Tirta Gangga - Lempuyang Temple)','Confirmed','C2I-BALI11',1,'2024-09-10','2024-09-10','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',1920000.00,'At the agreed time, our guide will pick you up to start the tour in the eastern part of Bali. The first place you will visit is Goa Lawah Temple. Goa Lawah Temple consists of two names, \"Goa\" which means cave and \"Lawah\" which means bat. Several thousand bats are flying in the cave as the name suggests. With the lights fading as you go deeper inside the cave, it gives off a very strange atmosphere. From Goa Lawah, we continue our way to Lempuyang Temple. Upon arrival, the temple will greet you with its gratifying panorama that extends into infinity. On a clear, sunny day, you\'ll be able to gaze out over the mountains, Amlapura city, and Mount Agung, an incredibly magnificent sight that\'s beautiful beyond words. This portrait of heaven is beautifully framed by the Gapura Candi Bentar (the gate of the temple). Our journey continues to visit Tirta Gangga. The site is a paradise surrounded by water, with all the pools decorated with unusual statues. With its seclusion and a view of the surrounding rice paddies, Tirta Gangga is a wonderful place. At the end of the trip we go to Tenganan Village, the most famous Bali Agas (the “original” Bali people) in the city. With its characteristics, the city village is arranged in parallel along the wide main road paved with rows of cobblestones. In Tenganan, women still weave the famous Kamben Geringsing, or \"burnt cloth,\" which has the power to immunize the wearer against evil. We take a close look at what they do in their daily lives in a traditional lifestyle. From Tenganan, we will transfer you to the hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-10\", \"text\": \"The Artini Dijiwa Ubud Jl. Raya Pengosekan Ubud, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-10\", \"text\": \"The Artini Dijiwa Ubud Jl. Raya Pengosekan Ubud, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5189942,'602','Mr. Francesc Dassis Martin Cuberto',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route (Taman Ayun-Jatiluwih-Bedugul-Tanah Lot)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-12','2024-09-12','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',1872000.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-12\", \"text\": \"The Artini Dijiwa Ubud Jl. Raya Pengosekan Ubud, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-12\", \"text\": \"The Artini Dijiwa Ubud Jl. Raya Pengosekan Ubud, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5189952,'604','Caroline Heisbourg',30680,200914,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-29','2024-08-30','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Single',896000.00,'Enjoy our spacious elegant deluxe room with 40 m2 of room size. Enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, hot and cold shower, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available)','{\"date\": \"2024-08-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5189966,'605','Ambra Preziosi',32766,218321,'3D2N Open Trip Komodo - Gamala / Deluxe Full Ocean','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-16','2024-08-18','Nicholas','Tami',2,'Per Person (Min. 2 Person)',10920000.00,'DAY 1 : Kelor Island - Manjerite Island - Kalong Island DAY 2 : Padar Island - Long / Pick Beach - Komodo Island - Manta Point - Taka Makasar DAY 3 : Kanawa Island',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": \"ETA 09.10 by Batik Air ID6333 from Denpasar on 16 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Komodo International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": \"ETD 15.25 by Garuda GA0453 to Jakarta on 18 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5189968,'602','Mr. Francesc Dassis Martin Cuberto',30644,201464,'4D3N Toraja Package (3N Toraja) - Santai Hotel Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-09-14','2024-09-17','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2 / Double)',15000000.00,NULL,NULL,'Accomodation : Double room','{\"date\": \"2024-09-14\", \"text\": \"ETA :09.10 by Wings Air IW1350 from Ujung Pandang on 14 Sept\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Palopo Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-17\", \"text\": \"ETD : 09.30 by Wings Air IW1351 to Ujung Pandang on 17 Sept\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Palopo Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5189972,'604','Caroline Heisbourg',30806,202002,'4D3N Borneo Orangutan & Reforestation Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO7',4,'2024-08-30','2024-09-02','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Person (1)',10360000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN – KUMAI PORT – TANJUNG HARAPAN Your “Orangutan & Reforestation Tour” begins upon arrival at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan is Cape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : TANJUNG HARAPAN VILLAGE – PROBOSCIS TOUR – CAMP LEAKEY After an extraordinary breakfast, you go to visit the village inside the national park, named Tanjung Harapan Village. Here you will see the activities of the locals. After the visit, you will return to the klotok cruise up to the Sekonyer River. You will see nice vegetation around the river bank, including Nipa Palm, Pandanus, and some kinds of trees that are growing up around the river. See some wildlifes such as birds, Macaques, Proboscis Monkeys and Orangutans. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large monitor lizards. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. Note: The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. Meals : Breakfast – Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : PONDOK TANGGUI – CAMP LEAKEY – BOAT After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continue to add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After lunch, you will have the opportunity to repeat feeding camp at Camp Leaky. It is a unique opportunity to dedicate more time to your observation and to discover more wild animals, along with the Orangutans. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note: If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast – Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 4 : KUMAI PORT – PANGKALAN BUN Today we end our stay in the jungles of Borneo. Our “Orangutan & Reforestation Tour” is about to finish. In the early morning we will have breakfast on the boat, to then go to the port and in turn, be transferred to the airport. The boat departure will be at the latest at 10am, but we adapt to your flights if your flight leaves earlier in the morning. If you decide to take an afternoon flight, we can take you directly to the airport at 10 or if you want a city tour in the Arut village to drop you off at the airport later, it could be arranged at extra cost. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5189976,'602','Mr. Francesc Dassis Martin Cuberto',30571,202567,'Superior Room + Return Airport Transfer','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-17','2024-09-18','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',1290000.00,'Located at the Second Floor, 35 sqm comfort living with a touch of Balinese style featuring completed fitting, Cable TV, a fancy bathroom comprises rain shower and good quality amenities. Also dedicated Wi-Fi Access to complete your day.',NULL,'Flifgts schedule Arrival/Departure ETA : 16.45 by Lion Air JT745 from Makassar on 17 Sept 2024 ETD : 10.10 by Wings Air IW1832 to Tambolaka on 18 Sept 2024 \"Please consult time to transfer Airport upon Check-in\"','{\"date\": \"2024-09-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5189982,'604','Caroline Heisbourg',30667,215579,'Amethyst Beo Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-08-31','2024-09-02','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Single',2396800.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-31\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5189987,'604','Caroline Heisbourg',30805,202689,'CGK-PKN','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-30','2024-08-30','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Person',1712000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5189993,'604','Caroline Heisbourg',30805,212246,'PKN-SRG','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-02','2024-09-02','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Person',2782000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5189999,'604','Caroline Heisbourg',30684,200640,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-03','2024-09-04','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Single',1528800.00,'Designed to embody fresher and younger ambience, our Deluxe Room is a convenient stay for those who plan a relatively shorter stay in Semarang. The room is provided with either a king size or deluxe twin beds.',NULL,'Please send the guarantee letter/voucher following procedure below: - 30 (thirty) days reservation notice prior to the arrival date for Normal Period. - 45 (forty-five) days reservation notice prior to the arrival date for High Season (June 1th to August 31st) and Peak Season (D-3 to D+4 Idul Fitri (April 18 - 25th, 2023 and December 21st, 2023 to January 5th, 2024) period. - Otherwise, the cancellation policy will be applied.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5190000,'604','Caroline Heisbourg',30688,201332,'Deluxe Legacy Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-02','2024-09-03','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Single',1568000.00,'Enjoying city view from a private balcony in room area of 377sq ft (35 m²) with a king bed and 2 twin beds capacity of 3 persons. Equipped with unlimited complimentary WIFI Internet connection, accessible room, 32\" flat-screen TV, safe deposit box, en suite bathroom with rain shower, and minibar with additional charge.1 extra bed possible, non-smoking rooms available upon request and daily turndown service is available.',NULL,'Please provide a copy of the voucher (certified agent in contract), which will be used by the FIT guest for check-in. The Hotel will only accept original copy issued by the Travel Company.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5190001,'604','Caroline Heisbourg',30805,202685,'SUB-DPS','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-04','2024-09-04','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Person',1070000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5190023,'606','Carlos Lopez Perez',30508,212291,'Airport to Jimbaran','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-17','2024-08-17','Guio','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',280000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": \"ETA 22.40 by Qatar QR960 from Doha on 17 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"I Gusti Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": \"Uluwatu St No.38, Jimbaran, South Kuta, Badung Regency, Bali 80361\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Lumbini Luxury Villas and Spa\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5190029,'606','Carlos Lopez Perez',30635,218534,'One Bedroom Deluxe Villa','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-08-17','2024-08-19','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',5712000.00,'Are you ready to boost your vivacity? This soothing hideaway nestled among elegant tropical gardens with an accent of bijou waterfall in front of living area will pamper your senses. Interior and exterior elements are designed tastefully and attractively to maximize your intimacy. The bedroom overlooking the pool will make it a perfect nuance for totally ultimate relaxation. Each villa is spread across 200 square meters covering a living area, dining area, private pool (2.5 m x 6.5 m) and gazebo.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5190030,'606','Carlos Lopez Perez',30508,202897,'Uluwatu Temple and Kecak Dance','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-18','2024-08-18','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',2385600.00,'This half-day tour, is an exciting tour package to visit Padang-Padang Beach, Uluwatu Temple, the famous Balinese Hindu Temple in south part of Bali with breathtaking view of sunset and Indian Ocean. Uluwatu Temple is one of Balinese Hindu Temples located right on the petrifying hill with the crevasse exist in the right and left side. Uluwatu Temple is one of Sad Khayangan (6 biggest temple in Bali) owns magnificent view of the Indian Ocean and sunset as a backdrop. This temple is very amazing where the location is right on the narrow peninsula with deep seawater under it. This tour package is combined with the spectacular Balinese traditional dance performance of Kecak Dance. Balinese Kecak Dance is a spectacular traditional dance with the group of people playing this dance with fire game. It is very exciting and unique dance due to the sound of gamelan is not using the normal gamelan but use their mouth. The dancers make the compact choir with the exquisite dance movement that is one of this dance features. After the dance we returned back to the hotel or seafood restaurant in Jimbaran.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": \"Uluwatu St No.38, Jimbaran, South Kuta, Badung Regency, Bali 80361\", \"time\": \"14:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Lumbini Luxury Villas and Spa\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5190038,'583','Sonia Garcia Lazaro',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-10','2024-08-10','Melysa','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',0.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": \"Adiwana Svarga Loka, Jalan Raya Penestanan Kelod, Sayan, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 979279\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": \"Adiwana Svarga Loka, Jalan Raya Penestanan Kelod, Sayan, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 979279\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5190053,'606','Carlos Lopez Perez',30508,202881,'Jatiluwih Rice Terrace - Banyumala Twin Waterfall - Wanagiri Hidden Hill','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-19','2024-08-19','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',1579200.00,'We begin the tour from a beautiful rice terrace of Jatiluwih. Unfolding from the foot of mountain until the coastal side, it is one of places in Bali with the beautiful view, as according to its name “Jati” and “Luwih”, where Jati mean really and Luwih meaning especial, good, and beautiful or the equivalent. The local paddies are planted in this place look typically of the high relative size plant if it is compared with other pre-eminent paddy planted by most farmers in Bali. Stroll around the area for a while and take a nice pictures, before we continue to Banyumala Twin Waterfall. The waterfall is special in that there are two flows of water to be seen, hence the name ‘twin’. Water cascades down steep rocks with gorgeous greenery surrounding them. Here you can take a refreshing dip in the plunge pool at the bottom - dunk your head and listen to the sounds of the water crashing down. After the refreshment, we conclude our day by heading to Wanagiri Hidden Hill. This hill has a charm of beauty that can make anyone who saw her feel hypnotized and fell in love Beautiful natural paintings depicting the beautiful mountains, the beautiful green trees, and the expanse of the lake can be seen clearly from this place. In addition to the panoramic view, cool and fresh air is also an added value that makes this tourist area worth visiting. Take photos and enjoy the scenery and then we head back to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": \"Uluwatu St No.38, Jimbaran, South Kuta, Badung Regency, Bali 80361\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Lumbini Luxury Villas and Spa\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": \"Jl. Kayu Putih - Munduk, Munduk, Kec. Banjar, Kabupaten Buleleng, Bali 81152\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Gumi Ayu EcoStay\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5190058,'606','Carlos Lopez Perez',32210,212635,'Deluxe Suite','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-08-19','2024-08-21','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',3808000.00,'Featuring 1 bedroom, this suite offers 1 bathroom with a bath, a seating area and terrace where you can relax. Among the room amenities are a tea and coffee maker, a wardrobe, a sofa as well as a patio and garden views. The unit has 1 bed.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5190060,'606','Carlos Lopez Perez',30508,202889,'Tamblingan Jungle Trek - Ulun Danu Temple','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-20','2024-08-20','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',2105600.00,'Today we will explore the nature of Buyan and Tamblingan lake in our lovely village, it will help you to escape from the crowds and fell the Nature atmosphere of the real jungle of Bali. We will pick you at your hotel at 07:30 AM and we drive to Tamblingan lake. Arrive in the trekking start point, we will have an explanation about the trekking. We will start the trek by entering a lush protected rain-forest area with giant old tress, animal such as macaque, black giant squirrel, birds and old legend temple inside in the Jungle. You will then walk along the shore of this lake situated in the caldera of an extinct Jungle Mountain. Our trekking guide will explain more detail about plants and living creatures in the jungle. This tour also combine with a session of thirty five minutes exploring the Tamblingan lake by dugout canoe to finishing point. Finish with trekking we will drop you to your hotel but we will make a stop at Ulun Danu Temple. Ulun Danu Temple Bratan, the famous temple stands on a small promontory located in the shore of Lake Bratan and has beautiful scenery with this lake and the mountains as backdrop sight.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-20\", \"text\": \"Jl. Kayu Putih - Munduk, Munduk, Kec. Banjar, Kabupaten Buleleng, Bali 81152\", \"time\": \"07:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Gumi Ayu EcoStay\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5190062,'606','Carlos Lopez Perez',30508,215968,'Gitgit Waterfall - Tanah Lot Temple','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-21','2024-08-21','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',2128000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": \"Jl. Kayu Putih - Munduk, Munduk, Kec. Banjar, Kabupaten Buleleng, Bali 81152\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Gumi Ayu EcoStay\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": \"Jl. Monkey Forest, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Komaneka at Rasa Sayang\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5190069,'606','Carlos Lopez Perez',30508,215968,'Tirta Empul - Besakih Temple','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-22','2024-08-22','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',1904000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-22\", \"text\": \"Jl. Monkey Forest, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Komaneka at Rasa Sayang\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5190078,'608','ANA GONZALEZ',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-08-16','2024-08-18','Jacob','Wiwik',2,'Persons (2)',10800000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Flight Detail: ETA: 07.35 by Citilink QG470 from Jakarta on 16 August 2024. ETD: 10.25 by Batik Air ID6303 to Semarang on 18 August 2024. Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5190083,'607','Juan Luis Moreno Fernández',30508,212292,'Airport to Munduk','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-03','2024-09-03','Guio','Komang',1,'Persons (1-3)',616000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-03\", \"text\": \"ETA : 17.35 by IBERIA IB7968 from Doha on 03 Sept 2024\", \"time\": \"17:35\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"International Ngurah Rai Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-03\", \"text\": \"Lesong Hotel Munduk, Gesing, Kec. Banjar, Kabupaten Buleleng, Bali 81161 Telepon: 0859-6594-4522\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Munduk\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5190130,'606','Carlos Lopez Perez',30712,200856,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-21','2024-08-24','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',8996400.00,'Spacious home-like rooms of 65 sqm furnished with modern Indonesian art and beautiful Indonesian textiles. The large private balcony or terrace looks out onto the garden or tropical mini-forest in the midst of the resort. Features a private balcony with a day bed. A TV is provided. Attached bathrooms provide shower facilities.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5190133,'606','Carlos Lopez Perez',30508,207379,'Ubud to Padang Bai','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-24','2024-08-24','Guio','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',560000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": \"Jl. Monkey Forest, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"10:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Komaneka at Rasa Sayang\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": \"ETD 13.30 to Gili Air by Gili Gili Fast Boat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Padang Bai Harbour\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5190145,'606','Carlos Lopez Perez',31300,205285,'One-Bedroom Villa with Private Pool','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-24','2024-08-27','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',9576000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5190152,'607','Juan Luis Moreno Fernández',32145,212183,'Standard Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-09-03','2024-09-05','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',1881600.00,'At Lesong Hotel, we offer the perfect blend of comfort and serenity with our double or twin bed with garden view and rice field view rooms. Each room provides a peaceful oasis for our guests, complete with breathtaking views of the surrounding tropical gardens and lush green rice fields. Enjoy the cool mountain breeze as you unwind and relax in the comfort of your twin bed. Our rooms are designed to ensure that you feel right at home. We also have safety deposit box, toilet, sofa, bathtub or shower, hardwood or parquet floors, towels, linens, desk sitting area, mosquito net, hairdryer, fan, electric kettle, wardrobe or closet clothes rack, toilet paper, board games/puzzles, hand sanitizer, air purifiers, yoga met, hot water.',NULL,'\"Honeymooner\"','{\"date\": \"2024-09-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5190169,'609','Sjaak Huizenga',31158,204473,'VIP Service Fast Track International Arrival by Galih (Not Inc. VOA)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-24','2024-07-24','Ayu','Ayu',1,'Person (1)',0.00,'Arrival International: Pick up at before immigration area.',NULL,'Meeting point: Your personal assistant will be waiting for you before the Visa-on-Arrival desk and the immigration area (near transfer desk/duty-free plaza), holding a sign of your name. They will assist you with during all arrival processes, including handling your visas and other essential documents as well as VoA (if prepaid), fast assistance at immigration counters, assistance through customs clearance, and help with the luggage. Lastly, the assistant will take you to meet the person who will pick you up at the airport, or help you find a taxi.','{\"date\": \"2024-07-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5190175,'606','Carlos Lopez Perez',30508,214949,'Padang Bai to Kuta','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-27','2024-08-27','Guio','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',560000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-27\", \"text\": \"ETA 12.30 from Gili Air by Gili Gili Fast Boat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Padang Bai Harbour\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-27\", \"text\": \"Jl. Kartika Plaza No.127, Kuta, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"The Vira Bali Boutique Hotel & Suite\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5190178,'606','Carlos Lopez Perez',30571,202567,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-27','2024-08-28','Guio','Tami',1,'Double',1372000.00,'Located at the Second Floor, 35 sqm comfort living with a touch of Balinese style featuring completed fitting, Cable TV, a fancy bathroom comprises rain shower and good quality amenities. Also dedicated Wi-Fi Access to complete your day.',NULL,'Flight information ETD 01.05 by Qatar QR961 to Doha on 28 Aug','{\"date\": \"2024-08-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5190182,'610','Mr. Sipke Huizenga ( +31652690915 )',31158,204473,'Fast Track International Arrival (Not Inc. VOA)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-24','2024-07-24','Ayu','Ayu',1,'Person (1)',0.00,'Arrival International: Pick up at before immigration area.',NULL,'Meeting point: Your personal assistant will be waiting for you before the Visa-on-Arrival desk and the immigration area (near transfer desk/duty-free plaza), holding a sign of your name. They will assist you with during all arrival processes, including handling your visas and other essential documents as well as VoA (if prepaid), fast assistance at immigration counters, assistance through customs clearance, and help with the luggage. Lastly, the assistant will take you to meet the person who will pick you up at the airport, or help you find a taxi.','{\"date\": \"2024-07-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5190240,'608','ANA GONZALEZ',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-21','2024-08-21','Jacob','Wiwik',1,'Persons (1-3)',420000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": \"ETA: 17.05 by Lion Air JT910 from Surabaya on 21 August 2024.\", \"time\": \"17:05\", \"locality\": \"Airport Ngurah Rai (Domestic)\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Purana Suite Ubud\", \"location\": \"Address: Jl. Raya Pengosekan No.1, MAS, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar. Phone: (0361) 971836\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5190242,'608','ANA GONZALEZ',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route (Taman Ayun-Jatiluwih-Ulundanu Beratan-Tanah Lot)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-22','2024-08-22','Jacob','Wiwik',2,'Persons (2)',1872000.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"PURANA SUITE UBUD\", \"location\": \"Jl. Raya Pengosekan No.1, MAS, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar. Phone: (0361) 971836\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"PURANA SUITE UBUD\", \"location\": \"Jl. Raya Pengosekan No.1, MAS, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar. Phone: (0361) 971836\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5190250,'608','ANA GONZALEZ',30508,202895,'Goa Lawah - Tenganan Village - Tirta Gangga','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-23','2024-08-23','Jacob','Wiwik',2,'Persons (2)',1956000.00,'In this part of the trip, we set off along the East Coast of the island. The first site visit will be the Kusamba Village, a fishing village where colorful Prahu in the black sand beaches. We will announce the salt making process by traditional method. We continue our journey on the east coast to reach Goa Lawah, Gua Lawah or Bat Cave is one of favorite places of interest in Bali and it is located near of hilly bank so it is called reef of Middle hill. We continue our trip to Tenganan Village, Tenganan Village is one of the oldest Balinese Traditional located in Karangasem Regency, east part of Bali. This village is much referred by cultural literature science of Tenganan Pegringsingan, which is very famous in the island. It owns very unique local community life pattern which is one example of Bali Aga Village cultures (Hindu Prehistoric) and different with other countryside in plain of Bali. From here, we go to Amlapura to visit the Royal Palace, The town of Amlapura is the capital of Karangasem (\'East Bali\'). The palace of the former kings of the region is located here, and their descendants have opened parts of the complex to the public. We will finish our trip with visit heaven of Tirta Gangga, Tirta Gangga is a beautiful park with the huge water fountain. At the end of tour we will transfer you back to the hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"PURANA SUITE UBUD\", \"location\": \"Jl. Raya Pengosekan No.1, MAS, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar. Phone: (0361) 971836\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"PURANA SUITE UBUD\", \"location\": \"Jl. Raya Pengosekan No.1, MAS, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar. Phone: (0361) 971836\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5190254,'608','ANA GONZALEZ',30508,207379,'Ubud to Padang Bai','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-26','2024-08-26','Jacob','Wiwik',1,'Persons (1-3)',600000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": \"PURANA SUITE UBUD\", \"location\": \"Jl. Raya Pengosekan No.1, MAS, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar. Phone: (0361) 971836\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"PADANG BAI HARBOUR\", \"location\": \"Office GiliGili Fast Boat to Gili Air (ETD: 08.30 AM)\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5190286,'608','ANA GONZALEZ',30728,207487,'Exploring North Lombok','Confirmed','EXC 11',1,'2024-08-31','2024-08-31','Jacob','Wiwik',2,'Persons (2)',2220000.00,'This journey will impress you from the start, driving through many kinds the vegetation such as rice fields, villages, rice terraces, forest and hills before reach flat valley of Sembalun, surrounded by the massive of the great Rinjani volcano. Pusuk Pass is a viewpoint elevated more than 1000m above sea level and overseeing Sembalun Village. Monkeys from the nearby Forest also love the views, but more the views of your bags, food and belongings. Please be very aware! Passing by Sasak villages, Lawang & Bumbung. We may have chance to visit Beleq Village, an abandoned traditional Sasak Village and trek Selong Hill to enjoy unique panorama of plantations. Local people here work as farmers who used to plant, many kinds of vegetables and fruits. If you are lucky you may pick strawberry in the season. Next destination is the Sendang Gile Waterfall (125m), set among tranquil lush surroundings. A lunch will be served at local restaurant. On the way back to your hotel, you will pass by the northern coastline which dominated the beautiful black sands and stop by at Malimbu hill for picture taking.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-31\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"JIVANA RESORT KUTA LOMBOK\", \"location\": \"Jl. Raya Kuta, Kuta, Kec. Pujut, Kabupaten Lombok Tengah, Nusa Tenggara Barat. Phone: 0853-3316-6838\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-31\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"JIVANA RESORT KUTA LOMBOK\", \"location\": \"Jl. Raya Kuta, Kuta, Kec. Pujut, Kabupaten Lombok Tengah, Nusa Tenggara Barat. Phone: 0853-3316-6838\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5190290,'608','ANA GONZALEZ',30805,208054,'LOP-CGK','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-02','2024-09-02','Jacob','Wiwik',2,'Person',3960000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5190292,'608','ANA GONZALEZ',30805,202685,'SUB-DPS','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-21','2024-08-21','Jacob','Wiwik',2,'Person',2200000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5190294,'608','ANA GONZALEZ',30805,212246,'PKN-SRG','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-18','2024-08-18','Jacob','Wiwik',2,'Person',5720000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5190295,'608','ANA GONZALEZ',30805,202689,'CGK-PKN','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-16','2024-08-16','Jacob','Wiwik',2,'Person',3520000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5190416,'612','Neus Artigas',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-08-18','2024-08-20','Nicholas','Febrina',3,'Persons (3)',12600000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5190418,'612','Neus Artigas',30673,200584,'Deluxe Twin Room + 1 Extra Bed','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-20','2024-08-21','Nicholas','Febrina',1,'Twin',1320000.00,'Escape the nature with family, friends, colleague and just relax.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5190480,'612','Neus Artigas',31015,203230,'2D1N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Tour','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-08-20','2024-08-21','Nicholas','Febrina',3,'Persons (3)',5400000.00,NULL,NULL,'2D1N Surabaya - Bromo Tour - Surabaya, with English speaking guide Excluding Horse Riding Bromo D1/20 Aug 2024: Arrival in Surabaya - Transfer to Bromo D2/21 Aug 2024: Bromo Tour - Transfer to Surabaya Flight detail: ETA 10:00 by Batik Air ID6134 from Pangkalan Bun on 20 Aug Accommodation in Bromo: Bromo Terrace Hotel J;. Raya Bromo, Sapikerep, Sukapura, Probolingo, Jawa Timur Phone: +62335 5871975 / +62821 35662509 Drop off in Surabaya on 21 Aug 2024: Platinum Hotel Tunjungan Surabaya Jl. Tunjungan No. 11-21, Genteng, Surabaya, Jawa Timur 60275 Phone: +6231 99255028','{\"date\": \"2024-08-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191237,'614','Paula Campelos Fernandez',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-16','2024-08-16','Jacob','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',360000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": \"ETA 21.35 by Super Air Jet IU738 from Jakarta on 16 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"I Gusti Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": \"Jalan Tirta Tawar, Kutuh, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Swahita Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5191252,'614','Paula Campelos Fernandez',30508,215968,'Goa Gajah – Tampaksiring – Gunung Kawi Sebatu – Tegalalang','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-17','2024-08-17','Jacob','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',2280000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": \"Jalan Tirta Tawar, Kutuh, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Swahita Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191254,'614','Paula Campelos Fernandez',30508,202889,'Tamblingan Jungle Trek - Ulun Danu Temple - Tanah Lot Temple','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-18','2024-08-18','Jacob','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',2640000.00,'Today we will explore the nature of Buyan and Tamblingan lake in our lovely village, it will help you to escape from the crowds and fell the Nature atmosphere of the real jungle of Bali. We will pick you at your hotel at 07:30 AM and we drive to Tamblingan lake. Arrive in the trekking start point, we will have an explanation about the trekking. We will start the trek by entering a lush protected rain-forest area with giant old tress, animal such as macaque, black giant squirrel, birds and old legend temple inside in the Jungle. You will then walk along the shore of this lake situated in the caldera of an extinct Jungle Mountain. Our trekking guide will explain more detail about plants and living creatures in the jungle. This tour also combine with a session of thirty five minutes exploring the Tamblingan lake by dugout canoe to finishing point. Finish with trekking we will drop you to your hotel but we will make a stop at Ulun Danu Temple. Ulun Danu Temple Bratan, the famous temple stands on a small promontory located in the shore of Lake Bratan and has beautiful scenery with this lake and the mountains as backdrop sight.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": \"Jalan Tirta Tawar, Kutuh, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"07:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Swahita Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191256,'614','Paula Campelos Fernandez',33091,218670,'Suite Room','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-08-16','2024-08-20','Jacob','Tami',1,'Double',9600000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5191258,'614','Paula Campelos Fernandez',30508,202897,'Uluwatu Temple and Kecak Dance','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-20','2024-08-20','Jacob','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',1836000.00,'This half-day tour, is an exciting tour package to visit Padang-Padang Beach, Uluwatu Temple, the famous Balinese Hindu Temple in south part of Bali with breathtaking view of sunset and Indian Ocean. Uluwatu Temple is one of Balinese Hindu Temples located right on the petrifying hill with the crevasse exist in the right and left side. Uluwatu Temple is one of Sad Khayangan (6 biggest temple in Bali) owns magnificent view of the Indian Ocean and sunset as a backdrop. This temple is very amazing where the location is right on the narrow peninsula with deep seawater under it. This tour package is combined with the spectacular Balinese traditional dance performance of Kecak Dance. Balinese Kecak Dance is a spectacular traditional dance with the group of people playing this dance with fire game. It is very exciting and unique dance due to the sound of gamelan is not using the normal gamelan but use their mouth. The dancers make the compact choir with the exquisite dance movement that is one of this dance features. After the dance we returned back to the hotel or seafood restaurant in Jimbaran.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-20\", \"text\": \"Jalan Tirta Tawar, Kutuh, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"13:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Swahita Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-20\", \"text\": \"Jl. Kayu Aya No.68, Seminyak, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"IZE Seminyak\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191284,'614','Paula Campelos Fernandez',30598,201188,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-08-20','2024-08-22','Jacob','Tami',1,'Double',2786400.00,'There’s so much to do in Seminyak, and further afield across the great island of Bali, but you need that cool haven to come back to after shopping, sightseeing or enjoying Seminyak’s legendary nightlife – that’s what an IZE Seminyak Deluxe Room provides. Enjoy calming Scandinavian-inspired decor, rainforest shower, flat-screen TV, sofa/day-bed, small balcony and more. Kick back, unwind and recharge for your next Seminyak adventure.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5191290,'614','Paula Campelos Fernandez',30508,207273,'Seminyak to Sanur','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-22','2024-08-22','Jacob','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',300000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-22\", \"text\": \"Jl. Kayu Aya No.68, Seminyak, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361\", \"time\": \"05:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"IZE Seminyak\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-22\", \"text\": \"ETD 07.30 to Nusa Penida by Maruti Fast Boat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sanur Harbour\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5191310,'614','Paula Campelos Fernandez',30508,207112,'1D Nusa Penida West Tour','Confirmed','C2I-BALI19',1,'2024-08-22','2024-08-22','Jacob','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',1020000.00,'Today, embark on a unique adventure as you explore the enchanting Nusa Penida, a neighboring island of Bali. Your day begins with a convenient hotel pick-up, followed by a journey to the Sanur port where a fast boat awaits to transport you to Nusa Penida in just 30 minutes. Nusa Penida, located in the southeast of Bali, is a true paradise waiting to be discovered. Upon your arrival, a friendly driver will be ready to guide you through the day\'s captivating itinerary. Your first destination is the mesmerizing Angel\'s Billabong, a natural wonder resembling a pristine pool nestled in the heart of nature. Take a refreshing swim, but exercise caution on the steps and heed your driver\'s recommendations. Next, we head to Broken Beach, a charming bay that was once a cave, now open to the sky, offering a unique and captivating scenery. Although inaccessible by land, the view from above is nothing short of breathtaking. Keep an eye out for the possibility of spotting giant manta rays gracefully gliding on the water\'s surface. Our journey continues to the renowned Kelingking Beach, famous for its stunning cliffs and the iconic hand-shaped mountain. This beach is not only one of the island\'s most famous attractions but also a favorite subject for photographers. We conclude the day at the pristine Crystal Beach, where white sands meet turquoise waters in perfect harmony. As the sun sets, you\'ll have the opportunity to relax and savor the beauty that surrounds you. This unforgettable experience concludes with a return boat trip to Bali from the Toya Pakeh port at 16:30, followed by a comfortable transfer to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-22\", \"text\": \"ETD 08.00 by Maruti Fast Boat from Sanur\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Toya Pakeh Harbour\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-22\", \"text\": \"Jalan Raya Sakti Nusa Penida, Sakti, Nusa Penida, Klungkung Regency, Bali 80771\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Namaste Bungalows\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191315,'614','Paula Campelos Fernandez',31039,203394,'Deluxe Bungalow Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-08-22','2024-08-24','Jacob','Tami',1,'Double',1920000.00,'At 30 m2 room size, built to accommodate 2 people, this air-conditioned bungalow in wood and colored concrete has its private terrace, a large double bed for 2 people and an extra single bed, a waxed concrete bathroom with hot water and quipped with a standard WC Europeans.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5191352,'616','Mr. Abraham Valdivia Martín',30680,200912,'Superior Room + Round Trip Airport Transfer','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-30','2024-08-31','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',784000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Flight Details: 30 Aug ETA 07:40 by Qatar Airways QR958 from Doha 31 Aug ETD 06:00 by Batik Air ID6202 to Pangkalan Bun Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-08-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-31\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5191354,'616','Mr. Abraham Valdivia Martín',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-08-31','2024-09-02','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',10080000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-31\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191355,'614','Paula Campelos Fernandez',31242,205019,'One-Bedroom Villa with Private Pool','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-08-24','2024-08-28','Jacob','Tami',1,'Double',15912000.00,'Our villas feels like that warm feeling you get when you rediscover a fond lost memory of home. More than that, it feels authentic, featuring wood that’s over 100 years old. More than a simple luxurious experience, it is a journey through history with all of the modern comforts. Discover an old culture fused with modern lifestyle. You’ll never want to leave.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5191361,'616','Mr. Abraham Valdivia Martín',30783,216589,'4D3N Jogja-Bromo-Surabaya Incl. Train / A. The Phoenix (Deluxe Room) & Jiwa Jawa Bromo (Deluxe Room)','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-09-02','2024-09-05','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2 / Double)',19440000.00,'D1 : Arrival Yogyakarta International Airport – Visit Prambanan Temple – Transfer to hotel D2 : Borobudur temple incl. Mendut and Pawon ,Yogyakarta City Tour Visit Sultan Palace, Watercastle and Bird/Traditional Market D3 : Jogja – Mojokerto by Train then continue drive to Bromo – overnight in Bromo D4 : Sunrise and Mt. Bromo crater tour incl. Jeep ( Horse rise Exclude ) – Transfer to Surabaya airport',NULL,'- Hotel in Yogyakarta based on The Phienix Hotel - Double Deluxe Legacy room - Hotel in Bromo based on Jiwa Jawa - Double Deluxe room 02 Sept /D1 : Pickup at Semarang Airport - Watercastle and Bird Market/Malioboro - check in hotel 03 Sept /D2 : Borobudur temple - Sultan Palace - Prambanan temple 04 Sept /D3 : Transfer to Bromo by Train 05 Sept / D4 : Bromo Sunrise Tour - Transfer to Surabaya Airport \"The Guest is Honeymooner\"','{\"date\": \"2024-09-02\", \"text\": \"ETA : 11.25 by Batik Air ID6303 from Pangkalan Bun on 02 Sept 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ahmad Yani Airport Semarang\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-05\", \"text\": \"ETD : 15.25 by Lion Air JT920 to Denpasar on 05 Sept 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Juanda International Airport Surabaya\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191372,'614','Paula Campelos Fernandez',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-28','2024-08-29','Jacob','Tami',1,'Double',840000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-08-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5191373,'616','Mr. Abraham Valdivia Martín',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-05','2024-09-05','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',784000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-05\", \"text\": \"ETA : 17.25 by Lion Air JT920 from Surabaya on 05 Sept 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-05\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Tejaprana Bisma Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5191374,'614','Paula Campelos Fernandez',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-08-29','2024-08-31','Jacob','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',10800000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-29\", \"text\": \"ETA 07.15 by Batik Air ID6202 from Jakarta on 29 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pangkalan Bun Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-31\", \"text\": \"ETD 14.10 by Nam Air IN191 to Jakarta on 31 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191375,'616','Mr. Abraham Valdivia Martín',30623,200583,'Garden Villa','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-09-05','2024-09-09','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',11872000.00,'The Garden Villas provide an ideal sanctuary, featuring a private garden that ensures a peaceful and intimate atmosphere for guests seeking the perfect retreat. These one-bedroom villas are well-equipped with a floor area of 100 m², a king-size bed, air conditioning, sleek appointed bathroom with a rainfall showerhead, beautiful view of the garden, and various amenities for a comfortable stay. Unwind in the serenity of the villa’s private outdoor haven, whether it’s within the comforting embrace of the gazebo, lounging by the refreshing plunge pool, or indulging in pure relaxation while soaking in the outdoor natural stone bathtub.',NULL,'\"The Guest is Honeymooner\"','{\"date\": \"2024-09-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5191379,'616','Mr. Abraham Valdivia Martín',30508,215968,'1D Bali Tour Campuhan Trekk-Tegalalang-Tirta Empul-Gunung Kawi-Tegenungan Waterfall','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-06','2024-09-06','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',2128000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-06\", \"text\": \"Tejaprana Bisma Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-06\", \"text\": \"Tejaprana Bisma Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191383,'614','Paula Campelos Fernandez',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-31','2024-09-01','Jacob','Tami',1,'Double',840000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-08-31\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5191401,'616','Mr. Abraham Valdivia Martín',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route (Taman Ayun-Jati Luwih-Bedugul-Tanah Lot)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-07','2024-09-07','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',1747200.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-07\", \"text\": \"Tejaprana Bisma Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-07\", \"text\": \"Tejaprana Bisma Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191410,'616','Mr. Abraham Valdivia Martín',30606,203160,'Beach Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-09','2024-09-10','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',4754400.00,'The Beach Room are a stylish, sleek and serene addition to our hotel on Seminyak Beach. Witness a marriage of contemporary design and Balinese tradition, complete with yielding beds, sunny balconies and lavish en-suite bathrooms with indulgent soaking tubs and powerful rain showers. Hand-carved wooden accents are offset by warm-toned furnishings and fabrics that span the spectrum from burgundy via espresso to cappuccino.',NULL,'\"The Guest is Honeymooner\"','{\"date\": \"2024-09-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5191416,'616','Mr. Abraham Valdivia Martín',30508,207278,'Full Day Tour Car & Driver (8-10 hours)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-09','2024-09-09','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (1-3)',1120000.00,NULL,NULL,'\" The guest will doing Activity Surfing in Seminyak\" The driver pickup in Ubud, delivers and waits at the surf spot until finish (2 hours) and then dropoff to Hotel in Seminyak \"not include guide, entrance fee, ticket and parking\"','{\"date\": \"2024-09-09\", \"text\": \"Tejaprana Bisma Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-09\", \"text\": \"Jl. Kayu Aya, Pantai Seminyak, Kuta, Seminyak, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Telepon: (0361) 730814\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"The Seminyak Beach Resort\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5191439,'616','Mr. Abraham Valdivia Martín',30508,207273,'Seminyak to Sanur','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-10','2024-09-10','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',600000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-10\", \"text\": \"The Seminyak Beach Resort & Spa Jl. Kayu Aya, Pantai Seminyak, Kuta, Seminyak, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung\", \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Seminyak\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-10\", \"text\": \"ETD 07:30AM by Maruti Fastboat to Penida\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sanur Harbour\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5191459,'616','Mr. Abraham Valdivia Martín',30508,207112,'1D Nusa Penida West Tour','Confirmed','C2I-BALI19',1,'2024-09-10','2024-09-10','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',952000.00,'Today, embark on a unique adventure as you explore the enchanting Nusa Penida, a neighboring island of Bali. Your day begins with a convenient hotel pick-up, followed by a journey to the Sanur port where a fast boat awaits to transport you to Nusa Penida in just 30 minutes. Nusa Penida, located in the southeast of Bali, is a true paradise waiting to be discovered. Upon your arrival, a friendly driver will be ready to guide you through the day\'s captivating itinerary. Your first destination is the mesmerizing Angel\'s Billabong, a natural wonder resembling a pristine pool nestled in the heart of nature. Take a refreshing swim, but exercise caution on the steps and heed your driver\'s recommendations. Next, we head to Broken Beach, a charming bay that was once a cave, now open to the sky, offering a unique and captivating scenery. Although inaccessible by land, the view from above is nothing short of breathtaking. Keep an eye out for the possibility of spotting giant manta rays gracefully gliding on the water\'s surface. Our journey continues to the renowned Kelingking Beach, famous for its stunning cliffs and the iconic hand-shaped mountain. This beach is not only one of the island\'s most famous attractions but also a favorite subject for photographers. We conclude the day at the pristine Crystal Beach, where white sands meet turquoise waters in perfect harmony. As the sun sets, you\'ll have the opportunity to relax and savor the beauty that surrounds you. This unforgettable experience concludes with a return boat trip to Bali from the Toya Pakeh port at 16:30, followed by a comfortable transfer to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-10\", \"text\": \"ETA : 08.00 by Maruti Fastboat from Sanur on 10 Sept 2024\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Banjar Nyuh harbour\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-10\", \"text\": \"Sakti, Kec. Nusa Penida, Kabupaten Klungkung, Bali 80771 Telepon: (0361) 6208999\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Maua Nusa Penida\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191464,'616','Mr. Abraham Valdivia Martín',30582,203387,'One Bedroom Luxury Villas','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-10','2024-09-11','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',4224000.00,'Each One Bedroom Luxury Villa is designed with a private infinity pool, scenic view across the Gamat Bay or garden view, and some have a small private garden. Every villas features the following: An integrated universal power outlet, Room safe (suitable for storing laptops), Cable TV with international news and movie channels, Eco-friendly bathroom amenities, Coffee and tea-making facilities.',NULL,'\"The Guest is Honeymooner\"','{\"date\": \"2024-09-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5191472,'616','Mr. Abraham Valdivia Martín',30508,207391,'Transfer Out Nusa Penida','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-11','2024-09-11','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',448000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-11\", \"text\": \"Sakti, Kec. Nusa Penida, Kabupaten Klungkung\", \"time\": \"07:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Maua Nusa Penida\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-11\", \"text\": \"ETD 09:00AM by BlueWater Express to Gili Trawangan\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Buyuk Harbour\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5191474,'607','Juan Luis Moreno Fernández',30508,202889,'Tamblingan Jungle Trek - Ulun Danu Temple','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-05','2024-09-05','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',2105600.00,'Today we will explore the nature of Buyan and Tamblingan lake in our lovely village, it will help you to escape from the crowds and fell the Nature atmosphere of the real jungle of Bali. We will pick you at your hotel at 07:30 AM and we drive to Tamblingan lake. Arrive in the trekking start point, we will have an explanation about the trekking. We will start the trek by entering a lush protected rain-forest area with giant old tress, animal such as macaque, black giant squirrel, birds and old legend temple inside in the Jungle. You will then walk along the shore of this lake situated in the caldera of an extinct Jungle Mountain. Our trekking guide will explain more detail about plants and living creatures in the jungle. This tour also combine with a session of thirty five minutes exploring the Tamblingan lake by dugout canoe to finishing point. Finish with trekking we will drop you to your hotel but we will make a stop at Ulun Danu Temple. Ulun Danu Temple Bratan, the famous temple stands on a small promontory located in the shore of Lake Bratan and has beautiful scenery with this lake and the mountains as backdrop sight.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-05\", \"text\": \"Lesong Hotel Munduk, Gesing, Kec. Banjar, Kabupaten Buleleng, Bali 81161 Telepon: 0859-6594-4522\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Munduk\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-05\", \"text\": \"Bucu View Resort Ubud, Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 975976\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191481,'616','Mr. Abraham Valdivia Martín',31242,205019,'One-Bedroom Villa with Private Pool','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-09-11','2024-09-14','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',11138400.00,'Our villas feels like that warm feeling you get when you rediscover a fond lost memory of home. More than that, it feels authentic, featuring wood that’s over 100 years old. More than a simple luxurious experience, it is a journey through history with all of the modern comforts. Discover an old culture fused with modern lifestyle. You’ll never want to leave.',NULL,'\"The Guest is Honeymooner\"','{\"date\": \"2024-09-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5191484,'607','Juan Luis Moreno Fernández',30615,201040,'Valley Suite Room with Breakfast','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-09-05','2024-09-09','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',7168000.00,'Relax after a long day in our bathtub with river view in the Valley suite. This air-conditioned room comes with a TV, mosquito nets, and a fridge with minibar. The private bathroom offers hot water.',NULL,'\"Honeymooner\"','{\"date\": \"2024-09-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5191485,'616','Mr. Abraham Valdivia Martín',30648,203996,'1 Bedroom Pool Villa','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-14','2024-09-15','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',3808000.00,'At 90 sqm indoor / outdoor space with private pool and tropical garden. Guests will have a special experience as this suite features a private pool. This spacious suite is consisted of of 1 living room, 1 separate bedroom and 1 bathroom with a shower and free toiletries. In the kitchen, guests will find a stovetop, a refrigerator, kitchenware and a microwave. The air-conditioned suite offers a flat-screen TV with satellite channels, a private entrance, a mini-bar, a tea and coffee maker as well as garden views. The unit offers 1 bed.',NULL,'\"The Guest is Honeymooner\"','{\"date\": \"2024-09-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5191488,'607','Juan Luis Moreno Fernández',30508,215968,'1D Bali Tour (Custom Itinerary)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-06','2024-09-06','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',1792000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191490,'607','Juan Luis Moreno Fernández',30508,215968,'1D Bali Tour (Taman Ayun - Batukaru Temple - Jatiluwih - Tanah Lot))','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-06','2024-09-06','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',1792000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-06\", \"text\": \"Bucu View Resort Ubud, Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 975976\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-06\", \"text\": \"Bucu View Resort Ubud, Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 975976\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191494,'607','Juan Luis Moreno Fernández',30508,215968,'1D Bali Tour (Goa Gajah – Tampaksiring - Gunung Kawi – Tegalalang)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-07','2024-09-07','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',1904000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-07\", \"text\": \"Bucu View Resort Ubud, Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 975976\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-07\", \"text\": \"Bucu View Resort Ubud, Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 975976\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191512,'607','Juan Luis Moreno Fernández',30508,202893,'Lempuyang Temple Tour - Virgin Beach - Tenganan','Confirmed','C2I-BALI11',1,'2024-09-08','2024-09-08','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',1792000.00,'At the agreed time, our guide will pick you up to start the tour in the eastern part of Bali. The first place you will visit is Goa Lawah Temple. Goa Lawah Temple consists of two names, \"Goa\" which means cave and \"Lawah\" which means bat. Several thousand bats are flying in the cave as the name suggests. With the lights fading as you go deeper inside the cave, it gives off a very strange atmosphere. From Goa Lawah, we continue our way to Lempuyang Temple. Upon arrival, the temple will greet you with its gratifying panorama that extends into infinity. On a clear, sunny day, you\'ll be able to gaze out over the mountains, Amlapura city, and Mount Agung, an incredibly magnificent sight that\'s beautiful beyond words. This portrait of heaven is beautifully framed by the Gapura Candi Bentar (the gate of the temple). Our journey continues to visit Tirta Gangga. The site is a paradise surrounded by water, with all the pools decorated with unusual statues. With its seclusion and a view of the surrounding rice paddies, Tirta Gangga is a wonderful place. At the end of the trip we go to Tenganan Village, the most famous Bali Agas (the “original” Bali people) in the city. With its characteristics, the city village is arranged in parallel along the wide main road paved with rows of cobblestones. In Tenganan, women still weave the famous Kamben Geringsing, or \"burnt cloth,\" which has the power to immunize the wearer against evil. We take a close look at what they do in their daily lives in a traditional lifestyle. From Tenganan, we will transfer you to the hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-08\", \"text\": \"Bucu View Resort Ubud, Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 975976\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-08\", \"text\": \"Bucu View Resort Ubud, Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 975976\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191514,'607','Juan Luis Moreno Fernández',30508,213032,'Ubud to Kusamba','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-09','2024-09-09','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (1-3)',784000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,'Please ready on hotel lobby for pickup at 07.00','{\"date\": \"2024-09-09\", \"text\": \"Bucu View Resort Ubud, Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 975976\", \"time\": \"07:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-09\", \"text\": \"ETD : 09.00 by The Angkal Fastboat from Kusamba to Nusa Penida\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Kusamba Port\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5191521,'607','Juan Luis Moreno Fernández',30508,207112,'1D Nusa Penida West Tour','Confirmed','C2I-BALI19',1,'2024-09-09','2024-09-09','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',952000.00,'Today, embark on a unique adventure as you explore the enchanting Nusa Penida, a neighboring island of Bali. Your day begins with a convenient hotel pick-up, followed by a journey to the Sanur port where a fast boat awaits to transport you to Nusa Penida in just 30 minutes. Nusa Penida, located in the southeast of Bali, is a true paradise waiting to be discovered. Upon your arrival, a friendly driver will be ready to guide you through the day\'s captivating itinerary. Your first destination is the mesmerizing Angel\'s Billabong, a natural wonder resembling a pristine pool nestled in the heart of nature. Take a refreshing swim, but exercise caution on the steps and heed your driver\'s recommendations. Next, we head to Broken Beach, a charming bay that was once a cave, now open to the sky, offering a unique and captivating scenery. Although inaccessible by land, the view from above is nothing short of breathtaking. Keep an eye out for the possibility of spotting giant manta rays gracefully gliding on the water\'s surface. Our journey continues to the renowned Kelingking Beach, famous for its stunning cliffs and the iconic hand-shaped mountain. This beach is not only one of the island\'s most famous attractions but also a favorite subject for photographers. We conclude the day at the pristine Crystal Beach, where white sands meet turquoise waters in perfect harmony. As the sun sets, you\'ll have the opportunity to relax and savor the beauty that surrounds you. This unforgettable experience concludes with a return boat trip to Bali from the Toya Pakeh port at 16:30, followed by a comfortable transfer to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-09\", \"text\": \"ETA : 09.20 by The Angkal Fastboat from Kusamba on 09 Sept 2024\", \"time\": \"09:20\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sampalan Port\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-09\", \"text\": \"Adiwana Warnakali Nusa Penida, Sakti, Nusa Penida, Kabupaten Klungkung, Bali 80771 Telepon: (0361) 6207000\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Nusa Penida\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191547,'607','Juan Luis Moreno Fernández',30508,212475,'Nusa Penida Hotel to Buyuk Harbour','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-10','2024-09-10','Guio','Komang',1,'Persons (1-3)',280000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,'Please ready on hotel lobby for pickup at 07.00','{\"date\": \"2024-09-10\", \"text\": \"Adiwana Warnakali Nusa Penida, Sakti, Nusa Penida, Kabupaten Klungkung, Bali 80771 Telepon: (0361) 6207000\", \"time\": \"07:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Nusa Penida\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-10\", \"text\": \"ETD : 09.15 by Bluewater Express to Gili Air on 10 Sept 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Buyuk Harbour\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5191556,'617','Marc Urgell Olle',32766,216809,'3D2N Open Trip Komodo - Lady Grace / Full Ocean','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-23','2024-08-25','Nicholas','Tami',2,'Per Person (Min. 2 Person)',15240000.00,'DAY 1 : Kelor Island - Manjerite Island - Kalong Island DAY 2 : Padar Island - Long / Pick Beach - Komodo Island - Manta Point - Taka Makasar DAY 3 : Kanawa Island',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-23\", \"text\": \"Jl. Soekarno Hatta, Labuan Bajo, Kec. Komodo, Kabupaten Manggarai Barat\", \"time\": \"09:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Seaesta Komodo Hostel & Hotel\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-25\", \"text\": \"ETD 15.25 by Garuda Indonesia GA453 to Jakarta on 25 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Komodo International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191586,'607','Juan Luis Moreno Fernández',30852,202033,'Villa Surya - One Bedroom Private Pool and Tropical Garden','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-09-10','2024-09-13','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',11760000.00,'Our cozy one bed Villa Surya is perfect for a solo traveler or a romantic getaway at 150 sqm private property. The spacious bedroom features a king-size bed with an extra thick mattress with 100% cotton linen, ensuring a blissful sleep. With high-ceilings, large windows, and a pivoting door onto your patio, the space is able to breathe whilst being basked in a beautiful, natural light. The ensuite bathroom, equipped with a bespoke basin area, rainfall shower, quality toiletries and 100% cotton towels leads out to the real star of this villa, the indulgent open-air bathtub. Large enough for two, with views of your private pool and tropical garden, while away hours in pure relaxation.',NULL,'\"Honeymooner\"','{\"date\": \"2024-09-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5191601,'607','Juan Luis Moreno Fernández',30547,200475,'Ocean View Suite Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-09','2024-09-10','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',2460000.00,'Adiwana Warnakali boasts a collection of 12 Ocean View suites, all situated on the lower level, have a room size 56 sqm and the type bed single or double. Each of these suites offers a generously-sized balcony that unveils breathtaking vistas of the vast, cerulean expanse of the Nusa Lembongan ocean and the majestic presence of Mount Agung. Here, your mornings resemble scenes from a captivating movie, with the invigorating scent of the sea and the soothing melody of waves crashing against the rugged cliffs. The spacious rooms are designed for your utmost comfort, sporting a nautical theme that incorporates oars as charming decorative elements. The bathrooms are adorned with striking blue tiles, adding to the overall maritime charm. Immerse yourself in an unforgettable and idyllic stay at Adiwana Warnakali.',NULL,'\"Honeymooner\"','{\"date\": \"2024-09-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5191621,'607','Juan Luis Moreno Fernández',30508,212301,'Padang Bai to Uluwatu','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-13','2024-09-13','Guio','Komang',1,'Persons (1-3)',560000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-13\", \"text\": \"ETA : 12.30 by Gili Gili Fastboat from Gili Air to Padang Bay on 13 Sept 2024\", \"time\": \"12:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Padang Bay Harbour\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-13\", \"text\": \"Green Escape, Jl. Bangbang Metuug, Pecatu, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Telepon: 0811-3997-903\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Uluwatu\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5191622,'216','Edith Brown',30508,202894,'Kehen Temple - Pengelipuran - Tukad Cepung Waterfall','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-01','2024-08-01','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Persons (2)',1568000.00,'Our wonderful tour starts from Kehen Temple. It is an ancient Hindu temple complex boasting unique architectural features. The staircases reaching from the ground to temple courtyard are carved sandstone mythical animal and Balinese folklore figure statues and also the central vestibule. The temple’s walls are also ornate with Chinese porcelain plates, which are a tribute to the historical relations between the local Bali kingdom and China. Afterwards, we continue to Penglipuran, a village that succeeded in preserving its 75-hectare bamboo forest located in the northern part of the village. Members of this village have a strong commitment to the system of \'Ayahan Desa\' - a philosophy committed to respecting the land on which the village stands. To concludes the day, we stop by at Tukad Cepung Waterfall. Well-guarded by the circular cliffs, this waterfall is difficult to locate for the first time visitor. The circular cliffs give you the feeling of being in a cave, while the open sky right from where the waterfall emerges, gives you the most enchanting view. The sunlight falls on the glistering waterfall creating a rainbow, which feels as though it is projected right up to you. If you have never seen water flowing from the sky, then this would be your chance! After spending your time there, we go back to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-01\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in hotel lobby at the mentioned time.\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191630,'607','Juan Luis Moreno Fernández',30930,202592,'One Bedroom Bungalow','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-13','2024-09-14','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',2688000.00,'Room size : 37 sqm. Our One-Bedroom Bungalow is a unique Romantic Eco-Boho Bungalow nestles in Green Escape Resort. You will stay in a sumptuous air-conditioned bungalow that has been handcrafted using recycled wood and tastefully decorated to offer you an authentic Balinese getaway. It\'s the very epitome of a tranquil escape. This Bungalow offers a deluxe king-size bed and a daybed to relax. It offers a comfy mattress, as we know the benefits of a good night’s sleep. The semi-outdoor bathroom with a rain shower will help you revive yourself. Enjoy the comfy sofa on your private terrace which opens onto the exotic garden & pool. The daybed can be used to extend the sleeping capacity of your private bungalow.',NULL,'\"Honeymooner\"','{\"date\": \"2024-09-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5191633,'618','Giovanny Martin Rodriguez',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-15','2024-08-16','Jacob','Tami',1,'Double',840000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-08-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5191639,'607','Juan Luis Moreno Fernández',30508,216161,'Uluwatu to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-14','2024-09-14','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (1-3)',784000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,'Please ready on hotel lobby for pickup at 14.00','{\"date\": \"2024-09-14\", \"text\": \"Green Escape, Jl. Bangbang Metuug, Pecatu, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Telepon: 0811-3997-903\", \"time\": \"14:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Uluwatu\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-14\", \"text\": \"ETD : 19.10 by IBERIA IB7979 to Doha on 14 Sept 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"International Ngurah Rai Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5191643,'618','Giovanny Martin Rodriguez',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-08-16','2024-08-18','Jacob','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',10800000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": \"ETA 07.15 by Batik Air ID6202 from Jakarta on 16 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pangkalan Bun Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": \"ETD 08.50 by Batik Air ID6134 to Surabaya on 18 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191652,'618','Giovanny Martin Rodriguez',31015,203232,'3D2N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Ijen Tour Package drop Bali','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-18','2024-08-20','Jacob','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',8880000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": \"ETA 10.00 by Batik Air ID6134 from Pangkalan Bun on 18 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Surabaya International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-20\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 2\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191665,'618','Giovanny Martin Rodriguez',30673,200562,'Deluxe Double Room Hill View','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-18','2024-08-19','Jacob','Tami',1,'Double',1500000.00,'Overlooking the hills and plantations, deluxe hill view offering breathtaking views of nature. Just relax on the terrace, laze away the hours with a good book and hot coffee.',NULL,'Honeymooners','{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5191688,'618','Giovanny Martin Rodriguez',30803,202852,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-19','2024-08-20','Jacob','Tami',1,'Double',840000.00,'At 25 sqm of room size with 46 rooms available. This smart room category is more contemporary in appearance and comes with its own terrace or balcony. Minimalist furnishings are balanced by a neutral decor to soothe the senses and ensure restful slumber. Including a double bed (king or queen) or 2 single beds (twin) with maximum capacity of 2 adults + 1 child or 3 adults. The en-suite bathroom features a modern shower cubicle enclosed in glass together with a marble vanity.',NULL,'Honeymooners','{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5191691,'618','Giovanny Martin Rodriguez',30620,200812,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-08-20','2024-08-24','Jacob','Tami',1,'Double',4320000.00,'20 units (10 double bed and 10 twin bed) of 29 sqm each superior rooms with valley view and garden are modern‐minimalism designed. Advance facilities such as LCD TV, coffee/tea maker, balcony/terrace, safety deposit box, minibar, and complete bathroom facilities.',NULL,'Honeymooners','{\"date\": \"2024-08-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5191695,'618','Giovanny Martin Rodriguez',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-21','2024-08-21','Jacob','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',1872000.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 2\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191699,'618','Giovanny Martin Rodriguez',30508,215968,'Goa Gajah – Tampaksiring – Gunung Kawi Sebatu Temple – Tegalalang','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-22','2024-08-22','Jacob','Tami',2,'Person (1)',2280000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-22\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 2\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191703,'618','Giovanny Martin Rodriguez',30508,202897,'Uluwatu Temple and Kecak Dance','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-24','2024-08-24','Jacob','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',1836000.00,'This half-day tour, is an exciting tour package to visit Padang-Padang Beach, Uluwatu Temple, the famous Balinese Hindu Temple in south part of Bali with breathtaking view of sunset and Indian Ocean. Uluwatu Temple is one of Balinese Hindu Temples located right on the petrifying hill with the crevasse exist in the right and left side. Uluwatu Temple is one of Sad Khayangan (6 biggest temple in Bali) owns magnificent view of the Indian Ocean and sunset as a backdrop. This temple is very amazing where the location is right on the narrow peninsula with deep seawater under it. This tour package is combined with the spectacular Balinese traditional dance performance of Kecak Dance. Balinese Kecak Dance is a spectacular traditional dance with the group of people playing this dance with fire game. It is very exciting and unique dance due to the sound of gamelan is not using the normal gamelan but use their mouth. The dancers make the compact choir with the exquisite dance movement that is one of this dance features. After the dance we returned back to the hotel or seafood restaurant in Jimbaran.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"13:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 2\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": \"Gg. Mertasari, Pecatu, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sal Secret Spot\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191726,'618','Giovanny Martin Rodriguez',30508,213032,'Ubud to Kusamba','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-23','2024-08-23','Jacob','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',420000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-23\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 2\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-23\", \"text\": \"ETD 08.00 to Nusa Penida by The Angkal Fast Boat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Kusamba Harbour\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5191738,'619','Daniel Ruiz',30662,213274,'3D2N Medan - Leuser National Park Tracking','Confirmed','RVL-3D Boh-Lst',3,'2024-08-29','2024-08-31','Jacob','Eddy',2,'Persons (2-3 / Double)',9540000.00,'DAY 01 : MEDAN - BUKIT LAWANG Arrival at Kuala Namu Int airport Airport Medan drive to Bukit Lawang with stop at several Plantation for rubber and Palm oil. After that arrival at Bukit Lawang check in to hotel. Meals : - Accommodation : Bukit Lawang Cottages or Rindu Alam Hotel DAY 02 : BUKIT LAWANG - FULL DAY TRACKING LEUSER PARK After breakfast walking to the jungle to start a jungle tracking to explore the nature of Leuser National park with their flora and fauna, the possibility to see Orang Utan on their own habitat and other kind of animal such as Thomas leaf monkeys, long tail macaque, gibbon, black gibbon and other kind of flora and fauna of tropical rain forest. This fullday tracking will finish in the afternoon and then return back to hotel. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Accommodation : Bukit Lawang Cottages or Rindu Alam Hotel DAY 03 : BUKIT LAWANG - MEDAN / AIRPORT After breakfast free at own leisure for swimming or walking and then drive to Medan arrival in Medan directly transfer to airport. Meals : Breakfast',NULL,'29 - 31 AUG 2024 ( 2 NIGHT) HOTEL Bukit Lawang Cottages – Butterfly room) DAY 01 / 29 Aug 2024: MEDAN – BUKIT LAWANG (Bukit Lawang Cottages – Butterfly room After breakfast pick up by our guide then drive to Bukit Lawang with stop at several Plantation for rubber and Palm oil arrival at Bukit Lawang check in to hotel. -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- DAY 02 / 30 Aug 2024: BUKIT LAWANG – FULL DAY TRACKING LEUSER PARK (B,L) After breakfast walking to the jungle to start a jungle tracking to explore the nature of Leuser National park with their flora and fauna, the possibility to see Orang Utan on their own habitat and other kind of animal such as Thomas leaf monkeys, long tail macaque, gibbon, black gibbon and other kind of flora and fauna of tropical rain forest. This fullday tracking will finish in the afternoon and then return back to hotel. -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- DAY 03 / 31 Aug 2024: BUKIT LAWANG – MEDAN / AIRPORT (B) After breakfast free at own leisure for swimming or walking and then drive to Medan arrival in Medan directly transfer to airport.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-29\", \"text\": \"Emerald Garden Hotel\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-31\", \"text\": \"ETD: 31 AUGUST AT 14:10 - FLIGHT AK396 de Air Asia\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"AIRPORT\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191755,'618','Giovanny Martin Rodriguez',30508,207112,'1D Nusa Penida West Tour','Confirmed','C2I-BALI19',1,'2024-08-23','2024-08-23','Jacob','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',1020000.00,'Today, embark on a unique adventure as you explore the enchanting Nusa Penida, a neighboring island of Bali. Your day begins with a convenient hotel pick-up, followed by a journey to the Sanur port where a fast boat awaits to transport you to Nusa Penida in just 30 minutes. Nusa Penida, located in the southeast of Bali, is a true paradise waiting to be discovered. Upon your arrival, a friendly driver will be ready to guide you through the day\'s captivating itinerary. Your first destination is the mesmerizing Angel\'s Billabong, a natural wonder resembling a pristine pool nestled in the heart of nature. Take a refreshing swim, but exercise caution on the steps and heed your driver\'s recommendations. Next, we head to Broken Beach, a charming bay that was once a cave, now open to the sky, offering a unique and captivating scenery. Although inaccessible by land, the view from above is nothing short of breathtaking. Keep an eye out for the possibility of spotting giant manta rays gracefully gliding on the water\'s surface. Our journey continues to the renowned Kelingking Beach, famous for its stunning cliffs and the iconic hand-shaped mountain. This beach is not only one of the island\'s most famous attractions but also a favorite subject for photographers. We conclude the day at the pristine Crystal Beach, where white sands meet turquoise waters in perfect harmony. As the sun sets, you\'ll have the opportunity to relax and savor the beauty that surrounds you. This unforgettable experience concludes with a return boat trip to Bali from the Toya Pakeh port at 16:30, followed by a comfortable transfer to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-23\", \"text\": \"ETA 08.30 from Kusamba by The Angkal Fast Boat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sampalan Harbour Nusa Penida\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-23\", \"text\": \"ETD 16.00 to Kusamba by The Angkal Fast Boat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5191758,'618','Giovanny Martin Rodriguez',30508,207384,'Kusamba to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-23','2024-08-23','Jacob','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',600000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-23\", \"text\": \"ETA 16.30 from Nusa Penida by The Angkal Fast Boat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Kusamba Harbour\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-23\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 2\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5191764,'618','Giovanny Martin Rodriguez',30621,200788,'Standard Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-08-24','2024-08-26','Jacob','Tami',1,'Double',3445200.00,'The standard rooms in main Sal building are an oasis of tranquility, with garden and pool views they will offer you the comfort and eclectic beauty of Indonesian and Mediterranean inspired features. With comfortable beds and lovely mosquito nets, large bathrooms the charming standard rooms represent a great option for your stay. Room amenities; Wireless Internet Access, Air-conditioning, Mini Bar, Safety Box. Located in the stunning Bukit region, this intimate eco boutique resort is one of the best kept secrets in Bali, offering you the best service and beautiful amenities such as our gorgeous swimming pools.',NULL,'Honeymooners','{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5191778,'618','Giovanny Martin Rodriguez',30508,212543,'Uluwatu to Seminyak','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-26','2024-08-26','Jacob','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',300000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-26\", \"text\": \"Gg. Mertasari, Pecatu, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361\", \"time\": \"12:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sal Secret Spot\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-26\", \"text\": \"Jl. Petitenget, Kerobokan Kelod, Kec. Kuta Utara, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"The Kayana Seminyak Bali\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5191793,'618','Giovanny Martin Rodriguez',31003,203149,'Pool Villa (One Bedroom Villa with Private Swimming Pool)','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-26','2024-08-29','Jacob','Tami',1,'Double',14580000.00,'At 180 sqm villa size, the Kayana offers Eleven exclusive of One Bedroom Pool Villas each of which comes with 7-metre private swimming pool. With the same seclusion and luxurious standards as the deluxe villas.',NULL,'Honeymooners','{\"date\": \"2024-08-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5191795,'618','Giovanny Martin Rodriguez',30508,207270,'Seminyak to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-29','2024-08-29','Jacob','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',240000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-29\", \"text\": \"Jl. Petitenget, Kerobokan Kelod, Kec. Kuta Utara, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361\", \"time\": \"11:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"The Kayana Seminyak Bali\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-29\", \"text\": \"ETD 14.20 by Super Air Jet IU735 to Jakarta on 29 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"I Gusti Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5192406,'620','Dhimant Patel',31158,204473,'VIP Service Fast Track International Arrival by Galih (Not Inc. VOA)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-20','2024-07-20','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Person (1)',1008000.00,'Arrival International: Pick up at before immigration area.',NULL,'Your personal assistant will be waiting for you before the Visa-on-Arrival desk and the immigration area (near transfer desk/duty-free plaza), holding a sign of your name. They will assist you with during all arrival processes, including handling your visas and other essential documents as well as VoA (if prepaid), fast assistance at immigration counters, assistance through customs clearance, and help with the luggage. Lastly, the assistant will take you to meet the person who will pick you up at the airport, or help you find a taxi.','{\"date\": \"2024-07-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5192697,'621','Matteo Fornasari',30508,202890,'Mount Batur Sunrise Trekking Tour','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-26','2024-07-26','Nicholas','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',1200000.00,'Enjoy trek or climb Mount Batur and see the sunrise from the top of Batur Volcano. The Batur Volcano is one of the sacred mountain according to Hindu believe. We will get in ahead of schedule morning around 02.00 am depend the area of you stay, and afterward we specifically going to Mount Batur starting point. Starting in the dark under starlight sky, you will be guided to ascend the slope of Mount Batur. You will approach the peak of Mount Batur (1717 meters) at about 06.00 am. While waiting for the sunrise you will have a simple breakfast and hot coffee or tea served by your guide in Mount Batur. Witness the breathtaking sunrise overlooking the majestic view of Lake Batur and Mount Rinjani. After witnessing the sunrise, continue for our descent, at about 9 am, you will be arriving at the finishing point.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-26\", \"text\": \"Doni House & Villa, G7HH+V87, Tegallalang, Kec. Tegallalang, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80561\", \"time\": \"02:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-26\", \"text\": \"Doni House & Villa, G7HH+V87, Tegallalang, Kec. Tegallalang, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80561\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5192733,'502','Mr. David Esteso Villar',33113,218703,'Upper Flow Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-10-03','2024-10-05','Melysa','Praba',1,'Double',3840000.00,NULL,NULL,'Honeymooners','{\"date\": \"2024-10-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5192738,'235','Cynthia Cleveland',30571,202567,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-28','2024-08-29','Rendy','Wiwik',1,'Single',1372000.00,'Located at the Second Floor, 35 sqm comfort living with a touch of Balinese style featuring completed fitting, Cable TV, a fancy bathroom comprises rain shower and good quality amenities. Also dedicated Wi-Fi Access to complete your day.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5192852,'622','Mr. Andrea Aristo',31015,203232,'3D2N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Ijen Tour Package drop Bali','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-03','2024-08-05','Jacob','Praba',2,'Persons (2)',8880000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-03\", \"text\": \"ETA 21:20PM by Citilink QG726 from Jakarta\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Juanda International Airport Surabaya\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-05\", \"text\": \"Umaya Villa Ubud Jl. Nyuh Bojog No.34, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5192854,'622','Mr. Andrea Aristo',31196,204658,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-03','2024-08-04','Jacob','Praba',1,'Double',1428000.00,'Room type deluxe, with spacious room 3,41 m x 6,09 m and have type bed king size or twin bed. This type of room is available on the 2nd, 3rd and 4th floors and has of the hills view.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5192855,'622','Mr. Andrea Aristo',30803,202852,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-04','2024-08-05','Jacob','Praba',1,'Double',840000.00,'At 25 sqm of room size with 46 rooms available. This smart room category is more contemporary in appearance and comes with its own terrace or balcony. Minimalist furnishings are balanced by a neutral decor to soothe the senses and ensure restful slumber. Including a double bed (king or queen) or 2 single beds (twin) with maximum capacity of 2 adults + 1 child or 3 adults. The en-suite bathroom features a modern shower cubicle enclosed in glass together with a marble vanity.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5192859,'622','Mr. Andrea Aristo',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route (Taman Ayun-Jatiluwih-Ulun Danu Bratan-Tanah Lot)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-06','2024-08-06','Jacob','Praba',2,'Persons (2)',1872000.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-06\", \"text\": \"Umaya Villa Ubud Jl. Nyuh Bojog No.34, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-06\", \"text\": \"Umaya Villa Ubud Jl. Nyuh Bojog No.34, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5192871,'622','Mr. Andrea Aristo',30508,215968,'1D Bali Tour (Kanto Lampo Waterfall - Tibumana Waterfall - Tirta Empul - Pura Gunung Kawi)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-07','2024-08-07','Jacob','Praba',2,'Persons (2)',2160000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-07\", \"text\": \"Umaya Villa Ubud Jl. Nyuh Bojog No.34, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-07\", \"text\": \"Umaya Villa Ubud Jl. Nyuh Bojog No.34, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5192877,'622','Mr. Andrea Aristo',30508,202894,'Kehen Temple - Pengelipuran - Tukad Cepung Waterfall','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-08','2024-08-08','Jacob','Praba',2,'Persons (2)',1680000.00,'Our wonderful tour starts from Kehen Temple. It is an ancient Hindu temple complex boasting unique architectural features. The staircases reaching from the ground to temple courtyard are carved sandstone mythical animal and Balinese folklore figure statues and also the central vestibule. The temple’s walls are also ornate with Chinese porcelain plates, which are a tribute to the historical relations between the local Bali kingdom and China. Afterwards, we continue to Penglipuran, a village that succeeded in preserving its 75-hectare bamboo forest located in the northern part of the village. Members of this village have a strong commitment to the system of \'Ayahan Desa\' - a philosophy committed to respecting the land on which the village stands. To concludes the day, we stop by at Tukad Cepung Waterfall. Well-guarded by the circular cliffs, this waterfall is difficult to locate for the first time visitor. The circular cliffs give you the feeling of being in a cave, while the open sky right from where the waterfall emerges, gives you the most enchanting view. The sunlight falls on the glistering waterfall creating a rainbow, which feels as though it is projected right up to you. If you have never seen water flowing from the sky, then this would be your chance! After spending your time there, we go back to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": \"Umaya Villa Ubud Jl. Nyuh Bojog No.34, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": \"Umaya Villa Ubud Jl. Nyuh Bojog No.34, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5192900,'622','Mr. Andrea Aristo',30508,202893,'Lempuyang Temple Tour (Goa Lawah - Pura Lempuyang - Tirta Gangga - Tenganan)','Confirmed','C2I-BALI11',1,'2024-08-09','2024-08-09','Jacob','Praba',2,'Persons (2)',1920000.00,'At the agreed time, our guide will pick you up to start the tour in the eastern part of Bali. The first place you will visit is Goa Lawah Temple. Goa Lawah Temple consists of two names, \"Goa\" which means cave and \"Lawah\" which means bat. Several thousand bats are flying in the cave as the name suggests. With the lights fading as you go deeper inside the cave, it gives off a very strange atmosphere. From Goa Lawah, we continue our way to Lempuyang Temple. Upon arrival, the temple will greet you with its gratifying panorama that extends into infinity. On a clear, sunny day, you\'ll be able to gaze out over the mountains, Amlapura city, and Mount Agung, an incredibly magnificent sight that\'s beautiful beyond words. This portrait of heaven is beautifully framed by the Gapura Candi Bentar (the gate of the temple). Our journey continues to visit Tirta Gangga. The site is a paradise surrounded by water, with all the pools decorated with unusual statues. With its seclusion and a view of the surrounding rice paddies, Tirta Gangga is a wonderful place. At the end of the trip we go to Tenganan Village, the most famous Bali Agas (the “original” Bali people) in the city. With its characteristics, the city village is arranged in parallel along the wide main road paved with rows of cobblestones. In Tenganan, women still weave the famous Kamben Geringsing, or \"burnt cloth,\" which has the power to immunize the wearer against evil. We take a close look at what they do in their daily lives in a traditional lifestyle. From Tenganan, we will transfer you to the hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": \"Umaya Villa Ubud Jl. Nyuh Bojog No.34, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": \"Umaya Villa Ubud Jl. Nyuh Bojog No.34, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5192909,'622','Mr. Andrea Aristo',30508,207379,'Ubud to Padang Bai','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-10','2024-08-10','Jacob','Praba',1,'Persons (2)',600000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": \"Umaya Villa Ubud Jl. Nyuh Bojog No.34, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": \"ETD 08:30AM by Gili Gili Fastboat to Gili Trawangan\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Padang Bai Harbour\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5192919,'617','Marc Urgell Olle',30783,213061,'Transfer from Semarang Airport to Yogyakarta Hotel','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-28','2024-08-28','Nicholas','Febrina',1,'Per Car',960000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-28\", \"text\": \"ETA in Semarang at 11:25 by Batik Air ID6303 from Pangkalan Bun on 28 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Semarang Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-28\", \"text\": \"Jl. Prawirotaman 2 No.613, Brontokusuman, Mergangsan, Yogyakarta 55153. Phone: +62274 413888\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Adhisthana Hotel\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5192933,'622','Mr. Andrea Aristo',30508,207390,'Transfer In Nusa Penida','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-11','2024-08-11','Jacob','Praba',1,'Persons (2)',240000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-11\", \"text\": \"ETA 16:40 by BlueWater Express from Gili Trawangan\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Buyuk Harbour Nusa Penida\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-11\", \"text\": \"Dbelish Village and Resto Jl. Bunga mekar, desa bunga mekar, kec. Nusa Penida\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Nusa Penida\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5192936,'617','Marc Urgell Olle',30783,201659,'Borobudur Temple - Prambanan Temple','Confirmed','C2I-JAVA17',1,'2024-08-29','2024-08-29','Nicholas','Febrina',2,'Persons (2)',3840000.00,'You will be picked up early morning at the hotel at the indicated time and we will begin our wonderful day! Sunrise over the great stupa… We will arrive at Borobudur Temple sometime before sunrise. Prepare yourself for an amazing scenery with many faces of Buddha enlightened with the sunlight. Feel the calm breeze in this peaceful morning. Borobudur is the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. After sunrise, we will tour the temple, observing hundreds of centuries-old Buddha statues and how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically, it was made during the relatively brief Shailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC. It is under constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighboring Merapi volcano have produced during its history. The world heritage… Afterwards, we will go towards Prambanan, the temple of Hinduists which had been classified as a World Heritage Site by UNESCO since 1991. This temple was completed around the year 856 to commemorate the return of Shailendra dynasty of Central Java. Take your time to admire each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the perched stones gives off in this set of more than 200 Hinduist smaller temples. They are dedicated to the Trimurti, the expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the Destroyer. After this day that you will never forget, we will take you back to your hotel.',NULL,'FD Tour Borobudur Temple - Prambanan Temple, with Spanish speaking guide','{\"date\": \"2024-08-29\", \"text\": \"Jl. Prawirotaman 2 No.613, Brontokusuman, Mergangsan, Yogyakarta 55153. Phone: +62274 413888\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Adhisthana Hotel\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-29\", \"text\": \"Jl. Prawirotaman 2 No.613, Brontokusuman, Mergangsan, Yogyakarta 55153. Phone: +62274 413888\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Adhisthana Hotel\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5192959,'573','Elena María Duran Agosto 2024',31322,218317,'Suite room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-13','2024-08-14','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',4440000.00,'Munduk Tentrem offers four (4) Deluxe Tentrem Room has 180 panoramic view modern replicas of the traditional Javanese styled wooden house. Every room enjoys extensive views of the surrounding hills and the bay view. Fitted with a king size master bedroom suite and two additional bedrooms with twin beds (convertible to create a king size bed). This room can accommodate up to 2 guests.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5193037,'590','Marta Vara Espuga',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-04','2024-08-05','Melysa','Febrina',2,'Double',1568000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Roundtrip airport transfers. Flight details: ETA 17:35 by Turkish Airlines TK56 from Istanbul on 04 Aug ETD 08:25 by Super Air Jet IU732 to Denpasar on 05 Aug Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-08-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5193539,'622','Mr. Andrea Aristo',30508,207112,'1D Nusa Penida West Tour','Confirmed','C2I-BALI19',1,'2024-08-12','2024-08-12','Jacob','Praba',2,'Persons (2)',1020000.00,'Today, embark on a unique adventure as you explore the enchanting Nusa Penida, a neighboring island of Bali. Your day begins with a convenient hotel pick-up, followed by a journey to the Sanur port where a fast boat awaits to transport you to Nusa Penida in just 30 minutes. Nusa Penida, located in the southeast of Bali, is a true paradise waiting to be discovered. Upon your arrival, a friendly driver will be ready to guide you through the day\'s captivating itinerary. Your first destination is the mesmerizing Angel\'s Billabong, a natural wonder resembling a pristine pool nestled in the heart of nature. Take a refreshing swim, but exercise caution on the steps and heed your driver\'s recommendations. Next, we head to Broken Beach, a charming bay that was once a cave, now open to the sky, offering a unique and captivating scenery. Although inaccessible by land, the view from above is nothing short of breathtaking. Keep an eye out for the possibility of spotting giant manta rays gracefully gliding on the water\'s surface. Our journey continues to the renowned Kelingking Beach, famous for its stunning cliffs and the iconic hand-shaped mountain. This beach is not only one of the island\'s most famous attractions but also a favorite subject for photographers. We conclude the day at the pristine Crystal Beach, where white sands meet turquoise waters in perfect harmony. As the sun sets, you\'ll have the opportunity to relax and savor the beauty that surrounds you. This unforgettable experience concludes with a return boat trip to Bali from the Toya Pakeh port at 16:30, followed by a comfortable transfer to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-12\", \"text\": \"Dbelish Village and Resto Jl. Bunga mekar, desa bunga mekar, kec. Nusa penida\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Nusa Penida\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-12\", \"text\": \"Dbelish Village and Resto Jl. Bunga mekar, desa bunga mekar, kec. Nusa penida\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Nusa Penida\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5193541,'623','Anna Arago & Party (4)',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-08-18','2024-08-20','Jacob','Eddy',2,'Double',3360000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. ETA : 18 AUG 07.40am QR 958 by Qatar Airways From Doha ETD : 20 AUG 06.00 to Pangkalanbun ID6202 by Batik Air PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup & Drop off Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": \"ETA : 18 AUG 07.40am QR 958 by Qatar Airways From Doha\", \"time\": \"07:40\", \"locality\": \"AIRPORT JAKARTA\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-20\", \"text\": \"ETD : 20 AUG 06.00 to Pangkalanbun ID6202 by Batik Air\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"AIRPORT JAKARTA\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5193544,'623','Anna Arago & Party (4)',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-08-20','2024-08-22','Jacob','Eddy',4,'Persons (4)',14880000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-20\", \"text\": \"ETA : 20 AUG 0715 From Jakarta ID6202 by Batik Air\", \"time\": \"07:15\", \"locality\": \"AIPORT PANGKALANBUN\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-22\", \"text\": \"ETD : 22 AUG 1025 to Semarang ID6303 by Batik Air\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5193555,'623','Anna Arago & Party (4)',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-24','2024-08-24','Jacob','Eddy',4,'Persons (4-6)',3360000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": \"ETA : 24 AUG 1215 From Yogyakarta JT3560 by Lion Air\", \"time\": \"12:15\", \"locality\": \"AIRPORT DENPASAR\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": \"ROYAL CASA GANESHA \\\"ADDRESS : Jl. A.A. Gede Rai No.88, Lodtunduh, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571, Indonesia Phone : +62361 8493577 | Whatsapp: +62813-3750-4252\\\"\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5193557,'623','Anna Arago & Party (4)',30771,201374,'Suite Room','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-08-24','2024-08-28','Jacob','Eddy',2,'Double',21120000.00,'Traveling with friends or loved ones will be an experience to remember, especially when you’re staying at our Suite Room. The bathtube will be the perfect rendezvous spot. At 84,6 m2 room size, a spacious room with a balcony offering views of rice fields and the Infinity Pool. It includes a seating area, dining table, wardrobe, and private bathroom with a bathtub.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5193559,'623','Anna Arago & Party (4)',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route (Templo Taman Ayun - Jatiluwih - Templo Ulun Danu Bratan - Tanah Lot )','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-25','2024-08-25','Jacob','Eddy',4,'Persons (4)',2832000.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-25\", \"text\": \"ROYAL CASA GANESHA \\\"ADDRESS : Jl. A.A. Gede Rai No.88, Lodtunduh, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571, Indonesia Phone : +62361 8493577 | Whatsapp: +62813-3750-4252\\\"\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-25\", \"text\": \"ROYAL CASA GANESHA \\\"ADDRESS : Jl. A.A. Gede Rai No.88, Lodtunduh, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571, Indonesia Phone : +62361 8493577 | Whatsapp: +62813-3750-4252\\\"\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5193562,'622','Mr. Andrea Aristo',30508,207391,'Transfer Out Nusa Penida','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-13','2024-08-13','Jacob','Praba',1,'Persons (2)',240000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": \"Dbelish Village and Resto Jl. Bunga mekar, desa bunga mekar, kec. Nusa penida\", \"time\": \"13:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Nusa Penida\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": \"ETD 14:30PM by The Angkal Fastboat to Sanur\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Banjar Nyuh Harbour Nusa Penida\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5193564,'623','Anna Arago & Party (4)',30508,202894,'Templo Kehen – Panglipuran Village – Kintamani','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-26','2024-08-26','Jacob','Eddy',4,'Persons (4)',2448000.00,'Our wonderful tour starts from Kehen Temple. It is an ancient Hindu temple complex boasting unique architectural features. The staircases reaching from the ground to temple courtyard are carved sandstone mythical animal and Balinese folklore figure statues and also the central vestibule. The temple’s walls are also ornate with Chinese porcelain plates, which are a tribute to the historical relations between the local Bali kingdom and China. Afterwards, we continue to Penglipuran, a village that succeeded in preserving its 75-hectare bamboo forest located in the northern part of the village. Members of this village have a strong commitment to the system of \'Ayahan Desa\' - a philosophy committed to respecting the land on which the village stands. To concludes the day, we stop by at Tukad Cepung Waterfall. Well-guarded by the circular cliffs, this waterfall is difficult to locate for the first time visitor. The circular cliffs give you the feeling of being in a cave, while the open sky right from where the waterfall emerges, gives you the most enchanting view. The sunlight falls on the glistering waterfall creating a rainbow, which feels as though it is projected right up to you. If you have never seen water flowing from the sky, then this would be your chance! After spending your time there, we go back to your hotel.','Templo Kehen – Panglipuran Village – Kintamani',NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-26\", \"text\": \"ROYAL CASA GANESHA \\\"ADDRESS : Jl. A.A. Gede Rai No.88, Lodtunduh, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571, Indonesia Phone : +62361 8493577 | Whatsapp: +62813-3750-4252\\\"\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-26\", \"text\": \"ROYAL CASA GANESHA \\\"ADDRESS : Jl. A.A. Gede Rai No.88, Lodtunduh, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571, Indonesia Phone : +62361 8493577 | Whatsapp: +62813-3750-4252\\\"\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5193567,'623','Anna Arago & Party (4)',30508,207262,'Ubud to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-28','2024-08-28','Jacob','Eddy',4,'Persons (4-6)',3360000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-28\", \"text\": \"ROYAL CASA GANESHA \\\"ADDRESS : Jl. A.A. Gede Rai No.88, Lodtunduh, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571, Indonesia Phone : +62361 8493577 | Whatsapp: +62813-3750-4252\\\"\", \"time\": \"04:30\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-28\", \"text\": \"ETD : 28 AUG 0800 To Labuan Bajo ID6333 by Batik Air\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"AIRPORT DENPASAR\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5193577,'623','Anna Arago & Party (4)',31083,212380,'3D2N LOB Rinca - Padar - Komodo Island Tour (Base 1N Boat & 1N Hotel ) (Medium Standard B. - Purisar','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-28','2024-08-30','Jacob','Eddy',4,'Persons (4-5)',41688000.00,'TOUR ITINERARY Highlights: Menjarite, Kelor, Kalong, Rinca, Padar, Komodo island, Pink Beach, Taka Makassar, Manta Point, Kanawa, Batu Cermin Mirror Cave DAY 1 : DENPASAR - LABUAN BAJO - MENJARITE - PADAR - KELOR - KALONG ISLAND Arrival at Komodo Airport in Labuan Bajo west Flores, meeting service with our tour guide and transfer to the pier of Labuan Bajo for Rinca Island. It’s about 2 hours sail to the island of Komodo Dragon, stop at Menjarite island for snorkeling then continue to Rinca island-the Island of Komodo dragon, you will find not just e Dragons but also many wild animals like, deer, wild buffalo, long-tailed macaque and wild pig also numerous of birds. Keep your eyes look up as sometime you will find the young Komodo dragons on the trees. A local ranger will lead you through this natural preservation. Late afternoon sailing directly to Kalong Rinca Island to see the hundreds of fling foxes set out from the mangrove tree at 06-07 pm, the lovely sunset from the boat trip really enjoyable here. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Boat Cabin Air Conditioning DAY 2 : KALONG - PADAR - KOMODO - PINK BEACH - MANTA POINT - TAKA MAKASSAR - LABUAN BAJO After having breakfast in your boat, heading to Padar Island, taking trek to Padar Island until having the top view point to get breathtaking scenery of three bays around, Padar Island hike in Komodo has some of the most amazing views in Indonesia, trek to downhill and back to the Boat for sailing directly to Loh Liang – the Ranger station in Komodo Island. By passing through many small islands, After registering start to take basic trekking to see the GIANT RIZARD / KOMODO DRAGON and other wild animals as: Timor deer, wild pig, wild chicken and many variously of tropical bird. Please keep your look at any directions as sometimes you will also find young Komodo dragon hanging over the trees. A local ranger will be led you during the trek. Return to the boat on to Pink beach for snorkeling, swimming and relaxing. It is really spectacular and unspoiled coral reef and many color fish. This is one of best side for snorkeling diving. Sail toward MANTA POINT to exploring Huge Mantas by snorkeling even watching from your boat trip (can’t be guaranteed if weather is not good, like wave and current are strongly) visit also the taka Makaasar its really tiny island with white sand beach really enjoyable to relaxing or beach walking then heading to Labuan bajo for overnight and dinner at above hotel list option. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner DAY 3 : LABUAN BAJO - DENPASAR After breakfast taking your next excursion with visiting local marke and Batu Cermin (Mirror Stone) Cave. The grotto is 75 by 75 meters large, and contains stalactites and stalagmites. Some tunnels are narrow and dark but in others sunlight falls, then process to the airport for flight to Denpasar or to your next destination. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Attention: The itinerary is subject to change due to the weather, tide level and operating conditions without prior notice.',NULL,'28 - 29 AUG SLEEP AT MEDIUM STANDART BOAT (4 PERSON) 29 - 30 AUG SLEEP AT (PURI SARI HOTEL – (2DBL) SUPERIOR ROOM','{\"date\": \"2024-08-28\", \"text\": \"ETA : 28 AUG 0910 From Denpasar ID6333 by Batik Air\", \"time\": \"09:10\", \"locality\": \"AIRPORT LABUAN BAJO\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-30\", \"text\": \"ETD : 30 AUG 1200 To Lombok ID6328 by Batik Air\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"AIRPORT LABUAN BAJO\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5193587,'624','Brent Imschoot',30845,201963,'Standard Huts Garden View','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-09-17','2024-09-20','Purnomo','Komang',1,'Double',4284000.00,'Simple yet charming, each of our rustic garden huts is the perfect sanctuary for two. With it\'s spacious room at 12 square meters with 12 units available. Enjoy the comfort of air conditioning inside or unwind on your private veranda and listen to bird songs in a nature-filled tropical setting. Take a cool shower under the sky in the en-suite open-air bathroom, and get a good night’s sleep on the comfortable queen bed with a mosquito net to keep those pesky bugs away.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5193588,'544','Abyssworld Group 04-15 November 202420234949',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-15','2024-11-16','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Single',784000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Guarantee early check-in time at 10.00. Check-out time is 12:00. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-11-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5193627,'622','Mr. Andrea Aristo',30508,207269,'Sanur to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-13','2024-08-13','Jacob','Praba',1,'Persons (2)',300000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": \"ETA 15:20PM by The Angkal Fastboat from Penida\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sanur Harbour\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": \"ETD 21:05PM by Super Air Jet IU747 to Jakarta\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5193628,'624','Brent Imschoot',33117,218731,'Suite Pool View','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-09-15','2024-09-17'