8 sqm with private balcony for a sophisticated Ubud getaway. Interiors feature extensive use of wood and fine Indonesian textiles and art, lending an understated elegance to the space. Featuring a private balcony, this room includes a flat-screen TV and an en-suite bathroom with a bathtub and a shower, and many more.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5198358,'645','COMPANY CASTELLO / ANNA',30508,215968,'1D Bali Tour (TEGALALANG – TANAH LOT )','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-19','2024-08-19','Guio','Komang',5,'Person (1)',3360000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": \"Komaneka Bisma Ubud, Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 971933\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": \"Melia Bali Nusa Dua, Jl. Kw. Nusa Dua Resort Itdc Lot 1, Jl. Nusa Dua, Benoa, Kec. Kuta Sel., Bali, 80363 Telepon: (0361) 771510\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Nusa Dua\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5198359,'645','COMPANY CASTELLO / ANNA',30579,212708,'Premium Room Garden View','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-08-19','2024-08-23','Guio','Komang',2,'Double + Twin',27552000.00,'Tropical accommodation to enhance the enjoyment of a Balinese paradise experience. With a double four-poster bed, a desk in polished wood and a full bathroom with a bathtub or shower. Enjoy the garden views from your furnished terrace.',NULL,'Include Dinner in Hotel on 19,20,21,22 August','{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5198581,'634','David Alegrete Bernal',30508,207390,'Transfer In Nusa Penida','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-10','2024-08-10','Rendy','Praba',1,'Persons (2)',240000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": \"ETA 16:50PM by EkaJaya Fastboat from Gili AIr\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Banjar Nyuh Harbour Penida\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": \"Banjar Penage, Sakti, Kec. Nusa Penida\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"BB Resort Villa and Spa Nusa Penida\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5198594,'650','Brady Kerry Chace',30719,201080,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-11-24','2024-11-26','Ayu','Praba',1,'Twin',1904000.00,'Swiss-Belhotel Sorong boast 126 guest rooms in Sorong with all the comforts you would expect from an international chain of four-star hotels in Sorong. Enjoy 37-inch LED TVs, cable channels, high-speed internet access and a full range of other amenities that will make your stay here the most comfortable one possible.',NULL,'Check-in time 14.00 Check-out time 12.00 Early check-in is subject to availability upon arrival.','{\"date\": \"2024-11-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5198606,'645','COMPANY CASTELLO / ANNA',33140,218856,'Deluxe Ocean Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-16','2024-08-17','Guio','Komang',1,'Double + Twin',2040640.00,'Overlooking of sea, our Deluxe Ocean Room located on the second floor, this 35.45 sqm room feature a comfortable king size bed and private balcony.',NULL,'Activity Seing Dolphin on 17 August 2024','{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5198627,'645','COMPANY CASTELLO / ANNA',30508,207268,'Nusa Dua to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-23','2024-08-23','Guio','Komang',1,'Persons (1-3)',280000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-23\", \"text\": \"Melia Bali Nusa Dua , Jl. Kw. Nusa Dua Resort Itdc Lot 1, Jl. Nusa Dua, Benoa, Kec. Kuta Sel., Bali, 80363 Telepon: (0361) 771510\", \"time\": \"15:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Nusa Dua\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-23\", \"text\": \"ETD : 19.40 by EMIRATES EK369 to Dubai on 23 August 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"International Ngurah Rai Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5198638,'634','David Alegrete Bernal',30914,202451,'Deluxe Pool Access','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-13','2024-08-14','Rendy','Praba',1,'Double',2820000.00,'At 51 sqm with king and twin size beds capacity of 2 (two) adults and 2 (two) child below 12 years old. Ideal for family or group of friends traveling together, the Deluxe Pool Access rooms allows guests a direct access from a private balcony to a communal pool shared with several other Deluxe Pool Access rooms, making it easy to have a refreshing swim.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5198957,'602','Mr. Francesc Dassis Martin Cuberto',30705,201147,'Premier Room Garden View','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-12','2024-09-13','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',1638000.00,'Get back to nature in one of our Premier Garden View suites. These spacious, light-filled rooms have beautiful Balinese double doors that can be closed to create a cool air-conditioned space or opened to merge indoor and outdoor living. The balconies overlook the resort’s lush gardens, which are awash in tropical flowers and foliage.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5198960,'602','Mr. Francesc Dassis Martin Cuberto',30508,215968,'1D Bali Tour (Tirta empul - Uluwatu - Kecak Dance)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-11','2024-09-11','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',1920000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-11\", \"text\": \"The Artini Dijiwa, Jl. Raya Pengosekan Ubud, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 972385\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-11\", \"text\": \"The Artini Dijiwa, Jl. Raya Pengosekan Ubud, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 972385\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5198963,'602','Mr. Francesc Dassis Martin Cuberto',30508,215968,'HD Bali Tour (Monkey Forest - Goa Gajah)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-13','2024-09-13','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',1680000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-13\", \"text\": \"The Artini Dijiwa Ubud, The Artini Dijiwa Ubud Jl. Raya Pengosekan Ubud, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-13\", \"text\": \"ETD : 18.50 by Lion Air JT740 to Ujung Pandang on 13 Sept 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5198999,'602','Mr. Francesc Dassis Martin Cuberto',31106,203994,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-13','2024-09-14','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',810000.00,'Discover Makassar from a very comfortable room with a king-size bed (or two single beds), a practical desk with an executive chair, and a modern bathroom with an open shower. You will also really like the welcome minibar to start your stay as you deserve. Inside the room has flat-screen TV, high speed Wi-Fi, and refrigerator.',NULL,'Flights schedule : ETA : 20.15 by Lion Air JT740 from Denpasar on 13 Sept 2024 ETD : 0815 by Wings Air IW1350 to Palopo on 14 Sept 2024 \"Please consult time to transfer Airport upon check-in\"','{\"date\": \"2024-09-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5199010,'652','Barbara Krystyna Brzeska',30662,212912,'(Journaway) 7D6N Medan - Bukit Lawang - Brastagi - Lake Toba','Confirmed',NULL,7,'2024-11-30','2024-12-06','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Persons (2-3 / Double)',22348480.00,'Day-01 : AIRPORT/MEDAN - BUKIT LAWANG Arrival at Kualanamu International Airport Medan meet by our tour guide and then drive to Bukit Lawang with enroute stop at several plantations for rubber and oil palm. Arriving in Bukit Lawang check-in to hotel. Meals : - • Overnight at : Eco-lodge Bukit Lawang Cottages - Standard Room Day-02 : BUKIT LAWANG - LEUSER PARK TREKKING (B,L,D) After breakfast walking to the jungle to start a jungle trekking to explore the nature of Leuser National Park with its rich flora and fauna, there will be chances to see Orangutans on their own natural habitat and other kinds of animal such as Thomas-leaf monkeys, long tail macaque, gibbon, black gibbon and other kind of flora and fauna of this tropical rain-forest. Lunch and dinner provided. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner • Overnight at : Tent or Shelter in the jungle Day-03 : CONTINUE TREKKING - RETURN TO BUKIT LAWANG (TUBING) (B,L) After breakfast prepared by tour guide continue trekking, today is full day walking and explore the rain tropical forest with its wildlife living in their natural habitat. In mid-afternoon, we will make our way back by tubing in the river. At the end, we will return to the hotel for check-in. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch • Overnight at : Eco-lodge Bukit Lawang Cottages - Standard Room Day-04 : BUKIT LAWANG - BERASTAGI (B) After breakfast drive to Berastagi with enroute stop at Sembahe river, arriving in Berastagi visiting Lumbhini Park to see the replica of the Shwedagon pagoda, and visit at Fruit Market. In mid-afternoon check-in to hotel. Meals : Breakfast • Overnight at : Mikie Holiday Resort - Superior Room • Alternative : Hotel Sinabung Hills - Superior Room Day-05 : SIBAYAK VOLCANO HIKING - TRANSFER TO SAMOSIR/LAKE TOBA (B) At early morning (take away your Breakfast Box) and transferred to the slope of Sibayak Volcano and then start hiking to the top of the Sibayak Volcano, to go and back will spend about 3 hours. Arriving on its peak enjoy the scenic panorama of its surroundings and the sunrise (weather depends). After take a rest and enjoy its view, start trekking back to Berastagi and then continuing the drive head for Samosir Island in Lake Toba via TELE. En-route stop at : • Dokan (to see the traditional village of the Batak Karo tribe) • Sipisopiso Waterfall (from here you can admire the scenic view of the Lake Toba from its northern tip combined with the slender 90 meters high waterfall) • Tele (a nice place for over-viewing the lake from its western part) • Efrata (another beautiful waterfall found on the way to Samosir Island) • Lumban Suhi-suhi (to see the Tobanase traditional houses where we could observe also the women doing the weaving) In mid-afternoon arriving at Tuktuk area on Samosir and check-in to hotel. Meals : Breakfast • Overnight at : Tabo Cottages - Deluxe Room • Alternative : Samosir Villa - Deluxe Room Day-06: SAMOSIR EXCURSION - AIRPORT/MEDAN CITY (B) After breakfast we start for our fullday excursion by car in the interior of Samosir Island with en-route visits at : • Ambarita (to see the stone chairs and tables where once used as the execution site by the ancient tribal chieftains) • Aek Natonang (here we can see the small lake found of the top of Samosir Island and its panorama view) • Tomok (to see the old sarcophages belonged to former Sidabutar Kings and his descendants) At mid-day, we will return to the harbor to catch the 1 PM ferry back to Parapat (1 hour sailing duration). Arriving at Parapat harbour continue the driving directly to Medan via Pematang Siantar and Tebing Tinggi (about 5 hours driving time). We will drop you off at the airport for overnight at airport hotel and be ready for morning flight departure. Meals : Breakfast Overnight: Hotel Horison Sky Kualanamu - Deluxe Room Day-07 : DEPARTURE After an early breakfast, you will continue to the departure terminal for your flight. TOUR ENDS. Meals : Breakfast','- All the above prices are not valid during Super High Season period for Idul Fitri (01-20 April 2024), Christmas & New Year festive season (18 December 2024 - 08 January 2025). - Surcharge to be advised','Per confirmed program: Day-01: AIRPORT/MEDAN – BUKIT LAWANG Day-02: BUKIT LAWANG – GUNUNG LEUSER NATIONAL PARK TREKKING Day-03: CONTINUE TREKKING – RETURN TO BUKIT LAWANG Day-04: BUKIT LAWANG – BERASTAGI Day-05: SIBAYAK VOLCANO HIKING – TRANSFER TO SAMOSIR/LAKE TOBA Day-06: SAMOSIR EXCURSION – AIRPORT/MEDAN CITY Day-07: DEPARTURE MEDAN Accommodation based on 1 Double Room: 2 Nights at Bukit Lawang Eco-Lodge – Thomas Monkey Room 1 Night in Tent/shelter 1 Night Mikie Holiday Resort – Deluxe Room 1 Nights at Tabo Cottages – Deluxe Room 1 Night at Hotel Anara Sky Kualanamu – Deluxe Room Flights information: ETA: 08.30 by Batik Air Malaysia OD322 from Kuala Lumpur on 30 Nov ETD: 10.30 by Batik Air ID7147 to Singapore on 06 Dec','{\"date\": \"2024-11-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-12-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5199073,'653','Javier Maria Garcia Jimenez',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-25','2024-08-26','Guio','Tami',1,'Twin',784000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-08-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5199090,'653','Javier Maria Garcia Jimenez',30806,202002,'4D3N Borneo Orangutan & Reforestation Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO7',4,'2024-08-26','2024-08-29','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',13104000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN – KUMAI PORT – TANJUNG HARAPAN Your “Orangutan & Reforestation Tour” begins upon arrival at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan is Cape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : TANJUNG HARAPAN VILLAGE – PROBOSCIS TOUR – CAMP LEAKEY After an extraordinary breakfast, you go to visit the village inside the national park, named Tanjung Harapan Village. Here you will see the activities of the locals. After the visit, you will return to the klotok cruise up to the Sekonyer River. You will see nice vegetation around the river bank, including Nipa Palm, Pandanus, and some kinds of trees that are growing up around the river. See some wildlifes such as birds, Macaques, Proboscis Monkeys and Orangutans. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large monitor lizards. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. Note: The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. Meals : Breakfast – Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : PONDOK TANGGUI – CAMP LEAKEY – BOAT After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continue to add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After lunch, you will have the opportunity to repeat feeding camp at Camp Leaky. It is a unique opportunity to dedicate more time to your observation and to discover more wild animals, along with the Orangutans. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note: If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast – Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 4 : KUMAI PORT – PANGKALAN BUN Today we end our stay in the jungles of Borneo. Our “Orangutan & Reforestation Tour” is about to finish. In the early morning we will have breakfast on the boat, to then go to the port and in turn, be transferred to the airport. The boat departure will be at the latest at 10am, but we adapt to your flights if your flight leaves earlier in the morning. If you decide to take an afternoon flight, we can take you directly to the airport at 10 or if you want a city tour in the Arut village to drop you off at the airport later, it could be arranged at extra cost. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-26\", \"text\": \"ETA 07.15 by Batik Air ID6202 from Jakarta on 26 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pangkalan Bun Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-29\", \"text\": \"ETD 10.25 by Batik Air ID6303 to Semarang on 29 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5199093,'653','Javier Maria Garcia Jimenez',30783,218076,'6D5N Jogja-Merapi-Bromo-Ijen-Bali Overland / B. Gallery Prawirotaman (Deluxe)&Lereng Bromo (Deluxe)&','Confirmed',NULL,6,'2024-08-29','2024-09-03','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',24360000.00,'D1 Arrival at Yogyakarta International airport - Transfer to hotel D2 Borobudur temple incl. Mendut and Pawon temple - Merapi lava Tour Incl .Jeep D3 Yogjakarta City Tour visit Sultan Palace, Wateracstle and Bird Market - Prambanan temple D4 Jogja to Bromo drive - overnight in Bromo D5 Mt. Bromo Sunrise tour incl. Jeep - Transfer to Banyuwangi/Ijen Hotel for overnight D6 Mt. Ijen crater tour - transfer to Bali accross Ketapang - Gilimanuk harbour - drop at your hotel in Bali',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-29\", \"text\": \"ETA 11.25 by Batik Air ID6303 from Pangkalan Bun on 29 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Semarang International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-03\", \"text\": \"Jl. Suweta, Bentuyung Sakti, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Visesa Ubud Resort\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5199100,'653','Javier Maria Garcia Jimenez',30985,212179,'Jungle Suite Room with Private Balcony','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-09-03','2024-09-07','Guio','Tami',1,'Twin',8736000.00,'Escape the hustle and bustle of everyday life and immerse yourself in the beauty of nature with our Jungle Suite with Private Balcony. Located in the heart of the lush tropical rainforest, this Suite offers a unique opportunity to immerse yourself in nature while still enjoying all the comforts of modern living. The real highlight of this room category is the private balcony overlooking the jungle canopy. Relax in your own personal paradise as you listen to the sounds of nature, watch the birds playing in the trees, and breathe in the fresh air while taking in the breathtaking views.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5199104,'653','Javier Maria Garcia Jimenez',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-05','2024-09-05','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',1747200.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-05\", \"text\": \"Jl. Suweta, Bentuyung Sakti, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Visesa Ubud Resort\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5199105,'653','Javier Maria Garcia Jimenez',30508,202894,'Kehen Temple - Pengelipuran - Tukad Cepung Waterfall','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-06','2024-09-06','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',1568000.00,'Our wonderful tour starts from Kehen Temple. It is an ancient Hindu temple complex boasting unique architectural features. The staircases reaching from the ground to temple courtyard are carved sandstone mythical animal and Balinese folklore figure statues and also the central vestibule. The temple’s walls are also ornate with Chinese porcelain plates, which are a tribute to the historical relations between the local Bali kingdom and China. Afterwards, we continue to Penglipuran, a village that succeeded in preserving its 75-hectare bamboo forest located in the northern part of the village. Members of this village have a strong commitment to the system of \'Ayahan Desa\' - a philosophy committed to respecting the land on which the village stands. To concludes the day, we stop by at Tukad Cepung Waterfall. Well-guarded by the circular cliffs, this waterfall is difficult to locate for the first time visitor. The circular cliffs give you the feeling of being in a cave, while the open sky right from where the waterfall emerges, gives you the most enchanting view. The sunlight falls on the glistering waterfall creating a rainbow, which feels as though it is projected right up to you. If you have never seen water flowing from the sky, then this would be your chance! After spending your time there, we go back to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-06\", \"text\": \"Jl. Suweta, Bentuyung Sakti, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Visesa Ubud Resort\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5199106,'653','Javier Maria Garcia Jimenez',30508,202893,'Lempuyang Temple Tour','Confirmed','C2I-BALI11',1,'2024-09-07','2024-09-07','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',1792000.00,'At the agreed time, our guide will pick you up to start the tour in the eastern part of Bali. The first place you will visit is Goa Lawah Temple. Goa Lawah Temple consists of two names, \"Goa\" which means cave and \"Lawah\" which means bat. Several thousand bats are flying in the cave as the name suggests. With the lights fading as you go deeper inside the cave, it gives off a very strange atmosphere. From Goa Lawah, we continue our way to Lempuyang Temple. Upon arrival, the temple will greet you with its gratifying panorama that extends into infinity. On a clear, sunny day, you\'ll be able to gaze out over the mountains, Amlapura city, and Mount Agung, an incredibly magnificent sight that\'s beautiful beyond words. This portrait of heaven is beautifully framed by the Gapura Candi Bentar (the gate of the temple). Our journey continues to visit Tirta Gangga. The site is a paradise surrounded by water, with all the pools decorated with unusual statues. With its seclusion and a view of the surrounding rice paddies, Tirta Gangga is a wonderful place. At the end of the trip we go to Tenganan Village, the most famous Bali Agas (the “original” Bali people) in the city. With its characteristics, the city village is arranged in parallel along the wide main road paved with rows of cobblestones. In Tenganan, women still weave the famous Kamben Geringsing, or \"burnt cloth,\" which has the power to immunize the wearer against evil. We take a close look at what they do in their daily lives in a traditional lifestyle. From Tenganan, we will transfer you to the hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-07\", \"text\": \"Jl. Suweta, Bentuyung Sakti, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Visesa Ubud Resort\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-07\", \"text\": \"Jl. Raya Sengkidu, Sengkidu, Kec. Manggis, Kabupaten Karangasem, Bali 80801\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ramayana Candidasa\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5199109,'653','Javier Maria Garcia Jimenez',30508,202882,'The Mother Temple Besakih and Surrounding','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-08','2024-09-08','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',1724800.00,'The first destination is Kusamba Beach, it is one of the favorite places of interest in Bali which is famous with the beautiful beach, we can also meet a fish market in this place which is usually held between 10 am until 4 pm. Then we go to Goa Lawah, this is one of the favourite place to be visited, because here is a nature cave dwelt by thousands of tail bat located at north side from Jeroan/center of Goa Lawah Temple. Next we go to Bukit Jambul, it is strategically located beside of the main road from Denpasar to Besakih Temple and it is one of the tourist destinations that visited on Besakih Tour. It is situated in the plateau area which is blessed with the beautiful panorama of rice terrace and green coconuts three unfolding to the sea. After visit Bukit Jambul, we’ll continue to Besakih Temple is the biggest Hindu temple in Bali which the local people call Pura Besakih. It owns beautiful view from the top of temple area where we can see the wide nature panorama until to the ocean so that’s why this temple is many visited by tourists from all over the world. Then go to Kertagosa, This place also owns Taman Gili, a building floating or sees like floating because it is intentionally founded in the middle of a fish pond.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-08\", \"text\": \"Jl. Raya Sengkidu, Sengkidu, Kec. Manggis, Kabupaten Karangasem, Bali 80801\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ramayana Candidasa\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5199699,'653','Javier Maria Garcia Jimenez',30508,202897,'Uluwatu Temple and Kecak Dance','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-09','2024-09-09','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',1713600.00,'This half-day tour, is an exciting tour package to visit Padang-Padang Beach, Uluwatu Temple, the famous Balinese Hindu Temple in south part of Bali with breathtaking view of sunset and Indian Ocean. Uluwatu Temple is one of Balinese Hindu Temples located right on the petrifying hill with the crevasse exist in the right and left side. Uluwatu Temple is one of Sad Khayangan (6 biggest temple in Bali) owns magnificent view of the Indian Ocean and sunset as a backdrop. This temple is very amazing where the location is right on the narrow peninsula with deep seawater under it. This tour package is combined with the spectacular Balinese traditional dance performance of Kecak Dance. Balinese Kecak Dance is a spectacular traditional dance with the group of people playing this dance with fire game. It is very exciting and unique dance due to the sound of gamelan is not using the normal gamelan but use their mouth. The dancers make the compact choir with the exquisite dance movement that is one of this dance features. After the dance we returned back to the hotel or seafood restaurant in Jimbaran.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-09\", \"text\": \"Jl. Raya Sengkidu, Sengkidu, Kec. Manggis, Kabupaten Karangasem, Bali 80801\", \"time\": \"11:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ramayana Candidasa\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-09\", \"text\": \"Jl. Kartika Plaza No.127, Kuta, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"The Vira Bali Boutique Hotel & Suite\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5199705,'653','Javier Maria Garcia Jimenez',30556,202034,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-09-07','2024-09-09','Guio','Tami',1,'Twin',3628800.00,'Deluxe Room on ground floor - 3rd floor of Deluxe Room building are designed in contemporary Balinese interiors and have a private balcony / terrace facing the lush tropical garden / resort area.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5199706,'105','Kevin STECKLER',30508,218878,'Ubud to Kuta','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-30','2024-07-30','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Persons (1-3)',392000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-30\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in hotel lobby at the mentioned time.\", \"time\": \"12:00\", \"locality\": \"Royal Kamuela Villas & Suites Ubud\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"The Stones Entertainment Center Kuta\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5199712,'105','Kevin STECKLER',30508,207266,'Kuta to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-31','2024-07-31','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Persons (1-3)',280000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-07-31\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in hotel lobby at the mentioned time.\", \"time\": \"05:00\", \"locality\": \"The Stones Entertainment Center\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-31\", \"text\": \"ETD: 07.00 by Garuda Indonesia GA401 to Jakarta on 31 Jul\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Denpasar Airport\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5199713,'653','Javier Maria Garcia Jimenez',30571,202567,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-09','2024-09-10','Guio','Tami',1,'Twin',1204000.00,'Located at the Second Floor, 35 sqm comfort living with a touch of Balinese style featuring completed fitting, Cable TV, a fancy bathroom comprises rain shower and good quality amenities. Also dedicated Wi-Fi Access to complete your day.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5199717,'653','Javier Maria Garcia Jimenez',31083,212383,'3D2N LOB Rinca - Padar - Komodo Island Tour (Superior Standard B. - Purisari Hotel','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-09-10','2024-09-12','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2-3)',35246400.00,'TOUR ITINERARY Highlights: Menjarite, Kelor, Kalong, Rinca, Padar, Komodo Island, Pink Beach, Taka Makassar, Manta Point, Kanawa, Batu Cermin Mirror Cave DAY 1 : DENPASAR - LABUAN BAJO - MENJARITE - PADAR - KELOR - KALONG ISLAND Arrival at Komodo Airport in Labuan Bajo west Flores, meeting service with our tour guide and transfer to the pier of Labuan Bajo for Rinca Island. It’s about 2 hours sail to the island of Komodo Dragon, stop at Menjarite island for snorkeling then continue to Rinca island-the Island of Komodo dragon, you will find not just e Dragons but also many wild animals like, deer, wild buffalo, long-tailed macaque and wild pig also numerous of birds. Keep your eyes look up as sometime you will find the young Komodo dragons on the trees. A local ranger will lead you through this natural preservation. Late afternoon sailing directly to Kalong Rinca Island to see the hundreds of fling foxes set out from the mangrove tree at 06-07 pm, the lovely sunset from the boat trip really enjoyable here. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Boat Cabin Air Conditioning DAY 2 : KALONG - PADAR - KOMODO - PINK BEACH - MANTA POINT - TAKA MAKASSAR - LABUAN BAJO After having breakfast in your boat, heading to Padar Island, taking trek to Padar Island until having the top view point to get breathtaking scenery of three bays around, Padar Island hike in Komodo has some of the most amazing views in Indonesia, trek to downhill and back to the Boat for sailing directly to Loh Liang – the Ranger station in Komodo Island. By passing through many small islands, After registering start to take basic trekking to see the GIANT RIZARD / KOMODO DRAGON and other wild animals as: Timor deer, wild pig, wild chicken and many variously of tropical bird. Please keep your look at any directions as sometimes you will also find young Komodo dragon hanging over the trees. A local ranger will be led you during the trek. Return to the boat on to Pink beach for snorkeling, swimming and relaxing. It is really spectacular and unspoiled coral reef and many color fish. This is one of best side for snorkeling diving. Sail toward MANTA POINT to exploring Huge Mantas by snorkeling even watching from your boat trip (can’t be guaranteed if weather is not good, like wave and current are strongly) visit also the taka Makaasar its really tiny island with white sand beach really enjoyable to relaxing or beach walking then heading to Labuan bajo for overnight and dinner at above hotel list option. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner DAY 3 : LABUAN BAJO - DENPASAR After breakfast taking your next excursion with visiting local marke and Batu Cermin (Mirror Stone) Cave. The grotto is 75 by 75 meters large, and contains stalactites and stalagmites. Some tunnels are narrow and dark but in others sunlight falls, then process to the airport for flight to Denpasar or to your next destination. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Attention: The itinerary is subject to change due to the weather, tide level and operating conditions without prior notice.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-10\", \"text\": \"ETA 09.10 by Batik Air ID6333 from Denpasar on 10 Sep\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Komodo International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-12\", \"text\": \"ETD 09.50 by Batik Air ID6332 to Denpasar on 12 Sep\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5199719,'653','Javier Maria Garcia Jimenez',30508,212287,'Airport to Sanur','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-12','2024-09-12','Guio','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',280000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-12\", \"text\": \"ETA 11.05 by Batik Air ID6332 from Labuan Bajo on 12 Sep\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"I Gusti Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-12\", \"text\": \"Jl. Kusuma Sari No.1, Sanur, Denpasar Selatan, Kota Denpasar, Bali 80227\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"ARTOTEL Sanur - Bali\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5199723,'653','Javier Maria Garcia Jimenez',31024,203296,'Studio 30 Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-12','2024-09-13','Guio','Tami',1,'Twin',1064000.00,'Our 81 units Studio 30 Room with 30 sqm of room area, adopts kites as it\'s main concept. This room is a canvas that showcases thought-provoking artworks by some of the most relevant Bali-based contemporary artists. This air-conditioned studio features a 49\" inch LED TV, high speed internet Wi-Fi, 24 hours in-room service, iPod dock, dolce gusto coffee maker, a minibar, en-suite bathroom comes with a shower, a hairdryer, free toiletries, and many more.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5199725,'653','Javier Maria Garcia Jimenez',30508,207269,'Sanur to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-13','2024-09-13','Guio','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',280000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-13\", \"text\": \"Jl. Kusuma Sari No.1, Sanur, Denpasar Selatan, Kota Denpasar, Bali 80227\", \"time\": \"15:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"ARTOTEL Sanur - Bali\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-13\", \"text\": \"ETD 19.15 by Emirates EK7785 to Singapore on 13 Sep\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"I Gusti Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5200019,'654','Noemi Alcantara Gonzalez',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-13','2024-08-13','Guio','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',336000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": \"ETA 17.35 by Qatar QR962 from Doha on 13 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"I Gusti Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": \"Br. Tanggayuda, Kedewatan, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Komaneka at Tanggayuda\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5200030,'654','Noemi Alcantara Gonzalez',30508,215968,'Taman Ayun - Jatiluwih - Ulun Danu Temple - Leke Leke Waterfall','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-14','2024-08-14','Guio','Tami',2,'Person (1)',1792000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-14\", \"text\": \"Br. Tanggayuda, Kedewatan, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Komaneka at Tanggayuda\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5200049,'654','Noemi Alcantara Gonzalez',30508,215968,'Tanah Lot Temple','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-15','2024-08-15','Guio','Tami',2,'Person (1)',1680000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-15\", \"text\": \"Br. Tanggayuda, Kedewatan, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"14:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Komaneka at Tanggayuda\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5200055,'654','Noemi Alcantara Gonzalez',30508,202890,'Mount Batur Sunrise Trekking Tour','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-16','2024-08-16','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',1120000.00,'Enjoy trek or climb Mount Batur and see the sunrise from the top of Batur Volcano. The Batur Volcano is one of the sacred mountain according to Hindu believe. We will get in ahead of schedule morning around 02.00 am depend the area of you stay, and afterward we specifically going to Mount Batur starting point. Starting in the dark under starlight sky, you will be guided to ascend the slope of Mount Batur. You will approach the peak of Mount Batur (1717 meters) at about 06.00 am. While waiting for the sunrise you will have a simple breakfast and hot coffee or tea served by your guide in Mount Batur. Witness the breathtaking sunrise overlooking the majestic view of Lake Batur and Mount Rinjani. After witnessing the sunrise, continue for our descent, at about 9 am, you will be arriving at the finishing point.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": \"Br. Tanggayuda, Kedewatan, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"02:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Komaneka at Tanggayuda\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-16\", \"text\": \"Pantai Suluban St, Pecatu, South Kuta, Badung Regency, Bali 80361\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Uluwatu Surf Villas\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5200096,'655','Mr. Stuart Alan Burton',30680,200914,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-12','2024-11-13','Ayu','Eddy',1,'Double',0.00,'Enjoy our spacious elegant deluxe room with 40 m2 of room size. Enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, hot and cold shower, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup & Drop Off Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-11-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5200100,'655','Mr. Stuart Alan Burton',30680,200914,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-12-05','2024-12-06','Ayu','Eddy',1,'Double',960000.00,'Enjoy our spacious elegant deluxe room with 40 m2 of room size. Enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, hot and cold shower, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup & Drop Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-12-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-12-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5200162,'559','Christian Lorente Family',31158,204473,'VIP Service Fast Track International Arrival (Not Inc. VOA)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-06','2024-08-06','Guio','Febrina',4,'Person (1)',4320000.00,'Arrival International: Pick up at before immigration area.',NULL,'Flight detail: ETA: 17.35h by Turkish Airline TK56 from Istanbul on 06 Aug Meet up with FM7 Staff Fast Track International Arrival Your personal assistant will be waiting for you before the Visa-on-Arrival desk and the immigration area (near transfer desk/duty-free plaza), holding a sign of your name. They will assist you with during all arrival processes, including handling your visas and other essential documents as well as VoA (if prepaid), fast assistance at immigration counters, assistance through customs clearance, and help with the luggage. Lastly, the assistant will take you to meet the person who will pick you up at the airport, or help you find a taxi.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5200175,'654','Noemi Alcantara Gonzalez',30508,212545,'Uluwatu to Sanur','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-17','2024-08-17','Guio','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',280000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": \"Pantai Suluban St, Pecatu, South Kuta, Badung Regency, Bali 80361\", \"time\": \"05:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Uluwatu Surf Villas\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": \"ETD 07.30 to Nusa Penida by Maruti Fast Boat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sanur Harbour\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5200176,'654','Noemi Alcantara Gonzalez',30508,207112,'1D Nusa Penida West Tour','Confirmed','C2I-BALI19',1,'2024-08-17','2024-08-17','Guio','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',952000.00,'Today, embark on a unique adventure as you explore the enchanting Nusa Penida, a neighboring island of Bali. Your day begins with a convenient hotel pick-up, followed by a journey to the Sanur port where a fast boat awaits to transport you to Nusa Penida in just 30 minutes. Nusa Penida, located in the southeast of Bali, is a true paradise waiting to be discovered. Upon your arrival, a friendly driver will be ready to guide you through the day\'s captivating itinerary. Your first destination is the mesmerizing Angel\'s Billabong, a natural wonder resembling a pristine pool nestled in the heart of nature. Take a refreshing swim, but exercise caution on the steps and heed your driver\'s recommendations. Next, we head to Broken Beach, a charming bay that was once a cave, now open to the sky, offering a unique and captivating scenery. Although inaccessible by land, the view from above is nothing short of breathtaking. Keep an eye out for the possibility of spotting giant manta rays gracefully gliding on the water\'s surface. Our journey continues to the renowned Kelingking Beach, famous for its stunning cliffs and the iconic hand-shaped mountain. This beach is not only one of the island\'s most famous attractions but also a favorite subject for photographers. We conclude the day at the pristine Crystal Beach, where white sands meet turquoise waters in perfect harmony. As the sun sets, you\'ll have the opportunity to relax and savor the beauty that surrounds you. This unforgettable experience concludes with a return boat trip to Bali from the Toya Pakeh port at 16:30, followed by a comfortable transfer to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": \"ETA 08.00 from Sanur by Maruti Fast Boat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Toyapakeh Harbour\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": \"ETD 16.30 to Sanur by Maruti Fast Boat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5200177,'654','Noemi Alcantara Gonzalez',30508,212456,'Sanur to Uluwatu','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-17','2024-08-17','Guio','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',280000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": \"ETA 17.00 from Nusa Penida by Maruti Fast Boat\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sanur Harbour\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-17\", \"text\": \"Pantai Suluban St, Pecatu, South Kuta, Badung Regency, Bali 80361\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Uluwatu Surf Villas\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5200180,'654','Noemi Alcantara Gonzalez',30508,218768,'Sidemen to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-19','2024-08-19','Guio','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',616000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": \"Banjar Dinas Pandangaji Kawan Desa Padang Aji Kedesaan, Pering Sari, Kec. Selat, Kabupaten Karangasem, Bali 80862\", \"time\": \"07:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Camaya Bali\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": \"ETD 13.45 by Air Asia X D7799 to Kuala Lumpur on 19 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5200252,'653','Javier Maria Garcia Jimenez',31158,204472,'VIP Service Fast Track International Arrival - Include VOA','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-25','2024-08-25','Guio','Febrina',2,'Person (1)',3628800.00,'Arrival International: Pick up at before immigration area.',NULL,'Flight detail: ETA 15.40 by Emirates EK356 from Dubai on 25 Aug 2024 Meet up with pick up from FM7 Resort Fast Track International Arrival Your personal assistant will be waiting for you before the Visa-on-Arrival desk and the immigration area (near transfer desk/duty-free plaza), holding a sign of your name. They will assist you with during all arrival processes, including handling your visas and other essential documents as well as VoA (if prepaid), fast assistance at immigration counters, assistance through customs clearance, and help with the luggage. Lastly, the assistant will take you to meet the person who will pick you up at the airport, or help you find a taxi.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5200265,'656','Vinay Nagarajan',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-14','2024-09-15','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Double',1680000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'NOTE : “Pure vegetarian- can’t eat meat, eggs, mushroom” Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-09-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5200268,'656','Vinay Nagarajan',30805,212247,'SRG-PKN','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-17','2024-09-17','Rendy','Rendy',4,'Person',7040000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5200283,'656','Vinay Nagarajan',30672,200737,'Studio 25 (Superior) Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-16','2024-09-17','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Double',1368000.00,'Studio 25 (Superior) room with 25 sqm sized room and with exclusive ARTOTEL bedding collection, some facilities in this room is 43\" inch lcd tv, 24 hours in-room service, high speed internet wi-fi, safety deposit box and hair dryer.',NULL,'Flight schedule Departure : ETD : 08.30 by Batik Air ID6302 to Pangkalan Bun on 17 Sept NOTE : “Pure vegetarian- can’t eat meat, eggs, mushroom”','{\"date\": \"2024-09-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5200284,'656','Vinay Nagarajan',30672,215075,'Airport Transfer - One Way','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-17','2024-09-17','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Per Car',360000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5200288,'656','Vinay Nagarajan',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-09-17','2024-09-19','Rendy','Rendy',4,'Persons (4)',14880000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board. NOTE : “Pure vegetarian- can’t eat meat, eggs, mushroom”','{\"date\": \"2024-09-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5200290,'656','Vinay Nagarajan',30667,215578,'Emerald Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-09-17','2024-09-19','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Double',6288000.00,NULL,NULL,'NOTE : Guests are vegetarian, totally can\'t eat meats, eggs, cheese and mushrooms.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5200296,'656','Vinay Nagarajan',30617,200924,'BEJI Villa (One Bedroom Suite Pool Villa)','Confirmed',NULL,5,'2024-09-19','2024-09-24','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Double',41340000.00,'A contemporary designed private one bedroom villa, a blend of local and modern architecture. Semi open bathroom with bathub, don\'t miss the time of soaking in the bathub with the secluded atmosphere. A king size bed equipped by mosquito net to give a touch of romantic, will be an additional value for this villa. Beji villa has a spacious space at its dressing room that could be added by maximal two extra beds for option of family.',NULL,'NOTE : “Pure vegetarian- can’t eat meat, eggs, mushroom”','{\"date\": \"2024-09-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5200297,'656','Vinay Nagarajan',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-19','2024-09-19','Rendy','Komang',1,'Persons (1-3)',420000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-19\", \"text\": \"ETA : 14.00 by Lion Air JT804 from Surabaya on 19 Sept 2024\", \"time\": \"14:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-19\", \"text\": \"Kajane Mua Ubud, Jl. Monkey Forest No.20, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 972877\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5200298,'656','Vinay Nagarajan',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-20','2024-09-20','Rendy','Rendy',4,'Persons (4)',2832000.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-20\", \"text\": \"Kajane Mua Ubud, Jl. Monkey Forest No.20, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 972877\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-20\", \"text\": \"Kajane Mua Ubud, Jl. Monkey Forest No.20, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 972877\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5200299,'656','Vinay Nagarajan',30508,202894,'Kintamani Highlands - Kehen Temple - Pengelipuran Village','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-21','2024-09-21','Rendy','Rendy',4,'Persons (4)',2448000.00,'Our wonderful tour starts from Kehen Temple. It is an ancient Hindu temple complex boasting unique architectural features. The staircases reaching from the ground to temple courtyard are carved sandstone mythical animal and Balinese folklore figure statues and also the central vestibule. The temple’s walls are also ornate with Chinese porcelain plates, which are a tribute to the historical relations between the local Bali kingdom and China. Afterwards, we continue to Penglipuran, a village that succeeded in preserving its 75-hectare bamboo forest located in the northern part of the village. Members of this village have a strong commitment to the system of \'Ayahan Desa\' - a philosophy committed to respecting the land on which the village stands. To concludes the day, we stop by at Tukad Cepung Waterfall. Well-guarded by the circular cliffs, this waterfall is difficult to locate for the first time visitor. The circular cliffs give you the feeling of being in a cave, while the open sky right from where the waterfall emerges, gives you the most enchanting view. The sunlight falls on the glistering waterfall creating a rainbow, which feels as though it is projected right up to you. If you have never seen water flowing from the sky, then this would be your chance! After spending your time there, we go back to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-21\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in hotel lobby at the mentioned time.\", \"time\": \"05:30\", \"locality\": \"Kajane Mua Ubud\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-21\", \"text\": \"Kajane Mua Ubud, Jl. Monkey Forest No.20, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 972877\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5200301,'656','Vinay Nagarajan',30508,207278,'Full Day Tour Car & Driver (8-10 hours)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-23','2024-09-23','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Persons (4)',900000.00,NULL,NULL,'Car & Driver only Not include : Entrance fee, guide, parking,any ticket','{\"date\": \"2024-09-23\", \"text\": \"Jl. Monkey Forest No.20, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 972877\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Kajane Mua Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-23\", \"text\": \"Jl. Monkey Forest No.20, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 972877\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Kajane Mua Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5200305,'656','Vinay Nagarajan',30508,207262,'Ubud to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-24','2024-09-24','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Persons (4-6)',840000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-24\", \"text\": \"Jl. Monkey Forest No.20, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 972877\", \"time\": \"06:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Kajane Mua Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-24\", \"text\": \"ETD : 10.50 by AirAsia QZ642 to Labuan Bajo on 24 Sept 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5200306,'656','Vinay Nagarajan',31083,212380,'3D2N LOB Rinca - Padar - Komodo Island Tour (Medium Standard B. - Purisari, etc)','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-09-24','2024-09-26','Rendy','Rendy',4,'Persons (4-5)',41688000.00,'TOUR ITINERARY Highlights: Menjarite, Kelor, Kalong, Rinca, Padar, Komodo island, Pink Beach, Taka Makassar, Manta Point, Kanawa, Batu Cermin Mirror Cave DAY 1 : DENPASAR - LABUAN BAJO - MENJARITE - PADAR - KELOR - KALONG ISLAND Arrival at Komodo Airport in Labuan Bajo west Flores, meeting service with our tour guide and transfer to the pier of Labuan Bajo for Rinca Island. It’s about 2 hours sail to the island of Komodo Dragon, stop at Menjarite island for snorkeling then continue to Rinca island-the Island of Komodo dragon, you will find not just e Dragons but also many wild animals like, deer, wild buffalo, long-tailed macaque and wild pig also numerous of birds. Keep your eyes look up as sometime you will find the young Komodo dragons on the trees. A local ranger will lead you through this natural preservation. Late afternoon sailing directly to Kalong Rinca Island to see the hundreds of fling foxes set out from the mangrove tree at 06-07 pm, the lovely sunset from the boat trip really enjoyable here. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Boat Cabin Air Conditioning DAY 2 : KALONG - PADAR - KOMODO - PINK BEACH - MANTA POINT - TAKA MAKASSAR - LABUAN BAJO After having breakfast in your boat, heading to Padar Island, taking trek to Padar Island until having the top view point to get breathtaking scenery of three bays around, Padar Island hike in Komodo has some of the most amazing views in Indonesia, trek to downhill and back to the Boat for sailing directly to Loh Liang – the Ranger station in Komodo Island. By passing through many small islands, After registering start to take basic trekking to see the GIANT RIZARD / KOMODO DRAGON and other wild animals as: Timor deer, wild pig, wild chicken and many variously of tropical bird. Please keep your look at any directions as sometimes you will also find young Komodo dragon hanging over the trees. A local ranger will be led you during the trek. Return to the boat on to Pink beach for snorkeling, swimming and relaxing. It is really spectacular and unspoiled coral reef and many color fish. This is one of best side for snorkeling diving. Sail toward MANTA POINT to exploring Huge Mantas by snorkeling even watching from your boat trip (can’t be guaranteed if weather is not good, like wave and current are strongly) visit also the taka Makaasar its really tiny island with white sand beach really enjoyable to relaxing or beach walking then heading to Labuan bajo for overnight and dinner at above hotel list option. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner DAY 3 : LABUAN BAJO - DENPASAR After breakfast taking your next excursion with visiting local marke and Batu Cermin (Mirror Stone) Cave. The grotto is 75 by 75 meters large, and contains stalactites and stalagmites. Some tunnels are narrow and dark but in others sunlight falls, then process to the airport for flight to Denpasar or to your next destination. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Attention: The itinerary is subject to change due to the weather, tide level and operating conditions without prior notice.',NULL,'Flight schedule arrival/departure : ETA : 12.10 by AirAsia QZ642 from Denpasar on 24 Sept ETD : 09.50 by Batik Air ID6332 to Denpasar on 26 Sept NOTE : “Pure vegetarian- can’t eat meat, eggs, mushroom”','{\"date\": \"2024-09-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5200310,'656','Vinay Nagarajan',30508,207250,'Airport to Kuta','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-26','2024-09-26','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Persons (4-6)',720000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-26\", \"text\": \"ETA : 11.05 by Batik Air ID6332 from Labuan Bajo on 26 Sept 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Denpasar Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-26\", \"text\": \"Jl. Kartika Plaza, Tuban, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Telepon: (0361) 2090477\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Anvaya Beach Resort Bali\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5200314,'656','Vinay Nagarajan',30508,202897,'Uluwatu Temple and Kecak Dance','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-27','2024-09-27','Rendy','Komang',4,'Persons (4)',2760000.00,'This half-day tour, is an exciting tour package to visit Padang-Padang Beach, Uluwatu Temple, the famous Balinese Hindu Temple in south part of Bali with breathtaking view of sunset and Indian Ocean. Uluwatu Temple is one of Balinese Hindu Temples located right on the petrifying hill with the crevasse exist in the right and left side. Uluwatu Temple is one of Sad Khayangan (6 biggest temple in Bali) owns magnificent view of the Indian Ocean and sunset as a backdrop. This temple is very amazing where the location is right on the narrow peninsula with deep seawater under it. This tour package is combined with the spectacular Balinese traditional dance performance of Kecak Dance. Balinese Kecak Dance is a spectacular traditional dance with the group of people playing this dance with fire game. It is very exciting and unique dance due to the sound of gamelan is not using the normal gamelan but use their mouth. The dancers make the compact choir with the exquisite dance movement that is one of this dance features. After the dance we returned back to the hotel or seafood restaurant in Jimbaran.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-27\", \"text\": \"Jl. Kartika Plaza, Tuban, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Telepon: (0361) 2090477\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"The Anvaya Resort Bali\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-27\", \"text\": \"Jl. Kartika Plaza, Tuban, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Telepon: (0361) 2090477\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"The Anvaya Resort Bali\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5200315,'656','Vinay Nagarajan',30508,207266,'Kuta to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-28','2024-09-28','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Persons (4-6)',720000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-28\", \"text\": \"Jl. Kartika Plaza, Tuban, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Telepon: (0361) 2090477\", \"time\": \"20:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"The Anvaya Resort Bali\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-28\", \"text\": \"ETD : 00.35 by Emirates EK399 to Dubai on 29 Sept 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"International Airport Ngurah Rai\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5200317,'656','Vinay Nagarajan',32589,215925,'Premiere Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-26','2024-09-27','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Double',5640000.00,'The Premiere Suites offer beautiful décor, exquisite style and lavish comfort. Located in the heart of the resort, the suites incorporate modern touches complemented by Balinese jewelry motifs representing the Hindu Bali period. Premiere Suite feature 85.50 square meters in size, balcony with an expansive seating area – perfect for sunset indulgence while enjoying the breeze off Kuta Beach and the stunning views. Ideal for families, these suites offer an inter-connecting option adjoining Premiere Rooms and feature separate shower, free-standing bathtub and the finest Sensatia Botanicals amenities product also daily refreshment for mini bar.',NULL,'NOTE : “Pure vegetarian- can’t eat meat, eggs, mushroom”','{\"date\": \"2024-09-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5200319,'657','Marina Alvarez Buxo',30608,218915,'Standard Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-07-30','2024-07-31','Purnomo','Tami',1,'Double',526400.00,NULL,NULL,'PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN','{\"date\": \"2024-07-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-07-31\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5200463,'263','Danny Van Belle 20235019',30683,203329,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-12-12','2024-12-13','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Twin',980000.00,'Feel at home in one of our Superior Rooms - warm colors giving an inviting feel and ambiance. Although you are in the heart of Soekarno - Hatta Airport you can find a small oasis of relaxation where you will leave the hustle and bustle of traveling far behind spacious 24 square meters. Superior room with a king or twin beds offering comfortable stay equipped with modern facilities such as air conditioning, arm chair, work desk & chair, flat screen TV with cable and satellite channels, free access internet & Wi-Fi, in room safe, coffee/tea maker, mini cooler, private bathroom with shower and hair dryer, and many more.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel.','{\"date\": \"2024-12-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-12-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5200585,'659','Mr. Manuel Fernandez Carrillo',30680,200914,'Deluxe Room + Extra Bed','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-08','2024-08-09','Jacob','Praba',1,'Double',1380000.00,'Enjoy our spacious elegant deluxe room with 40 m2 of room size. Enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, hot and cold shower, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Flight details: 8 August 2024: ETA 14:40PM by Etihad Airways EY474 from Abu Dhabi 9 August 2024: ETD 11:00AM by Batik Airways ID6344 to Yogyakarta Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-08-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5200638,'659','Mr. Manuel Fernandez Carrillo',30783,213438,'3D2N Best of Yogyakarta City Tour / C. Ayaartta (Deluxe Room) + Extra Bed','Confirmed','JS-Java01',3,'2024-08-09','2024-08-11','Jacob','Praba',3,'Persons (3)',10710000.00,'Day 1 : Arrival at Yogyakarta Welcome to the cradle of Indonesian culture, Yogyakarta. A tourist destination for its ancient palaces, temples, batik workshops, gamelan music orchestras, court dances and wayang puppet shows. Upon your arrival in Yogyakarta a representative of Come2Indonesia will be waiting for you with a sign indicating your name to take you to your hotel and the rest of the day is free for you. Meals : - Accommodation : C. Ayaartta Hotel - Deluxe Room Day 2 : Yogyakarta City Tour - Prambanan and Borobodur You will start your day with breakfast at the hotel. Today’s excursion will make us get lost in the authentic magic of Yogyakarta. One of the most beautiful and complete routes of the cultural capital of Indonesia. At the scheduled time, your guide will pick you up to begin your tour to Borobudur Temple (Candi Borobudur), the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. We will tour around the temple, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano have been producing during its history. After visiting one of the most important Buddhist temples in Southeast Asia, we continue our journey to the heart of the city. We will visit the Keraton, known as the Sultan’s Palace. The palace is a complex building two centuries old, located in the heart of the city. You will hear the song of “freedom” in the bird market. We will visit the “Water Castle” that occupies the highest part at the northern end of the vast complex of Taman Sari. Then we continue to Malioboro Street, main street of Yogyakarta, with its merchants, horse carriages, taxi-bikes and markets. An incredible experience that will make hours fly by. Finishing the tour in the centre of the city of Yogyakarta, we will head northeast towards Candi Prambanan, the temple of Hinduists which have been classified as a World Heritage Site by UNESCO since 1991. It was finished around the year 856 to commemorate the victory of the descendant Sanjaya of Siva, Rikai Pikatan on the last sovereign Sailendra of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to the Trimurti, the expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the Destroyer. After this unforgettable day, we will take you back to your hotel. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : C. Ayaartta Hotel - Deluxe Room Day 3 : Hotel - Airport You will enjoy a well-deserved breakfast at the hotel and according to the time of your flight, we will pick you up to take you to the airport and take the flight to your next destination. End of our services. Thank you very much for exploring Yogyakarta with Come2indonesia. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'D1/0908: Llegada a Yogyakarta - Templo Prambanan D2/1008: Yogyakarta City Tour – Templo Borobudur D3/1108: Transfer out YIA','{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": \"ETA 12:10PM by Batik Airways ID6344 from Jakarta\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Yogyakarta International Airport\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-11\", \"text\": \"ETD 07:00AM by Lion Air JT560 to Denpasar connecting ETD 10:10AM by Batik Airways ID6329 to Labuan Bajo\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Yogyakarta International Airport\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5200729,'659','Mr. Manuel Fernandez Carrillo',30805,212255,'CGK-YIA','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-09','2024-08-09','Jacob','Praba',3,'Person',3829254.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5200732,'659','Mr. Manuel Fernandez Carrillo',30805,215716,'YIA-DPS-LBJ','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-11','2024-08-11','Jacob','Praba',3,'Person',11880000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5200733,'659','Mr. Manuel Fernandez Carrillo',30805,202740,'LBJ-DPS','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-14','2024-08-14','Jacob','Praba',3,'Person',3571619.70,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5200735,'659','Mr. Manuel Fernandez Carrillo',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-14','2024-08-14','Jacob','Praba',1,'Persons (3)',420000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-14\", \"text\": \"ETA 20:40PM by Air Asia QZ649 from Labuan Bajo\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Ngurah Rai International Airport\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-14\", \"text\": \"Jl. Raya Kedewatan, Kedewatan, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Jungle Retreat Ubud\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5200747,'659','Mr. Manuel Fernandez Carrillo',30508,207379,'Ubud to Padang Bai','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-19','2024-08-19','Jacob','Praba',3,'Persons (3)',1800000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": \"Jl. Raya Kedewatan, Kedewatan, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar\", \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": \"Jungle Retreat Ubud\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": \"ETD 08:30 by Gili Gili Fastboat to Gili Air\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Padang Bai Harbor\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5200757,'659','Mr. Manuel Fernandez Carrillo',30805,208054,'LOP-CGK','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-21','2024-08-21','Jacob','Praba',3,'Person',4711278.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5200759,'659','Mr. Manuel Fernandez Carrillo',30680,200914,'Deluxe Room + Extra Bed','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-21','2024-08-22','Jacob','Praba',1,'Double',1380000.00,'Enjoy our spacious elegant deluxe room with 40 m2 of room size. Enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, hot and cold shower, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Flight details: 21 August 2024: ETA 15:30PM by Super Air Jet IU765 from Lombok 22 August 2024: ETD 06:00AM by Batik Air ID6202 to Pangkalan Bun Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-08-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5200761,'660','MARIO PUERTO',30783,201656,'[1D Yogyakarta Tour] Sunrise Setumbu - Borobudur Temple - Prambanan Temple','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-14','2024-08-14','Jacob','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',4260000.00,'At the appointed time, you will head northeast towards the Borobudur Temple (Candi Borobudur) the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. You will tour around the temple, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano has been producing during its history. From here you will go to Dieng. On your way to Dieng, you will go through tobacco and tea plantations. Dieng is an isolated 2,000 meter high plateau, almost always wrapped in darkness, there are eight small temples, simple in terms of details, but of extraordinary beauty in terms of location and proximity to the activity volcanic, with its interesting sulfur emissions of bright colors and bubbling muddy holes. The main temples are dedicated to the heroes of Mahabharata and are all of Hindu style. You will find the Telaga Warna (red lake) with fluorescent nuances due to the release of sulfur. After having this day full of visits, transfer to the hotel.',NULL,'Pickup & Dropoff Hotel in Yogyakarta : The Alana Hotel Yogyakarta Jl Mayjen Sutoyo No. 52, Mantrijeron, Yogyakarta, 55143, Indonesia Pickup time : 04.00 AM','{\"date\": \"2024-08-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5200763,'659','Mr. Manuel Fernandez Carrillo',33144,218921,'Deluxe Suite + Extra Bed','Confirmed',NULL,5,'2024-08-14','2024-08-19','Jacob','Praba',1,'Double',20640000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5200773,'659','Mr. Manuel Fernandez Carrillo',30805,202689,'CGK-PKN','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-22','2024-08-22','Jacob','Praba',3,'Person',3744114.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5200775,'659','Mr. Manuel Fernandez Carrillo',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-08-22','2024-08-24','Jacob','Praba',3,'Persons (3)',12600000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-22\", \"text\": \"ETA 07:15AM by Batik Air ID6202 from Jakarta\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Bandar Udara Iskandar Pangkalan Bun\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": \"ETD 08:50AM by Batik Air ID6134 to Surabaya\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Bandar Udara Iskandar Pangkalan Bun\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5200783,'659','Mr. Manuel Fernandez Carrillo',30805,212272,'PKN-SUB','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-24','2024-08-24','Jacob','Praba',3,'Person',4344120.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5200791,'659','Mr. Manuel Fernandez Carrillo',31015,203232,'3D2N - Surabaya - Jodipan - Tumpak Sewu - Mount Bromo Tour Package drop Surabaya','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-24','2024-08-26','Jacob','Praba',3,'Persons (3)',8280000.00,NULL,NULL,'D1/2408: Arrival Surabaya - Jodipan - Tumpak Sewu Hostel D2/2508: Tumpak Sewu Waterfall - Bromo Hotel D3/2608: Bromo Sunrise Tour - Surabaya Airport','{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": \"ETA 10:00AM by Batik Air ID6134 from Pangkalan Bun\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Juanda International Airport Surabaya\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-26\", \"text\": \"ETD 16:00PM by Batik Air ID6587 to Jakarta\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Juanda International Airport Surabaya\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5200816,'659','Mr. Manuel Fernandez Carrillo',30680,200914,'Deluxe Room + Extra Bed','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-26','2024-08-27','Jacob','Praba',1,'Double',1380000.00,'Enjoy our spacious elegant deluxe room with 40 m2 of room size. Enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, hot and cold shower, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Flight Details: 26 August 2024: ETA 17:30PM by Batik Air ID6587 from Surabaya 27 August 2024: ETD 17:45PM by Etihad Airways EY475 to Abu Dhabi Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-