nfirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-13','2024-08-13','Ayu','Ayu',2,'Persons (2)',1320000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5203206,'669','Mikhail PAVLOV',31591,207373,'3D2N Tangkoko','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-25','2024-08-27','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Persons (2)',6600000.00,'Day 1 : MANADO - TANGKOKO - The expedition begins The adventure begins with meeting your guide at the Manado airport. Then you will start the journey of about 2 and a half hours by car to the Tangkoko Forest where you will do the check in at your Homestay or Lodge. Upon arrival, you will have a talk about what you will see and preparations for the trekking. Meals : Dinner Accommodation : Bird House Homestay or Similar Days 02 : Tangkoko Nature Reserve These days will be dedicated to exploring the jungle in search of animals and bird watching. You will start the trekking that will take you to Tangkok National Park. In just 40 minutes by boat, you will reach the Batuangus beach where you will then climb Mount Tangkoko (1500 m). The dense and virgin jungle is home to some unique animal species in North Sulawesi such as the crested black macaque and the tarsier spectrum that has become known as \"the smallest primate in the world\". As you will be trekking through the lush jungle, you will probably see and hear the red gnarled hornbill as well as the Maleo which is a Megapod Bird that lays eggs on large mounds it builds on the black sand. You can also find couscous, which is a relative of the Australian koala. The forest ranger will accompany you all the way to the top of Tangkoko Mountain. In the afternoon you will return to the station. Alternatively, you can have three hours of trekking in the lowland jungle or swimming on the black sand beach of Tangkoko Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Bird House Homestay or Similar Day 03 : Tangkoko - Manado After breakfast, you can spend the morning in the surroundings of the National Park and at the agreed time, with your guide, you will have the transfer to Manado. Thank you for exploring this unique jungle with us. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-25\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in hotel lobby at the mentioned time.\", \"time\": \"12:00\", \"locality\": \"Cocotinos Lembeh Resort\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-27\", \"text\": \"ETD: TBA\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Manado Airport\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5203209,'668','Oriol Ribel /+34686 283718',30508,202893,'Lempuyang Temple Tour (Lempuyang-Tirta Gangga-Tenganan-Goa Lawah)','Confirmed','C2I-BALI11',1,'2024-08-09','2024-08-09','Nicholas','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',1920000.00,'At the agreed time, our guide will pick you up to start the tour in the eastern part of Bali. The first place you will visit is Goa Lawah Temple. Goa Lawah Temple consists of two names, \"Goa\" which means cave and \"Lawah\" which means bat. Several thousand bats are flying in the cave as the name suggests. With the lights fading as you go deeper inside the cave, it gives off a very strange atmosphere. From Goa Lawah, we continue our way to Lempuyang Temple. Upon arrival, the temple will greet you with its gratifying panorama that extends into infinity. On a clear, sunny day, you\'ll be able to gaze out over the mountains, Amlapura city, and Mount Agung, an incredibly magnificent sight that\'s beautiful beyond words. This portrait of heaven is beautifully framed by the Gapura Candi Bentar (the gate of the temple). Our journey continues to visit Tirta Gangga. The site is a paradise surrounded by water, with all the pools decorated with unusual statues. With its seclusion and a view of the surrounding rice paddies, Tirta Gangga is a wonderful place. At the end of the trip we go to Tenganan Village, the most famous Bali Agas (the “original” Bali people) in the city. With its characteristics, the city village is arranged in parallel along the wide main road paved with rows of cobblestones. In Tenganan, women still weave the famous Kamben Geringsing, or \"burnt cloth,\" which has the power to immunize the wearer against evil. We take a close look at what they do in their daily lives in a traditional lifestyle. From Tenganan, we will transfer you to the hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": \"Banjar Kepitu, Kenderan, Kec. Tegallalang, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80561 Telepon: (0361) 4792553\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"The Kayon Resort Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-09\", \"text\": \"Banjar Kepitu, Kenderan, Kec. Tegallalang, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80561 Telepon: (0361) 4792553\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"The Kayon Resort Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5203215,'317','Donovan CLEUET',30680,200923,'Day Use - Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-10','2024-08-10','Rendy','Rendy',5,'Double',3080000.00,'Enjoy our spacious elegant deluxe room with 42 m2 of room size. This room equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, hot and cold shower, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Flight details: ETA: 07.40 by Turkish Airlines TK508 from Istanbul on 10 Aug ETD: 14.15 by Batik Air ID6524 to Labuan Bajo on 10 Aug Maximum stay 6 hours. Earliest check-in time is 10:00. Latest check-out time is 18.00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\":