26-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5208975,'694','Fernando Clark',30508,207268,'Nusa Dua to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-25','2024-08-25','Melysa','Tami',2,'Persons (4-6)',1344000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-25\", \"text\": \"Kawasan Wisata Nusa Dua Lot S-3, Benoa, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali\", \"time\": \"20:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Merusaka Nusa Dua\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-25\", \"text\": \"ETD 00.05 by Emirates EK399 to Dubai on 26 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"I Gusti Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5209013,'694','Fernando Clark',30508,207268,'Nusa Dua to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-26','2024-08-26','Melysa','Tami',1,'Persons (4-6)',672000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-26\", \"text\": \"Kawasan Wisata Nusa Dua Lot S-3, Benoa, Kec. Kuta Sel., Kabupaten Badung, Bali\", \"time\": \"20:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Merusaka Nusa Dua\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-26\", \"text\": \"ETD 00.05 by Emirates EK399 to Dubai on 27 Aug\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"I Gusti Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5209059,'649','Dr. Chien Chuan-I ( +6592283198 )',31158,216309,'Fast Track International Departure','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-10','2024-08-10','Ayu','Ayu',1,'Person (1)',0.00,'Departure International: Service start from meet clients at departure hall until client boarding.',NULL,'MEETING POINT: Your personal will be waiting for you at the drop-zone area of international departure terminal building, holding a sign with your name. They will assist you from the check-in process, immigration and accompany you until the boarding gate.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5209555,'698','Angelika Sipeki',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-09-16','2024-09-18','Nicholas','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',10800000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-16\", \"text\": \"ETA 07.15 by Batik Air ID6202 from Jakarta on 16 Sep\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pangkalan Bun Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-18\", \"text\": \"ETD 10.25 by Batik Air ID6303 to Semarang on 18 Sep\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5209560,'698','Angelika Sipeki',30783,217825,'3D2N Yogya-Bromo / B. Gallery Prawirotaman (Superior Room) & Lereng Bromo (Deluxe)','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-09-18','2024-09-20','Nicholas','Tami',2,'Persons (2 / Double)',15840000.00,'D1 Pick up at hotel in Jogja. By Train to Mojokerto then continue drive to Bromo: Welcome to the cradle of Indonesian culture, Yogyakarta. A tourist destination for its ancient palaces, temples, batik workshops, gamelan music orchestras, court dances and wayang puppet shows. You will enjoy your breakfast at the hotel, and at the indicated time, with your guide, you will travel to Jombang / Mojokerta by train. Then by private car you will go to your hotel located on the slopes of the Bromo volcano. In total it will be about 8 hours of travel. Upon arrival, you check-in at The hotel and enjoy your deserved rest. D2 Mt. Penanjakan Sunrise and Bromo crater tour including Jeep – Transfer to Ijen: Very early, your guide and a jeep driver will be waiting for you at the hotel to attend one of the most spectacular sunrises in Indonesia. Even though you have to get up early, it will be worth it. You will climb to a high point first in full darkness and, little by little the first rays of sun are giving way to a huge and indescribable caldera that makes up the entire view of the Bromo and Semeru Natural Park. With Bromo, a volcano of great fumaroles and behind it, the Semeru Volcano with explosions every 20 minutes exactly, will make you have one of the most rewarding experiences ever. After enjoying the sunset, by jeep, we will go to the slopes of the volcano where you can go to the Bromo volcano and after climbing some stairs you can reach the very edge of its crater and see the impressive activity it has. We return to the hotel to cool off and enjoy your breakfast. At the agreed time, we will leave for our next destination, the Ijen volcano. This section lasts about 7-8 hours by car where we will make a stop to eat. Take this trip to rest. Arriving in Ijen, we will leave you at your hotel, where you will check in and enjoy your well-deserved rest. D3 Mt. Ijen crater tour – Drop at hotel in Bali: The day has finally come to visit one of the most attractive volcanoes in Indonesia! One of the last open pit sulfur mines that survive on the planet. For this climb you can choose between two schedules. Or leave very early to see the blue lava (leaving the hotel about 1.30am) or leave more quietly only for sunrise (about 4am). Depending on how tired you are of the trip from Bromo to Ijen, you can decide the day before with your guide. Once we pick you up at your hotel, you will head towards the village of Licin to reach the slope of the volcano to begin the steep climb to the crater of the volcano. During this trek, your guide will give you double filter masks to protect you from the natural chemicals of sulfur. Once above, at an altitude of 2883 meters and when dawn begins, your eyes will open before your eyes an incredible contrast of colors. A yellow earth scene and a large turquoise blue lake inside the crater that contrast with a suspended white cloud that is continuously expelling the volcano. In turn, among so much beauty you will see the locals work where it is said, it is one of the toughest jobs in the world. These miners go down to the crater of the volcano to load 80 to 100 kilos of sulfur on their shoulders and then sell it. After this amazing experience on the edge of the Ijen volcano crater, we begin the descent with an incredible panoramic view of the mountains that make up the national park. We will take you to your hotel to cool off and have breakfast and we start the road to Bali for about 5 hours. To do this, we will go first to the port of Banyuwangui where we will take the ferry to cross to Bali. It is a journey of only 30 minutes where you must remember to add an hour to your watch, because we change the time slot. Welcome to the island of the Gods.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-18\", \"text\": \"ETA 11.25 by Batik Air ID6303 from Pangkalan Bun on 18 Sep\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Semarang International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-20\", \"text\": \"ETD 19.10 by Lion Air JT920 to Denpasar on 20 Sep\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Surabaya International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5209561,'698','Angelika Sipeki',30571,202567,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-20','2024-09-21','Nicholas','Tami',1,'Double',1290000.00,'Located at the Second Floor, 35 sqm comfort living with a touch of Balinese style featuring completed fitting, Cable TV, a fancy bathroom comprises rain shower and good quality amenities. Also dedicated Wi-Fi Access to complete your day.',NULL,'Flight Information ETA 21.10 by Lion Air JT920 from Surabaya on 20 Sep ETD 08.00 by Batik Air ID6333 to Labuan Bajo on 21 Sep','{\"date\": \"2024-09-20\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5209562,'698','Angelika Sipeki',31083,212380,'3D2N LOB Rinca - Padar - Komodo Island Tour (Medium Standard B. - Purisari, etc)','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-09-21','2024-09-23','Nicholas','Tami',2,'Persons (2-3)',25764000.00,'TOUR ITINERARY Highlights: Menjarite, Kelor, Kalong, Rinca, Padar, Komodo island, Pink Beach, Taka Makassar, Manta Point, Kanawa, Batu Cermin Mirror Cave DAY 1 : DENPASAR - LABUAN BAJO - MENJARITE - PADAR - KELOR - KALONG ISLAND Arrival at Komodo Airport in Labuan Bajo west Flores, meeting service with our tour guide and transfer to the pier of Labuan Bajo for Rinca Island. It’s about 2 hours sail to the island of Komodo Dragon, stop at Menjarite island for snorkeling then continue to Rinca island-the Island of Komodo dragon, you will find not just e Dragons but also many wild animals like, deer, wild buffalo, long-tailed macaque and wild pig also numerous of birds. Keep your eyes look up as sometime you will find the young Komodo dragons on the trees. A local ranger will lead you through this natural preservation. Late afternoon sailing directly to Kalong Rinca Island to see the hundreds of fling foxes set out from the mangrove tree at 06-07 pm, the lovely sunset from the boat trip really enjoyable here. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Boat Cabin Air Conditioning DAY 2 : KALONG - PADAR - KOMODO - PINK BEACH - MANTA POINT - TAKA MAKASSAR - LABUAN BAJO After having breakfast in your boat, heading to Padar Island, taking trek to Padar Island until having the top view point to get breathtaking scenery of three bays around, Padar Island hike in Komodo has some of the most amazing views in Indonesia, trek to downhill and back to the Boat for sailing directly to Loh Liang – the Ranger station in Komodo Island. By passing through many small islands, After registering start to take basic trekking to see the GIANT RIZARD / KOMODO DRAGON and other wild animals as: Timor deer, wild pig, wild chicken and many variously of tropical bird. Please keep your look at any directions as sometimes you will also find young Komodo dragon hanging over the trees. A local ranger will be led you during the trek. Return to the boat on to Pink beach for snorkeling, swimming and relaxing. It is really spectacular and unspoiled coral reef and many color fish. This is one of best side for snorkeling diving. Sail toward MANTA POINT to exploring Huge Mantas by snorkeling even watching from your boat trip (can’t be guaranteed if weather is not good, like wave and current are strongly) visit also the taka Makaasar its really tiny island with white sand beach really enjoyable to relaxing or beach walking then heading to Labuan bajo for overnight and dinner at above hotel list option. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner DAY 3 : LABUAN BAJO - DENPASAR After breakfast taking your next excursion with visiting local marke and Batu Cermin (Mirror Stone) Cave. The grotto is 75 by 75 meters large, and contains stalactites and stalagmites. Some tunnels are narrow and dark but in others sunlight falls, then process to the airport for flight to Denpasar or to your next destination. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Attention: The itinerary is subject to change due to the weather, tide level and operating conditions without prior notice.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-21\", \"text\": \"ETA 09.10 by Batik Air ID6333 from Denpasar on 21 Sep\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Komodo Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-23\", \"text\": \"ETD 08.50 by Air Asia QZ645 to Denpasar on 23 Sep\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5209563,'699','Almudena Ezquerra Perez',32766,216809,'3D2N Open Trip Komodo - Lady Grace / Full Ocean','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-09-06','2024-09-08','Nicholas','Tami',2,'Per Person (Min. 2 Person)',15240000.00,'DAY 1 : Kelor Island - Manjerite Island - Kalong Island DAY 2 : Padar Island - Long / Pick Beach - Komodo Island - Manta Point - Taka Makasar DAY 3 : Kanawa Island',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-06\", \"text\": \"Macang Tanggar, Komodo, West Manggarai Regency, East Nusa Tenggara\", \"time\": \"09:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Luwansa Beach Resort\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-08\", \"text\": \"They will be picked up by Sudamala Seraya team to proceed their trip to Seraya Island\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Dermaga Biru\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5210004,'573','Elena María Duran Agosto 2024',30508,212292,'Airport to Munduk','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-13','2024-08-13','Guio','Komang',1,'Persons (1-3)',616000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": \"ETA : 22.40 by Qatar Airways QR960 from Doha on 13 Aug 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"International Airport Ngurah Rai\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-13\", \"text\": \"Jl. Raya Asah Gobleg, Br. Dinas Asah Desa Gobleg, Buleleng, Munduk, Kec. Banjar, Bali 81152 Telepon: 0812-3788-7877\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Munduk Tentrem\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5210023,'573','Elena María Duran Agosto 2024',30508,215968,'HD Bali Tour (MUNDUK WATERFALL - ULUN DANU BERATAN)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-14','2024-08-14','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',1904000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-14\", \"text\": \"Jl. Raya Asah Gobleg, Br. Dinas Asah Desa Gobleg, Buleleng, Munduk, Kec. Banjar, Bali 81152 Telepon: 0812-3788-7877\", \"time\": \"12:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Munduk Tentrem\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-14\", \"text\": \"Jl. A.A. Gede Rai No.88, Lodtunduh, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 8493577\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Royal Casa Ganesha\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5210071,'235','Cynthia Cleveland',30508,207254,'Kuta to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-24','2024-08-24','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Persons (1-3)',392000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in hotel lobby at the mentioned time.\", \"time\": \"12:00\", \"locality\": \"Holiday Inn Express Baruna Bali\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Komaneka at Bisma\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5210107,'701','Maria Luisa Bordeje Laguna',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-28','2024-08-29','Melysa','Tami',4,'3 Double + 1 Twin',3360000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-08-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5210215,'701','Maria Luisa Bordeje Laguna',30783,217901,'3D2N Surabaya - Bromo - Jogja / C. Bromo Terrace (Deluxe) & Adhisthana (Superior) Incl T