national Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-31\", \"text\": \"Jl. Gajahmada No.101, Miroto, Kec. Semarang Tengah, Kota Semarang, Jawa Tengah\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"ARTOTEL Gajahmada Semarang\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5210237,'701','Maria Luisa Bordeje Laguna',30673,200559,'Deluxe Double Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-29','2024-08-30','Melysa','Tami',3,'Double',3780000.00,'Designed to capture nature vibes. Slide open the door to your private terrace to let in the fresh mountain air and relax.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5210241,'701','Maria Luisa Bordeje Laguna',30673,200584,'Deluxe Twin Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-29','2024-08-30','Melysa','Tami',1,'Twin',1320000.00,'Escape the nature with family, friends, colleague and just relax.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5210267,'701','Maria Luisa Bordeje Laguna',30672,200747,'Studio 30 (Deluxe) Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-31','2024-09-01','Melysa','Tami',4,'3 Double + 1 Twin',3216000.00,'Studio 30 (Deluxe) room with 25 sqm sized room, and exclusive ARTOTEL bedding collection, with facilities 43\" inch lcd tv, 24 hours in-room service, high speed internet wi-fi, safety deposit box, hair dryer.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-31\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5210273,'701','Maria Luisa Bordeje Laguna',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-09-01','2024-09-03','Melysa','Tami',8,'Persons (8)',25440000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-01\", \"text\": \"ETA 09.30 by Batik Air ID6302 from Semarang on 01 Sep\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pangkalan Bun Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-03\", \"text\": \"ETD 08.50 by Batik Air ID6134 to Surabaya on 03 Sep\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5210275,'701','Maria Luisa Bordeje Laguna',30508,207256,'Airport to Canggu','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-03','2024-09-03','Melysa','Tami',1,'Persons (7-10)',1200000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-03\", \"text\": \"ETA 14.00 by Lion Air JT804 from Surabaya on 03 Sep\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"I Gusti Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-03\", \"text\": \"Jl. Pantai Batu Bolong No.117x, Canggu, Kuta Utara, Badung Regency, Bali 80361\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Hotel Tugu Bali\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5210281,'701','Maria Luisa Bordeje Laguna',30508,207278,'Full Day Tour Car & Driver (8-10 hours)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-04','2024-09-04','Melysa','Tami',1,'Persons (7-10)',1200000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Hotel Tugu Bali\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-04\", \"text\": \"Jl. Pantai Batu Bolong No.117x, Canggu, Kuta Utara, Badung Regency, Bali 80361\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Hotel Tugu Bali\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5210291,'701','Maria Luisa Bordeje Laguna',30863,202152,'Dedari Suites Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-09-03','2024-09-05','Melysa','Tami',4,'3 Double + 1 Twin',37440000.00,'Nestled behind an antique wooden door, surrounded by tropical luxurious garden, the Dedari Suites are remarkable for their timeless ambience. Kick off your shoes and fling yourselves down on the massive canopy bed, enveloped in romantic white flowing curtains. The suite features a tropical plunge pool outside, a private spa area with a unique sunken bath in open air bathroom, along with a dreamy traditional daybed. Incense and candles give you the perfect ambience to spend memorable hours lying about in plush towels whilst listening to the waves in the ocean.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5210300,'701','Maria Luisa Bordeje Laguna',30508,213303,'Canggu to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-05','2024-09-05','Melysa','Tami',1,'Persons (7-10)',1200000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-05\", \"text\": \"Jl. Pantai Batu Bolong No.117x, Canggu, Kuta Utara, Badung Regency, Bali 80361\", \"time\": \"12:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Hotel Tugu Bali\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-05\", \"text\": \"Jl. Tirta Tawar, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Villa Jepun\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5210303,'701','Maria Luisa Bordeje Laguna',30508,207262,'Ubud to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-07','2024-09-07','Melysa','Tami',1,'Persons (7-10)',1200000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-07\", \"text\": \"Jl. Tirta Tawar, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": \"04:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Villa Jepun\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-07\", \"text\": \"ETD 08.00 by Batik Air ID6333 to Labuan Bajo on 07 Sep\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"I Gusti Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5210333,'701','Maria Luisa Bordeje Laguna',31176,219092,'Villa Jepun - 6 Bedroom Pool Villa','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-09-05','2024-09-07','Melysa','Tami',1,'Double',27264000.00,NULL,NULL,'Villa Jepun Jl. Tirta Tawar, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571','{\"date\": \"2024-09-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5210344,'701','Maria Luisa Bordeje Laguna',31083,212384,'3D2N LOB Rinca - Padar - Komodo Island Tour (Superior Standard B. - Bintang Flores, etc)','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-09-07','2024-09-09','Melysa','Tami',8,'Persons (8-9)',74016000.00,'TOUR ITINERARY Highlights: Menjarite, Kelor, Kalong, Rinca, Padar, Komodo Island, Pink Beach, Taka Makassar, Manta Point, Kanawa, Batu Cermin Mirror Cave DAY 1 : DENPASAR - LABUAN BAJO - MENJARITE - PADAR - KELOR - KALONG ISLAND Arrival at Komodo Airport in Labuan Bajo west Flores, meeting service with our tour guide and transfer to the pier of Labuan Bajo for Rinca Island. It’s about 2 hours sail to the island of Komodo Dragon, stop at Menjarite island for snorkeling then continue to Rinca island-the Island of Komodo dragon, you will find not just e Dragons but also many wild animals like, deer, wild buffalo, long-tailed macaque and wild pig also numerous of birds. Keep your eyes look up as sometime you will find the young Komodo dragons on the trees. A local ranger will lead you through this natural preservation. Late afternoon sailing directly to Kalong Rinca Island to see the hundreds of fling foxes set out from the mangrove tree at 06-07 pm, the lovely sunset from the boat trip really enjoyable here. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Boat Cabin Air Conditioning DAY 2 : KALONG - PADAR - KOMODO - PINK BEACH - MANTA POINT - TAKA MAKASSAR - LABUAN BAJO After having breakfast in your boat, heading to Padar Island, taking trek to Padar Island until having the top view point to get breathtaking scenery of three bays around, Padar Island hike in Komodo has some of the most amazing views in Indonesia, trek to downhill and back to the Boat for sailing directly to Loh Liang – the Ranger station in Komodo Island. By passing through many small islands, After registering start to take basic trekking to see the GIANT RIZARD / KOMODO DRAGON and other wild animals as: Timor deer, wild pig, wild chicken and many variously of tropical bird. Please keep your look at any directions as sometimes you will also find young Komodo dragon hanging over the trees. A local ranger will be led you during the trek. Return to the boat on to Pink beach for snorkeling, swimming and relaxing. It is really spectacular and unspoiled coral reef and many color fish. This is one of best side for snorkeling diving. Sail toward MANTA POINT to exploring Huge Mantas by snorkeling even watching from your boat trip (can’t be guaranteed if weather is not good, like wave and current are strongly) visit also the taka Makaasar its really tiny island with white sand beach really enjoyable to relaxing or beach walking then heading to Labuan bajo for overnight and dinner at above hotel list option. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner DAY 3 : LABUAN BAJO - DENPASAR After breakfast taking your next excursion with visiting local marke and Batu Cermin (Mirror Stone) Cave. The grotto is 75 by 75 meters large, and contains stalactites and stalagmites. Some tunnels are narrow and dark but in others sunlight falls, then process to the airport for flight to Denpasar or to your next destination. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Attention: The itinerary is subject to change due to the weather, tide level and operating conditions without prior notice.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-07\", \"text\": \"ETA 09.10 by Batik Air ID6333 from Denpasar on 07 Sep\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Labuan Bajo Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-09\", \"text\": \"ETD 09.50 by Batik Air ID6332 to Denpasar on 09 Sep\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5210819,'702','MARTA SUBRA',32766,216810,'3D2N Open Trip Komodo - Lady Grace / Deluxe Cabin','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-30','2024-09-01','Guio','Wiwik',2,'Per Person (Min. 2 Person)',12840000.00,'DAY 1 : Kelor Island - Manjerite Island - Kalong Island DAY 2 : Padar Island - Long / Pick Beach - Komodo Island - Manta Point - Taka Makasar DAY 3 : Kanawa Island',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-30\", \"text\": \"Pick Up Time: 09.00 - 10.00 (H-1 will update the fixed pick up time)\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Cool Breeze Flores Labuan Bajo Authentic Hotel.\", \"location\": \"Kampung Baru Labuan Bajo, Desa Gorontalo, Kec. Komodo, Kabupaten Manggarai Barat, Nusa Tenggara Tim. Phone: 0812-4669-6371\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Bintang Flores Hotel.\", \"location\": \"Jl. Pantai Pede, Labuan Bajo, Kec. Komodo, Kabupaten Manggarai Barat, Nusa Tenggara Tim. Phone: (0385) 2443755\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5210827,'702','MARTA SUBRA',30783,213061,'Transfer from Semarang Airport to Yogyakarta Hotel (With Stop Borobudur)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-06','2024-09-06','Guio','Wiwik',1,'Per Car',960000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-06\", \"text\": \"ETA: 11.25 by Batik Air ID6303 from Pangkalan Bun on 06 September 2024.\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Airport Semarang\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"The Alana Hotel & Conference Center - Malioboro.\", \"location\": \"Jl. Mayjend Sutoyo No.52, Mantrijeron, Kec. Mantrijeron, Kota Yogyakarta, Daerah Istimewa Yogyakarta 55143 Phone: (0