',NULL,1,'2024-09-05','2024-09-05','Jacob','Wiwik',1,'Persons (4-6)',840000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting at the arrival hall exit, holding a signboard of your name/group name. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 3 hours after the flight’s estimated arrival time (ETA). - For any flight delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-09-05\", \"text\": \"ETA: 17.25 by Lion Air JT920 from Surabaya on 05 September 2024.\", \"time\": \"17:25\", \"locality\": \"NGURAH RAI INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT (TERMINAL DOMESTIC)\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"UDDHARA UBUD VILLA\", \"location\": \"Jl. Cocoa II, Kedewatan, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571. Phone: 0812-3800-3706\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5218220,'731','MARTA SANTIAGO MORA',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route (TAMAN AYUN-JATILUWIH-ULUNDANU BERATAN-TANAH LOT)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-08','2024-09-08','Jacob','Wiwik',4,'Persons (4)',2832000.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"UDDHARA UBUD VILLA\", \"location\": \"Jl. Cocoa II, Kedewatan, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571. Phone: 0812-3800-3706\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"UDDHARA UBUD VILLA\", \"location\": \"Jl. Cocoa II, Kedewatan, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571. Phone: 0812-3800-3706\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5218247,'731','MARTA SANTIAGO MORA',30508,202893,'BESAKIH - LEMPUYANG - TAMAN SUKASADA UJUNG','Confirmed','C2I-BALI11',1,'2024-09-09','2024-09-09','Jacob','Wiwik',4,'Persons (4)',2928000.00,'At the agreed time, our guide will pick you up to start the tour in the eastern part of Bali. The first place you will visit is Goa Lawah Temple. Goa Lawah Temple consists of two names, \"Goa\" which means cave and \"Lawah\" which means bat. Several thousand bats are flying in the cave as the name suggests. With the lights fading as you go deeper inside the cave, it gives off a very strange atmosphere. From Goa Lawah, we continue our way to Lempuyang Temple. Upon arrival, the temple will greet you with its gratifying panorama that extends into infinity. On a clear, sunny day, you\'ll be able to gaze out over the mountains, Amlapura city, and Mount Agung, an incredibly magnificent sight that\'s beautiful beyond words. This portrait of heaven is beautifully framed by the Gapura Candi Bentar (the gate of the temple). Our journey continues to visit Tirta Gangga. The site is a paradise surrounded by water, with all the pools decorated with unusual statues. With its seclusion and a view of the surrounding rice paddies, Tirta Gangga is a wonderful place. At the end of the trip we go to Tenganan Village, the most famous Bali Agas (the “original” Bali people) in the city. With its characteristics, the city village is arranged in parallel along the wide main road paved with rows of cobblestones. In Tenganan, women still weave the famous Kamben Geringsing, or \"burnt cloth,\" which has the power to immunize the wearer against evil. We take a close look at what they do in their daily lives in a traditional lifestyle. From Tenganan, we will transfer you to the hotel.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": \"UDDHARA UBUD VILLA\", \"location\": \"Jl. Cocoa II, Kedewatan, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571. Phone: 0812-3800-3706\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"SAKA VILLA AMED\", \"location\": \"Jl. Bunutan - Bangle, Bunutan, Kec. Abang, Kabupaten Karangasem. Telepon: 0812-3814-8227\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5218248,'731','MARTA SANTIAGO MORA',30508,213366,'Amed to Padang Bai','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-11','2024-09-11','Jacob','Wiwik',1,'Persons (4-6)',1680000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"05:30\", \"locality\": \"SAKA VILLA AMED\", \"location\": \"Jl. Bunutan - Bangle, Bunutan, Kec. Abang, Kabupaten Karangasem. Telepon: 0812-3814-8227\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-11\", \"text\": \"BlueWater Express Padang Bai office +628113809777 (available on WhatsApp)\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Office BlueWater Express Padangbai located at Central Parking Silkayukti\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5218252,'733','Karen Benn',30806,208758,'3D2N Shared Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO8',3,'2024-09-04','2024-09-06','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Person (1)',3920000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.00 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you canhave your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan is Cape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even see crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Shared Klotok Boat *The SHARED klotok will be ready by 10.30 AM and will depart at 12.00 PM sharp. Check-in time: Klotok at 10.30 AM, check-out time: 08.00 AM *If you arrive at the port before 12 PM, you may walk around the area of the port by yourself. Alternatively, when the boat is ready, you can also wait for the other travelers on the boat. Note: The guide may not assist you during the waiting time. *All participants should arrive at the latest 10.30 AM at Pangkalanbun Airport. If you arrive late, you must take the speedboat to join the klotok. The speedboat costs around IDR 600.000/boat/way to be paid directly to the captain. Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continue to add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Shared Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board. Flights information ETA: 07.15 by Batik Air ID6202 from Jakarta on 04 Sep ETD: 08.50 by Batik Air ID6134 to Surabaya on 06 Sep','{\"date\": \"2024-09-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5218255,'732','Ms. Angela Mid',30783,201659,'Borobudur Temple - Prambanan Temple','Confirmed','C2I-JAVA17',1,'2024-09-08','2024-09-08','Jacob','Praba',2,'Persons (2)',3840000.00,'You will be picked up early morning at the hotel at the indicated time and we will begin our wonderful day! Sunrise over the great stupa… We will arrive at Borobudur Temple sometime before sunrise. Prepare yourself for an amazing scenery with many faces of Buddha enlightened with the sunlight. Feel the calm breeze in this peaceful morning. Borobudur is the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. After sunrise, we will tour the temple, observing hundreds of centuries-old Buddha statues and how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically, it was made during the relatively brief Shailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC. It is under constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighboring Merapi volcano have produced during its history. The world heritage… Afterwards, we will go towards Prambanan, the temple of Hinduists which had been classified as a World Heritage Site by UNESCO since 1991. This temple was completed around the year 856 to commemorate the return of Shailendra dynasty of Central Java. Take your time to admire each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the perched stones gives off in this set of more than 200 Hinduist smaller temples. They are dedicated to the Trimurti, the expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the Destroyer. After this day that you will never forget, we will take you back to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-08\", \"text\": \"Jl. Malioboro No.42, Suryatmajan, Kec. Danurejan, Kota Yogyakarta, Daerah Istimewa Yogyakarta\", \"time\": \"07:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Aveta Hotel Malioboro\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-08\", \"text\": \"Jl. Malioboro No.42, Suryatmajan, Kec. Danurejan, Kota Yogyakarta, Daerah Istimewa Yogyakarta\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Aveta Hotel Malioboro\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5218614,'499','MARIA DEL PILAR FRETES BIZARRO',30806,208758,'3D2N Shared Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO8',3,'2024-09-28','2024-09-30','Guio','Eddy',4,'Person (1)',15680000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.00 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you canhave your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan is Cape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even see crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Shared Klotok Boat *The SHARED klotok will be ready by 10.30 AM and will depart at 12.00 PM sharp. Check-in time: Klotok at 10.30 AM, check-out time: 08.00 AM *If you arrive at the port before 12 PM, you may walk around the area of the port by yourself. Alternatively, when the boat is ready, you can also wait for the other travelers on the boat. Note: The guide may not assist you during the waiting time. *All participants should arrive at the latest 10.30 AM at Pangkalanbun Airport. If you arrive late, you must take the speedboat to join the klotok. The speedboat costs around IDR 600.000/boat/way to be paid directly to the captain. Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continue to add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Shared Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-28\", \"text\": \"ETA : 28SEP 0715 From (CGK) Jakarta ID6202 by Batik Air\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-30\", \"text\": \"ETD : 30SEP 1025 To (SRG) Semarang ID6303 by Batik Air\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5218632,'499','MARIA DEL PILAR FRETES BIZARRO',30783,213070,'3D2N Best of Yogyakarta City Tour / C. Adhisthana (Superior Room) (car and driver)','Confirmed','JS-Java01',3,'2024-09-30','2024-10-02','Guio','Eddy',4,'Persons (2 / Double)',7560000.00,'Day 1 : Arrival at Yogyakarta Welcome to the cradle of Indonesian culture, Yogyakarta. A tourist destination for its ancient palaces, temples, batik workshops, gamelan music orchestras, court dances and wayang puppet shows. Upon your arrival in Yogyakarta a representative of Come2Indonesia will be waiting for you with a sign indicating your name to take you to your hotel and the rest of the day is free for you. Meals : - Accommodation : C. Adhisthana Hotel - Superior Room Day 2 : Yogyakarta City Tour - Prambanan and Borobodur You will start your day with breakfast at the hotel. Today’s excursion will make us get lost in the authentic magic of Yogyakarta. One of the most beautiful and complete routes of the cultural capital of Indonesia. At the scheduled time, your guide will pick you up to begin your tour to Borobudur Temple (Candi Borobudur), the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. We will tour around the temple, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano have been producing during its history. After visiting one of the most important Buddhist temples in Southeast Asia, we continue our journey to the heart of the city. We will visit the Keraton, known as the Sultan’s Palace. The palace is a complex building two centuries old, located in the heart of the city. You will hear the song of “freedom” in the bird market. We will visit the “Water Castle” that occupies the highest part at the northern end of the vast complex of Taman Sari. Then we continue to Malioboro Street, main street of Yogyakarta, with its merchants, horse carriages, taxi-bikes and markets. An incredible experience that will make hours fly by. Finishing the tour in the centre of the city of Yogyakarta, we will head northeast towards Candi Prambanan, the temple of Hinduists which have been classified as a World Heritage Site by UNESCO since 1991. It was finished around the year 856 to commemorate the victory of the descendant Sanjaya of Siva, Rikai Pikatan on the last sovereign Sailendra of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to the Trimurti, the expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the Destroyer. After this unforgettable day, we will take you back to your hotel. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : C. Adhisthana Hotel - Superior Room Day 3 : Hotel - Airport You will enjoy a well-deserved breakfast at the hotel and according to the time of your flight, we will pick you up to take you to the airport and take the flight to your next destination. End of our services. Thank you very much for exploring Yogyakarta with Come2indonesia. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'exclude : Guide, entrance fee, tipping 3D2N Yogyakarta Tour (coche y conductor) 0930 Día 04: Semarang – Yogyakarta 1001 Día 05: Templo Borobudur – Yogyakarta Tour (Kraton - Tamansari) 1002 Día 06: Templo Prambanan - Yogyakarta – Aiport','{\"date\": \"2024-09-30\", \"text\": \"ETA : 30SEP 1125 From (PKN) Pangkalanbun ID6303 by Batik Air\", \"time\": \"11:25\", \"locality\": \"AIRPORT SRG\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-02\", \"text\": \"ETD : 02OCT 1820 To (DPS) Denpasar JT566 by Lion Air\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"AIRPORT YIA\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5218751,'676','Juan Ballesteros',31015,203233,'4D3N - Surabaya Bromo Ijen Sukamade drop Bali','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-10-03','2024-10-06','Nicholas','Febrina',4,'Persons (4)',16800000.00,NULL,NULL,'4D3N Surabaya - Bromo - Ijen - Sukamade - Drop off Bali, with English speaking guide D1/03 Oct 2024: Arrival in Surabaya Airport - Transfer Bromo D2/04 Oct 2024: Bromo Tour - Transfer to Ijen D3/05 Oct 2024: Ijen Tour - Sukamade Tour (D) Accommodation: Sukamade Guest House - 2 Rooms (1 DOUBLE + 1 TWIN BED) D4/06 Oct 2024: Sukamade - Drop off Bali (B) Hotel in Bromo: Lava View Lodge on 03 - 04 Oct 2024 Hotel in Banyuwangi: Ketapang Indah Hotel on 04 - 05 Oct 2024 Flight detail on 03 Oct 2024: ETA in Surabaya at 09.00 by Batik Air ID6134 from Pangkalan Bun. Drop off in Bali on 06 Oct 2024: Narasoma Homestay & Retreat Jl. Monkey Forest Gg. Beji No. 35, Ubud Phone: +62823-4167-3020','{\"date\": \"2024-10-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5218794,'735','Alejandro Palma del Moral',31158,216310,'VIP Service Fast Track Domestic Departure & International Departure - Jakarta Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-22','2024-08-22','Guio','Febrina',5,'Person (1)',7020000.00,'Departure International: Service start from meet clients at departure hall until client boarding.',NULL,'Flight details: ETA 15.15 by Super Air Jet IU735 from Denpasar on 22 Aug ETD 18.30 by Qatar Airways QR957 to Doha on 22 Aug Meet our assistance, who will be waiting for you at the end of the aviobridge and then escort and assist you to the conveyor belt to collect their luggage (if any). Then escort you to international departure gate for the check in and fast assistance at immigration counters, assistance through customs clearance waiting until boarding time. Please be informed that our Airport Representative will bring a paging board with your name “Mr. Alejandro Palma del Moral\" on it.','{\"date\": \"2024-08-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5219304,'736','Guadalupe Tinaquero Domínguez',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-10','2024-09-11','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',784000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-09-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5219320,'720','Kimberly Cohen',30508,202897,'Uluwatu Temple and Kecak Dance','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-22','2024-09-22','Ayu','Eddy',1,'Person (1)',1472800.00,'This half-day tour, is an exciting tour package to visit Padang-Padang Beach, Uluwatu Temple, the famous Balinese Hindu Temple in south part of Bali with breathtaking view of sunset and Indian Ocean. Uluwatu Temple is one of Balinese Hindu Temples located right on the petrifying hill with the crevasse exist in the right and left side. Uluwatu Temple is one of Sad Khayangan (6 biggest temple in Bali) owns magnificent view of the Indian Ocean and sunset as a backdrop. This temple is very amazing where the location is right on the narrow peninsula with deep seawater under it. This tour package is combined with the spectacular Balinese traditional dance performance of Kecak Dance. Balinese Kecak Dance is a spectacular traditional dance with the group of people playing this dance with fire game. It is very exciting and unique dance due to the sound of gamelan is not using the normal gamelan but use their mouth. The dancers make the compact choir with the exquisite dance movement that is one of this dance features. After the dance we returned back to the hotel or seafood restaurant in Jimbaran.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-22\", \"text\": \"Kayumas Seminyak Resort Jl. Pura Telaga Waja No.18A, Kerobokan Kelod\", \"time\": \"14:00\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-22\", \"text\": \"Kayumas Seminyak Resort Jl. Pura Telaga Waja No.18A, Kerobokan Kelod\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5219327,'736','Guadalupe Tinaquero Domínguez',30783,216589,'4D3N Jogja-Bromo-Surabaya Incl. Train / A. Melia Purosani (Deluxe Room) & Bromo Terrace (Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-09-11','2024-09-14','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2 / Double)',17472000.00,'D1 : Arrival Yogyakarta International Airport – Visit Prambanan Temple – Transfer to hotel D2 : Borobudur temple incl. Mendut and Pawon ,Yogyakarta City Tour Visit Sultan Palace, Watercastle and Bird/Traditional Market D3 : Jogja – Mojokerto by Train then continue drive to Bromo – overnight in Bromo D4 : Sunrise and Mt. Bromo crater tour incl. Jeep ( Horse rise Exclude ) – Transfer to Surabaya airport',NULL,'Flight schedule in YIA : ETA : 09.15 by Garuda Indonesia GA204 from Jakarta on 11 Sept Flight schedule in Surabaya : ETD : 14.10 by Lion Air JT910 to Denpasar on 14 Sept D1/11 Sept : Arrival Yogyakarta - City Tour - Prambanan Temple D2/12 Sept : Borobudur Temple - Candirejo D3/13 Sept : Yogyakarta to Bromo by Train D4/14 Sept : Bromo Sunrise - Transfer to Surabaya Airport Yogyakarta based on Melia Purosani - Double Deluxe room Bromo based on Bromo Terrace - Double Deluxe room','{\"date\": \"2024-09-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5219359,'720','Kimberly Cohen',30508,202897,'Padang Padang - Uluwatu Temple and Kecak Dance','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-22','2024-09-22','Ayu','Eddy',1,'Person (1)',1472800.00,'This half-day tour, is an exciting tour package to visit Padang-Padang Beach, Uluwatu Temple, the famous Balinese Hindu Temple in south part of Bali with breathtaking view of sunset and Indian Ocean. Uluwatu Temple is one of Balinese Hindu Temples located right on the petrifying hill with the crevasse exist in the right and left side. Uluwatu Temple is one of Sad Khayangan (6 biggest temple in Bali) owns magnificent view of the Indian Ocean and sunset as a backdrop. This temple is very amazing where the location is right on the narrow peninsula with deep seawater under it. This tour package is combined with the spectacular Balinese traditional dance performance of Kecak Dance. Balinese Kecak Dance is a spectacular traditional dance with the group of people playing this dance with fire game. It is very exciting and unique dance due to the sound of gamelan is not using the normal gamelan but use their mouth. The dancers make the compact choir with the exquisite dance movement that is one of this dance features. After the dance we returned back to the hotel or seafood restaurant in Jimbaran.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-22\", \"text\": \"Kayumas Seminyak Resort Jl. Pura Telaga Waja No.18A, Kerobokan Kelod\", \"time\": \"13:00\", \"locality\": \"READY AT LOBBY\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-22\", \"text\": \"Kayumas Seminyak Resort Jl. Pura Telaga Waja No.18A, Kerobokan Kelod\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5219360,'736','Guadalupe Tinaquero Domínguez',30508,212292,'Airport to Munduk','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-14','2024-09-14','Guio','Komang',1,'Persons (1-3)',616000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting at the arrival hall exit, holding a signboard of your name/group name. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 3 hours after the flight’s estimated arrival time (ETA). - For any flight delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-09-14\", \"text\": \"ETA : 16.10 by Lion Air JT910 from Surabaya on 14 Sept 2024\", \"time\": \"16:10\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-14\", \"text\": \"Jl. Asah Gobleg, Gobleg, Kec. Banjar, Kabupaten Buleleng, Bali 81152 Telepon: (0368) 2080123\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Munduk Moding Plantation\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5219375,'736','Guadalupe Tinaquero Domínguez',30578,212084,'One Bedroom Villa with Jacuzzi','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-09-14','2024-09-16','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',10674944.00,'Experience the epitome of luxury at our One Bedroom Villas with Jacuzzi, offering breathtaking vistas of the lush hills cascading down to the azure sea, with a backdrop of distant jungles. As the day transitions to dusk, immerse yourself in the captivating spectacle of the sun descending into the Java Sea. These spacious villas (95m²) envelop you in comfort, featuring merbau tropical hardwood parquet flooring in the bedroom and living area, complemented by Sulawesi cream marble in the bathroom. The opulent interiors boast king-size poster beds, handcrafted tropical hardwood couches, and locally inspired artwork, creating an inviting ambiance. Expansive glass panel doors envelop the villa, ensuring panoramic views from every angle. Unwind in a generously sized handcrafted terrazzo bathtub, filled with the soothing essence of the mountains’ water (available upon request). The indoor shower area, complete with separate sinks, offers convenience and elegance. For an immersive experience, an outdoor shower amidst a private garden adorned with flowers provides a refreshing connection with nature. Elevating your stay to unparalleled heights, a private jacuzzi awaits, allowing you to soak in pure relaxation while reveling in the tranquil surroundings of Munduk Moding Plantation.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5219397,'736','Guadalupe Tinaquero Domínguez',30508,215968,'1D Bali Tour (Munduk Waterfall-Ulun danu Beratan-Jati Luwih-Tanah Lot)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-16','2024-09-16','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',2128000.00,NULL,NULL,'The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-16\", \"text\": \"J