024-11-10','Norberto','Febrina',2,'Persons (2)',7920000.00,NULL,NULL,'3D2N Surabaya - Tumpak Sewu - Bromo Tour - Surabaya, with English speaking guide 08 Nov 2024 / Day 1: Arrival in Surabaya - Transfer to Tumpak Sewu 09 Nov 2024 / Day 2: Tumpak Sewu Waterfall Tour - Transfer to Bromo 10 Nov 2024 / Day 3: Bromo Tour - Transfer out to Surabaya Airport. Flight details on 08 Nov 2024: ETA in Surabaya at 15:35 by Lion Air JT879 from Ambon on 08 Nov Accommodation in Bromo on 09 - 10 Nov 2024: Jiwa Jawa Resort Bromo Drop off in Surabaya on 10 Nov 2024: Cordia Hotel Surabaya Airport','{\"date\": \"2024-11-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5219530,'737','Begona Velasco Makuba',30684,200640,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-09','2024-11-10','Norberto','Febrina',1,'Double',1638000.00,'Designed to embody fresher and younger ambience, our Deluxe Room is a convenient stay for those who plan a relatively shorter stay in Semarang. The room is provided with either a king size or deluxe twin beds.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-11-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5219531,'737','Begona Velasco Makuba',31365,216725,'Standard Room (Room Breakfast)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-10','2024-11-11','Norberto','Febrina',1,'Double',576000.00,'This twin or double room has air conditioning, desk and a flat-screen cable TV. Private bathroom comes with a shower and free toiletries.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-11-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5219558,'737','Begona Velasco Makuba',30528,215444,'6D5N East-West Sumba Tour','Confirmed','6DSW-ST',6,'2024-11-11','2024-11-16','Norberto','Febrina',2,'Persons (2)',26280000.00,'START : TMC AIRPORT (TAMBOLAKA) FINISH : WGP AIRPORT (WAINGAPU) DAY 1 : ARRIVAL TMC AIRPORT - SUMBA CULTURAL HOUSE - SUMBA\'S CASHEW & COFFEE PRODUCT JOURNEY - LENDONGARA HILL SUNSET Upon arrival at the airport of Tambolaka in Waitabula, meet and greet with your driver and guide, the Explore Sumba Team. Before starting our journey, you will go to the local restaurant for lunch first. After that, you will visit Rumah Budaya Sumba (Sumba’s cultural house). This is a good place to start, a place where you can learn about the island. It was built in the style of a traditional Sumbanese house, and the surrounding grounds are dotted with Marapu stone carvings. Among other artifacts, the collection includes ikat, stone and wood carvings, traditional jewelry, and a handful of everyday items you can find here. Next, you go to visit the Talasi Estate Factory. Here you can find the locals producing the Sumbanese cashew and coffee. They will also take you to explore their farm and connect with the Talasi community and farmers. You will also get a chance to taste the cashew milk or weejewa coffee, produced directly by the farmers here. Then check in at your hotel and take a bit of rest until the perfect time to catch the beautiful sunset on Lendongara Hill. In the quite a quiet place where you can sit and relax by enjoying the stunning hill view, the ocean view from a distance, as well as the panorama of the villages. After the sunset, you go back to the hotel. Meals : Lunch Accomodation : A. Maringi Eco Resort (Bamboo Pavilion) DAY 2 : WEEKURI LAKE - MANDORAK BEACH - RATENGGARO VILLAGE - PERO BEACH SUNSET Breakfast at the hotel. Today you will explore more of the South-West part of Sumba Island. You’re going to the Kodi area, and you will make a visit to Weekuri Lake, a crystal-clear lake that makes it a great place to swim and to relax. Spend some time in the lake for a short (or long) dip. Do not miss the opportunity to walk around the rocks and reefs where you can also see the Oceans from one side. Next to Weekuri Lake, you will find Mandorak Beach, guarded by two huge rock ridges pointing to the middle and crystal-clear water. Lunch boxes will be provided here because there are no restaurants in the area. The next visit will be to Ratenggaro Village. Here you will see the traditional high rooftops houses (actually the highest rooftops in whole Sumba) made all by hand and traditionally. This village is the only one of a few traditional villages left in the area, and while the village is just a compound of some houses, each house can accommodate up to 50 family members. During the harvesting season, however, most of the villagers will stay in their fields to work and only leave the elders and children in the village. This village is beautiful because it is built in front of the beach. After visiting the village, you will go to Pero beach to enjoy the sunset view. Then back to the hotel. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Box Accomodation : A. Maringi Eco Resort (Bamboo Pavilion) DAY 3 : LOCAL MARKET - WAIKACURA RICEFIELD - LAPOPU WATERFALL After breakfast, you will check out the hotel today, and go explore West Sumba. On the way, you will visit a local market where you can engage with the locals and see that they sell their local products directly. Try to connect with them with our guide assistance! Continuing to make a visit to the Waikacura area, do a short trek in the ricefield, where you can also enjoy the beautiful view of the small river located in the middle of the ricefield. Then you go to the local restaurant for lunch. Next on our adventure will be the Lapopu Waterfall. After a drive through the endless hilly and green landscape of Sumba, you will arrive near the waterfall. To visit the waterfall, you will need to do a small hike of approximately 15 minutes and cross a bamboo bridge to get there. There is a nice spot to sit down where you can watch the water find its way down the hill. After that, you will go to your resort. Meals : Breakfast Accomodation : A. Rua Beach Resort (Deluxe Room) DAY 4 : PRAIJING VILLAGE - ANAKALANG VILLAGE - WALAKARI BEACH SUNSET Having breakfast and checking out from of the hotel. Today you will go to the east part of Sumba, and during the long drive you will make some visits on the way. Our first visit will be to the village of Praijing. Praijing village is a traditional village uphill, surrounded by lots of greenery. This is one of the few villages where you can actually have a beautiful overview of the entire village and get an idea of how the village is conducted. Take some time to walk around the village; the elders occupy most of the houses, and kids are always around to share their smiles. Next, drive to East Sumba. On the way, you make a visit to the village of Anakalang, which is located in central Sumba. In this village, you will get a chance to visit the big megalithic tomb stone owned by the late king of Sumba in Pasunga Village. A lunch box will be provided. Next, go to your hotel in East Sumba for check-in. Take a bit of rest until the perfect time for the sunset at Walakiri Beach. You will be watching the sunset here while exploring the beach with its beautiful mangroves. Don’t hesitate and walk towards the small and magical trees that are growing inside the water. When the sun has disappeared, go to the hotel, where you can take a rest. Meals : Lunch Accomodation : A. Morinda Villa (Deluxe Hill View Room) DAY 5 : TANGGEDU WATERFALL - PURU KAMBERA BEACH AND SAVANNAH Enjoying the breakfast at the hotel. When you have enough rest, we will start our adventure today to explore the beauty of the waterfall and savannah in East Sumba, where you can see the horses and the cows free to walk to find their own space and foods. On the way to Tanggedu waterfall, we will have a view of Puru Kambera Savannah. You can make a stop here to enjoy the ambience. Tanggedu is a stunning waterfall in East Sumba. To get into this waterfall we need to do about 20 minutes of flat trekking and about 15 minutes of passing the stairs. The view that you will get along the way is really amazing. Your lunch box will be prepared. After the trekking, we will visit Puru Kambera Beach. Relax on the beach until the time you want to go back to the hotel. Meals : Lunch Accomodation : A. Morinda Villa (Deluxe Hill View Room) DAY 6 : IKAT TENUN VILLAGE - OUT WGP AIRPORT After breakfast and checking out of the hotel, you will continue the trip to do the last visit of our trip today, to the village that produces Ikat Tenun, the traditional Sumbanese fabrics and costumes. You may try to wear the Ikat Tenun and make a family picture by wearing a Sumbanese traditional costume here. Then go to the airport for your flight back home or to your next destination. End of the trip. Meals : Breakfast Accomodation : -',NULL,'6D5N East-West Sumba Tour, with English speaking guide 11 Nov 2024 / DAY 01: Arrival Waingapu Airport – Hotel Accommodation: Morinda Villa (Deluxe Hill View) 12 Nov 2024 / DAY 02: Ikat Tenun Village – Tanggedu Waterfall – Puru Kambera Beach & Savanah (B,L) Accommodation : Morinda Villa (Deluxe Hill View) 13 Nov / DAY 03: Wairinding Hill – Lapopu Waterfall – Praijing Village (B,L) Accommodation : The Sanubari Resort (Garden Pool Villa) 14 Nov / DAY 04: Free Day (B) Accommodation : The Sanubari Resort (Garden Pool Villa) 15 Nov / DAY 05: Sumba Hospitality Foundation - Ratenggaro Village – Weekuri Lake – Mandorak Beach – Lendongara Hill Sunset (B,L) Accommodation : Mario Beach Hotel (Deluxe Jineng Room) 16 Nov / DAY 06: Out Tambolaka Airport Accommodation : - Flight details: ETA in Waingapu at 16:35 by Wings Air IW1884 from Denpasar on 11 Nov ETD from Tambolaka at 12:25 by Wings Air IW1833 to Denpasar on 16 Nov','{\"date\": \"2024-11-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5219564,'737','Begona Velasco Makuba',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-16','2024-11-16','Norberto','Febrina',2,'Persons (1-3)',840000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting at the arrival hall exit, holding a signboard of your name/group name. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 3 hours after the flight’s estimated arrival time (ETA). - For any flight delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-11-16\", \"text\": \"ETA 13:00 by Wings Air IW1833 from Tambolaka on 16 Nov\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Denpasar Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Tejaprana Resort\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5219574,'737','Begona Velasco Makuba',30508,207262,'Ubud to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-22','2024-11-22','Norberto','Febrina',2,'Persons (1-3)',840000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver will wait up to 30 minutes after your scheduled pickup time. - Please keep in mind that any further delay could affect your timely arrival at the airport for your flight. - For any changes in flight departure time, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available). - Requests for pickup time earlier than originally booked are subject to availability.','{\"date\": \"2024-11-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"09:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Tejaprana Bisma\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-22\", \"text\": \"ETD 13:45 by Garuda Indonesia GA409 to Jakarta on 22 Nov\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Denpasar Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5219575,'737','Begona Velasco Makuba',30805,207114,'DPS-CGK','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-22','2024-11-22','Norberto','Febrina',2,'Person',3520000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-11-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5219597,'736','Guadalupe Tinaquero Domínguez',30508,207112,'1D Nusa Penida West Tour','Confirmed','C2I-BALI19',1,'2024-09-19','2024-09-19','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',952000.00,'Today, embark on a unique adventure as you explore the enchanting Nusa Penida, a neighboring island of Bali. Your day begins with a convenient hotel pick-up, followed by a journey to the Sanur port where a fast boat awaits to transport you to Nusa Penida in just 30 minutes. Nusa Penida, located in the southeast of Bali, is a true paradise waiting to be discovered. Upon your arrival, a friendly driver will be ready to guide you through the day\'s captivating itinerary. Your first destination is the mesmerizing Angel\'s Billabong, a natural wonder resembling a pristine pool nestled in the heart of nature. Take a refreshing swim, but exercise caution on the steps and heed your driver\'s recommendations. Next, we head to Broken Beach, a charming bay that was once a cave, now open to the sky, offering a unique and captivating scenery. Although inaccessible by land, the view from above is nothing short of breathtaking. Keep an eye out for the possibility of spotting giant manta rays gracefully gliding on the water\'s surface. Our journey continues to the renowned Kelingking Beach, famous for its stunning cliffs and the iconic hand-shaped mountain. This beach is not only one of the island\'s most famous attractions but also a favorite subject for photographers. We conclude the day at the pristine Crystal Beach, where white sands meet turquoise waters in perfect harmony. As the sun sets, you\'ll have the opportunity to relax and savor the beauty that surrounds you. This unforgettable experience concludes with a return boat trip to Bali from the Toya Pakeh port at 16:30, followed by a comfortable transfer to your hotel.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-19\", \"text\": \"ETA : 08.20 by The Angkal Fastboat from Kusamba\", \"time\": \"08:20\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Sampalan Port, Nusa Penida\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-19\", \"text\": \"Sakti, Kec. Nusa Penida, Kabupaten Klungkung, Bali 80771 Telepon: (0361) 6208999\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Maua Nusa Penida\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5219604,'736','Guadalupe Tinaquero Domínguez',30508,207337,'Snorkeling to Nusa Penida (from Nusa Penida) (Sharing Trip)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-20','2024-09-20','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',1232000.00,NULL,NULL,'The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-20\", \"text\": \"Sakti, Kec. Nusa Penida, Kabupaten Klungkung, Bali 80771 Telepon: (0361) 6208999\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Maua Nusa Penida\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-20\", \"text\": \"Sakti, Kec. Nusa Penida, Kabupaten Klungkung, Bali 80771 Telepon: (0361) 6208999\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Maua Nusa Penida\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5219605,'736','Guadalupe Tinaquero Domínguez',30508,207391,'Transfer Out Nusa Penida','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-21','2024-09-21','Guio','Komang',1,'Persons (1-3)',224000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-21\", \"text\": \"Sakti, Kec. Nusa Penida, Kabupaten Klungkung, Bali 80771 Telepon: (0361) 6208999\", \"time\": \"07:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Maua Nusa Penida\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-21\", \"text\": \"ETD : 09.15 by Bluewater Express to Gili Air\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Buyuk Harbour\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5219608,'736','Guadalupe Tinaquero Domínguez',30805,212255,'CGK-YIA','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-11','2024-09-11','Guio','Komang',2,'Person',3210000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5219612,'736','Guadalupe Tinaquero Domínguez',30805,202685,'SUB-DPS','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-14','2024-09-14','Guio','Komang',2,'Person',1712000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5219617,'736','Guadalupe Tinaquero Domínguez',32602,215975,'One Bedroom Pool Villa','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-09-21','2024-09-24','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',19620000.00,'Each room offers the same comfort: one bedroom villas with terrace, swimming pool, kitchenette and office space, comfortable sunbeds, lovely coconut garden. Particular care to the quality of the beddings, the home stylist Valérie Barkowski has added her touch of originality with a predominant colour selection of orange, grey, red, green, bordeaux or black. Choose your holiday colour!',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-24\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5219697,'739','Mrs. SANDRA OTOBALEA IBAÑEZ',31015,203230,'2D1N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Tour drop Mojokerto Train Station','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-08-30','2024-08-31','Nicholas','Praba',2,'Persons (2)',4480000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-30\", \"text\": \"Domestic Arrival ETA 10:00 by Batik Air ID6134 from Pangkalan Bu\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Juanda International Airport Surabaya\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-31\", \"text\": \"ETD 17:31 by Sancaka Executive to Yogyakarta\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Mojokerto Train Station\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5219700,'738','J.V. Tolsá & Party (2pax)',31015,214881,'3D2N Surabaya - Tumpak Sewu (only transfer) - Bromo - Ijen - Drop Bali / C. Bromo Terrace (Deluxe Ro','Confirmed','C2I-JAVA10',3,'2024-10-18','2024-10-20','Jacob','Eddy',2,'Persons (2 / Double)',11040000.00,'Day 1 : Surabaya - Bromo Volcano Skirts Upon arrival at Surabaya airport, our representative will be waiting for you with a sign indicating your name to begin the journey of about 4 hours to your hotel on the slopes of the majestic Bromo Volcano. Check-in at your hotel for deserved rest after so many hours traveling. Meals : - Accommodation : C. Bromo Terrace - Deluxe Room Day 2 : Bromo Tour, The Dawn - Fumaroles - Ijen Very early, your guide and a jeep driver will be waiting for you at the hotel to attend one of the most spectacular sunrises in Indonesia. Even though you have to get up early, it will be worth it. You will climb to a high point first in full darkness and, little by little the first rays of sun are giving way to a huge and indescribable caldera that makes up the entire view of the Bromo and Semeru Natural Park. With Bromo, a volcano of great fumaroles and behind it, the Semeru Volcano with explosions every 20 minutes exactly, will make you have one of the most rewarding experiences ever. After enjoying the sunrise, by jeep, you will descend to the sea of sand. You can walk across the sand dune and go to Bromo volcano. After climbing some stairs you can reach the very edge of its crater and see the impressive activity it has. You return to the hotel to cool off and enjoy your breakfast. At the agreed time, you will leave for our next destination, the Ijen volcano. This section lasts about 7-8 hours by car where you will make a stop to eat. Take this trip to rest. You will arrive at the appointed hotel near Ijen crater, where you will check in and enjoy your well-deserved rest. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : C. Ketapang Indah - Superior Room Day 3 : Trekking Ijen - Bali The day has finally come to visit one of the most attractive volcanoes in Indonesia! One of the last open pit sulfur mines that survive on the planet. For this climb you can choose between two schedules; leave very early at 1 AM to see the blue fire (please note that it is not always visible, for example during rainy days) or leave more quietly at 4 AM only for the sunrise. You can decide later when you meet the guide. Once you pick you up at your hotel, you will head towards the village of Licin to reach the slope of the volcano to begin the steep climb to the crater of the volcano. During this trek, your guide will give you double filter masks to protect you from the natural chemicals of sulfur. At an altitude of 2883 meters and when dawn begins, an incredible contrast of colors will open before your eyes. A yellow earth scene and a large turquoise blue lake inside the crater that contrast with a suspended white cloud that is continuously expelling the volcano. In turn, among so much beauty you will see the local miners do what is said to be one of the toughest jobs in the world. These miners go down to the crater of the volcano to load 80 to 100 kilos of sulfur on their shoulders and then sell it. After this amazing experience on the edge of Ijen volcano crater, you will begin the descent with an incredible panoramic view of the mountains that make up the national park. You will be taken you to your hotel to cool off and have breakfast and you will start the journey to Bali for about 5 hours at least, depending on where you stay in Bali. To do this, you will go first to the port of Banyuwangi where you will take the ferry to cross to Bali. It is a journey of only 30 minutes, but remember to adjust your watch by an hour due to the time zone change. Welcome to the island of the Gods. End of service. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'18 - 19 OCT 2024 Bromo Terrace 19 - 20 OCT 2024 Ketapang Indah 18 OCT Arrival Surabaya – Tumbak Sewu( not include tumpak sewu tickets they will buy there,only transfer) – Bromo 19 OCT Tour Bromo – Ijen 20 OCT Tour Ijen - Bali','{\"date\": \"2024-10-18\", \"text\": \"ETA : SUB APT / 18 OCT 08:35 IP200 by Pelita Air From Jakarta\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"SURABAYA AIRPORT\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-20\", \"text\": \"The Nest Canggu - Surf Hostel and Homestay Address : Jl. Nelayan No.8a, Canggu, Kec. Kuta Utara, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80361 Phone: 0878-6117-5200\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5219707,'738','J.V. Tolsá & Party (2pax)',30673,200559,'Deluxe Double Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-18','2024-10-19','Jacob','Eddy',1,'Double',1260000.00,'Designed to capture nature vibes. Slide open the door to your private terrace to let in the fresh mountain air and relax.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5219710,'739','Mrs. SANDRA OTOBALEA IBAÑEZ',30783,201646,'Borobudur Temple - Yogyakarta City Tour - Prambanan Temple','Confirmed','C2I-JAVA15',1,'2024-09-01','2024-09-01','Nicholas','Praba',2,'Persons (2)',3696000.00,'This excursion will make you lose yourselves in the authentic magic of Yogyakarta. One of the most beautiful and complete routes of the cultural capital of Indonesia. At the scheduled time, your guide will pick you up to begin the tour of Borobudur, the great Stupa, the largest Buddhist monument in the world and one of the seven wonders. Depending on where you stay in the city, the drive can be 1-1,5 hours to the temple. Arrival at the temple, you will walk around the garden area, observe the hundreds and centenary statues of Buddha and witness how dozens of Buddhists come to preach from all over the world. Historically it was established during the relatively brief Sailendra dynasty of Central Java between 778 and 856 BC and is in constant restoration due to the breaks that the tremors of the neighbouring Merapi volcano has been producing during its history. After visiting one of the most important Buddhist temples in Southeast Asia, you will continue the journey to the heart of the city. You will visit the Keraton, or also known as the Sultan’s Palace. The palace is a complex building two centuries old. Next, you will hear the song of the “freedom” of the birds in the bird market, you will visit the “Water Castle” that occupies the highest part at the northern end of the vast complex of Taman Sari. Then, stroll around Malioboro Street, one of the main streets of Yogyakarta, with its merchants, horse carriages, taxi-bikes and markets. An incredible experience that will make the hours fly by. Finishing the tour in the centre of the city of Yogyakarta, you will head northeast towards Prambanan, the temple of Hinduists and classified as a World Heritage Site by UNESCO since 1991. This temple was completed in 856 AD to commemorate the victory of the descendant of Sanjaya dynasty, Rikai Pikatan, against the last Shailendra sovereign of Central Java. Take your time to enjoy each carving on the rocks and feel the spirituality that each of the stones perched in this set of more than 200 Hindu temples that are dedicated to Shiva, one of the Trimurti which is an expression of God as the Creator, the Preserver and the Destroyer. After this unforgettable day, and take you to your hotel.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-01\", \"text\": \"Jl. Jend. Sudirman No.69, Terban, Kec. Gondokusuman, Kota Yogyakarta, Daerah Istimewa Yogyakarta\", \"time\": \"07:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Swiss-Belboutique Yogyakarta\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-01\", \"text\": \"Jl. Jend. Sudirman No.69, Terban, Kec. Gondokusuman, Kota Yogyakarta, Daerah Istimewa Yogyakarta\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Swiss-Belboutique Yogyakarta\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5219718,'739','Mrs. SANDRA OTOBALEA IBAÑEZ',30673,200559,'Deluxe Double Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-08-30','2024-08-31','Nicholas','Praba',1,'Double',1176000.00,'Designed to capture nature vibes. Slide open the door to your private terrace to let in the fresh mountain air and relax.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-08-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-08-31\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5219723,'739','Mrs. SANDRA OTOBALEA IBAÑEZ',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route (Taman Ayun - Jatiluwih - Ulun Danu Bratan - Tanah Lot)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-03','2024-09-03','Nicholas','Praba',2,'Persons (2)',1747200.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-03\", \"text\": \"Jl. Raya Semat, gg. Jalak Indah no. 9, Badung, Bali Telepon: 0813-3749-5233\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Amandaya Canggu\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-03\", \"text\": \"Jln. Kayangan, Kenderan, Tegallalang, Kabupaten Gianyar Telphone: (0361) 9086234/ WA +62812 39363585\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Kayangan Villa Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5219729,'740','Alicia Morato Gonzalez',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-04','2024-09-05','Jacob','Wiwik',1,'Double',784000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'FLIGHT DETAIL: ETA: 07.40 by QR958 From Doha on 04 Sept 2024. ETD: 06.00 by Batik Air ID6202 to Pangkalan Bun on 05 Sept 2024. Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-09-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5219730,'740','Alicia Morato Gonzalez',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-09-05','2024-09-07','Jacob','Wiwik',2,'Persons (2)',10080000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'FLIGHT DETAIL: ETA: 07.15 by Batik Air ID6202 from Jakarta on 05 Sept 2024. ETD: 10.25 by Batik Air ID6303 to Semarang on 07 Sept 2024. Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5219732,'701','Maria Luisa Bordeje Laguna',30728,207377,'The Southern Gilis Tour (Nanggu, Sudak, Kedis)','Confirmed','EXC 09',1,'2024-09-10','2024-09-10','Melysa','Tami',8,'Persons (6-9)',8294400.00,'Discover the beauty of the New Generation of Gili islands in development. We sail from Batu Kijuk harbor, by traditional motorized outriggers to pristine islands and beaches, amazing snorkeling and no mass tourism on these pearls of islands. On your way to the islands we stop off at the village of Banyumulek to see the Sasak women producing earthenware pottery, as they have done for generations. We then reach the harbor for the trip to Gili Nanggu, an exotic small island with the turquoise water and magnificent aquatic life. We do some island hopping to Gili Sudak where a delicious lunch awaits you in Nirvana Gili Sudak and free at own your leisure. Then, continue to Gili Kedis, a tiny island with the white sand beach where you can get absolute relaxation of the day. On the way back to your hotel, you may stop by at Mareje hill for picture taking.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-10\", \"text\": \"Jl. Sorong Jukung No.Desa, Kandang Kaoq, Tanjung, Kec. Tj., Kabupaten Lombok Utara\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Diamond Beach Villa - Lombok\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5219751,'741','DEBRA ANN WIERUS ONEILL',30719,201080,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-29','2024-09-30','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Twin',952000.00,'Swiss-Belhotel Sorong boast 126 guest rooms in Sorong with all the comforts you would expect from an international chain of four-star hotels in Sorong. Enjoy 37-inch LED TVs, cable channels, high-speed internet access and a full range of other amenities that will make your stay here the most comfortable one possible.',NULL,'Check-in time 14.00 Check-out time 12.00 Early check-in is subject to availability upon arrival.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5219752,'741','DEBRA ANN WIERUS ONEILL',30719,214471,'Transport Fee (from Airport to Hotel)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-29','2024-09-29','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Per Car',280000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5219762,'736','Guadalupe Tinaquero Domínguez',30582,203387,'One Bedroom Luxury Villas','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-09-19','2024-09-21','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',7884800.00,'Each One Bedroom Luxury Villa is designed with a private infinity pool, scenic view across the Gamat Bay or garden view, and some have a small private garden. Every villas features the following: An integrated universal power outlet, Room safe (suitable for storing laptops), Cable TV with international news and movie channels, Eco-friendly bathroom amenities, Coffee and tea-making facilities.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5219763,'740','Alicia Morato Gonzalez',30644,201464,'4D3N Toraja Package (3N Toraja)/Santai Hotel - Deluxe','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-09-16','2024-09-19','Jacob','Wiwik',2,'Persons (2 / Double)',14000000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-16\", \"text\": \"ETA: 09.10 by Wings Air IW1350 from Makassar on 16 Sept 2024.\", \"time\": \"09:10\", \"locality\": \"PALOPO AIRPORT\", \"location\": null}','{\"da