24-09-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5220939,'742','Sara Rea Maquieira',30508,215968,'1D Bali Tour (Kehen Temple – Pengelipuran – Tukad Cepung – Besakih)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-12','2024-09-12','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',1792000.00,NULL,NULL,'The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-12\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kec. Gianyar, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 978018\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 1 Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-12\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kec. Gianyar, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 978018\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 1 Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5220944,'742','Sara Rea Maquieira',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route (Taman Ayun-Jati Luwih-Bedugul- Tanah Lot','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-13','2024-09-13','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',1747200.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-13\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kec. Gianyar, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 978018\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 1 Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-13\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kec. Gianyar, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 978018\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 1 Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5220949,'742','Sara Rea Maquieira',30508,202893,'Lempuyang Temple Tour (enganan – Playa Virgin – Templo Lempuyang – Tirta Gangga)','Confirmed','C2I-BALI11',1,'2024-09-14','2024-09-14','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',1792000.00,'At the agreed time, our guide will pick you up to start the tour in the eastern part of Bali. The first place you will visit is Goa Lawah Temple. Goa Lawah Temple consists of two names, \"Goa\" which means cave and \"Lawah\" which means bat. Several thousand bats are flying in the cave as the name suggests. With the lights fading as you go deeper inside the cave, it gives off a very strange atmosphere. From Goa Lawah, we continue our way to Lempuyang Temple. Upon arrival, the temple will greet you with its gratifying panorama that extends into infinity. On a clear, sunny day, you\'ll be able to gaze out over the mountains, Amlapura city, and Mount Agung, an incredibly magnificent sight that\'s beautiful beyond words. This portrait of heaven is beautifully framed by the Gapura Candi Bentar (the gate of the temple). Our journey continues to visit Tirta Gangga. The site is a paradise surrounded by water, with all the pools decorated with unusual statues. With its seclusion and a view of the surrounding rice paddies, Tirta Gangga is a wonderful place. At the end of the trip we go to Tenganan Village, the most famous Bali Agas (the “original” Bali people) in the city. With its characteristics, the city village is arranged in parallel along the wide main road paved with rows of cobblestones. In Tenganan, women still weave the famous Kamben Geringsing, or \"burnt cloth,\" which has the power to immunize the wearer against evil. We take a close look at what they do in their daily lives in a traditional lifestyle. From Tenganan, we will transfer you to the hotel.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-14\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kec. Gianyar, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 978018\", \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 1 Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-14\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kec. Gianyar, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 978018\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 1 Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5220963,'742','Sara Rea Maquieira',30508,207112,'1D Nusa Penida West Tour','Confirmed','C2I-BALI19',1,'2024-09-15','2024-09-15','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',952000.00,'Today, embark on a unique adventure as you explore the enchanting Nusa Penida, a neighboring island of Bali. Your day begins with a convenient hotel pick-up, followed by a journey to the Sanur port where a fast boat awaits to transport you to Nusa Penida in just 30 minutes. Nusa Penida, located in the southeast of Bali, is a true paradise waiting to be discovered. Upon your arrival, a friendly driver will be ready to guide you through the day\'s captivating itinerary. Your first destination is the mesmerizing Angel\'s Billabong, a natural wonder resembling a pristine pool nestled in the heart of nature. Take a refreshing swim, but exercise caution on the steps and heed your driver\'s recommendations. Next, we head to Broken Beach, a charming bay that was once a cave, now open to the sky, offering a unique and captivating scenery. Although inaccessible by land, the view from above is nothing short of breathtaking. Keep an eye out for the possibility of spotting giant manta rays gracefully gliding on the water\'s surface. Our journey continues to the renowned Kelingking Beach, famous for its stunning cliffs and the iconic hand-shaped mountain. This beach is not only one of the island\'s most famous attractions but also a favorite subject for photographers. We conclude the day at the pristine Crystal Beach, where white sands meet turquoise waters in perfect harmony. As the sun sets, you\'ll have the opportunity to relax and savor the beauty that surrounds you. This unforgettable experience concludes with a return boat trip to Bali from the Toya Pakeh port at 16:30, followed by a comfortable transfer to your hotel.',NULL,'Return Fastboat by The Angkal Fastboat ETD : 08.00 fastboat to Nusa Penida from Kusamba ETA : 16.00 fastboat from Nusa Penida to Kusamba The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-15\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kec. Gianyar, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 978018\", \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 1 Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-15\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kec. Gianyar, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 978018\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 1 Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5220971,'742','Sara Rea Maquieira',30508,207379,'Ubud to Padang Bai','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-16','2024-09-16','Guio','Komang',1,'Persons (1-3)',560000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-16\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kec. Gianyar, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 978018\", \"time\": \"06:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Pertiwi Bisma 1 Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-16\", \"text\": \"ETD : 08.30 by Gili Gili Fastboat from Padangbai to Gili Air\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Padangbai Harbour\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5220976,'743','MR. ADRIAN ENRIQUE RAGA GIL',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-12','2024-10-13','Guio','Praba',1,'Double',882000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Flight details: 12 October 2024 ETA 07:40 by Turkish Airlines TK508 from Istanbul 13 October 2024 ETD 06:00 by Batik Air ID6202 to Pangkalan Bun Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-10-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5221007,'742','Sara Rea Maquieira',32607,215991,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-09-16','2024-09-19','Guio','Komang',1,'Double',4032000.00,'At 30 m2 room size, welcome to Deluxe Room with garden view. Sleep soundly during your trip to one of Gili Islands in Lombok, West Nusa Tenggara, Indonesia in our Deluxe Room, with its comfortable twin bed or double bed.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-19\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5221011,'743','MR. ADRIAN ENRIQUE RAGA GIL',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-10-13','2024-10-15','Guio','Praba',2,'Persons (2)',10800000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board. - HONEYMOONERS - Connecting flight ETD 12:00 by Lion Air JT804 to Denpasar on 15 Oct 2024','{\"date\": \"2024-10-13\", \"text\": \"ETA 07:15 by Batik Air ID6202 from Jakarta\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Bandar Udara Iskandar Pangkalan Bun\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-15\", \"text\": \"ETD 08:50 by Batik Air ID6134 to Surabaya\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Bandar Udara Iskandar Pangkalan Bun\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5221015,'743','MR. ADRIAN ENRIQUE RAGA GIL',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-15','2024-10-15','Guio','Praba',1,'Persons (2)',420000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting at the arrival hall exit, holding a signboard of your name/group name. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 3 hours after the flight’s estimated arrival time (ETA). - For any flight delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-10-15\", \"text\": \"Arrival Domestic ETA 14:00 by Lion Air JT804 from Surabaya\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-15\", \"text\": \"Jalan Kelabang Moding, Banjar Bentuyung, Ubud, Bali Telephone: 0361-9081383\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Blue Karma Dijiwa Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5221018,'742','Sara Rea Maquieira',30508,207385,'Padang Bai to Nusa Dua','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-19','2024-09-19','Guio','Komang',2,'Persons (1-3)',1120000.00,'At the 