: null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5224854,'755','Mr. Frenai Charlex',30683,203335,'Mini-stay Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-03','2024-09-03','Melysa','Praba',1,'Double',600000.00,'Feel at home in one of our Superior Rooms - warm colors giving an inviting feel and ambiance. Although you are in the heart of Soekarno - Hatta Airport you can find a small oasis of relaxation where you will leave the hustle and bustle of traveling far behind Spacious 24 square meters Superior room with a king or twin beds offering comfortable stay equipped with modern facilities such as air conditioning, arm chair, work desk & chair, flat screen TV with cable and satellite channels, free access internet & Wi-Fi, in room safe, coffee/tea maker, mini cooler, private bathroom with shower and hair dryer, and many more.','Room usage for up to 6 hours Earliest check-in time 09.00 Latest check-out time 23.00 Including transfer between terminals','Flight Details: ETA 13:25 by Garuda Indonesia GA605 from Kendari ETD 23:15 by Korean Air KE5644 to Incheon Seoul','{\"date\": \"2024-09-03\", \"text\": \"ETA 13:25 by Garuda Indonesia GA605 from Kendari\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Soekarno Hatta International Airport\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-03\", \"text\": \"ETD 23:15 by Korean Air KE5644 to Incheon Seoul\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Soekarno Hatta International Airport\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5224898,'756','JORGE ADRIAN MONJEAU',31658,208138,'Villa Room','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-09-05','2024-09-07','Igo','Komang',1,'Single',2016000.00,'The villa features a fireplace. Room facilities inside such as; shower, balcony, air conditioning. Boasting a terrace with sea views, this villa also provides a mini-bar and a flat-screen TV with cable channels. Safe deposit box, Slippers, Terrace, Work desk, Seating area, Wardrobe, Tiled/marble floor, Private entrance, Fax machine, Telephone, Alarm clock, Dustbin, Pool towels.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5224905,'756','JORGE ADRIAN MONJEAU',31083,218825,'Komodo Island Full Day Tour (Slow Wooden Boat - Drop Off Labuan Bajo)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-06','2024-09-06','Igo','Komang',1,'Person (1)',9236080.00,'TOUR ITINERARY Highlights: Padar Island, Komodo Island, Pink Beach, Manta Point & Kanawa. PICK UP / ARRIVE LABUAN BAJO - PADAR - KOMODO - PINK BEACH - MANTA POINT - LABUAHAN BAJO Pick up & meeting service with our tour guide and transfer to the pier of Labuan Bajo for sailing directly to Loh Liang – the Ranger station in Komodo Island. By passing through many small islands, it will be 3 hours with slow wooden boat and 1.50 hours by speed boat to reach the pier of Komodo island. After registering start to take basic trekking to see the GIANT RIZARD / KOMODO DRAGON and other wild animals as: Timor deer, wild pig, wild chicken and many variously of tropical bird. Please keep your look at any directions as sometimes you will also find young Komodo dragon hanging over the trees. A local ranger will be led you during the trek. Return to the boat on to Pink beach for snorkeling, swimming and relaxing. It is really spectacular and unspoiled coral reef and many color fish. Sail toward MANTA POINT to exploring Huge Mantas by snorkeling even watching from your boat trip (can’t be guaranteed if weather is not good, like wave and current are strongly). Lunch will be provided on board. Late in the afternoon back to Labuan Bajo harbor and transfer to your prefer Hotel for overnight and Dinner. Meals : Lunch Attention: The itinerary is subject to change due to the weather, tide level and operating conditions without prior notice.',NULL,'Include Return Transfer from/to Airport - Hotel Labuan Bajo : ETA : 17.40 by Batik Air ID6524 from Jakarta on 5 Sept ETD : 14.00 by Batik Air ID6527 to Jakarta on 07 Sept Hotel : LUWANSA HOTEL Labuan Bajo, Macang Tanggar, Kec. Komodo, Kabupaten Manggarai Barat, Nusa Tenggara Tim. Telepon: (0385) 2443677','{\"date\": \"2024-09-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5225118,'744','Barbara Little',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-10-08','2024-10-10','Melysa','Komang',4,'Persons (4)',14880000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-10-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5225202,'744','Barbara Little',31015,203230,'2D1N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Tour','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-10-10','2024-10-11','Melysa','Komang',4,'Persons (4)',6840000.00,NULL,NULL,'Flights schedule in Surabaya Airport ETA : 10.00 by Batik Air ID6134 from Pangkalan Bun on 10 Oct 2024 ETD : 14.00 by Super Airjet IU726 to Labuan Bajo on 11 Oct 2024 Hotel in Bromo : JIWA JAWA BROMO Jl. Raya Bromo, Wonotoro, Kec. Sukapura, Kabupaten Probolinggo, Jawa Timur 67254 Telepon: 0822-7202-6000','{\"date\": \"2024-10-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5225310,'744','Barbara Little',30684,200640,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-10','2024-10-11','Melysa','Komang',2,'Double',3276000.00,'Designed to embody fresher and younger ambience, our Deluxe Room is a convenient stay for those who plan a relatively shorter stay in Semarang. The room is provided with either a king size or deluxe twin beds.',NULL,'Please send the guarantee letter/voucher following procedure below: - 30 (thirty) days reservation notice prior to the arrival date for Normal Period. - 45 (forty-five) days reservation notice prior to the arrival date for High Season (June 1th to August 31st) and Peak Season (D-3 to D+4 Idul Fitri (April 18 - 25th, 2023 and December 21st, 2023 to January 5th, 2024) period. - Otherwise, the cancellation policy will be applied.','{\"date\": \"2024-10-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5225314,'744','Barbara Little',32156,212197,'3D2N Leisure Package','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-10-12','2024-10-14','Melysa','Komang',1,'(1-4 Persons) /boat',57600000.00,'KLM Jofiel, Traditional Phinisi ironwood schooner with an Indonesian touching is a fusion between traditions and modern design. Discover the infinite islands of Indonesian Archipelago and coral reef of Komodo National Park. Cruising, Adventure, Island Hoping, Relaxation, share and hospitality provides unforgettable Charter liveaboard for any kind of desire and dream. Simply Fantastic! Itinerary Leisure Komodo National Park 3 Days 2 Night: Day 1: - Kelor Island - Menjerite Island - Rinca Kalong Day 2: - Padar Island - Pink Beach - Komodo Island - Taka Makassar - Manta Point Day 3: - Sebayur Island - Kanawa / Bidadari Island - Labuan Bajo BOAT SPECIFICATION: - Length : 20 Meters - Width : 4 Meters - Capacity : 7 Person - Built : 2017 - Speed :-+8 Knots /hour - GT : 41 No. 111/OOm - Materials : Teak and Ironwood - Main Engine : 6D/16 or 6 Cylinder Mitsubishi, Generators with 10 Kva and 7,5 Kva generators, 2 x 25 KVA Dynamos - Navigation : GPS Garmin, Marine Maps, Binoculars, Radio Communication. - Safety Tools : Emergency Rafts, Life Vest, Fire Extinguishers, Search light, First Aid Kits, Oxygen Tank Set, Parachute Signal, Ringbuoys - Water Capacity : 2.000 Liters Fresh Water *Itineraries, times, dive sites and number of dives are subject to change due to weather and sea conditions, availability of safe anchorage, government regulations, dive skill, special requests or circumstances and other factors, Every effort will be made to carry out the program as planned.',NULL,'Pickup & Dropoff point in Labuan Bajo : SUDAMALA RESORT KOMODO Jl. Pantai Pede No.Km. 3, Labuan Bajo, Kabupaten Manggarai Barat, Nusa Tenggara Tim. 86554 Telepon: (0385) 2385555 Pickup time Between 09.00 - 10.00','{\"date\": \"2024-10-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5225357,'744','Barbara Little',30696,202104,'Kelimutu Deluxe Suite','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-14','2024-10-15','Melysa','Komang',2,'Double',7080000.00,'Opening the aura of relaxation while connecting with the beauty of nature. Restoring a sense of longing for a soul-soothing green landscape is the main reason this suite was built. A rustic themed room with a minimalist touch. Aura of relaxation is felt once you first open the two-panel wooden door wide enough to let that tropical wind roll into the room. Directly facing the opposite of the wide balcony, the green landscape is ready to calm your soul. Our Kelimutu Deluxe Suite has 32 units, 16 lower level suites (44 sqm), overlooking to the garden from private terrace and 16 upper level suite (40 sqm) with private balcony and tropical garden view. This suite is equipped with luxurious king-sized and twin bed, efficient and sustainable air-conditioning, 43\" smart TV, complimentary wireless internet, safe deposit box, water heater, private bathroom with bathroom amenities, hairdryer, bathrobe, daily turndown service, and many more.',NULL,'Include Oneway Airport Transfer (private)/ Flight schedule : ETD : 14.00 by Batik Air ID6527 to Jakarta on 15 Oct 2024 Please consult transfer time to Airport upon check-in','{\"date\": \"2024-10-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-15\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5225360,'757','Elisa Duran Rubi',33209,219340,'3D2N Open Trip Sailing Komodo - Carnaby Liveaboard (Superior Cabin)','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-08-30','2024-09-01','Yuli','Yuli',2,'Person (1)',11400000.00,NULL,NULL,'Pick up on 30 Aug 2024: La Prima Hotel Labuan Bajo Drop off on 01 Sep 2024: Labuan Bajo Airport Flight details: ETD 17.35 by Batik Air ID6334 to Denpasar','{\"date\": \"2024-08-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5226166,'758','Ana Maria Hernandez Martinez',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-11','2024-09-11','Guio','Tami',1,'Persons (1-3)',392000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting at the arrival hall exit, holding a signboard of your name/group name. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 3 hours after the flight’s estimated arrival time (ETA). - For any flight delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-09-11\", \"text\": \"ETA 16.55 by Qatar QR962 from Doha on 11 Sep\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"I Gusti Ngurah Rai International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-11\", \"text\": \"Jl. Bisma, Ubud, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Tejaprana Bisma\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09: