INSERT INTO `booked_products` VALUES (5247905,'817','Miguel Del rio',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-09','2024-10-10','Norberto','Komang',1,'Double',882000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-10-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5247947,'817','Miguel Del rio',30805,202689,'CGK-PKN','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-10','2024-10-10','Norberto','Komang',2,'Person',3520000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5247950,'817','Miguel Del rio',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-10-10','2024-10-12','Norberto','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',10800000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board.','{\"date\": \"2024-10-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5247969,'817','Miguel Del rio',30805,212245,'PKN-CGK','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-12','2024-10-12','Norberto','Komang',2,'Person',3520000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5247974,'817','Miguel Del rio',30805,207115,'CGK-MDC','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-12','2024-10-12','Norberto','Komang',2,'Person',7260000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5247982,'817','Miguel Del rio',31591,207373,'3D2N Tangkoko','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-10-12','2024-10-14','Norberto','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',0.00,'Day 1 : MANADO - TANGKOKO - The expedition begins The adventure begins with meeting your guide at the Manado airport. Then you will start the journey of about 2 and a half hours by car to the Tangkoko Forest where you will do the check in at your Homestay or Lodge. Upon arrival, you will have a talk about what you will see and preparations for the trekking. Meals : Dinner Accommodation : Bird House Homestay or Similar Days 02 : Tangkoko Nature Reserve These days will be dedicated to exploring the jungle in search of animals and bird watching. You will start the trekking that will take you to Tangkok National Park. In just 40 minutes by boat, you will reach the Batuangus beach where you will then climb Mount Tangkoko (1500 m). The dense and virgin jungle is home to some unique animal species in North Sulawesi such as the crested black macaque and the tarsier spectrum that has become known as \"the smallest primate in the world\". As you will be trekking through the lush jungle, you will probably see and hear the red gnarled hornbill as well as the Maleo which is a Megapod Bird that lays eggs on large mounds it builds on the black sand. You can also find couscous, which is a relative of the Australian koala. The forest ranger will accompany you all the way to the top of Tangkoko Mountain. In the afternoon you will return to the station. Alternatively, you can have three hours of trekking in the lowland jungle or swimming on the black sand beach of Tangkoko Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Bird House Homestay or Similar Day 03 : Tangkoko - Manado After breakfast, you can spend the morning in the surroundings of the National Park and at the agreed time, with your guide, you will have the transfer to Manado. Thank you for exploring this unique jungle with us. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Flight Schedule in Manado Airport : ETA : 16.15 by Batik Air ID6272 from Jakarta on 12 October Dropoff point : Pantai Surabaya Likupang Minahasa ETD : 13.00 pickup by Bastianos Bangka Time transfer to port (Pantai Surabaya) : 12.00','{\"date\": \"2024-10-12\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5248163,'818','Maria Guzman Lopez',30783,213061,'Transfer from Semarang Airport to Yogyakarta Hotel','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-25','2024-09-25','Nicholas','Tami',1,'Per Car',540000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-09-25\", \"text\": \"ETA 11.25 by Batik Air ID6303 from Pangkalan Bun on 25 Sep\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Semarang International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-25\", \"text\": \"Jl. Masjid No.7, Purwokinanti, Pakualaman, Kota Yogyakarta\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Puri Pangeran Hotel\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5248181,'817','Miguel Del rio',32195,214479,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-17','2024-10-18','Norberto','Komang',1,'Double',1080000.00,NULL,NULL,'Flight Schedule : ETD : 06.00 by Lion Air JT741 to Denpasar on 18 October Time transfer to Airport between : 04.15-04.30 AM','{\"date\": \"2024-10-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5248202,'817','Miguel Del rio',30805,207116,'MDC-DPS','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-18','2024-10-18','Norberto','Komang',2,'Person',4840000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5248205,'817','Miguel Del rio',30805,212248,'DPS-TMC','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-18','2024-10-18','Norberto','Komang',2,'Person',6160000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5248210,'817','Miguel Del rio',30528,215500,'4D3N Explore Sumba Special Experience, Culture & Adventure Trip / A. Mario Hotel - Rua Beach Hotel','Confirmed','4DSW-S',4,'2024-10-18','2024-10-21','Norberto','Komang',2,'Persons (2 / Double)',18960000.00,'DAY 1 : ARRIVAL TMC - BONDO KAPUMBU VILLAGE - SALT FARMERS VISIT - LENDONGARA HILL SUNSET Meet and greet with our guide at the Tambolaka airport in south-west Sumba.After that, we go to a local restaurant for lunch. Then we will start our journey by visiting Bondo Kapumbu Village, a hidden traditional village in south-west Sumba. Continuing to Ketewel Beach, you can visit the salt farmers, where you can see how they make the salt in a traditional way. Then we head to Lendongara to watch the sunset over the hills and the Sumba landscape. Then we go to your hotel to check in and rest. Meals : Lunch Accomodation : A. Mario Hotel (Deluxe Jineng Room) DAY 2 : SUMBA CASHEW FARM & PRODUCTION - WAIKACURA RICE FIELD - WATUBELA BEACH After breakfast, we will go to Talasi to see the cashew farm and production. Here you will get a chance to try their original cashew milk. After that, we go to the Waikacura area, where you can go trekking to the rice fields. Get a chance to see the local farmers do their activities, and at the end of the trek you will see the stunning river in the middle of the rice field. Next, after trekking, we go to West Sumba and have lunch at a local restaurant. After lunch, we go to visit the beautiful hidden beach of Watubela. On the way, you will pass a small village and palm garden to get to the beach. Relax on the beach, and we\'ll go to your hotel after that. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Accomodation : A. Rua Beach Hotel (Deluxe Room) DAY 3 : SUMBANESE COOKING & ACTIVITIES EXPERIENCE - LAPOPU WATERFALL Breakfast at the hotel, then we go to the traditional village in West Sumba, where you will be warmly welcomed by the locals. Talking with them and listening to the story of the village and the island. After engaging with them, they will invite you to join them in cooking Sumba\'s traditional foods. Once the foods are ready, have lunch together. Have coffee or tea after lunch, sit with them for a while, then say goodbye. Our trip is continuing to Lapopu Waterfall. After a drive through the endless hilly and green landscape of Sumba, you will arrive near the waterfall. To visit the waterfall, you will need to do a short hike of approximately 15 minutes and cross a bamboo bridge to get there. There is a nice spot to sit down where you can watch the water find its way down the hill. After the visits, go back to the hotel to rest. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Accomodation : A. Rua Beach Hotel (Deluxe Room) DAY 4 : PRAIJING VILLAGE - OUT TMC AIRPORT After breakfast and checking out of the hotel, we will go to visit the village of Praijing, a traditional village uphill surrounded by lots of greenery. This is one of the few villages where we can actually have a beautiful overview of the entire village and get an idea of how the village is conducted. Take some time to walk around the village, the elders occupy most of the houses, and kids are always around to share their smiles. And then go to the airport to catch a flight to your next destination. Meals : Breakfast Accomodation : -',NULL,'18-19 Oct : Based on Mario Beach Hotel - Superior Sea View room 19-21 Oct : Based on Rua Beach Hotel - Deluxe room','{\"date\": \"2024-10-18\", \"text\": \"ETA : 15.05 by Wings Air IW1834 from Denpasar on 18 October\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Tambolaka Airport, Sumba\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-21\", \"text\": \"ETD : 12.25 by Wings Air IW1833 to Denpasar on 21 October\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Tambolaka Airport, Sumba\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5248228,'817','Miguel Del rio',30508,212287,'Airport to Sanur','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-21','2024-10-21','Norberto','Komang',1,'Persons (1-3)',300000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting at the arrival hall exit, holding a signboard of your name/group name. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 3 hours after the flight’s estimated arrival time (ETA). - For any flight delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-10-21\", \"text\": \"ETA : 13.55 by Wings IW1833 from Tambolaka on 21 October\", \"time\": \"13:55\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Airport Ngurah Rai\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-21\", \"text\": \"Jl. Danau Tamblingan No.87, Sanur Kaja, Denpasar Selatan, Kota Denpasar, Bali 80228 Telepon: (0361) 286286\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Parigata Resort, Sanur\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5248260,'817','Miguel Del rio',30508,207269,'Sanur to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-23','2024-10-23','Norberto','Komang',1,'Persons (1-3)',300000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel and transfer you to the airport for your flight to the next destination.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver will wait up to 30 minutes after your scheduled pickup time. - Please keep in mind that any further delay could affect your timely arrival at the airport for your flight. - For any changes in flight departure time, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available). - Requests for pickup time earlier than originally booked are subject to availability.','{\"date\": \"2024-10-23\", \"text\": \"Jl. Danau Tamblingan No.87, Sanur Kaja, Denpasar Selatan, Kota Denpasar, Bali 80228 Telepon: (0361) 286286\", \"time\": \"14:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Parigata Resort Sanur\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-23\", \"text\": \"ETD : 17.25 by Garuda Indonesia GA419 to Jakarta on 23 October\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Ngurah Rai Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5248270,'817','Miguel Del rio',30721,219635,'One Bedroom Plunge Pool Villa','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-10-21','2024-10-23','Norberto','Komang',1,'Double',3480000.00,'Villas are spaciously appointed with high thatched ceiling and adjoining bathroom with their own garden views. A room service is available for those who would to dinner in their own villa. At the end of a long day of exploring the island, shopping and sunshine guests can enjoy the luxury of cooling off in their own private swimming pool and jacuzzi spending the sunset hour on their terrace.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5248275,'817','Miguel Del rio',30805,212249,'TMC-DPS','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-21','2024-10-21','Norberto','Komang',2,'Person',6160000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-21\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5248289,'789','Gregory Abbott',30806,208758,'3D2N Shared Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO8',3,'2024-11-04','2024-11-06','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Person (1)',7840000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.00 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you canhave your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan is Cape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even see crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Shared Klotok Boat *The SHARED klotok will be ready by 10.30 AM and will depart at 12.00 PM sharp. Check-in time: Klotok at 10.30 AM, check-out time: 08.00 AM *If you arrive at the port before 12 PM, you may walk around the area of the port by yourself. Alternatively, when the boat is ready, you can also wait for the other travelers on the boat. Note: The guide may not assist you during the waiting time. *All participants should arrive at the latest 10.30 AM at Pangkalanbun Airport. If you arrive late, you must take the speedboat to join the klotok. The speedboat costs around IDR 600.000/boat/way to be paid directly to the captain. Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continue to add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Shared Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Meals preference: Mrs Marina Abbott is vegan (no meat, fish, eggs, milk, butter, and other dairy products)','{\"date\": \"2024-11-04\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in hotel lobby at the mentioned time.\", \"time\": \"10:00\", \"locality\": \"Mercure Hotel Pangkalan Bun\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-06\", \"text\": \"ETD: 07.55 by Batik Air ID6203 to Jakarta on 06 Nov\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Pangkalan Bun Airport\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5248292,'789','Gregory Abbott',32766,218299,'3D2N Open Trip Komodo - Lamborajo 2 / Superior Cabin','Confirmed',NULL,3,'2024-10-25','2024-10-27','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Per Person (Min. 2 Person)',11160000.00,'DAY 1 : Kelor Island - Manjerite Island - Kalong Island DAY 2 : Padar Island - Long / Pick Beach - Komodo Island - Manta Point - Taka Makasar DAY 3 : Kanawa Island',NULL,'Meals preference: Mrs Marina Abbott is vegan (no meat, fish, eggs, milk, butter, and other dairy products)','{\"date\": \"2024-10-25\", \"text\": \"Please be ready in hotel lobby at the mentioned time.\", \"time\": \"10:00\", \"locality\": \"Komodo Suites Downtown\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Golo Hilltop Hotel\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5248300,'819','Delia Maria Marrero Garcia',31015,203230,'2D1N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Tour','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-10-10','2024-10-11','Nicholas','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',4800000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-10\", \"text\": \"ETA 10.45 by Sancaka (98) from Yogyakarta on 10 Oct\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Surabaya Gubeng Train Station\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-11\", \"text\": \"ETD 18.15 by Super Air Jet IU708 to Denpasar on 11 Oct\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Surabaya International Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5248308,'819','Delia Maria Marrero Garcia',30684,200640,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-10','2024-10-11','Nicholas','Tami',1,'Double',1638000.00,'Designed to embody fresher and younger ambience, our Deluxe Room is a convenient stay for those who plan a relatively shorter stay in Semarang. The room is provided with either a king size or deluxe twin beds.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-10\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5248554,'820','Thomas Lo',30508,207250,'Airport to Kuta','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-22','2024-09-22','Ayu','Wiwik',3,'Persons (1-3)',900000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting at the arrival hall exit, holding a signboard of your name/group name. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 3 hours after the flight’s estimated arrival time (ETA). - For any flight delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-09-22\", \"text\": \"ETA 16.35 by Air Asia D7792 from Kuala Lumpur on 22 September 2024\", \"time\": \"16:35\", \"locality\": \"Ngurah Rai Airport (TERMINAL INTERNATIONAL)\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-22\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Episode Hotel Kuta\", \"location\": \"Jl. Bypass Ngurah Rai No.99, Kuta, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80362\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5248559,'820','Thomas Lo',30508,212305,'Kuta to Sanur','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-23','2024-09-23','Ayu','Wiwik',3,'Persons (1-3)',900000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"06:30\", \"locality\": \"Episode Hotel Kuta Bali\", \"location\": \"Jl. Bypass Ngurah Rai No.99, Kuta, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80362\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Sanur Port (The Angkal Fastboat to Penida - ETD: 08.30)\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5248561,'820','Thomas Lo',30508,207112,'1D Nusa Penida West Tour','Confirmed','C2I-BALI19',1,'2024-09-23','2024-09-23','Ayu','Wiwik',3,'Persons (3)',1080000.00,'Today, embark on a unique adventure as you explore the enchanting Nusa Penida, a neighboring island of Bali. Your day begins with a convenient hotel pick-up, followed by a journey to the Sanur port where a fast boat awaits to transport you to Nusa Penida in just 30 minutes. Nusa Penida, located in the southeast of Bali, is a true paradise waiting to be discovered. Upon your arrival, a friendly driver will be ready to guide you through the day\'s captivating itinerary. Your first destination is the mesmerizing Angel\'s Billabong, a natural wonder resembling a pristine pool nestled in the heart of nature. Take a refreshing swim, but exercise caution on the steps and heed your driver\'s recommendations. Next, we head to Broken Beach, a charming bay that was once a cave, now open to the sky, offering a unique and captivating scenery. Although inaccessible by land, the view from above is nothing short of breathtaking. Keep an eye out for the possibility of spotting giant manta rays gracefully gliding on the water\'s surface. Our journey continues to the renowned Kelingking Beach, famous for its stunning cliffs and the iconic hand-shaped mountain. This beach is not only one of the island\'s most famous attractions but also a favorite subject for photographers. We conclude the day at the pristine Crystal Beach, where white sands meet turquoise waters in perfect harmony. As the sun sets, you\'ll have the opportunity to relax and savor the beauty that surrounds you. This unforgettable experience concludes with a return boat trip to Bali from the Toya Pakeh port at 16:30, followed by a comfortable transfer to your hotel.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-23\", \"text\": \"Boat by The Angkal from Sanur\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": \"BANJAR NYUH PORT\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"16:30\", \"locality\": \"Banjar Nyuh Port by The Angkal to Sanur\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5248562,'820','Thomas Lo',30508,212491,'Sanur to Kuta','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-23','2024-09-23','Ayu','Wiwik',3,'Persons (1-3)',900000.00,'At the appointed time, meeting service with your driver who will take you to the designated destination.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"17:30\", \"locality\": \"Sanur Port (The Angkal Fastboat from Penida)\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-23\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Episode Hotel Kuta Bali\", \"location\": \"Jl. Bypass Ngurah Rai No.99, Kuta, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80362\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5248565,'820','Thomas Lo',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-25','2024-09-25','Ayu','Wiwik',3,'Persons (3)',2160000.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,'Bali Fantastic Route Tour visiting: Taman Ayun Temple - Jatiluwih Rice Terraces - Ulundanu Beratan Temple - Tanah Lot Temple The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": \"Episode Hotel Kuta Bali\", \"location\": \"Jl. Bypass Ngurah Rai No.99, Kuta, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80362\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-25\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Episode Hotel Kuta Bali\", \"location\": \"Jl. Bypass Ngurah Rai No.99, Kuta, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80362\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5248566,'771','Abyssworld Group Samambaia 18-29 November 2024',30680,200912,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-29','2024-11-30','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Double',784000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-11-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5248569,'820','Thomas Lo',30508,202893,'Lempuyang Temple Tour','Confirmed','C2I-BALI11',1,'2024-09-26','2024-09-26','Ayu','Wiwik',3,'Persons (3)',2232000.00,'At the agreed time, our guide will pick you up to start the tour in the eastern part of Bali. The first place you will visit is Goa Lawah Temple. Goa Lawah Temple consists of two names, \"Goa\" which means cave and \"Lawah\" which means bat. Several thousand bats are flying in the cave as the name suggests. With the lights fading as you go deeper inside the cave, it gives off a very strange atmosphere. From Goa Lawah, we continue our way to Lempuyang Temple. Upon arrival, the temple will greet you with its gratifying panorama that extends into infinity. On a clear, sunny day, you\'ll be able to gaze out over the mountains, Amlapura city, and Mount Agung, an incredibly magnificent sight that\'s beautiful beyond words. This portrait of heaven is beautifully framed by the Gapura Candi Bentar (the gate of the temple). Our journey continues to visit Tirta Gangga. The site is a paradise surrounded by water, with all the pools decorated with unusual statues. With its seclusion and a view of the surrounding rice paddies, Tirta Gangga is a wonderful place. At the end of the trip we go to Tenganan Village, the most famous Bali Agas (the “original” Bali people) in the city. With its characteristics, the city village is arranged in parallel along the wide main road paved with rows of cobblestones. In Tenganan, women still weave the famous Kamben Geringsing, or \"burnt cloth,\" which has the power to immunize the wearer against evil. We take a close look at what they do in their daily lives in a traditional lifestyle. From Tenganan, we will transfer you to the hotel.',NULL,'Lempuyang Temple Tour visiting: Goa Lawah - Lempuyang Temple - Tirta Gangga - Tenganan The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"08:00\", \"locality\": \"Episode Hotel Kuta Bali\", \"location\": \"Jl. Bypass Ngurah Rai No.99, Kuta, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80362\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-26\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Episode Hotel Kuta Bali\", \"location\": \"Jl. Bypass Ngurah Rai No.99, Kuta, Kec. Kuta, Kabupaten Badung, Bali 80362\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5248570,'820','Thomas Lo',30508,207266,'Kuta to Airport','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-27','2024-09-27','Ayu','Wiwik',3,'Persons (1-3)',900000.00,'At the appointed time, your driver will pick you up from the hotel 