"ETD : 17.50 by NZ065 to AKL on 21 Oct 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"International Ngurah Rai Airport\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5252935,'832','Elisabeth Stephanie KOLAR',30806,212931,'3D2N Best Borneo Orangutan Tour','Confirmed','C2B-BORNEO1',3,'2024-11-14','2024-11-16','Ayu','Ayu',2,'Persons (1-3)',0.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN - KUMAI PORT - TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan isCape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY - CAMP LEAKEY Today you will wake up to the sounds and colors of the jungle. Without a doubt, you will never forget how you woke up on the river, surrounded by overflowing nature. After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continueto add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note : The Birate Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. *If your return flight leaves early in the morning (around 7 a.m.), tonight the klotok will sleep closer to the port in order to get you to the airport in time. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT - PANGKALAN BUN In the early morning you will enjoy the last moments of the sounds of the jungle before heading to the port to, in turn, be transferred to the airport. The check-out time will be at 8 a.m. If you decide to take a flight in the afternoon, we can take you directly to the airport, or if you want a city tour in the town of Arut to be transferred to the airport later, this can be organized at an additional cost. Thank you for joining us on this Borneo Orangutan Tour by Come2Indonesia! Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Note: IDR 100.000/person/camp for surcharge of Sunday / Collective Leave Day / National or Public Holiday is excluded in the tour and it has to be paid on-board. Note: Regina is allergy to pumpkin Flight information: ETA 07.15 by Batik Air ID6202 from Jakarta on 14 November 2024 ETD 08.50 by Batik Air ID6134 to Surabaya on 16 November 2024','{\"date\": \"2024-11-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-16\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5253411,'827','Sr. Antonio CALAMA RODRIGUEZ',30783,218075,'6D5N Jogja-Merapi-Bromo-Ijen-Bali Overland / A. The Phoenix (Deluxe) & Jiwa Jawa Bromo (Deluxe) & Ij','Confirmed',NULL,6,'2024-10-09','2024-10-14','Jacob','Agus',2,'Persons (2)',0.00,'D1 Arrival at Yogyakarta International airport - Transfer to hotel D2 Borobudur temple incl. Mendut and Pawon temple - Merapi lava Tour Incl .Jeep D3 Yogjakarta City Tour visit Sultan Palace, Wateracstle and Bird Market - Prambanan temple D4 Jogja to Bromo drive - overnight in Bromo D5 Mt. Bromo Sunrise tour incl. Jeep - Transfer to Banyuwangi/Ijen Hotel for overnight D6 Mt. Ijen crater tour - transfer to Bali accross Ketapang - Gilimanuk harbour - drop at your hotel in Bali',NULL,'Arrival 09 Oct 2024 : Yogyakarta Airport ETA 12.45 by Garuda GA 253 from Jakarta Drop off Bali 14 Oct 2024 : MERUSAKA Nusa Dua Program : 09 Oct : Yogyakarta Airport - Magelang - Check in Plataran Borobudur Resort 10 Oct : Tour Candirejo - Borobudur Temple - Transfer to Yogyakarta Overnight at Tentrem Hotel 11 Oct : Yogyakarta City Tour - Prambanan Temple - Ballet Ramayana at Puriwisata - Dinner Overnight at Tentrem Hotel 12 Oct : Yogyakarta - Mojokerto by Train - Drive to Bromo Overnight Plataran Bromo 13 Oct : Bromo Sunrise Tour - Drive to Ijen - Overnight Ijen RESORT 14 Oct : Ijen Trek- Ferry to Bali - Transfer to Nusa Dua - Merusaka Hotel','{\"date\": \"2024-10-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5253417,'833','Rosa Maria Artola',30508,207254,'Airport to Ubud','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-28','2024-10-28','Jacob','Komang',1,'Persons (1-3)',420000.00,'Upon your arrival at the airport, meeting service with the driver who will take you to the booked accommodation.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting at the arrival hall exit, holding a signboard of your name/group name. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 3 hours after the flight’s estimated arrival time (ETA). - For any flight delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-10-28\", \"text\": \"ETA : 22.20 by Emirates EK398 from Dubai on 28 October 2024\", \"time\": \"22:20\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"International Ngurah Rai Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-28\", \"text\": \"Jl. Suweta, Bentuyung Sakti, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 2091788\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Visesa Resort Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5253431,'833','Rosa Maria Artola',30985,212179,'Jungle Suite Room with Private Balcony','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-10-28','2024-11-01','Jacob','Komang',1,'Double',9360000.00,'Escape the hustle and bustle of everyday life and immerse yourself in the beauty of nature with our Jungle Suite with Private Balcony. Located in the heart of the lush tropical rainforest, this Suite offers a unique opportunity to immerse yourself in nature while still enjoying all the comforts of modern living. The real highlight of this room category is the private balcony overlooking the jungle canopy. Relax in your own personal paradise as you listen to the sounds of nature, watch the birds playing in the trees, and breathe in the fresh air while taking in the breathtaking views.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5253440,'833','Rosa Maria Artola',30508,202894,'Kehen Temple - Pengelipuran - Tukad Cepung Waterfall','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-30','2024-10-30','Jacob','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',1680000.00,'Our wonderful tour starts from Kehen Temple. It is an ancient Hindu temple complex boasting unique architectural features. The staircases reaching from the ground to temple courtyard are carved sandstone mythical animal and Balinese folklore figure statues and also the central vestibule. The temple’s walls are also ornate with Chinese porcelain plates, which are a tribute to the historical relations between the local Bali kingdom and China. Afterwards, we continue to Penglipuran, a village that succeeded in preserving its 75-hectare bamboo forest located in the northern part of the village. Members of this village have a strong commitment to the system of \'Ayahan Desa\' - a philosophy committed to respecting the land on which the village stands. To concludes the day, we stop by at Tukad Cepung Waterfall. Well-guarded by the circular cliffs, this waterfall is difficult to locate for the first time visitor. The circular cliffs give you the feeling of being in a cave, while the open sky right from where the waterfall emerges, gives you the most enchanting view. The sunlight falls on the glistering waterfall creating a rainbow, which feels as though it is projected right up to you. If you have never seen water flowing from the sky, then this would be your chance! After spending your time there, we go back to your hotel.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-10-30\", \"text\": \"Jl. Suweta, Bentuyung Sakti, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 2091788\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Visesa Resort Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-30\", \"text\": \"Jl. Suweta, Bentuyung Sakti, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 2091788\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Visesa Resort Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5253442,'833','Rosa Maria Artola',30508,202892,'Fantastic Route','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-29','2024-10-29','Jacob','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',1872000.00,'At the appointed time, pick you up at your hotel and begin our tour to enjoy the beauty of Bali. First we’ll go to Taman Ayun Temple, it is a Royal Temple of Mengwi Empire and it is located in Mengwi Village, Mengwi sub district, It is set on the land which is surrounded by the big fish pond and look like a drift on the water. Then we go to Rice Terrace Jatiluwih, the rice terrace forms beautiful sight at all seasons, during the watering, or before planting the rice looks, as far as u go, u can see the beautiful greens of it, then continue to Ulun Danu Bratan Temple, is a Balinese Hindu Temple located at Candi Kuning countryside, Baturiti sub district and Tabanan regency. It is set at lakeside of Beratan with beautiful lake view and hills surround it. It is situated in the plateau area with cool atmosphere surround it and hills as a backdrop. It was the unique Bali temple which are now many tourists paying a visit to this place. And last we go to Tanah Lot Temple, the big Holy Temples in Bali. The temple is built on the rock with 3 acre size and reachable in a few minute by walk, because it is just 20 meters from the coastal lip. This temple is very famous among tourist destinations in Bali with spectacular view of sunset.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-10-29\", \"text\": \"Jl. Suweta, Bentuyung Sakti, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 2091788\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Visesa Resort Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-29\", \"text\": \"Jl. Suweta, Bentuyung Sakti, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 2091788\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Visesa Resort Ubud\"}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5253475,'833','Rosa Maria Artola',30508,215968,'1D Bali Tour (Goa Gajah-Tampak Siring-Gunung Kawi-Tegalalang)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-31','2024-10-31','Jacob','Komang',2,'Persons (2)',2040000.00,NULL,NULL,'The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-10-31\", \"text\": \"Jl. Suweta, Bentuyung Sakti, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 80571 Telepon: (0361) 2091788\", \"time\": \"09:00\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Visesa Resort Ubud\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-31\", \"text\": \"Jl. Suweta, Bentuyung Sakti, Kecamatan Ubud, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali 805