 Your day begins with a convenient hotel pick-up, followed by a journey to the Sanur port where a fast boat awaits to transport you to Nusa Penida in just 30 minutes. Nusa Penida, located in the southeast of Bali, is a true paradise waiting to be discovered. Upon your arrival, a friendly driver will be ready to guide you through the day\'s captivating itinerary. Your first destination is the mesmerizing Angel\'s Billabong, a natural wonder resembling a pristine pool nestled in the heart of nature. Take a refreshing swim, but exercise caution on the steps and heed your driver\'s recommendations. Next, we head to Broken Beach, a charming bay that was once a cave, now open to the sky, offering a unique and captivating scenery. Although inaccessible by land, the view from above is nothing short of breathtaking. Keep an eye out for the possibility of spotting giant manta rays gracefully gliding on the water\'s surface. Our journey continues to the renowned Kelingking Beach, famous for its stunning cliffs and the iconic hand-shaped mountain. This beach is not only one of the island\'s most famous attractions but also a favorite subject for photographers. We conclude the day at the pristine Crystal Beach, where white sands meet turquoise waters in perfect harmony. As the sun sets, you\'ll have the opportunity to relax and savor the beauty that surrounds you. This unforgettable experience concludes with a return boat trip to Bali from the Toya Pakeh port at 16:30, followed by a comfortable transfer to your hotel.',NULL,'The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-28\", \"text\": \"Sakti, Nusa Penida, Klungkung Regency, Bali 80771\", \"time\": \"08:30\", \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Māua Nusa Penida\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-28\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5258447,'842','Jimmy LAU',30508,207278,'Full Day Tour Car & Driver (8-10 hours)','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-27','2024-09-27','Ayu','Wiwik',1,'Persons (9)',0.00,NULL,NULL,'The driver will be waiting in the hotel lobby or at the specified pickup point. IMPORTANT: - The driver may wait up to 30 minutes after the scheduled pickup time. Please be advised that extended wait times could affect your planned activities. - For any potential delays, please inform us in advance at +62813 37165036 (WhatsApp available), or inform the driver upon meeting them.','{\"date\": \"2024-09-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": \"09:30\", \"locality\": \"Private Villa\", \"location\": \"Jalan Batur Sari No. 45B, Sanur\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-27\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Jambe Asri ATV\", \"location\": \"Jl. Pura Dalem Tegal Tamu, Batubulan, Kec. Sukawati, Kabupaten Gianyar, Bali\"}','2026-08-28 07:09:31','2026-08-28 07:09:31'),(5258466,'843','Francisco Javier Garcia Gil de Bernabe',31015,203230,'2D1N - Surabaya Mount Bromo Tour','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-10-17','2024-10-18','Jacob','Tami',2,'Persons (2)',4800000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-17\", \"text\": \"ETA 10.00 by Batik Air ID6134 from Pangkalan Bun on 17 Oct\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": \"Surabaya International Airport\"}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-18\", \"text\": \"ETD - TBA\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5258484,'843','Francisco Javier Garcia Gil de Bernabe',30684,200640,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-10-17','2024-10-18','Jacob','Tami',1,'Double',1638000.00,'Designed to embody fresher and younger ambience, our Deluxe Room is a convenient stay for those who plan a relatively shorter stay in Semarang. The room is provided with either a king size or deluxe twin beds.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-10-17\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-18\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5259955,'255','Andrew Howard',30602,219767,'Meet and Greet International Arrival','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-09-30','2024-09-30','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Person (1)',472640.00,NULL,NULL,'MEETING POINT: Your personal assistant will be waiting for you before the Visa-on-Arrival desk and the immigration area (near transfer desk/duty-free plaza), holding a sign of your name. They will direct you to the Visa-on-Arrival desk and immigration checkpoint but no assistance will be provided. You will meet the assistant again past the immigration, and they will assist you through customs clearance, and help with the luggage. Lastly, the assistant will take you to meet the person who will pick you up at the airport. Meet up with pickup transfer by Four Points Manado +62431 8803999','{\"date\": \"2024-09-30\", \"text\": \"ETA: 13.15 by Scoot TR216 from Singapore on 30 Sep\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-09-30\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5260254,'709','Yuen Jackie Freeman',30680,200912,'6 Double + 2 Twin Superior Rooms','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-15','2024-11-16','Ayu','Eddy',8,'Double + Twin',6272000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available). Yuen Jackie Freeman Room 7 (Twin) M Ng Cheuk Wai Alex ADT M Yuen Jackie Freeman ADT Room 1 (Double) (2) M Lee Wai Chun F Chen Hiu Kwan Room 2 (Double) (2) F Lam Sze Yan M Yeung Hong Yu Room 3 (Double) (2) M Chan Hei Wai Henry F Lee Lok Chi Room 4 (Twin) (2) F Lee Yuen Yu Amy F Wong Ka Lai Room 5 (Double) (1) M Kwok Charles Cheong Ping Room 6 (Double) (1) M Chan Hang Piu Room 8 (Double) (1) M Chan Hoi Wah','{\"date\": \"2024-11-15\", \"text\": \"ETA 10.10 by Garuda GA683 from Sorong on 15 Nov 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-16\", \"text\": \"ETD 07.25 by Garuda GA860 to Hong Kong on 16 Nov 2024\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5260375,'847','Aryana',31137,204154,'5D4N BALIKPAPAN IKN - BANJARMASIN - LOKSADO TRIP','Confirmed',NULL,5,'2024-09-29','2024-10-03','Yuli','Ayu',3,'Persons (7-9)',45696000.00,'DAY 01: BALIKPAPAN - SAMARINDA - MAHAKAM Upon arrival at Balikpapan airport, meeting service and transfer to Loa Janan, to board houseboat for exciting adventure on Mahakam river. Meals provided and overnight on houseboat. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Houseboat with Airconditioning All Twin Share DAY 02: MUARA MUNTAI - MANCONG - TANJUNG ISUY - MUARA PAHU Short sight seeing at Muara Muntai Wooden village, then crossing Jempang Lake by motor canoe to Mancong. During the cruise you could see Rain forest and wildlife at Ohong creek like monkey’s and birds, Upon arrival at Mancong, welcomed with a traditional ceremony by the Dayaq Benuaq, one of the Oldest Dayak Longhouse of East Kalimantan can be found here, Late afternoon by motor canoe to Tanjung Isuy for sightseeing and continue to Houseboat for dinner and overnight. Houseboat will cruise up to Muara Pahu. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Houseboat with Airconditioning All Twin Share DAY 03: MUARA PAHU - KEDANG PAHU RIVER - MOUNT BAYAN - TERBISAK - DOWNSTREAM Arrive at Muara Pahu, cruise upstream the Kedang Pahu River by canoe for more then one hour by canoe to Mount Bayan to visit Terbisak Dayak village known of it’s Longhouse of the Benauq Dayak tribe which is still habituated by about 100 Dayak people living in their community house, and traditions of dry rise fielding and hunting, continue downstream by canoe, along the river bank, we will enjoy the exotic nature, and wildlife as otters, leave monkeys, endangered proboscis monkeys and birds, before we move to the delta of the Belowan river as a black water peat swamp forest land, with opportunities to spot the fresh water dolphins in the the Kedang Pahu and the Bolowan River, return to houseboat for upstream to Melak. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Houseboat with Airconditioning All Twin Share DAY 04: MELAK - EHENG - OMBAU ASA Arrive in Melak then drive to Eheng by Jeep / Minibus passing beautiful highland to reach the old longhouse of Dayak Tunjung. Afterwards visit Kersik Luway and explore the forest, if lucky the famous black orchid can be seen. Afternoon to Ombau Asa waterfall, an exciting place for swimming. Return to Melak then board to the houseboat and downstream to Tenggarong. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Houseboat with Airconditioning All Twin Share DAY 05: TENGGARONG - BALIKPAPAN Arrive at Tenggarong, visiting the former palace of Sultan Kutai Kertanegara. Where you will see the Sultan\'s impressive collection of heirlooms, ceramics, Dayak\'s art and culture items. Afterwards by car to Balikpapan airport for your onward flight to your next destination. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch',NULL,'Bedding type: 1 DBL Kingsize bed room & 1 Twin bed room Allergies: NO BEEF and 1 person allergies shellfish. Program: 29 Sept. Arrive Balikpapan - Transfer to Grand Senyiur Hotel (D) 30 Sept. Visit Indonesia Future Capital City Nusantara / IKN - Transfer to Balikpapan Airport to take flight to Banjarmasin. Arrive Banjarmasin - Transfer to Swiss Bel Hotel Banjarmasin (B/L/D) 01 Oct. Floating Market - Cempaka - Martapura - Nagara - Loksado. Transfer to Meratus Loksado Resort (B/L/D) 02 Oct. Loksado - Bamboo Rafting - Meratus Forest Trekking - Banjarmasin. Transfer to Aston Banjarbaru (B/L/D) 03 Oct. Departure Banjarmasin (B) Flight information: Balikpapan IKN Trip ETA 12.40 by Citilink QG445 from Denpasar on 29 September 2024 ETD 17.25 by Citilink QG1499 to Banjarmasin on 30 September 2024 Banjarmasin - Loksado Trip ETA 18.40 by Citilink QG1499 from Balikpapan on 30 September 2024 ETD 06.10 by Lion Air JT311 to Surabaya on 03 October 2024','{\"date\": \"2024-09-29\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5260386,'847','Aryana',30806,202007,'5D4N Borneo Orangutan Tour & Dayak Tribe','Confirmed',NULL,5,'2024-10-03','2024-10-07','Yuli','Ayu',3,'Persons (3)',27888000.00,'Day 1 : PANGKALAN BUN – KUMAI PORT – TANJUNG HARAPAN Arrive at Pangkalan Bun Airport, on the island of Borneo, better known by the Indonesians as Kalimantan. Upon arrival at the airport, your guide will be waiting for you. You will transfer to the port of Kumai in about 15-20 minutes by car, where you will embark on a great adventure! You arrive at our traditional wooden boat, called a klotok. Our guide will reconfirm with the crew that everything is ready and start the cruise up the river in the famous Sekonyer River aboard a klotok. If your flight arrives early (before 11.30 AM), you can arrive in time to the rehabilitation center of Tanjung Harapan, where at 3 o’clock in the afternoon, the rangers of the national park feed the orangutans, and you can have your first close encounters with them. The translation of Tanjung Harapan is Cape of Hope. This first camp is one of the ones with more wetlands, and being in the afternoon has more mosquitoes, so make sure you put on enough mosquito repellent. Here you also can do the reforestation, where you can be volunteers to plant a tree, and so take pride that you have contributed a grain of sand to conservation with your step over there. After visiting this Rangers Camp, you will continue upstream, resting on the boat, while you search for animals in the vicinity of the Sekonyer River. This afternoon, it is very frequent to see groups of proboscis monkeys and monkeys in the treetops, jumping from one branch to another, or even crocodiles, and lizards in the shallow waters of the sides of the river. Prepare for sunset. The boat moored on one side of the river to spend the night. Tonight, you can do a walk into the jungle to look for night animals like snakes, tarantulas or if you are lucky luminescent mushrooms or tarsiers. Meals : Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 2 : PONDOK TANGGUY – CAMP LEAKEY After an extraordinary breakfast, you will go in time to see the Pondok Tanggui Camp at the time of feeding (9 AM). Sooner or later, you will see how the branches of the treetops begin to move, and then you will see the silhouettes of the Orangutans arriving at the feeding platform. Pondok Tanggui was a release camp for young Orangutans that were rehabilitated, and they continue to add food every day to prevent the Orangutans from leaving because of a lack of food. They end up outside the National Park, with the following risk of falling into traps of settlers or fields of palm oil plantations. After the Orangutans begin to leave, you will return to the klotok again to go further up the river. You will see how the coloration of the river changes, and you will have the opportunity to see crocodiles and large lizards, together with Gibbon’s and proboscis monkeys. Arrival at Camp Leakey, the old orangutan research and rehabilitation center since 1971, when a student at UCLA Los Angeles University, Birutte Galdikas began studying the Orangutans there. The name Camp Leaky comes from Birutte’s own teacher, the Paleoanthropologist Louis Leakey. At least 200 orangutans had already been cured and returned to the jungles, thanks to this center. However, since 1995, the Government of Indonesia has banned the introduction of more Orangutans into this camp, so Orangutans are increasingly adapting more to freedom. To this day, this camp is used as an investigation into the behavior and feeding of Orangutans. You will take advantage of your guide to explore the interiors of the jungle a bit to look for orangutans in freedom and other animals. At 14.00, you can see the feeding time of the Orangutans. You can also visit the small museum made by the scientist Dr. Birute Galdikas. When you are finished observing the orangutans in this camp, and if the weather and conditions permit, you will make a short trek through the jungle on our way back to the boat to look for wild orangutans and other animals. You will have the opportunity to learn from our local guides, some of whom were born in the jungle, how to look for animals or plants, or simply listen to their experience of life in the jungle. The jungles of Borneo have given life and have been home to the settlers for many years. The jungles, under the eyes of the grandparents, are able to give you everything you need. Food, water, medicines, etc. Yes... Never put anything in your mouth without the recommendation of your guide. In the afternoon, if the circumstances permit, the boat will be docked near a firefly congregation, and you can enjoy the show of its luminescence. Note: The Birute Galdikas Museum at Camp Leaky is currently closed for maintenance purposes. Regrettably, visits to this site will not be possible until further notice. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on the reopening of the museum. Meals : Breakfast – Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Klotok Boat Day 3 : KUMAI PORT – PANGKALAN BUN – DAYAK VILLAGE After breakfast, you make a final sail towards Kumai, where you will approach the car and go to Dayak village. On the way, you will go through indigenous villages, river workers, and people making their living near the river. You will pass some rapids with caution. You will stop on the way to be able to have lunch. Upon reaching the Dayak village, our guide will take you to the Long House (they are the typical houses of the Dayak tribes in Borneo – very long houses where almost a village lives inside). Upon arrival, you will realize the kindness of the town. Normally, they celebrate that people from outside come to visit them, because for them, it is a source of pride that people from so far away travel so much to be able to keep them company. Due to that, on arrival, it is normal to celebrate this visit with dances and some other local liquor! After walking around, the communal dinner with the whole tribe arrives, and then they will ring the bell, with which the whole town will gather to do dances and enjoy the night with what they call Pesta Menarik Horn Bill (Horn Festival Bill). Note: The guest house will be based on the basic house of local people, where you can experience their lives and get closer to their culture, with very standard facilities, a shared bathroom, and a shared house with other guests. Meals : Breakfast – Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Basic Guest House in the Village Day 4 : DAYAK VILLAGE – PANGKALAN BUN In the morning, you can visit the surroundings of the village, share stories with them, and help them in their daily tasks. You can also take the opportunity to see the manual work they do and usually take to the city to sell, such as masks, carpets, statues, etc. After packing everything, start the way back to Pangkalan Bun. On the way, you can stop at the Kotawaringin Palace and take pictures around. Lunch will be on the way, with an arrival in the afternoon at Pangkalan Bun. Transfer to the hotel, and the rest of the afternoon is free. Meals : Breakfast – Lunch – Dinner Accommodation : Arsela Hotel or similar Day 5 : HOTEL – PANGKALAN BUN AIRPORT After breakfast, transfer to the airport. End of our services. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : -',NULL,'Bedding type: 1 DBL Kingsize bed room + 1 Twin bed room Allergies: NO BEEF and 1 person allergies shellfish Flight information: ETA 08.10 by Batik Air ID6135 from Surabaya on 03 October 2024 ETD 08.50 by Batik Air ID6134 to Surabaya on 07 October 2024 Accommodation: 03 - 04 Oct. Basic Guest House at Dayak 04 - 05 Oct. Mercure Hotel Pangkalan Bun - Premium Superior Room 05 - 06 Oct. Rimba Lodge - Amethyst Room 06 - 07 Oct. Standard klotok (no AC) Program: 03 Oct. Arrive Pangkalan Bun - Dayak Village. Overnight at Basic Guest House (L/D) 04 Oct. Dayak Village - Pangkalan Bun. Overnight at Mercure Pangkalan Bun (B/L/D) 05 Oct. Pangkalan Bun - Kumai Port - Tanjung Harapan Camp. Overnight Rimba Lodge (B/L/D) 06 Oct. Pondok Tangguy - Camp Leakey. Overnight standard klotok (no AC) (B/L/D) 07 Oct. Kumai port - Departure Pangkalan Bun (B)','{\"date\": \"2024-10-03\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-10-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5261347,'850','Mónica Morgado Cursach',30662,213260,'11D10N Medan - Tangkahan - Bukit Lawang - Brastagi - Samosir/ Lake Toba - Weh Island Tour','Confirmed','RVL 11D MTBKLT',11,'2024-11-04','2024-11-14','Nicholas','Komang',4,'Persons (2-3 / Double)',70080000.00,'DAY 01 : ARRIVAL IN MEDAN Upon arrival at Kualanamu International Airport pick up by our tour guide and then Transfer to hotel, afternoon free at own leisure. Meals : - Accommodation : Emerald Garden Hotel or Le Polonia Hotel or Similar Hotel DAY 02 : MEDAN - CITY TOUR - TANGKAHAN After breakfast, pick up by our tour guide and then transfer to town for city tour visiting Sultan Palace, Great Mosque, Chinese temple and then drive to Tangkahan via Binjai and Batang Serangan. Afternoon arrival at Tangkahan check in MEGA INN. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Mega Inn Lodge DAY 03 : TANGKAHAN - ELEPHANT WASHING & RIVER SAFARI After breakfast walking to the elephant station and then join with the Mahout during washing the Elephant, and then feed the elephant, after feeding the Elephant enjoying tubing through the river and stop will be made at Fantastic Buluh Waterfall where you may enjoy the waterfall where you can take nature shower and then you can enjoy sun bathing and swimming on the river and enjoying picnic lunch on the beach of the river. Afternoon arrival at the village you can get in touch with local people, where you can see the daily activities of the local people and then return to guest house by walking, arrival at guest house you can take a rest or visit hot springs and waterfall near the guest house. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Accommodation : Mega Inn Lodge DAY 04 : TANGKAHAN - BUKIT LAWANG BY JEEP After breakfast leave Tangkahan for Bukit Lawang by Jeep passing plantation and jungle raod, on the way stop at Plantation and several interesting places (school!!!) for enjoying the panorama and witness the activities of the local people. Upon arrival at Bukit Lawang check in to hotel and afternoon free at own leisure to enjoy the nature of Bukit Lawang. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Bukit Lawang Cottage or Rindu Alam Hotel DAY 05 : FULLDAY LEUSER NATIONAL PARK TRACKING After breakfast walking to the jungle to start a jungle tracking to explore the nature of Leuser National park with their flora and fauna, the possibility to see Orang Utan on their own habitat and other kind of animal such as Thomas leaf monkeys, long tail macaque, gibbon, black gibbon and other kind of flora and fauna of tropical rain forest. This fullday tracking will finish in the afternoon, after tracking return to hotel. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Accommodation : Bukit Lawang Cottages or Rindu Alam Hotel DAY 06 : BUKIT LAWANG - BRASTAGI After breakfast, drive to Brastagi via new road and passing several village such as Namu Ukur, Rumah Galuh and Simpang Kuta Buluh. On the way you can enjoying the panorama of Sinabung Volcano, and afternoon arrival in Brastagi visiting Lhumbini Park with its duplicate of Shwedagon pagoda, fruit market, and Gundaling hill, after that in afternoon check in to hotel. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Sinabung Hotel or Mikie Holiday Hotel DAY 07 : BRASTAGI - KETAMBE After breakfast drive to Ketambe, on the way visit Batak Karo traditional village at Lingga and then continue drive by passing Bukit Barisan with stop at several interesting places, arrival at Ketambe check in to simple guest house. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Thousand Hills Guesthouse or Friendship Guesthouse DAY 08 : FULLDAY JUNGLE TRACKING After breakfast tracking at Ketambe (Leuser National Park), to explore the primary tropical rain forest with their wild life living in their natural habitat. You will go deep into the jungle where you have chance to see the wild Orangutans, Gibbons, Monkeys, Deer, Wild Pigs and kind of birds. You will also see special plants and insects of the Sumatra jungle. You may enjoy hot, warm and cold bath as the hot water is flowing into the river and mix up with the cold. Afternoon return to guest house. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Accommodation : Thousand Hills Guesthouse or Friendship Guesthouse DAY 09 : KETAMBE - SAMOSIR ISLAND Early in the morning at 7.00 you proceed the journey to Samosir island via Sidikalang and Tele. And at Tele stop to enjoy fantastic view of Lake Toba, afternoon arrival at Samosir Island check in to hotel. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Thousand Hills Guesthouse or Friendship Guesthouse DAY 10 : SAMOSIR EXCURSION BY CAR After breakfast we start for our fullday excursion by car in the interior of Samosir island and en-route visiting : - Ambarita (to see the stone chairs and tables where once used as the execution site by the ancient tribal chieftains). - Aek Natonang (here we can see the small lake found of the top of Samosir Island and its panorama view). - Tomok (to see the old sarcophages belonged to former Sidabutar Kings and his descendants). In afternoon return back to hotel and free at leisure. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Thousand Hills Guesthouse or Friendship Guesthouse DAY 11 : SAMOSIR - MEDAN / AIRPORT After breakfast crossing back to Parapat and then drive Medan via Pematang Siantar and Tebingtinggi, stop will be made at several interesting places, this trip will take about 5 hours driving. Arrival in Medan directly transfer to airport for your flight to next destination. TOUR END. Meals : Breakfast',NULL,'Schedule Flight Medan 04 & 14 Nov : ETA : 16.00 MH864 from Kuala Lumpur on 04 November ETD : 09.20 MH865 to Kuala Lumpur on 14 November Schedule Flight Medan - Banda Aceh - Medan 10 & 13 Nov : 10 NOV 2024. KNO – BTJ at 13:20 – 14:30 by QG 904 13 NOV 2024. BTJ – KNO at 15:00 – 16:10 by QG 905 PROGRAM & ACOMMODATION : 04 NOV – DAY 01: ARRIVAL IN MEDAN – TANGKAHAN (Mega Inn Lodge - Standard room) 05 NOV – DAY 02: TANGKAHAN – ELEPHANT WASHING & RIVER SAFARI (Mega Inn Lodge - Standard room) 06 NOV – DAY 03: TANGKAHAN – BUKIT LAWANG BY JEEP (Bukit Lawang Cottage-Butterfly room) 07 NOV – DAY 04: BUKIT LAWANG – TRACKING – BRASTAGI (Sinabung Hotel - Superior room) 08 NOV – DAY 05: BRASTAGI – SAMOSIR/LAKE TOBA (Tabo Cottage - Deluxe room) 09 NOV – DAY 06: SAMOSIR EXCURSION BY CAR (Tabo Cottage - Deluxe room) 10 NOV – DAY 07: SAMOSIR – MEDAN – BANDA ACEH (Parkside Alhambra Hotel - Deluxe room) 11 NOV – DAY 08: BANDA ACEH – PULAU WEH (Casanemo Resort - Beachfront Bungalow) 12 NOV, DAY 09: WEH ISLAND – OWN PROGRAM (Casanemo Resort - Beachfront Bungalow) 13 NOV, DAY 10: PULAU WEH - MEDAN (Emerald Garden Hotel-Superior room) 14 NOV – DAY 11: MEDAN – AIRPORT (FLIGHT etd : 09.20)','{\"date\": \"2024-11-04\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-14\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5261510,'851','Karen Williams',30683,203336,'Mini-stay Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-01','2024-11-01','Ayu','Tami',1,'Double',560000.00,'Step into one of our comfortable and spacious Deluxe Rooms. Here you can kick back and relax at ease and prepare for your next flight or meeting. Spacious 24 square meters deluxe room with a king or twin beds offering comfortable stay equipped with modern facilities such as air conditioning, arm chair, work desk & chair, flat screen TV with cable and satellite channels, free access internet & Wi-Fi, in room safe, coffee/tea maker, mini cooler, private bathroom with shower and hair dryer, and many more.','Room usage for up to 6 hours Earliest check-in time 09.00 Latest check-out time 23.00 Including transfer between terminals',NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-11-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-01\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5261526,'852','Dale Martin',30671,200626,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-18','2024-11-19','Ayu','Eddy',1,'Twin',1120000.00,'Deluxe Room with a room area of 28 square meters each, there are 2 types of bed, king and twin bed with a size of 28 square meters each.',NULL,'Check-in time 14.00 Check-out time 12.00 Early check-in is