om','Confirmed',NULL,2,'2024-11-11','2024-11-13','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Double',3360000.00,'Sleep soundly in one of the 111 Superior Room with 25 m2 of room size, featuring plush bedding, extra bed is not allowed with this room type. Enjoy our modern bathroom with hot and cold shower or simply relax in front of the TV and enjoy our facilities as swimming pool, hot and cool whirlpool, sauna, steam, and fitness center with personal trainers. This room also equipped with LED TV 43\", local and international telephone, broadband internet access, safety deposit box, air conditioning, radio, non or smoking room option, 24 hours room service, minibar, tea & coffee maker, in room message, slippers, and hairdryer.',NULL,'Check-in time is 14:00. Check-out time is 12:00. Early check-in is based on availability upon arrival and at an additional charge payable directly to the hotel. PLEASE CONSULT YOUR AIRPORT TRANSFER TIME DURING CHECK-IN. FM7 Hotel Airport Pickup Service: +62811-8815-053 (WhatsApp available).','{\"date\": \"2024-11-11\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5262767,'855','Ilya Raskin',30662,213278,'4D3N Tangkahan - Bukit Lawang','Confirmed',NULL,4,'2024-11-02','2024-11-05','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Persons (2-3 / Double)',0.00,'DAY 01 : MEDAN - BUKIT LAWANG Arrival at Kuala Namu Int airport Medan drive to Bukit Lawang with stop at several plantations for Rubber and Palm oil, after that arrival at Bukit Lawang check in to hotel. Meals : - Accommodation : Bukit Lawang Cottages or Rindu Alam Hotel DAY 02 : FULLDAY LEUSER NATIONAL PARK TRACKING After breakfast walking to the jungle to start a jungle tracking to explore the nature of Leuser National park with their flora and fauna, the possibility to see Orang Utan on their own habitat and other kind of animal such as Thomas leaf monkeys, long tail macaque, gibbon, black gibbon and other kind of flora and fauna of tropical rain forest. This fullday tracking will finish in the afternoon and then return back to hotel. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch Accommodation : Bukit Lawang Cottages or Rindu Alam Hotel DAY 03 : BUKIT LAWANG - MEDAN After breakfast free at own leisure for swimming or walking and then drive to Medan, upon arrival in Medan, city tour by visiting Great Mosque, Sultan Palace and Chinese Temple. Meals : Breakfast Accommodation : Emerald Garden Hotel or Le Polonia Hotel DAY 04 : HOTEL - AIRPORT After breakfast transfer to Airport for your flight to next destination. Meals : Breakfast',NULL,'Itinerary: 02 Nov, Day 01: Arrival Medan – Tangkahan 03 Nov, Day 02: Tangkahan – Elephant Washing – River Safari – Bukit Lawang (B, L) 04 Nov, Day 03: Bukit Lawang Soft Trekking – Medan (B) 05 Nov, Day 04: Medan Departure (B) Accommodation: 02 - 03 Nov: Mega Inn - Twin Standard Room 03 - 04 Nov: Eco Lodge Bukit Lawang - Twin Butterfly Room 04 - 05 Nov: Hotel Emerald Garden Medan - Twin Superior Room','{\"date\": \"2024-11-02\", \"text\": \"ETA: 11.55 by Garuda Indonesia GA184 from Jakarta on 02 Nov\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Medan Airport\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-05\", \"text\": \"ETD: 08.00 by Super Air Jet IU363 to Surabaya on 05 Nov\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Medan Airport\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5262788,'855','Ilya Raskin',30684,200640,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-05','2024-11-06','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Twin',0.00,'Designed to embody fresher and younger ambience, our Deluxe Room is a convenient stay for those who plan a relatively shorter stay in Semarang. The room is provided with either a king size or deluxe twin beds.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-11-05\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5262793,'855','Ilya Raskin',30679,200582,'Deluxe Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-06','2024-11-07','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Twin',0.00,'Stylish, spacious and bright with an open-concept bedroom and bathroom, and a private balcony with daybed. Room includes a desk, a small sofa and a floor-to-ceiling window for maximum natural light.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-11-06\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-07\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5262795,'855','Ilya Raskin',30571,202567,'Superior Room','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-08','2024-11-09','Rendy','Rendy',1,'Twin',1290000.00,'Located at the Second Floor, 35 sqm comfort living with a touch of Balinese style featuring completed fitting, Cable TV, a fancy bathroom comprises rain shower and good quality amenities. Also dedicated Wi-Fi Access to complete your day.',NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-11-08\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 06:49:25','2026-08-28 06:54:29'),(5262798,'855','Ilya Raskin',31083,213615,'5D4N Flores Overland','Confirmed',NULL,5,'2024-11-09','2024-11-13','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Persons (2-3 / Double)',0.00,'TOUR ITINERARY DAY 1 : DENPASAR - MAUMERE / ENDE - MONI Upon arrival in MAUMERE meet and greet with our Tour Guide and driving directly to Moni. Visit Sikka Village to see the oldest Portuguese church heritage and ikat weaving, also Stop at Paga Beach and Koka beach for relaxing and beach-walking. On arrival at Moni checking in at Kelimutu Ecolodge / Kelimutu Paradiso Resort. Lunch en route, dinner at local restaurant in Moni. Meals : Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Kelimutu Ecolodge DAY 2 : MONI - KELIMUTU - BAJAWA It’s worth to experience the sun rise at Kelimutu three colored crater lakes, you will begin your day early in the morning (start about 04.00 o’clock). Last update: 15 Jul 2013, typical eruption style: Explosive, Kelimutu volcano eruptions: 1968, 1938, and 1865. Kelimutu (Keli Mutu) volcano in central Flores, Indonesia, is famous for its 3 colorful acid crater lakes, where different salts and oxides in suspension or solution give the lakes varying colors ranging from blue and dark green to intense red. In historic times, few small phreatic explosions have been the only activity at the volcano. The scenic craters with their lakes are popular tourist destinations. Background: The western lake, Tiwu Ata Mbupu (Lake of Old People) is commonly blue. Tiwu Nua Muri Kooh Tai (Lake of Young Men and Maidens) and Tiwu Ata Polo (Bewitched, or Enchanted Lake), which share a common crater wall, are commonly green- and red-coloured, respectively, although lake colours vary periodically. During the dry season reduction processes let Ba, Cu, and As minerals precipitate, in the wet season, the oxidation and precipitation of iron minerals (ferric oxide: Fe2O3) produces intense red colors. Active upwelling occurs at the two eastern lakes and is probably fed by subaqueous fumaroles. Kelimutu volcano is flanked by the older cones of Kelido and Kelibara 3 km to the north and 2 km to the south, respectively (Source: GVP) On the way you will experience the dramatic change in both nature pattern and ethnicity. You could be found yourself in the Lio ethnic’s environment – pay at call to their village Wologai and try to comprehend the locals daily life or just having closer look into their work of architectures. Lunch will be served at a local restaurant in Ende. Continue drive to Bajawa with Stop at Penggajawa Blue stone beach, here you could see local woman collect the stones to sell and building the house of garden. Before checking at hotel, drive to Soa hot spring, then checking at Virgo / Edelways Hotel. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Virgo Hotel or Edelways Hotel DAY 3 : BAJAWA - RUTENG Breakfast at hotel. Explore traditional village of Bajawa tribes. Visit Bena -a megalithic village where people do preserve their ancestral spirits believed and way of life-, which can be seen in their \"Ngadhu\" and \"Bhaga\". Ngadhu and Bhaga are conical thatched roof huts symbolized their Male and Female ancestral spirits. On the way stop on the slope of Inerie active volcano for taking pictures. Lunch will be provided enroute, then continue overland to Ruteng. Stops will be made at Aimere village to see \"arak\" distillation and fresh palm juice tapping and at \"Ranamese\" Lake, and snapshot at magnificent peak of Mt. Inerie -an active volcano-. Continue overland to Ruteng -cool and small town as the capital city of Manggarai Regency- where major Manggarainese tribe dwelt. On arrival direct check into spring hill hotel. Afternoon visit “Liang Bua” the home of Homo Florensies. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Spring Hill or Sindha or Revaya Hotel DAY 4 : RUTENG - LABUAN BAJO Breakfast at hotel. Driving to Labuan Bajo -the Western tip of Flores Island-. On the way stops will be made at Lembor or Cancar area to see the unexposed world wonder “Lingko” –The spider web shape rice fields–. It’s probably the only such a rice field ever exist on earth, then continue to Tengku lese to enjoy the fantastic Water fall, and other places according to local happenings. Lunch will be served at Local restaurant at Labuan bajo, Dinner and overnight at Puri Sari or La Cecile. Meals : Breakfast - Lunch - Dinner Accommodation : Seastra or Golo Hilltop or Puri Sari or La Cecile DAY 5 : LABUAN BAJO - DENPASAR After breakfast, taking short city sight seeing with visiting the Amelia sea view point Then local market before taking you to the airport for flight to Denpasar. Meals : Breakfast Attention: The itinerary is subject to change due to the weather, tide level and operating conditions without prior notice.',NULL,'Itinerary: 09 Nov, Day 08: Arrival Maumere – Moni (B, L) 10 Nov, Day 09: Moni – Kelimutu – Bajawa (B, L, D) 11 Nov, Day 10: Bajawa – Ruteng (B, L, D) 12 Nov, Day 11: Ruteng – Labuan Bajo (B, L, D) 13 Nov, Day 12: Labuan Bajo Departure (B) Accommodation: 09 - 10 Nov: Kelmutu Eco Lodge - Twin Standard Room 10 - 11 Nov: Manulalu Jungle Villa - Twin Bungalow 11 - 12 Nov: Spring Hill Hotel Ruteng - Twin Standard Room 12 - 13 Nov: Puri Sari Beach Hotel - Twin Superior Room','{\"date\": \"2024-11-09\", \"text\": \"ETA: 15.10 by Wings Air IW1821 from Kupang on 09 Nov\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Maumere Airport\", \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-13\", \"text\": \"ETD: 14.00 by Batik Air ID6527 to Jakarta on 13 Nov\", \"time\": null, \"locality\": \"Labuan Bajo Airport\", \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:00:34','2026-08-28 07:00:34'),(5262859,'855','Ilya Raskin',30805,207343,'CGK-KNO','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-02','2024-11-02','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Person',4620000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-11-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-02\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5262862,'855','Ilya Raskin',30805,207345,'DPS-MOF','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-09','2024-11-09','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Person',5720000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-11-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-09\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','2026-08-28 07:29:18','2026-08-28 07:29:18'),(5262863,'855','Ilya Raskin',30805,212510,'LBJ-CGK','Confirmed',NULL,1,'2024-11-13','2024-11-13','Rendy','Rendy',2,'Person',5500000.00,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"date\": \"2024-11-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"locality\": null, \"location\": null}','{\"date\": \"2024-11-13\", \"text\": null, \"time\": null, \"localit